{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5","id":1148951,"title":"RWBY Volume 5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-11T18:27:17-07:00","id":1148951,"title":"RWBY Volume 5","content":"Well, with one day until the theatrical release of Volume 5, I figured it was high time to set up the thread, especially since Volume 5's shaping up to be quite the action-packed volume (or at least more so than the prior volume). In case you haven't seen them, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bZAS_rzgCE0\" target=\"_blank\">here are Weiss's</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mTJzFCebdvQ\" target=\"_blank\">and Blake's character shorts</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xvVZMaIHhWM\" target=\"_blank\">this is the trailer for the season</a>. Yang's trailer is apparently hitting YouTube on Saturday, and while First Members get the episode on Saturday as usual (with it hitting YouTube next week, again as usual), free members have to wait until Tuesday to get it rather than Sunday. I'm a little disappointed about the Tuesday thing, but at least we won't have to wait a week to see it like with Camp Camp. Plus there's the whole pun thing -- I wonder if Barbara had a say in the release schedule...<br /> <br /> So, who here's hyped for the season? I know I am. The character shorts look awesome, and I can't wait to see what happens next!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T21:10:39-07:00","id":1148988,"title":"","content":"Got a ticket to tomorrow's theater release. I am ready for this Volume.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T06:58:25-07:00","id":1149079,"title":"","content":"I am experiencing all of the hype. RWBY is top-notch, thanks for the trailer link.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T07:29:58-07:00","id":1149090,"title":"","content":"Wait. Why is this in the exalted forum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T07:54:34-07:00","id":1149103,"title":"","content":"Because Volumes 1\u20134 were. And they were here because RWBY has very strong Exalted vibes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T08:35:30-07:00","id":1149126,"title":"","content":"In the Exalted context, I'm really excited about Adam Taurus this season. He's a good example of what a top Lunar warmonger should be like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T09:07:02-07:00","id":1149133,"title":"","content":"Racking up points with Amoth City-Smiter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T11:42:17-07:00","id":1149182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1149126#post1149126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Exalted context, I'm really excited about Adam Taurus this season. He's a good example of what a top Lunar warmonger should be like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunarness is tough to find in RWBY, since just about everyone tends to fall under the &quot;excellent ability&quot; vibe. I'd peg him just as easily as a solar or abyssal, for example. Especially abyssal since he has this genocidal penchant.<br /> <br /> Exceptions are what? Penny's an easy alchie, velvet's flexible combat mimicry is fertile ground for lunar prowess...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T11:48:39-07:00","id":1149187,"title":"","content":"I think what they're going with is that Faunuses (Fauna?) are all Lunars, due to their part-beast nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T11:54:00-07:00","id":1149189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1149182#post1149182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunarness is tough to find in RWBY</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue it is tough to find anywhere, in anything. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> since just about everyone tends to fall under the &amp;quot;excellent ability&amp;quot; vibe. I'd peg him just as easily as a solar or abyssal, for example. Especially abyssal since he has this genocidal penchant.<br /> <br /> Exceptions are what? Penny's an easy alchie, velvet's flexible combat mimicry is fertile ground for lunar prowess... </div> </div> </div>Qrow and Raven can shapeshift into birds and were raised by a roving bandit tribe. <br /> <br /> Other than that, most everyone is roughly equivalent to Dragon-Blooded, right down to hereditary heroism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T11:57:14-07:00","id":1149191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1149187#post1149187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what they're going with is that Faunuses (Fauna?) are all Lunars, due to their part-beast nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, Faunus are Creation's beastfolk. A few helpful mutations but nothing on the level of Terrestrial/Celestial power difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T12:54:09-07:00","id":1149210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1149182#post1149182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunarness is tough to find in RWBY, since just about everyone tends to fall under the &quot;excellent ability&quot; vibe. I'd peg him just as easily as a solar or abyssal, for example. Especially abyssal since he has this genocidal penchant.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;We're better than the Dragon-Blooded. We have everything the Dragon-Blooded have and more.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's the Lunar narrative right there. The Dragon-Blooded have what should be yours, and the best way to get it is to turn yourself into a monster and raze their cities to the ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T13:24:19-07:00","id":1149510,"title":"","content":"I'm not super hype about the premiere, but I'm happy that the volume is starting. It's likely to get moving fairly quickly, and there are several upcoming events I'm waiting for.<br /> <br /> The reunion of team RWBY. This is almost bound to happen, and I think it'll be sooner rather than later, but at least before the volume ends. It's bound to be good.<br /> <br /> There might be a confrontation with Adam. I wonder whose fight he is now. He's certainly Blake's conflict, but I think there's a good chance Yang will be the one doing the bashing.<br /> <br /> And I'm hoping we'll see Cinder back in action this volume as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T15:55:13-07:00","id":1149555,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping it's the last volume we see cinder in. Preferably because Ruby takes her head off, and Emerald's too.<br /> <br /> Yes, I'm still sore about Penny.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm guessing we'll see more Tyrian and the rest of Salem's lackeys actually do something. I mean that's the real question isn't it. What are they doing for her, and why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T17:29:27-07:00","id":1149573,"title":"","content":"Penny will be back. She's an android. The only question is if Jepetto or Roman puts her back together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T18:37:52-07:00","id":1149584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1149187#post1149187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Faunuses (Fauna?)</div> </div> </div> </div>The plural of Faunus is Faunus. I saw Arryn confirm that in a livestream following the V1 finale.<br /> <br /> She apparently had to REALLY work at it to keep from blurting out that Blake was a Faunus throughout the V1 buildup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T19:01:34-07:00","id":1149589,"title":"","content":"I don't see why; that was perhaps the worst kept secret ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T23:47:19-07:00","id":1149609,"title":"","content":"I'm going to be honest... I had no idea Blake was wearing a ribbon on her ears the first time I watched through volume 1, not until she took it off in front of RW-Y anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T02:41:07-07:00","id":1149628,"title":"","content":"I was honestly surprised it was supposed to be a secret at any point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T09:45:43-07:00","id":1149712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1149510#post1149510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reunion of team RWBY. This is almost bound to happen, and I think it'll be sooner rather than later, but at least before the volume ends. It's bound to be good.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually seems only somewhat likely. Blake is still locked down in a Menagerie plotline she's nowhere near resolving. That has an explicit and eventual tie back to Haven but which may not hit this season.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I'm hoping we'll see Cinder back in action this volume as well. </div> </div> </div>Team CNEM (or however you abbreviate it) really fell off the radar. I mean, Cinder did get maimed; she lost an eye and probably also an arm, and not as, uh, cleanly as Yang did. But eventually they need to get it in gear. They spent two seasons giving three of those four people a lot of characterization and dedicated an entire episode to their backstory, and then they sort of... vanished.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, the structure of the show is such that it's always moved like molasses; the first three seasons have about as much content as any one season of a more traditional show.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Penny will be back. She's an android. The only question is if Jepetto or Roman puts her back together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Roman is super ultra dead. The crew have been explicit and emphatic about this multiple times. He was eaten on-screen by an enormous Nevermore. He's not coming back.<br /> <br /> What I <i>want</i> to happen with Penny is that Ironwood secretly put her into Yang's arm as a surveillance and insurance policy.<br /> <br /> What I <i>expect</i> to happen is that Ironwood is rebuilding her without all those pesky human emotions to be his ultimate enforcer and Ruby is gonna need to fight her when the time comes to deal with Tin Man's raging boner for authoritarianism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":4742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","user":"Murcushio","date":". 10-14-2017, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T11:16:26-07:00","id":1149740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1149712#post1149712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This actually seems only somewhat likely. Blake is still locked down in a Menagerie plotline she's nowhere near resolving. That has an explicit and eventual tie back to Haven but which may not hit this season.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, I guess it doesn't need to happen. Still, both Ruby and Yang are now hunting the same target, and Weiss is rapidly closing in on Mistral as well. Three of them back together? I'll take it!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1149712#post1149712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Team CNEM (or however you abbreviate it) really fell off the radar. I mean, Cinder did get maimed; she lost an eye and probably also an arm, and not as, uh, cleanly as Yang did. But eventually they need to get it in gear. They spent two seasons giving three of those four people a lot of characterization and dedicated an entire episode to their backstory, and then they sort of... vanished.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, the structure of the show is such that it's always moved like molasses; the first three seasons have about as much content as any one season of a more traditional show.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it'd be a shame not to have them back again. Particularly Cinder for me, since as you said, we do know some things about Emerald's and Mercury's motivations, but Cinder is still a mystery. I want to know more about her!<br /> <br /> As for team name, when Roman was around, CRME for &quot;crime&quot; was the established moniker. Poor Neo didn't get a spot. Now, there's not really a catchy one. Maybe ENMC for &quot;enemies&quot;? But that's both weak, and also doesn't follow the rule of having the leader's name first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1149712#post1149712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Roman is super ultra dead. The crew have been explicit and emphatic about this multiple times. He was eaten on-screen by an enormous Nevermore. He's not coming back.<br /> <br /> What I <i>want</i> to happen with Penny is that Ironwood secretly put her into Yang's arm as a surveillance and insurance policy.<br /> <br /> What I <i>expect</i> to happen is that Ironwood is rebuilding her without all those pesky human emotions to be his ultimate enforcer and Ruby is gonna need to fight her when the time comes to deal with Tin Man's raging bone for authoritarianism.</div> </div> </div> </div>They will do something with Penny, yeah. They can't just literally cut up a beloved character and then not mention her again. My guess is she will be back in some form.<br /> <br /> No so for Roman or Pyrrha, of course. They are so dead.<br /> <br /> Well, time for me to watch this thing. Can't lie, I'm pretty excited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T12:18:57-07:00","id":1149760,"title":"","content":"I remember hearing once that Miles or someone else at Rooster Teeth said that Penny is their version of Ayanami Rei.<br /> <br /> And the heart breaking thing about her is that she was actually three different people, one replacing the last after the previous one died.<br /> <br /> Or, at least that's one interpretation of Rei.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping that's not the interpretation RT would seek to homage with Penny. I want <i>Penny </i>back, not a replacement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T12:21:55-07:00","id":1149762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1149740#post1149740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for team name, when Roman was around, CRME for &quot;crime&quot; was the established moniker. Poor Neo didn't get a spot. Now, there's not really a catchy one. Maybe ENMC for &quot;enemies&quot;? But that's both weak, and also doesn't follow the rule of having the leader's name first.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to imagine that during the Vytal Festival, they were Team Cinnamon (CNEM). Leader initial first, also a color, checks all the boxes.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T12:25:57-07:00","id":1149763,"title":"","content":"I have many more articles speculating about the four kingdoms and Menagerie, if anyone wants to check out my Tumblr.<br /> <br /> Plus, a lot more original Semblance ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T12:53:34-07:00","id":1149768,"title":"","content":"I want to see Neo again? That'd be nice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T16:28:44-07:00","id":1149787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1149712#post1149712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Roman is super ultra dead. The crew have been explicit and emphatic about this multiple times. He was eaten on-screen by an enormous Nevermore. He's not coming back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since when has being dead ever stopped someone in comics, anime, or fantasy from doing something if the authors want it done? Roman Torchwick is a reference to Romeo Candlewick from Pinocchio, the one who tempts Pinocchio into disobedience. Getting eaten alive by a giant whale wasn't a death sentence there, so getting eaten by a hippogriff Grimm is an easily reversible narrative situation if the needs of the story demand it.<br /> <br /> Also, I totally spaced the ending of that scene. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I <i>expect</i> to happen is that Ironwood is rebuilding her without all those pesky human emotions to be his ultimate enforcer and Ruby is gonna need to fight her when the time comes to deal with Tin Man's raging boner for authoritarianism. </div> </div> </div>I doubt he'd have her rebuilt without emotions. I'd more expect him to insist on some control mechanism to ensure her loyalty and obedience.<br /> <br /> Ironwood doesn't seem like he likes authoritarian control. To me it seems more like the only tool he's got to try and deal with the problems he's facing is a hammer and so he has to try to make all those problems look like nails.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T18:24:12-07:00","id":1149818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1149787#post1149787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since when has being dead ever stopped someone in comics, anime, or fantasy from doing something if the authors want it done? Roman Torchwick is a reference to Romeo Candlewick from Pinocchio, the one who tempts Pinocchio into disobedience. Getting eaten alive by a giant whale wasn't a death sentence there, so getting eaten by a hippogriff Grimm is an easily reversible narrative situation if the needs of the story demand it.<br /> <br /> Also, I totally spaced the ending of that scene. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I doubt he'd have her rebuilt without emotions. I'd more expect him to insist on some control mechanism to ensure her loyalty and obedience.<br /> <br /> Ironwood doesn't seem like he likes authoritarian control. To me it seems more like the only tool he's got to try and deal with the problems he's facing is a hammer and so he has to try to make all those problems look like nails.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The world's a mess, and I've just gotta rule it!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T19:36:20-07:00","id":1149827,"title":"","content":"I don't think that'd work anyway. I mean it wasn't penny's emotions or disobedience that caused problems. It was basically a highly planned out and thoroughly controlled assassination plan that struck while Pyrrha was an emotional wreck.<br /> <br /> There's no impetus to make her a zombie from ironwood's end.<br /> <br /> If that did happen it would likely be from the council's side since they have to put up the cash for this they'd expect to get more than a super hunter out of this. THey'd want a loyal super hunter.<br /> <br /> Which is of course missing the point but frankly I'd not be surprised if atlas council doesn't really understand why it's important to have individuality and free will in a world with aura. The upper tiers of atlas society seem to be infested by stupidity and short sightedness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T21:27:37-07:00","id":1149849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1149787#post1149787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since when has being dead ever stopped someone in comics, anime, or fantasy from doing something if the authors want it done? Roman Torchwick is a reference to Romeo Candlewick from Pinocchio, the one who tempts Pinocchio into disobedience. Getting eaten alive by a giant whale wasn't a death sentence there, so getting eaten by a hippogriff Grimm is an easily reversible narrative situation if the needs of the story demand it.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC Roman wasn't even supposed to live past the first episode, though (that's why he's such an incompetent fighter there, and suddenly becomes competent in later appearances.) They stretched out his role because he was unexpectedly popular in his brief appearance in Yang's trailer.<br /> <br /> (I sort of wish they kept him around, too, since he was more entertaining than most of his other villains.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T21:33:42-07:00","id":1149850,"title":"","content":"IS anyone working on a RWBY Splat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T21:40:22-07:00","id":1149852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1149827#post1149827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no impetus to make her a zombie from ironwood's end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, and I doubt he could force Penny's father to do it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If that did happen it would likely be from the council's side since they have to put up the cash for this they'd expect to get more than a super hunter out of this. THey'd want a loyal super hunter.<br /> <br /> Which is of course missing the point but frankly I'd not be surprised if atlas council doesn't really understand why it's important to have individuality and free will in a world with aura. The upper tiers of atlas society seem to be infested by stupidity and short sightedness. </div> </div> </div>Ironwood attended the party, but that doesn't make him one of the same kind of people as the wealthy social elite. We can't simply assume the other council members are, either.<br /> <br /> I know that America's previous president was pretty chummy with the Hollywood elite and those elites have gotten very vocal about backing Democratic policies, but as the current presidency shows, the wealth social elites and the executive branch of government can have completely different ideas about the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1149849#post1149849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC Roman wasn't even supposed to live past the first episode, though (that's why he's such an incompetent fighter there</div> </div> </div> </div>Incompetent? He never actually tries to fight. Fighting would have been a waste of his time, because beating Ruby wouldn't have accomplished anything he needed.<br /> <br /> And if Glynda hadn't arrived, we don't actually know what that exploding Fire Crystal would have done to Ruby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T00:12:27-07:00","id":1149866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1149850#post1149850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IS anyone working on a RWBY Splat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you need to? Yang is Brawl, Ruby is Melee, Weiss is Crane + Sorcery, Blake is Steel Devil (or Tiger) + Stealth. <br /> <br /> Also explains why Adam is so OP, he's using SPSitV","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T00:33:33-07:00","id":1149870,"title":"","content":"1.) What's SPSitV short for?<br /> <br /> 2.) NEED TO? probably not, it'd be perfectly possible to emulate most characters with various builds and exalt types. Just like it would be theoretically possible to emulate a magi-tech robot character by playing a twilight exalted who replaces most of his body with artifact prosthetics and lays down endless evocations to learn on them that let him do all sorts of screwy anime robot stuff, but Alchemicals is still a splat. Besides which the world itself probably rates a few tweaks, like a mod to the crafting system for remnant tech, new weapon types. Dust based magic/magi-tech instead of sorcery based. It's something I think is worth considering at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T00:59:28-07:00","id":1149871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1149870#post1149870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1.) What's SPSitV short for?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Single Point Shining into the Void.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T01:42:07-07:00","id":1149876,"title":"","content":"As an aside, the gag is that it's stupid OP (not that we're starting that again). <br /> <br /> And yeah, I don't mean there's literally no point in a splat, I was meant to point out <i><b>just how much</b></i> you can to with EX3 as is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T03:33:31-07:00","id":1149890,"title":"","content":"I dunno, I kind of want a martial art like Weiss's fighting style. Frozen Ballerina Style?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T08:15:47-07:00","id":1149926,"title":"","content":"I actually wouldn't mind an artifact sword like hers that has many hearthstones and can call upon evocations based on the element of the hearthstone in its primary chamber.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T08:26:57-07:00","id":1149929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1149890#post1149890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, I kind of want a martial art like Weiss's fighting style. Frozen Ballerina Style?</div> </div> </div> </div>Graceful Hummingbird, actually. A style that Holden homebrewed before and that we can ask the devs to bring back officially. Someone on this forum has already taken a &quot;stab&quot; at updating it for Third Edition.<br /> <br /> <br /> Dust magic could be homebrewed into something uniquely its own thing in Creation. We already have Fire Dust in Creation, and the way it is used in firewands is very similar to how Fire Dust is used in Remnant.<br /> <br /> Dust spells would be limited by ammunition rules like firewand firedust, and also generally require you to have (and protect) a financially solvent background to continue affording the supply.<br /> <br /> The &quot;spells&quot; would be structured like Evocations, with one trick leading to other tricks.<br /> <br /> <br /> Semblances are a different mix of elegance and complexity than Charmsets or <i>Naruto</i> Jutsus. By giving a character only one magical trick, it's easier to continue providing challenges that fall outside of their strengths or even continue challenging their strengths. They can learn how to adapt their Semblance to perform new tricks, but it all comes back to a single, mostly-well-defined ability.<br /> <br /> But it essentially makes everyone an Exigent; every &quot;Charmset&quot; needs to be homebrewed. What's more, Creation is a place where mind-altering powers are more commonplace than Remnant, so lacking the &quot;well-roundedness&quot; of a Charmset that must include mental defenses is a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T10:02:27-07:00","id":1149942,"title":"","content":"<b>Ruby Rose, fitting Exaltations: </b><br /> <br /> <i>Fire Aspect</i> (Athletics, Dodge, Firearms, Melee, Presence, Socialize) + Awareness, Craft, War<br /> <br /> <i>Chosen of Battles</i> (Archery, Brawl, Firearms, Melee, Presence, War) + Awareness, Craft, Dodge, Integrity + Martial Arts<br /> <br /> <i>Zenith </i>[Supernal: Athletics] + (Integrity, Lore, Survival, War) + Craft, Dodge, Firearms, Melee, Occult<br /> <br /> <i>Orichalcum </i>(Strength, Charisma, Intelligence) + Dexterity, Perception, Wits<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Yang Xiao-Long, fitting Exaltations:</b><br /> <br /> <i>Fire Aspect </i>(Athletics, Dodge, Firearms, Melee, Presence, Socialize) + Awareness, Brawl, Resistance<br /> <br /> <i>Chosen of Battles</i> (Archery, Brawl, Firearms, Melee, Presence, War) + Awareness, Dodge, Resistance, Socialize + Martial Arts<br /> <br /> <i>Dawn</i> [Supernal: Brawl] + (Awareness, Dodge, Firearms, Resistance) + Athletics, Craft, Drive, Presence, Socialize<br /> <br /> <i>Orichalcum</i> (Strength, Charisma, Intelligence) + Dexterity, Stamina, Wits<br /> <br /> <br /> With everyone as Dragon-Blooded, it can make total sense that Taiyang Xiao-Long was able to father two children so close together with both becoming Exalted.<br /> <br /> After all, they each would have had a different Dragon-Blooded mother. Ruby had worse odds than Yang, but Summer's generative potential alone was enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 10-15-2017, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T11:26:16-07:00","id":1149956,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry... What?<br /> <br /> I have no idea what you're trying to say here Sunder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T12:23:26-07:00","id":1149975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1149956#post1149956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry... What?<br /> <br /> I have no idea what you're trying to say here Sunder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which post?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T17:09:48-07:00","id":1150035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1149942#post1149942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ruby Rose, fitting Exaltations: </b><br /> <br /> <i>Fire Aspect</i> (Athletics, Dodge, Firearms, Melee, Presence, Socialize) + Awareness, Craft, War<br /> <br /> <i>Chosen of Battles</i> (Archery, Brawl, Firearms, Melee, Presence, War) + Awareness, Craft, Dodge, Integrity + Martial Arts<br /> <br /> <i>Zenith </i>[Supernal: Athletics] + (Integrity, Lore, Survival, War) + Craft, Dodge, Firearms, Melee, Occult<br /> <br /> <i>Orichalcum </i>(Strength, Charisma, Intelligence) + Dexterity, Perception, Wits<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Yang Xiao-Long, fitting Exaltations:</b><br /> <br /> <i>Fire Aspect </i>(Athletics, Dodge, Firearms, Melee, Presence, Socialize) + Awareness, Brawl, Resistance<br /> <br /> <i>Chosen of Battles</i> (Archery, Brawl, Firearms, Melee, Presence, War) + Awareness, Dodge, Resistance, Socialize + Martial Arts<br /> <br /> <i>Dawn</i> [Supernal: Brawl] + (Awareness, Dodge, Firearms, Resistance) + Athletics, Craft, Drive, Presence, Socialize<br /> <br /> <i>Orichalcum</i> (Strength, Charisma, Intelligence) + Dexterity, Stamina, Wits<br /> <br /> <br /> With everyone as Dragon-Blooded, it can make total sense that Taiyang Xiao-Long was able to father two children so close together with both becoming Exalted.<br /> <br /> After all, they each would have had a different Dragon-Blooded mother. Ruby had worse odds than Yang, but Summer's generative potential alone was enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one.<br /> <br /> I mean I think it might be some sort of sort hand for representing rwby characters in creation, maybe. The third bit seems like it would make sense if I had some context but I'm not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T18:01:00-07:00","id":1150039,"title":"","content":"I was expressing the idea that Ruby or Yang could fit as most of the same kinds of Exalted, and with what Castes and Ability spreads.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then I rounded back to the Dragon-Blooded possibility, and touched on how the current devs have revealed that Dragon-Blooded have a &quot;generative potential&quot; for conceiving children which a high chance of becoming Exalted, and that potential is exhausted for at least five years or even ten years (or longer?) after the child is conceived.<br /> <br /> Taiyang and Raven used up their potentials with Yang, but Summer hadn't born a child at all, so her and Taiyang together had enough potential that Ruby becoming an Exalt like her sister wouldn't be shocking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T14:41:49-07:00","id":1150207,"title":"","content":"I rhink Ozpin would be the only Sidereal in the show (maybe Salem, but we know little about her so far)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T14:55:24-07:00","id":1150214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1150207#post1150207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I rhink Ozpin would be the only Sidereal in the show (maybe Salem, but we know little about her so far)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSalem is far more like a Defiler Caste Infernal. Evil, corrupting, and pulling the strings in the shadows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-