ote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1151192#post1151192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone checked out other RWBY discussionsnyet? Holy cow the Ship to Ship combat is ramping up.</div> </div> </div> </div>The shipping combat has basically been maxed out since 2015 or so.<br /> <br /> I'm a veteran of the Zutara wars of the aughts. Compared to them anything RWBY throws at me is &quot;meh.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Cripes, is it really nine years since ATLA ended? The time does fly.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T23:20:38-07:00","id":1151223,"title":"","content":"You havnt seen the growing pitched battles between Lancaster and Pine Rose/Rose Garden (they havnt finalized on the ship name yet it seems)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T02:23:22-07:00","id":1151248,"title":"","content":"What are those exactly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T02:33:33-07:00","id":1151249,"title":"","content":"Lancaster: Ruby+Jaune<br /> <br /> Pine Rose: Ruby+Oscar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T03:50:11-07:00","id":1151260,"title":"","content":"If there's one thing good about Exalted, is that we don't fight over Swarianna vs Swilith. (Cause who'd want Arianna?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T04:24:12-07:00","id":1151262,"title":"","content":"Ok, guys, come on now, this thread is 100% off topic.<br /> <br /> If you want to talk on how to copy certain actions in the show with charms or how to re-adapt the story is a thing, but talking about the show itself should not be done here, there's an off-topic section for a reason. &quot;Has an Exalt vibe&quot; is not, by any mean, reason enough to be spoken here otherwise I could open Naruto and Dragonball threads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T05:34:48-07:00","id":1151278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1151262#post1151262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, guys, come on now, this thread is 100% off topic.<br /> <br /> If you want to talk on how to copy certain actions in the show with charms or how to re-adapt the story is a thing, but talking about the show itself should not be done here, there's an off-topic section for a reason. &quot;Has an Exalt vibe&quot; is not, by any mean, reason enough to be spoken here otherwise I could open Naruto and Dragonball threads.</div> </div> </div> </div>That ship has sailed, mate. It left the dock <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/547-rwby-thread\">four years ago</a>, or earlier if you consider the old White Wolf forums. It's been <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723380-rwby-season-3\">cruising</a> steadily ever since, and has made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/980953-rwby-volume-4\">multiple laps</a> around the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T07:20:11-07:00","id":1151303,"title":"","content":"I honestly do not care for your history. You've been off topic four years in a row, good for you, but I'm tired of seeing this useless thread bumping up and up while I'm looking for Exalted-themed stuff. Had you stick to a few posts, sure, but it's five pages now and god knows when you'll stop. Since the first one went on for 34 pages I think it's fair to ask for it to be moved rather than clogging the top lines of the Exalted board until you're all done and bored.<br /> <br /> Also, it's not a mark of shame or anything to have a topic in the proper forum section. It's not just a matter of not annoying Exalted-but-not-RWBY fans, it actually helps people partecipating by making it easier to find. What's the problem? Fanboy pride? =P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T08:01:15-07:00","id":1151321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1151303#post1151303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly do not care for your history. You've been off topic four years in a row, good for you, but I'm tired of seeing this useless thread bumping up and up while I'm looking for Exalted-themed stuff. Had you stick to a few posts, sure, but it's five pages now and god knows when you'll stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those five pages contain discussion on the plot of the show, connections between RWBY and Exalted mechanics, connections between RWBY and Exalted canon characters, and ties to other media. These things are interrelated by nature, since talking about RWBY in the context of Exalted obviously involves talking about RWBY. And then there's the usual forum train-of-thought nonsense that gets into any sufficiently long thread.<br /> <br /> Strict compartmentalization between these things feels unnecessary to me. We're not trying to write a reference book here - it's a form of conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T08:23:26-07:00","id":1151330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1151303#post1151303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the first one went on for 34 pages I think it's fair to ask for it to be moved rather than clogging the top lines of the Exalted board until you're all done and bored.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would submit that you direct this request to the mods, rather than randomly shouting about it in the thread itself. The mods are easily identifiable and reachable via direct message.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T08:45:15-07:00","id":1151340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1151303#post1151303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly do not care for your history. You've been off topic four years in a row, good for you, but I'm tired of seeing this useless thread bumping up and up while I'm looking for Exalted-themed stuff. Had you stick to a few posts, sure, but it's five pages now and god knows when you'll stop. Since the first one went on for 34 pages I think it's fair to ask for it to be moved rather than clogging the top lines of the Exalted board until you're all done and bored.<br /> <br /> Also, it's not a mark of shame or anything to have a topic in the proper forum section. It's not just a matter of not annoying Exalted-but-not-RWBY fans, it actually helps people partecipating by making it easier to find. What's the problem? Fanboy pride? =P</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no harm in seeing a topic you're not interested in on a forum you are, and declining to participate. I do it all the time. There are things relevant to other people's <i>Exalted</i> experience that I want no part of, and that's fine. Lots more topics on the board. Or I could create my own, if nothing strikes my fancy.<br /> <br /> To me, <i>RWBY</i> is an interesting source of inspiration for <i>Exalted,</i> partly because of commonalities that make it useful to borrow from, and partly because of differences that I'm certain I don't want to borrow, and those elements can be interesting to discuss in the context of <i>Exalted</i> with other <i>Exalted</i> fans. Or, for lurkers like I usually am, at least follow the discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T09:35:22-07:00","id":1151363,"title":"","content":"The Legend of Korra thread was also in this section while the show ran. Exalted-like shows just seem to end up here sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T11:50:47-07:00","id":1151411,"title":"","content":"Guys, stop feeding the troll","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T13:48:39-07:00","id":1151458,"title":"","content":"Eeeh, they're not a troll. They have a point.<br /> <br /> Let's the mods decide. It really doesn't matter that much anyway, except that it's more convenient for us here, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T18:24:18-07:00","id":1151525,"title":"","content":"It was thinking about Ruby Rose Exalting as a Lunar that got me thinking about a Martial Art based around two-handed firearms.<br /> <br /> It didn't seem right that as a Lunar Exalt, she could have special Charms based around using Crescent Rose's scythe form, but no Charms for its ranged attacks.<br /> <br /> <br /> I didn't get anywhere close to finished, but I came up with some ideas.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>First, some Tags:</i><br /> <br /> &quot;Scope&quot; allows you to use a single Aim action to attack someone at medium or greater range while also enjoying the Aim dice bonus.<br /> <br /> &quot;Laser&quot; allows you to flurry an Aim action together with an attack against a target no further than short range.<br /> <br /> &quot;Burst&quot; represents a special withering attack with a higher Overwhelming value and an Initiative cost; all shotgun slug-shots must be &quot;Burst&quot; attacks<br /> <br /> &quot;Full-Auto&quot; represents the projectile version of the special Chopping attack and an Initiative cost; all shotgun buck-shots must be &quot;Full-Auto&quot; attacks<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Now, Charms:</i><br /> <br /> &quot;From The Hip&quot; is how the martial artist reflexively draws her weapon and fires without careful aim. This Charm can be used to supplement projectile attacks at close range, reducing the penalty of &quot;Burst&quot; and &quot;Full-Auto&quot; attacks, because it represents a stable grip.<br /> <br /> &quot;Down The Sights&quot; is the opposite, emphasizing precision over stability as the shooter lines the gun up to their eye to aim with the scope or iron sights. This Charm supplements an Aim action similar to Righteous Devil's Kiss of the Sun Concentration, but has special interaction with guns that have the &quot;Scope&quot; tag.<br /> <br /> &quot;Steady Aim&quot; improves the benefits of using the environment to steady your weapon. If you go prone, you can use the ground (and negate the &quot;being prone&quot; penalty to the supplemented attack). If you're behind cover, you can rest your rifle over a tree branch, fence, or chest-high wall.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Form Charm would let you ignore the flurry penalties to Martial Arts attacks performed in the same turn as a Disengage or Take Cover action, and also let you use your two-handed gun as a striking weapon like Righteous Devil Form, or to shoot from a prone position without penalty even when not using Steady Aim.<br /> <br /> <br /> Further Charms would revolve around hiding in ambush for a surprise shotgun blast or distant sniping attack. Charms to enhance the use of cover while attempting to enter concealment and to remain concealed, especially while prone.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Mist-Gathering Practice&quot; like the Solar Thrown Charm<br /> <br /> &quot;Falling Icicle Strike&quot; like the Solar Thrown Charm","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T06:30:48-07:00","id":1151630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1151303#post1151303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly do not care for your history. You've been off topic four years in a row, good for you, but I'm tired of seeing this useless thread bumping up and up while I'm looking for Exalted-themed stuff. Had you stick to a few posts, sure, but it's five pages now and god knows when you'll stop. Since the first one went on for 34 pages I think it's fair to ask for it to be moved rather than clogging the top lines of the Exalted board until you're all done and bored.<br /> <br /> Also, it's not a mark of shame or anything to have a topic in the proper forum section. It's not just a matter of not annoying Exalted-but-not-RWBY fans, it actually helps people partecipating by making it easier to find. What's the problem? Fanboy pride? =P</div> </div> </div> </div>I spot two problems with your complaint.<br /> 1) Complaining in the thread because you don't like its content. This is no one's business but the reader's, and simple etiquette is to make the thread title self-explanatory so you don't have to bother opening it. This I feel the thread satisfies, and this complaint will fall on uncaring ears.<br /> <br /> 2) The rwby talks keep going into the plot and into exaltifying it, in an endless back and forth, for the show appeals more closely to exalted's aesthetics than any other game in this board. If &quot;this is too off-topic for Exalted&quot;, this is also too exalted for Off-Topic. We just <i>keep talking about exalted in it</i>. Grey areas, you know? This board is civil almost in its entirety, and one or two threads on the first page being less in-topic than the usual (open the first page. count how many threads overall are not deep into exalted) is not going to break anything. It isn't spamming the page. It isn't completely unrelated. It fits. Being stringent about minutiae just annoys everyone for little to no gain.<br /> <br /> <br /> Other than that, the only advice I can give you is to not go the insufferable route when you decide to go against your audience, like right now with your &quot;i don't cares&quot; and &quot;your conversation is useless&quot;. That'll only earn you needless antagonizing and <b>less</b> propensity to have your point heard.<br /> Despite your own words, you care so much you had to call it out. At least be practical and do it in a way that will have people talk to you on more amicable terms.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T15:49:39-07:00","id":1151774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1151630#post1151630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than that, the only advice I can give you is to not go the insufferable route when you decide to go against your audience, like right now with your &quot;i don't cares&quot; and &quot;your conversation is useless&quot;. That'll only earn you needless antagonizing and <b>less</b> propensity to have your point heard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the fact that a similar thread was off topic but not moved in a different section four years ago relevant to the fact that this thread should be moved because off topic? I think not, and writing that it should be allowed to stay here because no one moved the others is a syllogism. So I don't care about the RWBY topic history. And it's useless related to the Exalted franchise since it doesn't talk about Exalted.<br /> Yes, I may not beat around the bush but I think that those expression worked quite fine to express the issue at hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1) Complaining in the thread because you don't like its content. This is no one's business but the reader's, and simple etiquette is to make the thread title self-explanatory so you don't have to bother opening it. This I feel the thread satisfies, and this complaint will fall on uncaring ears. </div> </div> </div>Of course I'm not forced to read this, but why shouldn't I complain for an off topic thread? I already know that the blind fans won't bulge just to defend their show thread, but I still think they should know that not everyone is okay with this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) The rwby talks keep going into the plot and into exaltifying it, in an endless back and forth, for the show appeals more closely to exalted's aesthetics than any other game in this board. If &quot;this is too off-topic for Exalted&quot;, this is also too exalted for Off-Topic. We just <i>keep talking about exalted in it</i>. Grey areas, you know? </div> </div> </div>The first page has more of half of the posts talking about the show only, without even a comparison with Exalted. Second and fourth page have <u>no</u> reference to Exalted at all, while 3rd page was mostly relevant for this forum. Grey areas may appear here and there, but cmon, talking about going to the theatrical release or who's going to do X is no grey at all. You say it's too Exalted for the off topic section... perhaps, but the thread right now is more OT than IT. If you'd rather keep talking about unrelated stuff the thread should be moved, whether if you'd like to focus on the Exalted affinities then you should take an effort and make it relevant again.<br /> <br /> IMHO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T16:57:59-07:00","id":1151789,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, my proposed Style would support playing Soldier:76, Widowmaker, and Reaper. If the Reaper-inspired Abyssal is using a Firearms Charm that allows him to hold one two-handed shotgun in each hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T16:58:32-07:00","id":1151790,"title":"","content":"Back on topic, I hate Qrow's character design. I just hate Qrow in general really. He's every 14 year old boy's first rpg character rolled into one. <br /> <br /> He's immensely powerful<br /> Commands respect without responsibility<br /> comically drunk without actually being drunk<br /> he has an &quot;edgy&quot; cool hot topic look<br /> definitely isn't based on Dante from DMC<br /> He has a cape on a dress shirt wtf<br /> has a tragic power<br /> He's a &quot;Cool womanizer&quot;<br /> yadda yadda yadda. <br /> <br /> He has no real flaws and no stakes, I don't care if he succeeds or fails, and he only exists as an excuse to move the plot along. He needs to be taken out of the plot (a la Posioned) because he invalidates the combat abilities of RNJR. I'll bet anything that he splits asap because he's challenging Ruby for focal point of the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T18:47:13-07:00","id":1151811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1151790#post1151790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back on topic, I hate Qrow's character design. I just hate Qrow in general really. He's every 14 year old boy's first rpg character rolled into one. <br /> <br /> He's immensely powerful<br /> Commands respect without responsibility<br /> comically drunk without actually being drunk<br /> he has an &amp;quot;edgy&amp;quot; cool hot topic look<br /> definitely isn't based on Dante from DMC<br /> He has a cape on a dress shirt wtf<br /> has a tragic power<br /> He's a &amp;quot;Cool womanizer&amp;quot;<br /> yadda yadda yadda. <br /> <br /> He has no real flaws and no stakes, I don't care if he succeeds or fails, and he only exists as an excuse to move the plot along. He needs to be taken out of the plot (a la Posioned) because he invalidates the combat abilities of RNJR. I'll bet anything that he splits asap because he's challenging Ruby for focal point of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not wrong, but I like Qrow anyway. At least as a supporting character. He'd definitely get annoying as a long-term leader of the team - for the same reason comics often have the most powerful member written out so the other team members get some combat focus - but as a short-term member and plot mover, I think he's pretty great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T18:56:56-07:00","id":1151812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1151525#post1151525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was thinking about Ruby Rose Exalting as a Lunar that got me thinking about a Martial Art based around two-handed firearms.<br /> <br /> It didn't seem right that as a Lunar Exalt, she could have special Charms based around using Crescent Rose's scythe form, but no Charms for its ranged attacks.<br /> <br /> <br /> I didn't get anywhere close to finished, but I came up with some ideas.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>First, some Tags:</i><br /> <br /> &quot;Scope&quot; allows you to use a single Aim action to attack someone at medium or greater range while also enjoying the Aim dice bonus.<br /> <br /> &quot;Laser&quot; allows you to flurry an Aim action together with an attack against a target no further than short range.<br /> <br /> &quot;Burst&quot; represents a special withering attack with a higher Overwhelming value and an Initiative cost; all shotgun slug-shots must be &quot;Burst&quot; attacks<br /> <br /> &quot;Full-Auto&quot; represents the projectile version of the special Chopping attack and an Initiative cost; all shotgun buck-shots must be &quot;Full-Auto&quot; attacks<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Now, Charms:</i><br /> <br /> &quot;From The Hip&quot; is how the martial artist reflexively draws her weapon and fires without careful aim. This Charm can be used to supplement projectile attacks at close range, reducing the penalty of &quot;Burst&quot; and &quot;Full-Auto&quot; attacks, because it represents a stable grip.<br /> <br /> &quot;Down The Sights&quot; is the opposite, emphasizing precision over stability as the shooter lines the gun up to their eye to aim with the scope or iron sights. This Charm supplements an Aim action similar to Righteous Devil's Kiss of the Sun Concentration, but has special interaction with guns that have the &quot;Scope&quot; tag.<br /> <br /> &quot;Steady Aim&quot; improves the benefits of using the environment to steady your weapon. If you go prone, you can use the ground (and negate the &quot;being prone&quot; penalty to the supplemented attack). If you're behind cover, you can rest your rifle over a tree branch, fence, or chest-high wall.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Form Charm would let you ignore the flurry penalties to Martial Arts attacks performed in the same turn as a Disengage or Take Cover action, and also let you use your two-handed gun as a striking weapon like Righteous Devil Form, or to shoot from a prone position without penalty even when not using Steady Aim.<br /> <br /> <br /> Further Charms would revolve around hiding in ambush for a surprise shotgun blast or distant sniping attack. Charms to enhance the use of cover while attempting to enter concealment and to remain concealed, especially while prone.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Mist-Gathering Practice&quot; like the Solar Thrown Charm<br /> <br /> &quot;Falling Icicle Strike&quot; like the Solar Thrown Charm</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My biggest gripe is that I feel a shotgun and a sniper rifle should have 2 MA's for different &quot;feels&quot; in popular culture. A distant sniper vs ...well, Sarge really. Of course,t hat would mean Ruby has 3 MA's (White Reaper seems like a must to everyone else right?). Which would be...a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T19:23:26-07:00","id":1151817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1151812#post1151812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest gripe is that I feel a shotgun and a sniper rifle should have 2 MA's for different &quot;feels&quot; in popular culture. A distant sniper vs ...well, Sarge really.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not like I specifically wanted to lump both together, but...<br /> <br /> Well, look at those rough ideas I had, and tell me if you can think of a way to make different ones which play more to the strengths of shotguns than rifles or carbines.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course,t hat would mean Ruby has 3 MA's (White Reaper seems like a must to everyone else right?). Which would be...a lot. </div> </div> </div>Why three? She doesn't use a shotgun.<br /> <br /> White Reaper Style for the scythe form, Long Arm Style for the carbine/sniper rifle forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T19:53:08-07:00","id":1151824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1151817#post1151817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not like I specifically wanted to lump both together, but...<br /> <br /> Well, look at those rough ideas I had, and tell me if you can think of a way to make different ones which play more to the strengths of shotguns than rifles or carbines.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Why three? She doesn't use a shotgun.<br /> <br /> White Reaper Style for the scythe form, Long Arm Style for the carbine/sniper rifle forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>...for some reason I blanked on that, and just went &quot;oh split this in half, that makes 2, and then add white reaper&quot;. Whoops.<br /> <br /> Okay, looking at the ideas. ...And noting I'm not familar with firearms <i>that</i> much outside pop culture. <br /> I'd probably give the Shotgun MA some sort of reflexive attack for when someone came into close range. I <i>probably</i> wouldn't give it aim charms, since I don't tend to think of a shotgun as a percision implement, more a fire at the momment/ spray and pray. So probably something to help against battlegroups or high clustered targets. Maybe some mobillity charms?<br /> My bigger notion was seperating Sniper Rifle from shotgun, though, more than carbine/rifle from shotgun.<br /> <br /> So, snipers. The entering conceleament is good. I might add an abillity to force a rout check by targeting members of a group or other demoralizing abillities. Something to ignore cover and soak after lining up your shot. Given a sniper's sort of pop culture &quot;serial killer from a far&quot; thing (picking off targets as they panic from the first shot), I'd do something like, inflicting penalties or intimacies of fear after a shot? <br /> <br /> These are off the cuff thouhg, and include me ignoring that Shotgun's probably could be form weapons of Righteous devil... <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T19:55:17-07:00","id":1151826,"title":"","content":"1.) Ruby ... doesn't strike me as a lunar... at least not from a build stand point. I mean story wise yes she could exalt as anything, but her extant build is probably more in line with Solars. ... Which actually makes her exalting as a Lunar fairly interesting. Because up till this point she's been highly focused on abilities/skills over any particular attribute. Although I'd wager she's got pretty decent Dexterity, Intelligence, and Perception.<br /> <br /> 2.) For martial arts regarding guns. Well the shot gun style, or maybe shot-gun and pistol style should emphasize the close and short range, make use of their ability to generally be more useful in tight quarters, and ability to do a lot of damage quickly, but not as precisely, possibly some melee functionality in the form of pistol whips and butt clubbing, also a combat reload capability so they don't get caught with their chamber open. The sniper style should emphasize swift and/or stealthy movement in order to give them the distance they need to unleash their best attacks, aiming more rapidly, or getting more out of the aim action, or both, heavy penetration of both withering and decisive defenses, the ability to aim in adverse conditions such as falling through the air, hiding in water, crashing down a mountain side, riding a horse, or while using our feet to keep the jaws of a tyrant lizard from crashing down on you. You know average everyday issues like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11837,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","user":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","date":". 10-30-2017, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T22:20:58-07:00","id":1151865,"title":"","content":"<i>Righteous Devil</i> already covers shotguns just fine, even though it's ostensibly a pistolero inspired art. The &quot;video game&quot; shotgun is a close quarters boom stick, regardless of their real life range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T06:32:49-07:00","id":1151921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1151826#post1151826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1.) Ruby ... doesn't strike me as a lunar... at least not from a build stand point. I mean story wise yes she could exalt as anything, but her extant build is probably more in line with Solars. ... Which actually makes her exalting as a Lunar fairly interesting. Because up till this point she's been highly focused on abilities/skills over any particular attribute. Although I'd wager she's got pretty decent Dexterity, Intelligence, and Perception.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen a battles sidereal interpretation that I liked as well: She is an omen of change through violence. Almost literally prophesied to do battle.<br /> Her fighting is nothing esoteric, but neither are the sids' (too much) anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T06:38:41-07:00","id":1151924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1151790#post1151790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back on topic, I hate Qrow's character design. I just hate Qrow in general really. He's every 14 year old boy's first rpg character rolled into one.<br /> <br /> He's immensely powerful<br /> Commands respect without responsibility<br /> comically drunk without actually being drunk<br /> he has an &quot;edgy&quot; cool hot topic look<br /> definitely isn't based on Dante from DMC<br /> He has a cape on a dress shirt wtf<br /> has a tragic power<br /> He's a &quot;Cool womanizer&quot;<br /> yadda yadda yadda.<br /> <br /> He has no real flaws and no stakes, I don't care if he succeeds or fails, and he only exists as an excuse to move the plot along. He needs to be taken out of the plot (a la Posioned) because he invalidates the combat abilities of RNJR. I'll bet anything that he splits asap because he's challenging Ruby for focal point of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I half agree. He's on the power level of the other graduated elites. Few people, albeit important people for the story, respect him at all.<br /> <br /> He was put out almost as fast as he was put in the team: he only really fought Tyrian, remember? Everything else he was a rather useless.<br /> He can't stay much longer, that'd be the worst part. I have no idea how they'll do it. Odds are he'll take off to spy on raven or something... put a couple threats that can be handled alone and are on the level of &quot;dude what the fuck prep this place for salem invasions&quot; and he'll buzz off if his MO during the show is anything to do by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T08:35:46-07:00","id":1151944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1151824#post1151824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd probably give the Shotgun MA some sort of reflexive attack for when someone came into close range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a bad idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I <i>probably</i> wouldn't give it aim charms, since I don't tend to think of a shotgun as a percision implement, more a fire at the momment/ spray and pray. So probably something to help against battlegroups or high clustered targets. </div> </div> </div>That's all fine when the shotgun is loaded with buckshot, but they can be loaded with solid slugs as well. Slugs do require precise aim, but deliver massive damage to a single point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, snipers. The entering conceleament is good. I might add an abillity to force a rout check by targeting members of a group or other demoralizing abillities. Something to ignore cover and soak after lining up your shot. Given a sniper's sort of pop culture &quot;serial killer from a far&quot; thing (picking off targets as they panic from the first shot), I'd do something like, inflicting penalties or intimacies of fear after a shot? </div> </div> </div>Interesting ideas.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1151826#post1151826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1.) Ruby ... doesn't strike me as a lunar... at least not from a build stand point. I mean story wise yes she could exalt as anything, but her extant build is probably more in line with Solars. ... Which actually makes her exalting as a Lunar fairly interesting. Because up till this point she's been highly focused on abilities/skills over any particular attribute. Although I'd wager she's got pretty decent Dexterity, Intelligence, and Perception.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fully agree with all points.<br /> <br /> I read fanfiction in which characters from different series Exalt. Almost always as Solars. Which makes sense, as Solars are basically just &quot;this character, but better&quot;.<br /> <br /> I wanted to challenge myself and my readers by asking, &quot;Are we sure this couldn't work? Maybe this could be cool in a different way?&quot;<br /> <br /> (If Lunars can favor any four Attributes, I've got her pegged as Strength, Dexterity, Intelligence, Wits. Wits reflecting her need for swift reactions and her strong Resolve. She doesn't need to favor Perception to have a single Charm that lets her see clearly across vast distances.) (As an Orichalcum Caste Alchemical, she <i>would </i>favor Perception, as well as Charisma.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2.) For martial arts regarding guns. Well the shot gun style, or maybe shot-gun and pistol style should emphasize the close and short range make use of their ability to generally be more useful in tight quarters and ability to do a lot of damage quickly, but not as precisely, possibly some melee functionality in the form of pistol whips and butt clubbing, also a combat reload capability so they don't get caught with their chamber open. The sniper style should emphasize swift and/or stealthy movement in order to give them the distance they need to unleash their best attacks, aiming more rapidly, or getting more out of the aim action, or both, heavy penetration of both withering and decisive defenses, the ability to aim in adverse conditions such as falling through the air, hiding in water, crashing down a mountain side, riding a horse, or while using our feet to keep the jaws of a tyrant lizard from crashing down on you. You know average everyday issues like that. </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> The pistol style is basically Dante from <i>Devil May Cry</i>. If you're using pistols with anything but native Firearms Charms, then you're using a Style of impractical stances and stunts, like Noel Vermillion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T10:18:49-07:00","id":1151963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1151824#post1151824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to ignore cover and soak after lining up your shot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't ignore cover, quite the contrary in fact. You want people to take cover when they're facing a sniper because that's an aspect of how they're presented in pop culture.<br /> An additional consideration along these lines would be a way to gain Initiative without pulling the trigger so the character can be a master marksman who kills with every carefully considered shot, perhaps linking this to the demoralising effects like with the Latent Ability Predator's Menace (pg 555) so they still soften up their targets appropriately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T10:22:42-07:00","id":1151965,"title":"","content":"Thoughts on chapter 1 and 2 of volume 5.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The way these two episodes have kicked off the new season has really managed to pull me in. I wasn't that hyped before, but now when they've made it clear where the volume is going, I'm very interested.<br /> <br /> To begin with, both episodes have been over 20 minutes. That alone makes it much easier to invest in.<br /> <br /> Also, related to that: tempo. RWBY has never been a particularly fast show; even if the pacing with the set-ups and payoffs have been decent most of the time, each season is usually dedicated to one big thing happening in increments. That's why I'm pleasantly surprised by the sheer amount of key stuff that's already happened. Qrow and team RNJR have set a target, Weiss has arrived and been captured in a way that progresses the reunion of team RWBY and Yang is actively seeking out her mother in a manner that also progresses that reunion. Not only that, we see action on the part of the villains, with a recuperated and highly vengeful Cinder among other things. And, of course, the deposition of Sienna Khan as leader of the White Fang. I mean, all that could have been most of a volume previously. It's the second chapter! It all has a feeling of momentum and a motion towards a climax that's really pulling me along.<br /> <br /> Next point. Man, they stepped up their animation work. That's happened every volume, don't get me wrong, but they seem to have gotten much more familiar and comfortable with the Maya engine, and it's really showing. Yang's character short combat scene was fluid as hell, and Weiss' battle against the Lancers was some of the best I've seen her style looking, well, ever. I'm also really a fan of them working 2D images in; they're gorgeous and so much better than than stock 3D assets.<br /> <br /> That said, nooot to keen on the cartoon physics on that one bandit Yang clocked. I'm all for bringing funny back to this series, but that attempt felt like a swing and a miss. The context was much to badass for that to work.<br /> <br /> All in all, volume 5 feels very different from volume 4. I was afraid it wouldn't, but it's clear that CRWBY was working very deliberately to create these different feelings. You can hear it in the title songs as well: For season 4, we get &quot;Let's just live&quot;, and the season deals with the aftermath of trauma and very human and personal things. This season, the first lines we get are &quot;Back to the fairy tale&quot;, and the tone shift couldn't be more evident.<br /> <br /> I'm in this. Let's go.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 10-22-2017, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T18:44:18-07:00","id":1152085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1151790#post1151790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back on topic, I hate Qrow's character design. I just hate Qrow in general really. He's every 14 year old boy's first rpg character rolled into one.<br /> <br /> He's immensely powerful<br /> Commands respect without responsibility<br /> comically drunk without actually being drunk<br /> he has an &quot;edgy&quot; cool hot topic look<br /> definitely isn't based on Dante from DMC<br /> He has a cape on a dress shirt wtf<br /> has a tragic power<br /> He's a &quot;Cool womanizer&quot;<br /> yadda yadda yadda.<br /> <br /> He has no real flaws and no stakes, I don't care if he succeeds or fails, and he only exists as an excuse to move the plot along. He needs to be taken out of the plot (a la Posioned) because he invalidates the combat abilities of RNJR. I'll bet anything that he splits asap because he's challenging Ruby for focal point of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel you're giving him too much credit, if anything. He hasn't accomplished much on-screen as of yet, other than nearly getting himself killed trying to save team RNGR. As it stands, I'm thinking he's dangerously close to having a Mentor's Accident (i.e. he'll die or get crippled to show that things are now SERIOUS). <br /> <br /> As for how he looks... well. If I started complaining about that now, I'd never stop. It was clear from the day Ruby wore a corset outside her shirt that this world's fashion was all about what's cool at the expense of what's practical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T03:52:01-07:00","id":1153103,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ok, got my answer. No way could have called that</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T11:37:22-07:00","id":1154170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1152085#post1152085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel you're giving him too much credit, if anything. He hasn't accomplished much on-screen as of yet, other than nearly getting himself killed trying to save team RNGR. As it stands, I'm thinking he's dangerously close to having a Mentor's Accident (i.e. he'll die or get crippled to show that things are now SERIOUS).</div> </div> </div> </div>People keep pointing out that Ruby is helpless without her grimscythe.<br /> <br /> Theory: Ruby's scythe will get destroyed, then he'll die and Ruby will inherit his.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T13:59:10-07:00","id":1154216,"title":"","content":"Why would a weapon nut like Rubes accept a downgrade?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T14:43:44-07:00","id":1154230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1154216#post1154216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would a weapon nut like Rubes accept a downgrade?</div> </div> </div> </div>...Because hers is destroyed?<br /> And do we know Qrow's is a downgrade?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T16:04:51-07:00","id":1154242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1154230#post1154230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Because hers is destroyed?<br /> And do we know Qrow's is a downgrade?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the red ones are faster.<br /> <br /> But seriously, Ruby said it herself. Their weapons are extensions of themselves. As much a part of them as their unique hair styles and colorful costumes. <br /> <br /> Even Jaune only added parts of Pyrrha\u2019s costume to his weapon, and upgraded his weapon in his own personal way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T16:23:06-07:00","id":1154246,"title":"","content":"More than likely Qrow will be functioning as a mentor figure and not as front-line fighter after a fashion. I mean Ozpin seemed to know the most about what was going on and while Qrow knows a lot that's pretty much in comparison to people who didn't know anything about the situation. Now from what we saw in the last season Oscar seems to have Ozpin's knowledge and considering Ozpin seems to know the most about what's going on ,at the very least he probably knows more about Salem than anyone who isn't on her side, I would imagine that eventually Qrow will have to go down to functioning as a combination of mission control, and mentor and leave the fighting to the main cast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T16:28:10-07:00","id":1154247,"title":"","content":"I'm not so sure they'll kill off Qrow. He's a better fit than many others, for sure, but we're not seeing any actual hints that he's on his way out. Of course, we didn't really see that with Penny or Pyrrha either, so... But I do think he'll not be part of the main team forever, most assuredly not once team RWBY is back together.<br /> <br /> Ruby would probably use Qrow's scythe if she had to. If Crescent Rose was damaged, and she came into combat, she could probably use it. I don't think she'd keep it once Crescent Rose was repaired, though. And in most cases, it would be possible to repair it. Ruby designed it herself, and knows how it works. She might need help, but she definitely has intimate knowledge of how it works.<br /> <br /> Whether Qrow's scythe is a &quot;downgrade&quot; or not... hard to say. Power levels in RWBY has traditionally been all over the place in the first place. I think that Sunder has the right of it, though; even if both Crescent Rose and Qrow's scythe are scythes, they are fairly different weapons. Ruby's style uses the recoil of her sniper rifle to move and attack, a functionality that Qrow's weapon lacks. Instead, Qrow's scythe has a sword form, which gives more defensive options as Crescent Rose seems awkward to parry with. So while I think it's hard to say that one weapon is &quot;weaker&quot; than the other, it's probably true that Ruby would fight worse without the functionalities she's used to. Qrow probably as well.<br /> <br /> Edit: Shit, I need to learn not to post while drunk. Sorry I got your name wrong, Sunder. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 10-31-2017, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T10:03:01-07:00","id":1154422,"title":"","content":"To me RWBY was simply a choreography show, a kind of expansion over the Dead Fantasy series. Plotwise, the first season didn't catch my attention really, I found it sub-standard but I kept watching because of the cool ideas, weapons and fights in the show. Although third season I though was a step in the right direction.<br /> <br /> Later seasons, in my opinion, have become... a little more &quot;pretentious&quot;. Last season, and possibly the fifth one too, have become pretty boring for me to watch. RWBY's plot isn't something never seen, or very deep really, but I keep getting this feeling that the creators suddenly decided to put focus on the intrigue and different plotlines. Honestly I never saw the lore and story of RWBY as nothing more than an excuse for more coreographed fights to happen.<br /> <br /> Last episode I saw had this chase between some hornets and one of the protagonists. Argh... boring as hell... maybe in the old days the scene would have contained some high action ice-skating-rapiere-girl-stabbing the hornets with grace and power... Now we got a generic &quot;throw-them-some-crates-and-make-them-explode-approach&quot; (nice name for a combo though). It felt like I was watching some ordinary low action level kids-cartoon show.<br /> <br /> I may be a minority here, which I don't mind really, as I see that most people still enjoy RWBY. However, for me this has become a shadow of what I found interesting. I don't care about the knight guy, unsufferable thor-chick, the mute ninja, or even the cat-person. I just enjoy when they are well animated and kick somebody's ass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T10:15:15-07:00","id":1154430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1154230#post1154230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Because hers is destroyed?<br /> And do we know Qrow's is a downgrade?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for starters, it's a shotgun, Ruby is a rifle user.<br /> Two I'm not sure she'd know what to do with the sword form.<br /> Three, either Qrow doesn't Maintain and Modify his weapon to the limit of his current abilities like Ruby is likely to do with CR, or the damned thing is probably too heavy and high powered for her to use. <br /> Four ... ok this one is subjective, but it's just not as cool as Crescent Rose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T15:08:15-07:00","id":1154523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1154422#post1154422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last episode I saw had this chase between some hornets and one of the protagonists. Argh... boring as hell... maybe in the old days the scene would have contained some high action ice-skating-rapiere-girl-stabbing the hornets with grace and power... Now we got a generic &quot;throw-them-some-crates-and-make-them-explode-approach&quot; (nice name for a combo though). It felt like I was watching some ordinary low action level kids-cartoon show.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it would have felt like it belonged if Weiss had been zipping around through the air. Forcing her to stick to projectiles cuts into what choreography can be done in the scene.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's not always going to be as fun to watch as the White or Yellow trailers. Sometimes they'll swing and it will be a miss. This was one such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T21:15:26-07:00","id":1154610,"title":"","content":"Kinda fit into early S1 battles to me. The real big choreographed fights came later","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T03:34:33-07:00","id":1154661,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile, on the Interwebs, the SS Solar Flare* just opened fire on her opponents in the Shipping wars<br /> <br /> <br /> *Sun+Yang","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 11-01-2017, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T23:48:48-07:00","id":1154991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1154661#post1154661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, on the Interwebs, the SS Solar Flare* just opened fire on her opponents in the Shipping wars<br /> <br /> <br /> *Sun+Yang</div> </div> </div> </div>Puh-LEASE. If anything, those two will get together simply because they'd rather be in a three-way relationship with Blake than have <b>any</b> of this Love Triangle Bullshit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1154247#post1154247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or Pyrrha either, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>I must be some kind of freaking wizard. I mean, I was surprised that they Went There, sure, but I sure wasn't surprised that it was Pyrrha 'My First Name Means Victory At A Deep Cost' Nikos. Like, I had a feeling that if they were going to kill anybody, it'd be her, especially with the death flags she was setting off in V3.<br /> <br /> Penny I was a bit more surprised, though I saw the possibility of her being severely maimed or killed as a result of putting her up against Pyrrha in the finals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T01:02:35-07:00","id":1154998,"title":"","content":"You really think that Penny is dead?<br /> <br /> <br /> I do agree about Solar Flare though. Those two have never even directly interacted. But they would make great blonde bread for a Kitty sammich.<br /> <br /> we need to start some way of naming the 3somes. Some are good compromises to the various pair offs.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Speaking of pair ofds, anyone nktice Oscar seems rather smitten with Ruby? </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 11-02-2017, 07:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T03:58:36-07:00","id":1155012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1154998#post1154998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You really think that Penny is dead?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do. They made a big deal of the fact she had a soul. She was a real girl. And real girls die.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T09:28:41-07:00","id":1155091,"title":"","content":"Penny had a plan for a way to give Atlas the slip and attend Beacon with Ruby. We haven\u2019t yet seen that plan.<br /> <br /> Rooster Teeth apparently once said that Penny was like their Ayanami Rei, and one interpretation of Rei was \u201cone soul, many replacement bodies\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T09:29:54-07:00","id":1155092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1155012#post1155012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do. They made a big deal of the fact she had a soul. She was a real girl. And real girls die.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Death&quot; means something different when you're made of pieces that can be reassembled.* Plus, there was that shadowy figure watching the fight in season 3, who I presume was Penny's maker - if they don't reappear and do something important, that would be a substantial waste of plot-potential. I have difficulty imagining that &quot;something&quot; would not involve reintroducing Penny in some form.<br /> <br /> * On that note, the main reason I'm sure Pyrrha isn't coming back is because her body was incinerated and her armor was melted down. There's literally nothing left of her but memories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T20:50:23-07:00","id":1155275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1155092#post1155092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Plus, there was that shadowy figure watching the fight in season 3, who I presume was Penny's maker - if they don't reappear and do something important, that would be a substantial waste of plot-potential. I have difficulty imagining that &quot;something&quot; would not involve reintroducing Penny in some form.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is nothing to indicate he can make more Pennys. That he was shown could simply be:<br /> -To show that even her creator cared about her and was angry at her death.<br /> -To show that her creator is not happy and might become a minor villain later out of spite<br /> -To show that her creator is vowing to make the next model tougher but less compassionate<br /> -A red herring. (I don't believe this one either, but it is possible, in particular since scripting had to go to new writers, unfortunately.)<br /> <br /> Penny 2.0 is possible, but by no means guaranteed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T20:52:50-07:00","id":1155276,"title":"","content":"Anyone else notice how very, very oddly similar Raven and Adam are? Or just me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T22:41:15-07:00","id":1155302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1155276#post1155276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else notice how very, very oddly similar Raven and Adam are? Or just me?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends, they both have the my goal is all that matters thing going for them mixed with seeming to only have minimal care about other things. That said Raven had very little screen time so far, which does make it hard to get a bead on her personality. At least as far as extremes and how much of that is something comes from the job or is her own thing. Where are you thinking?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T03:58:35-07:00","id":1155339,"title":"","content":"They also appear to be wielding similar weapons (Katanas in sheaths that seem to be guns), fight similarly (from what little has been shown) and both wear red/black with white masks.<br /> <br /> What that means? I don't know. A Hyde-style dual personality? She trained him? Adam is Yang's brother? Coincidence? We might know more by the end of the season, but right now that aren't a lot of clues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://foru