=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Both wear grimm masks, have (as noted) a katanna that is red along the blade, fight in a similair style, and have similair color palletes, are in a protracted dispute with a cast member(Blake, Qrow) over whether they should focus on their own (Faunus, Branwen) over more global concerns, are neglectful/abusive towards a member of the main four, and have a rule by the strong mentality. Both were also involved in the destruction of settlements by grimm attacks, and both have &lt;spoilers&gt; killed significantly more intreasting characters or nearly done so&lt;/spoilers&gt; , are noted for being exceptionally charismatic and recently rising to promience in their organizations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait when did Raven kill,maim, or nearly kill anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T14:20:20-07:00","id":1155536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1155528#post1155528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait when did Raven kill,maim, or nearly kill anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking of the Neo fight. Which is a significant stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T14:44:35-07:00","id":1155545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1154998#post1154998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You really think that Penny is dead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, I don't. It's meta, but if Penny was dead, they'd have made a bigger deal of it. The fact that they've only mentioned her name a few times while Pyrrha's death has had a great effect on several main characters makes me think they're waiting for her to sink into the back of our minds before they spring Penny 2.0 at us.<br /> <br /> I mean, they should have made her death a bigger deal right away, and I agree that this is inconsistent with her having a soul like a real girl, but I don't think anyone ever gave RWBY points for writing consistently. I mean, there's a scene in season 2 they actually declared non-canon by Word of God, just like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1154998#post1154998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Speaking of pair ofds, anyone nktice Oscar seems rather smitten with Ruby? </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I saw it more as him being awkward. But I can see it. Ruby is attractive in a cute way and intriguing in that she possesses great power. Oscar could certainly do worse than Ruby. But I do wonder how it'd feel to know she'd also be dating her headmaster, not to mention that she just learned said headmaster is an ageless bodyjumper. I don't really care that much, but they'd have to at least bring that up before I can buy RubyxOscar.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T14:53:27-07:00","id":1155551,"title":"","content":"Actually it would be nice to hear about how the Ozpin/Oscar thing works. Like narratively speaking I don't think they'll reveal something that would mean Ozpin will eventually assimilate Oscar. Still, it would be nice to know if this is a temporary thing until Ozpin finds a means to regain a body, if he'll eventually fade into Oscar's mind, or if Oscar will have Ozpin in his head for the rest of his life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T14:54:03-07:00","id":1155552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1155276#post1155276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else notice how very, very oddly similar Raven and Adam are? Or just me?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I hadn't actually thought about that. They do share a lot of aesthetic details, use the same type of weapon, and are involved in a rebel/outcast organisation. They also have a philosophy promoting the rule of the strong.<br /> <br /> I think it might be a more thematically interesting comparison than something signifying a real relation between them, but I suppose we'll see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T15:37:25-07:00","id":1155565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1155545#post1155545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I mean, there's a scene in season 2 they actually declared non-canon by Word of God, just like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>What scene is that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T17:46:23-07:00","id":1155598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1155551#post1155551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually it would be nice to hear about how the Ozpin/Oscar thing works. Like narratively speaking I don't think they'll reveal something that would mean Ozpin will eventually assimilate Oscar. Still, it would be nice to know if this is a temporary thing until Ozpin finds a means to regain a body, if he'll eventually fade into Oscar's mind, or if Oscar will have Ozpin in his head for the rest of his life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay where did people get the impression that Ozpin will absorb Oscar? I got the impression that it would be the opposite. Ozpin would face in time, leaving Oscar as the primary personality, with the memories and skills of the Immortal before him. Then if they fail to stop Salem, Oscar moves on and jumps into another soul, who will gain all the memories of the incarnations past","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T18:25:14-07:00","id":1155611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1155598#post1155598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay where did people get the impression that Ozpin will absorb Oscar? I got the impression that it would be the opposite. Ozpin would face in time, leaving Oscar as the primary personality, with the memories and skills of the Immortal before him. Then if they fail to stop Salem, Oscar moves on and jumps into another soul, who will gain all the memories of the incarnations past</div> </div> </div> </div>I said I doubt they'd reveal something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T20:04:23-07:00","id":1155628,"title":"","content":"Another parallel between Adam and Raven: They're a major detriment to the survival of remnant just by existing, even without all this Salem stuff.<br /> <br /> I mean Adam may have had a point once, but the idea of a bandit tribe in Remnant is simply indefensibly evil. Especially in the case of Raven who was trained by a kingdom. Furthermore it indicates she didn't really absorb any of the important lessons of living in a city, like how having support staff lets you get stronger faster in whatever area you consider important. So another parallel would probably be either a massive case of tunnel vision, or outright stupidity.<br /> <br /> Also just because something has a soul doesn't mean it's seat of consciousness is tied to a backasswards kludge of a bio-computer like a human brain-body system. So Penny could well be alive if none of those wires cut through her actual seat of consciousness.<br /> <br /> That said they could have, or she could have gone nuts from being isolated without input for who knows how long in subjective time, or she could have abandoned the body and infiltrated the CCT. We're gonna have to wait on that since she has so many potential options our POS water-bag existences don't afford us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T21:09:08-07:00","id":1155643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1155565#post1155565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What scene is that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The post-credit scene where she meets Yang. Kerry and Miles didnt want it but Monty insisted. And it doesnt fit into the story anywhere. So they dont consider it canon anymore","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T01:52:01-07:00","id":1155669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1155565#post1155565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What scene is that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, as D said, it\u2019s after the credits when Yang meets Raven and Raven goes \u201cwe have a lot to talk about\u201d. They since said that it\u2019s not canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T14:22:20-07:00","id":1155854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1155628#post1155628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another parallel between Adam and Raven: They're a major detriment to the survival of remnant just by existing, even without all this Salem stuff.<br /> <br /> I mean Adam may have had a point once, but the idea of a bandit tribe in Remnant is simply indefensibly evil. Especially in the case of Raven who was trained by a kingdom. Furthermore it indicates she didn't really absorb any of the important lessons of living in a city, like how having support staff lets you get stronger faster in whatever area you consider important. So another parallel would probably be either a massive case of tunnel vision, or outright stupidity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's debatable and we'll have to see more to be certain.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">In the most recent episode, it's made clear that she does think heavily about emotions and their impact on Grimm. And we don't know why she rejects Ozpin yet. The major cities and their academies are heavily controlled by him, so if she feels he's not on the up-and-up her decision to reject them could make sense, especially if - as the way she shut down this fight implies - she knows how to operate without causing enough negativity to attract Grimm. It's possible that her &quot;bandit group&quot; actually provides a degree of order and stability in its area.<br /> <br /> Certainly she hasn't acted as insane as Adam has yet. Adam is <i>actively</i> helping the Grimm at this point as long as they're killing humans; Raven seems to be much more cautious.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T14:38:34-07:00","id":1155862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1155643#post1155643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The post-credit scene where she meets Yang. Kerry and Miles didnt want it but Monty insisted. And it doesnt fit into the story anywhere. So they dont consider it canon anymore</div> </div> </div> </div>Monty was creative and passionate and a harder worker than most of humanity. But sometimes it shows that he prioritized his latest cool idea over plot cohesion. Like throwing the Penny fight into the V1 finale, or the scrapped Raven vs JNPR fight from V3, or the whole Maiden idea seeming out of nowhere because Monty thought it up between Volumes 2 and 3.<br /> <br /> Honestly, sometimes the best thing a passionate and creative person can have is someone willing to say &quot;No, stop it, that's silly&quot;. It's like how Georges Lucas + others = Original Trilogy, but Lucas on his own = the Prequels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T17:49:21-07:00","id":1155900,"title":"","content":"On the matter of Penny's apparent death not being dealt with in the show as much as it maybe should have: Only two of the characters would likely be truly deeply affected. Ruby is the only one we see treating Penny as a friend, everyone else is as best mildly annoyed by her. But by the time Ruby gets the breather to work through that, she's lost another friend (whom more of her remaining friends were close to), possibly lost her sister to depression, had the weight of the world dumped on her, had to watch the city she lived in die, had two more friends bugger off without goodbye and needs to worry about other academies getting attacked. So she may have been a bit busy to have another mourning subplot.<br /> The only other person who'd be moved deeply without making the audience wonder why they suddenly care about Penny is Phyrra, being the one who accidentally killed her, but she died soon after.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is that dealing with Penny's death more than they did just didn't fit into the already overloaded narrative anywhere, so I'm not confident that should be seen as a sign that she's coming back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T22:39:44-07:00","id":1155956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1155854#post1155854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's possible that her &quot;bandit group&quot; actually provides a degree of order and stability in its area.</div> </div> </div> </div>While bringing death and destruction to those outside of it, of course.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T00:48:47-07:00","id":1155968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1155854#post1155854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly she hasn't acted as insane as Adam has yet. Adam is <i>actively</i> helping the Grimm at this point as long as they're killing humans; Raven seems to be much more cautious.</div> </div> </div> </div>She didn't lift a finger to help stop the train at the end of season 2, though. She may not be as insane as Adam or Torchwick, but she clearly doesn't care enough to stop them either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T01:11:42-08:00","id":1155976,"title":"","content":"I do think that her general outlook is &quot;I protect the people I care about and everyone else can just rot for all I care.&quot;<br /> <br /> Still, that's waaaaay less crazy than Adam, who seems to be actively trying to kill all non-Faunus (and is wiling to pursue a strategy that will, logically, result in large numbers of Faunus deaths as well, even.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T05:04:35-08:00","id":1156014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1155551#post1155551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually it would be nice to hear about how the Ozpin/Oscar thing works. Like narratively speaking I don't think they'll reveal something that would mean Ozpin will eventually assimilate Oscar. Still, it would be nice to know if this is a temporary thing until Ozpin finds a means to regain a body, if he'll eventually fade into Oscar's mind, or if Oscar will have Ozpin in his head for the rest of his life.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thought is that Ozpin will remain in Oscar\u2019s body, and that eventually, they\u2019ll get so used to one another that differentiation between them is meaningless. Not so much an assimilation as a mutual adaptation. That would mean that Ozpin would take on some of Oscar\u2019s characteristics, though, and I\u2019m not sure you can survive several such regenerations with your sense of purpose still intact, so perhaps it\u2019s not quite as benign a process.<br /> <br /> Even so, I do believe we\u2019ll see the Ozpin/Oscar divide for some time yet. I\u2019ve no doubt Ozpin would rather not deal with those teen hormones if he can at all avoid it.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, speaking of Rosegarden, despite all the things they really need to be brought up and worked with for that ship to be credible, I do think Ruby is a good match for Oscar. Because, let's remember, Ruby sees people. She's been helpful to Jaune when he (arguable rightly) felt that he wasn't worthy to lead JNPR. She's the only one who gave a crap about Penny. I really think that what Ozcar (is that an acceptable name for the Oscar/Ozpin fusion?) might need most of all right now is for someone to see the scared and uncertain Oscar, and not just the immortal and mysterious Ozpin, whenever they look at him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 11-05-2017, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T10:11:41-08:00","id":1156080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1155976#post1155976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think that her general outlook is &quot;I protect the people I care about and everyone else can just rot for all I care.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And of course, often she will <i>cause</i> them to rot, by murdering them and taking their shit and then leaving the survivors to be feasted on by the Grimm.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T00:25:15-08:00","id":1156251,"title":"","content":"I have this thing about people who try to spout garbage about the strong being worthy of survival and the weak not so much.<br /> <br /> 1. Everyone is weak at some point, and not just as babies, letting valuable, skilled, and experienced people die off before they teach everything they can to their replacements is a good way to get your ass extinct.<br /> <br /> 2. Define strength, physical brawn? Overall combat power? Group combat power? individual combat power? loyalty commanded? wealth wielded? No matter how you define strength there's going to be obvious examples of how other people with different skills are needed and vital to a culture.<br /> <br /> 3. Most of the time it's just self serving claptrap designed to elevate themselves and make them feel like they're allowed to push other people around because they're not part of the same group. Otherwise they'd have sought out and followed people who are ridiculously strong and well known, like Ozpin.<br /> <br /> Raven tried to pull this bullshit on her own brother, so without some pretty hefty evidence otherwise she either believes it, or is spouting it off because it's convenient. Neither scenario make me want to see anything happen to her except a swift death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T20:22:14-08:00","id":1156558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1156251#post1156251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have this thing about people who try to spout garbage about the strong being worthy of survival and the weak not so much.<br /> <br /> 1. Everyone is weak at some point, and not just as babies, letting valuable, skilled, and experienced people die off before they teach everything they can to their replacements is a good way to get your ass extinct.<br /> <br /> 2. Define strength, physical brawn? Overall combat power? Group combat power? individual combat power? loyalty commanded? wealth wielded? No matter how you define strength there's going to be obvious examples of how other people with different skills are needed and vital to a culture.<br /> <br /> 3. Most of the time it's just self serving claptrap designed to elevate themselves and make them feel like they're allowed to push other people around because they're not part of the same group. Otherwise they'd have sought out and followed people who are ridiculously strong and well known, like Ozpin.<br /> <br /> Raven tried to pull this bullshit on her own brother, so without some pretty hefty evidence otherwise she either believes it, or is spouting it off because it's convenient. Neither scenario make me want to see anything happen to her except a swift death.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it looks pretty likely that she believes strongly in whatever specific philosophy she's endorsing, and I don't agree with it, I feel like you're making some assumptions to assist in your rush to judgment. We don't know a lot of specifics of her creed. We don't know how much of it is shaped by the specific demands of the world of Remnant. We know she used to believe in something else, and then apparently had her faith broken, specifically by Ozpin. How, and how did that lead her to who she has become?<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to defend her as having a valid viewpoint or anything, but &quot;a swift death&quot; seems to be an overreaction, based on what we know so far. Raven and her people are rough, sure, and holding some territory by force, but seeing the parallels between RWBY and <i>Exalted</i>, and comparing her to my expectations of a Lunar warlord, she ranks more as an uneasy neighbor than someone who needs dealt with urgently. In my opinion, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T17:58:31-08:00","id":1156846,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" />