 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I personally didn't see anything SHIPPY about the hug, so much as Weiss has spent several months spending time with the worst members of her family (that is, the ones who aren't Winter) and then was kidnapped by Bandits and <i>Oh thank the GODS</i> it's someone she actually likes and supports her and treats her nicely and-</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T23:59:27-08:00","id":1156914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1156558#post1156558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While it looks pretty likely that she believes strongly in whatever specific philosophy she's endorsing, and I don't agree with it, I feel like you're making some assumptions to assist in your rush to judgment. We don't know a lot of specifics of her creed. We don't know how much of it is shaped by the specific demands of the world of Remnant. We know she used to believe in something else, and then apparently had her faith broken, specifically by Ozpin. How, and how did that lead her to who she has become?<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to defend her as having a valid viewpoint or anything, but &quot;a swift death&quot; seems to be an overreaction, based on what we know so far. Raven and her people are rough, sure, and holding some territory by force, but seeing the parallels between RWBY and <i>Exalted</i>, and comparing her to my expectations of a Lunar warlord, she ranks more as an uneasy neighbor than someone who needs dealt with urgently. In my opinion, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is precisely the specific demands of remnant. Her philosophy is the precise opposite of what is needed to advance society and technology, technology that is desperately needed, even by 'strong' people like Raven and her followers. Furthermore technology is the only advantage the remni have that could eventually free them from the threat of the Grimm, either by getting them off the planet, or by allowing them to field enough powerful weapons to take back the world the hard way. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T01:18:05-08:00","id":1156922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1156886#post1156886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I personally didn't see anything SHIPPY about the hug, so much as Weiss has spent several months spending time with the worst members of her family (that is, the ones who aren't Winter) and then was kidnapped by Bandits and <i>Oh thank the GODS</i> it's someone she actually likes and supports her and treats her nicely and-</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Exactly. The specific timeline wasn't revealed, but for all we know Weiss left for Atlas before Yang even got to a hospital after what happened, and she might not have heard a peep since (it didn't seem like she was talking much to Ironwood even). Just finally seeing that Yang isn't dead or permanently crippled would have been a relief, let alone the help her sudden arrival represented.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T03:35:36-08:00","id":1156948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1156914#post1156914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is precisely the specific demands of remnant. Her philosophy is the precise opposite of what is needed to advance society and technology, technology that is desperately needed, even by 'strong' people like Raven and her followers. Furthermore technology is the only advantage the remni have that could eventually free them from the threat of the Grimm, either by getting them off the planet, or by allowing them to field enough powerful weapons to take back the world the hard way. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You are not wrong in the general sense, but I'm seeing some assumptions about the specific character in question that I'm not sure are supported at this time. Maybe I missed something, but was she ever presented as anti-technology? All I am certain about is that she mistrusts the current society structure - which DEFINITELY has some real issues - and Ozpin in particular, who definitely has secrets remaining. Also, her philosophy of determination and personal achievement is not something that would have alienated, for instance, Tesla, Newton, or Ford. Maybe she goes one way or another in the end, but I think Raven has too much gray area left to conclude yet that she's definitely a force for ill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T04:50:07-08:00","id":1156965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1156886#post1156886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I personally didn't see anything SHIPPY about the hug, so much as Weiss has spent several months spending time with the worst members of her family (that is, the ones who aren't Winter) and then was kidnapped by Bandits and <i>Oh thank the GODS</i> it's someone she actually likes and supports her and treats her nicely and-</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>What you are describing here is the sensible, sane position. As such, it has no value in the Ship Wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T06:58:44-08:00","id":1156986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1156948#post1156948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are not wrong in the general sense, but I'm seeing some assumptions about the specific character in question that I'm not sure are supported at this time. Maybe I missed something, but was she ever presented as anti-technology? All I am certain about is that she mistrusts the current society structure - which DEFINITELY has some real issues - and Ozpin in particular, who definitely has secrets remaining. Also, her philosophy of determination and personal achievement is not something that would have alienated, for instance, Tesla, Newton, or Ford. Maybe she goes one way or another in the end, but I think Raven has too much gray area left to conclude yet that she's definitely a force for ill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Her apparent stated position is that she doesn't believe in carrying those members of society who can't fend for themselves. That directly opposes the possibility that someone will be able to dedicate their live to study and experimentation enough to develop advanced technology. Study and research take time, a lot of it, during which these people will need to be fed and supported by other members of the group.<br /> <br /> She doesn't have to be anti-technology. She may love the power that technology brings. But no tribe run by her based on the principles of 'no hand outs' is going to be developing any tech. No one will have the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T08:34:06-08:00","id":1157019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1156948#post1156948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, her philosophy of determination and personal achievement is not something that would have alienated, for instance, Tesla, Newton, or Ford.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tesla and Newton would have approved of a philosophy that says &quot;It's okay to descend on towns, plunder them, kill or subdue all who stand in your way, and then leave the survivors to be wiped out by the magical fear-monsters who wander the world and whom you caused to be strengthened and empowered by this act?&quot;<br /> <br /> I... kinda doubt that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe she goes one way or another in the end, but I think Raven has too much gray area left to conclude yet that she's definitely a force for ill. </div> </div> </div>Raven is absolutely a force for ill. She's a thief, a murderer, a Grimm-enabler, a kidnapper, and a human trafficker. Raven hits teenage girls who have just been through a shipwreck in the head and then ties them up and puts them in cages until she can extort a big pile of lien from their kin.<br /> <br /> She's Roman Torchwick with better legs, and she belongs in a cell just like he did.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T13:14:37-08:00","id":1157107,"title":"","content":"We haven't actually seen her bandit group in action. Not all &quot;bandit groups&quot; are the same.<br /> <br /> I think it's likely that her group is more akin to a Mafia or Yakuza sort of deal - extorting tribute from nearby villages with threats of violence, and taking valuable prisoners for ransom when they have the opportunity, but <i>also</i> providing a degree of order and protection from stuff like Grimm or from the &quot;legitimate&quot; government. I don't think they just recklessly attack villages and leave them to burn. I don't think they even ignore threats against local villages (if only because it's bad for business.)<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, that &quot;legitimate&quot; government is not actually squeaky-clean itself - and, for the record, doesn't seem to be democratically elected. If you asked her, Raven would probably tell you that the Academy is just a bigger bandit group with better PR. Obviously the academies are generally better (well, uh, when they're not controlled by <i>Salem</i> from behind the scenes, which the local one is), but something like eg. Schnee Dust Company? I'm not so sure.<br /> <br /> Like seriously, step back a moment and ask where the Academy system gets its legitimacy. Who the hell is paying for all those fancy structures and Atlas military machines and the like?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Raven is absolutely a force for ill. She's a thief, a murderer, a Grimm-enabler, a kidnapper, and a human trafficker. Raven hits teenage girls who have just been through a shipwreck in the head and then ties them up and puts them in cages until she can extort a big pile of lien from their kin. </div> </div> </div>Winter <i>in particular</i> is / was the heir of the Schnee Dust Company, which (I think) regularly kidnaps people and uses them as slave labor. And Raven isn't going to know that Winter has her doubts about that (for what that's worth, which, on its own, is almost nothing.) I think it's pretty reasonable for her to say &quot;fuck those guys, I'm bleeding them for what they're worth.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't mean to completely justify what Raven is doing; I definitely don't agree with her philosophy, and I agree that it's mostly just self-justification. But we haven't actually seen evidence that she's doing most of the worst stuff you're assuming, and the plot arc seems to be leading towards a big reveal where she explains what made her lose faith in the current system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 11-08-2017, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T13:45:26-08:00","id":1157112,"title":"","content":"There is a saying, &quot; Don't shit where you eat&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T15:39:21-08:00","id":1157142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1157107#post1157107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We haven't actually seen her bandit group in action.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, just the consequences of their being in action.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think they just recklessly attack villages and leave them to burn. </div> </div> </div>That is <i>precisely</i> what they do. We see the aftermath of just such an attack onscreen: Shion Village. Let's go to the tape, and get the testimony of the dying Huntsman from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rHjUHnG7WOQ&amp;t=313s#t=4m46\" target=\"_blank\">Volume 4, Chapter 2:</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> JAUNE: What happened? Who killed all of these people?<br /> <br /> HUNTSMAN: Bandits... the whole tribe... </div> </div> </div>But hey, maybe that wasn't Raven's tribe specifically that killed all those people and torched the town and left the survivors to be eaten by the Grimm... oh wait, <i>she totally admits it was them.</i> From <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GaB62PeuFwM#t=14m00\" target=\"_blank\">Volume 4, Chapter 4:</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> RAVEN: As leader, I will do everything in my power to ensure our survival!<br /> <br /> QROW: I saw. The people of Shion saw too.<br /> <br /> RAVEN: The weak die, the strong live. Those are the rules. </div> </div> </div>Yeeeeeah. You're a real statesman there, Raven.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Keep in mind, that &quot;legitimate&quot; government is not actually squeaky-clean itself </div> </div> </div>This in no way exculpates Raven and her band of, as her brother said, &quot;killers and thieves.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - and, for the record, doesn't seem to be democratically elected. </div> </div> </div>We don't know about the status or health of representative government in the Kingdoms, with the exception of Atlas being viewed as dangerously authoritarian. The second World of Remnant for Volume 2 states that the kingdoms are rules by councils who &quot;represent the people and their needs.&quot; This <i>implies</i> a form of representative government, especially since we also know from the WoR's from volumes three and four that the Vytal Treaty instituted widespread legal and governmental reform across Remnant and that during the Great War period and before, there was meaningful autocratic control in the form of actual kings.<br /> <br /> The government of Mistral might or might not be democratically elected.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you asked her, Raven would probably tell you that the Academy is just a bigger bandit group with better PR. </div> </div> </div>And she would deserve the same response to this that those who claim taxation is a form of theft do: scorching, withering contempt. And, again, even if this were true, it would<i> in no way</i> exculpate Raven from descending on towns, murdering a shit-ton of people, and then leaving the survivors to get fucked up by a Nucklavee.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like seriously, step back a moment and ask where the Academy system gets its legitimacy. Who the hell is paying for all those fancy structures and Atlas military machines and the like? </div> </div> </div>The Academies are government-financed, we do know that much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Winter <i>in particular</i> </div> </div> </div>Weiss.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> is / was the heir of the Schnee Dust Company, which (I think) regularly kidnaps people and uses them as slave labor. </div> </div> </div>Er.<br /> <br /> If this happens, we've seen no textual evidence of it.<br /> <br /> I mean. I wouldn't put it past Jacques. But man alive, if the SDC were kidnapping people enslaving them on the regular, you'd think Qrow would've mentioned it during the WoR episode devoted to them. They may have forms of deeply scummy business practices like debt peonage (&quot;sold my soul to the company store&quot;) but if they're out-and-out slavers it isn't really mentioned anywhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it's pretty reasonable for her to say &quot;fuck those guys, I'm bleeding them for what they're worth.&quot; </div> </div> </div>It is not reasonable, when coming upon an injured teenage girl who has just been thrown clear of an explosive shipwreck she was lucky to live through, to declare how lucky you just got and then <i>strike her brutally in the head</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But we haven't actually seen evidence that she's doing most of the worst stuff you're assuming, </div> </div> </div>I have provided copious amounts of it!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and the plot arc seems to be leading towards a big reveal where she explains what made her lose faith in the current system. </div> </div> </div>With this, I agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T19:04:54-08:00","id":1157173,"title":"","content":"From a practical standpoint it doesn't matter if the kingdoms are literally Hitler, humanity cannot survive, cannot escape, and cannot advance under Raven's philosophy. The system could be run by guys that make the pre-revolution french aristocracy look good, and they would still be better than Raven.<br /> <br /> She is basically fanon Sophia Hess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T07:30:22-08:00","id":1157276,"title":"","content":"I imagine that before Raven stepped outside, she was freaking out in her tent.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh shit, oh shit, oh shit, she found me. How did she find me? Oh shit, now the tribe is going to know I abandoned my own daughter. Now she's going to ask me questions. What do I do?<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay, run damage control; put on a production! She wants answers; I can bullshit something. I can distract the tribe; draw attention away from 'why have we never heard about her' by making them see Yang as someone who proved her worth and ambition in coming here. Maybe if I flatter her enough, and bullshit her answers good enough, she might even join us! If she becomes part of our family on her own, no one can say I'm a terrible mother!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T07:31:00-08:00","id":1157277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1157173#post1157173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a practical standpoint it doesn't matter if the kingdoms are literally Hitler, humanity cannot survive, cannot escape, and cannot advance under Raven's philosophy. The system could be run by guys that make the pre-revolution french aristocracy look good, and they would still be better than Raven.<br /> <br /> She is basically fanon Sophia Hess.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one's talking about naming her High Queen of Remnant. Jesus. No one is arguing that she's GOT A POINT, even. The argument is, whether or not she necessarily deserves summary execution based on what we currently know.<br /> <br /> Based on what little we actually know or can reasonably infer, she's basically the exact sort of bandit warlord that has existed in the real world for millennia. Not even notably successful, by their standards. So by those standards, yes. <br /> But we also know that there is substantially more to the story, and I personally think she's got too interesting a narrative position to end up as a morally bankrupt vanilla villain. I expect a swerve.<br /> <br /> As for anti-technology... not necessarily. A patronage system is basically guaranteed to already be in place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T08:41:19-08:00","id":1157284,"title":"","content":"Raven is anti-technology to the extent that she is anti-society. Her behavior prevents villages from prospering and contributes to the rate of their destruction by Grimm.<br /> <br /> This has little direct impact on the official cities of the kingdoms, except that it prevents villages from eventually growing into towns which could grow into cities.<br /> <br /> Raven likely doesn't raid the actual cities of Mistral, because those cities pay actual taxes to the kingdoms, and Mistral City wants to keep receiving taxes.<br /> <br /> She's an extremely petty bandit with big words and small goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T09:02:32-08:00","id":1157292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1157284#post1157284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raven is anti-technology to the extent that she is anti-society. Her behavior prevents villages from prospering and contributes to the rate of their destruction by Grimm.<br /> <br /> This has little direct impact on the official cities of the kingdoms, except that it prevents villages from eventually growing into towns which could grow into cities.<br /> <br /> Raven likely doesn't raid the actual cities of Mistral, because those cities pay actual taxes to the kingdoms, and Mistral City wants to keep receiving taxes.<br /> <br /> She's an extremely petty bandit with big words and small goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming, of course, that the banditry thing is her only angle. Which it might be, or it might not. We'll find out soon.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this whole debate about whether Raven's ideological merit seems to be rooted in in me saying something about how we don't know how we don't know how her outlook and methods were shaped by the nature of Remnant. People APPARENTLY took that to mean that it was time to debate the merits of Remnant being RULED that way. Which is not at all what I was saying.<br /> <br /> She may still be a generic barbarian bandit queen straight out of 1e Lunars, but I expect the reveal of her perspective on &quot;The Truth&quot; to turn her into something more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T09:15:42-08:00","id":1157295,"title":"","content":"The most I'm expecting out of her is that Ozpin told her the facts about his reincarnation business, Salem's existence, and the four relics and Maidens he's keeping away from Salem, and maybe also asked her to become the next Fall Maiden.<br /> <br /> I think Raven was freaked out about the prospect of fighting for something larger than herself in a shadow war where she might die before she could possibly achieve victory, and where no one would even know what she died for.<br /> <br /> I think Raven decided that was insane, that Ozpin asked too much of her, and so she left to look out for herself and her tribe alone, counting on Ozpin and the kingdoms to fight and die to preserve humanity against the Grimm and Salem.<br /> <br /> But if anyone is expecting &quot;Dumbledore Is Evil&quot;, I think they're going to be massively disappointed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-09-2017, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T09:54:16-08:00","id":1157304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1157295#post1157295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if anyone is expecting &amp;quot;Dumbledore Is Evil&amp;quot;, I think they're going to be massively disappointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree on this point, definitely. But remember the conversation between Qrow and Leo - there's a lot of truth to tell.<br /> <br /> Raven is an important character. She's family and former teammate to major characters, and a former member of the benevolent conspiracy. She's been hinted at here and there for ages. She's got a cool design and a backstory full of some shocking but interesting behavior. Meeting her is structured narratively to be a Big Deal. I feel it would be a waste of potential for her to be just someone who retreated when the protagonists stepped up. I at least would like some explanation that makes her behavior seem rational, instead of just pointless edgelord nonsense. That's lazy writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T10:24:51-08:00","id":1157313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1157295#post1157295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most I'm expecting out of her is that Ozpin told her the facts about his reincarnation business, Salem's existence, and the four relics and Maidens he's keeping away from Salem, and maybe also asked her to become the next Fall Maiden.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would actually be kinda interesting, because controlling who gets to be the next Maiden involves the previous officeholder dying. For Ozpin to ask Raven to the next one, he'd have to be either asking her to murder the current one in a way that make the possibility of the power leaping to her a high one, or the current one would have to have a high probability of dying of natural causes while Raven is still young enough to take up the mantle and they all come to an arrangement where she passes on the power willingly.<br /> <br /> There is also... we've assumed Raven got all her insider information from the Ozluminati, because she was a former member. That's a big big possibility, but there's also the chance that Raven knows what she knows via Vernal instead and has always kinda been on the outside looking in.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T11:55:37-08:00","id":1157329,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering if she knows that Leo has been compromised and is activly keeping that girl (does she have a name yet) from him. So despite not wanting to get involved, she is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T12:17:52-08:00","id":1157333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1157329#post1157329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering if she knows that Leo has been compromised and is activly keeping that girl (does she have a name yet) from him. So despite not wanting to get involved, she is.</div> </div> </div> </div>If she knows Leo has been compromised but didn't tell her brother before he walked right into Mistral, she's kind of a dick.<br /> <br /> The Spring Maiden's name is Vernal, but pronounced weird. &quot;Vur-nahl&quot; instead of &quot;vernl.&quot;<br /> <br /> That said, Raven is certainly keeping Vernal away from the Headmasters, although part of that is that Vernal herself doesn't want to play the Maiden game. Something I wish had been addressed more is that... well... in episode one, Qrow and Leo have a conversation that basically is Qrow asking for the resources to kidnap a grown-ass woman. (Although Vernal certainly deserves to be <i>arrested</i>, but they don't seem to care about bringing charges or anything.) And it's like... maybe one of the kids could have said something about that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":4742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","user":"Murcushio","date":". 11-09-2017, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T12:27:32-08:00","id":1157335,"title":"","content":"I highly doubt Raven knows\\would know that Leo is compromised. It isnt like she skips down to Mistral every sunday to buy bread and milk. And even Vernals intel is at least several years out of date","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T15:38:30-08:00","id":1157376,"title":"","content":"Given how seriously Raven was asking Qrow about whether Salem had the Relic of Choice, I doubt she would be very happy about Salem getting closer to acquiring the Relic of Knowledge.<br /> <br /> Raven actually gave Qrow warnings and information about Salem's activities before the Fall of Beacon, even if (after the fact) she seems convinced that Ozpin was bound to fail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T01:06:36-08:00","id":1157715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1157277#post1157277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No one's talking about naming her High Queen of Remnant. Jesus. No one is arguing that she's GOT A POINT, even. The argument is, whether or not she necessarily deserves summary execution based on what we currently know.<br /> <br /> Based on what little we actually know or can reasonably infer, she's basically the exact sort of bandit warlord that has existed in the real world for millennia. Not even notably successful, by their standards. So by those standards, yes.<br /> But we also know that there is substantially more to the story, and I personally think she's got too interesting a narrative position to end up as a morally bankrupt vanilla villain. I expect a swerve.<br /> <br /> As for anti-technology... not necessarily. A patronage system is basically guaranteed to already be in place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh she's not a vanilla villain, but she is morally bankrupt. She may not have started that way, but she is now. <br /> <br /> Also, yes her philosophy is inherently anti-tech. If people are being forced to spend their lives fighting, or training for fights in order for the tribe to not drop them like a hot potato then you can't advance technologically, you can't even maintain your existing infrastructure past a certain point, unless you buy or steal things form other people, and they can't build the infrastructure to have anything worth selling to get money to buy things with without either stealing stuff anyway or working as mercs. Raven has obviously chosen theft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T03:37:05-08:00","id":1157730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1157715#post1157715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh she's not a vanilla villain, but she is morally bankrupt. She may not have started that way, but she is now. <br /> <br /> Also, yes her philosophy is inherently anti-tech. If people are being forced to spend their lives fighting, or training for fights in order for the tribe to not drop them like a hot potato then you can't advance technologically, you can't even maintain your existing infrastructure past a certain point, unless you buy or steal things form other people, and they can't build the infrastructure to have anything worth selling to get money to buy things with without either stealing stuff anyway or working as mercs. Raven has obviously chosen theft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming that everyone lives that way. Raven appears to be living out what she considers an open expression of what she considers the world to be fundamentally like. This doesn't mean she expects everyone to.<br /> <br /> Assuming that physical strength and prowess is the only form of strength that matters, which is apparently false, as Raven leads a group of people, mostly weaker than herself. This strongly suggests a patronage system. If you're not strong enough yourself, find a way to make yourself valuable to someone who is. That's how an inventor thrives in this model. It's not ideal, but it's worked (to some extent) in the past.<br /> <br /> You're absolutely right that crime is disruptive to existing systems, and Raven is currently a huge criminal. But she is <i>disruptive,</i> not explicitly anti-technology, and being essentially a warlord with subordinates is what evolves into feudalism under the right conditions. Not a great system, but it's a transition away from disrupting the system into becoming the system. Maybe she's not going that direction. Maybe she is. I don't know, but I do know she used to believe in something else, and then switched to this, and I want to know why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T12:44:23-08:00","id":1157806,"title":"","content":"Thoughts on chapters 3, 4 and 5 of volume 5.<br /> <br /> We keep up the brisk pace here, despite the episodes growing shorter, which was expected if not approved of. It's fair to say that Yang and Weiss is in the most fertile ground like now, while it feels like Ruby and Blake are somewhat on the back burner; not that they aren't doing important stuff, but the cutting edge action is definitely on one side. The two of them are already reunited, and have confronted Raven, one of the ongoing Big Deals of the show.<br /> <br /> Also, that's not Freezer Burn, god damn it. It's just Weiss being happy her friend is alive.<br /> <br /> There's been some discussion of animation and choreography in the thread previously, and I must continue to assert that in my opinion, RWBY has never looked better. Artwork- and animation-wise, they're knocking it out of the park compared to earlier volumes. Combat choreography, though, is of course another matter. I personally feel that both the Weiss vs Lancers and Yang vs Raven's bandits fights were among the best since Monty's passing. Particularly Yang's fight managed to keep a very close and personal camera frame while still never making me lose mental track of her position, which has been something of a problem for them. They've solved it with panning overview shots a lot of the time, but those shots tend to slow down the action and contribute to a feeling of lapsing intensity. I'm happy they managed to work with that!<br /> <br /> Episode 5, though...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">One thing that really irked me was Blake's spiel on a person being the embodiment of a word. I get what she's saying; sometimes, you meet a person who's entire being screams a certain concept. I can imagine Adam being such a person; he's certainly intense, and I imagine not a little bit of a sociopath. I'm not finding myself liking where she's going with it, though. By assigning &quot;words&quot; to her friends, the implication becomes that they either have a very single-facet personality, or that this word isn't actually something they radiate but more of a best fitting overall descriptor, which hollows out the concept. Already at the end of that conversation, Sun has defeated the point of Blake's exercise, by asking what word he would be, and admitting to not knowing but coming up with an answer on the spot.<br /> <br /> I'm not against Blake thinking like that. I'd just like to point out that it's wrong. None of these characters are as monofocused as Adam, and it'd have been much better if Blake didn't assign words to those who were, in fact, not an embodiment of them. It kind of feels like a writer thing; come up with a word that informs this character. I don't think that needs to be made intradiegetic.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T20:11:32-08:00","id":1157860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1157806#post1157806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Episode 5, though...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">One thing that really irked me was Blake's spiel on a person being the embodiment of a word. I get what she's saying; sometimes, you meet a person who's entire being screams a certain concept. I can imagine Adam being such a person; he's certainly intense, and I imagine not a little bit of a sociopath. I'm not finding myself liking where she's going with it, though. By assigning &amp;quot;words&amp;quot; to her friends, the implication becomes that they either have a very single-facet personality, or that this word isn't actually something they radiate but more of a best fitting overall descriptor, which hollows out the concept. Already at the end of that conversation, Sun has defeated the point of Blake's exercise, by asking what word he would be, and admitting to not knowing but coming up with an answer on the spot.<br /> <br /> I'm not against Blake thinking like that. I'd just like to point out that it's wrong. None of these characters are as monofocused as Adam, and it'd have been much better if Blake didn't assign words to those who were, in fact, not an embodiment of them. It kind of feels like a writer thing; come up with a word that informs this character. I don't think that needs to be made intradiegetic.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I think the labels are decent enough for shorthand, but I think what I drew from that scene is more that Blake needs to label things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T00:51:22-08:00","id":1157895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1157730#post1157730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Assuming that everyone lives that way. Raven appears to be living out what she considers an open expression of what she considers the world to be fundamentally like. This doesn't mean she expects everyone to.<br /> <br /> Assuming that physical strength and prowess is the only form of strength that matters, which is apparently false, as Raven leads a group of people, mostly weaker than herself. This strongly suggests a patronage system. If you're not strong enough yourself, find a way to make yourself valuable to someone who is. That's how an inventor thrives in this model. It's not ideal, but it's worked (to some extent) in the past.<br /> <br /> You're absolutely right that crime is disruptive to existing systems, and Raven is currently a huge criminal. But she is <i>disruptive,</i> not explicitly anti-technology, and being essentially a warlord with subordinates is what evolves into feudalism under the right conditions. Not a great system, but it's a transition away from disrupting the system into becoming the system. Maybe she's not going that direction. Maybe she is. I don't know, but I do know she used to believe in something else, and then switched to this, and I want to know why.</div> </div> </div> </div>A patronage system can be suggested all it wants. The simple fact is that her philosophy is incompatible with technological advance or more specifically the investments you need to make to make it happen. Nobody knows how to make a phone. There are people who can assemble the hardware, there are people who can write the software, there are people who can manage the networks, there are people who can build and maintain the infrastructure, and there are people who can do similar tasks for the infrastructure required for the phones to have infrastructure. No one can do every task needed to make phones work, much less keep a significant number of such operational. There are multiple full time jobs involved here. That's not even getting into making newer, better phones.<br /> <br /> The whole point of specialization is that it allows people to focus on specific tasks rather than trying to do everything. This allows people who are not particularly suited for some tasks to contribute by focusing on tasks they are suited for.<br /> <br /> This leads to some people being less powerful than others because the tasks they are suited for don't involve punching giant monsters to death or sticking sharp bits of metal into people who punch giant monsters to death.<br /> <br /> This is balanced by the fact that in specialization friendly societies the warriors can train more and more efficiently, as well as be supplied with superior tools, logistics, and support by the noncombat specialists. This further allows greater population concentrations so even as the percentage of fighters decreases their total number generally increases.<br /> <br /> However with a philosophy where the 'weak' are left to die alone there's only motivation to specialize as whatever the leader/tribe sees as a strong role. Which leads to the choice to become mercs, thieves, or dead. Raven does not have a patronage system, she has a lot of bullyboys who fit some minimum definition of strong in her mind, and then rapes and pillages other societies to get what her half-assed tribe can't make for themselves because they're too busy training to be better rapers and pillagers. If she was actually using some sort of patronage system to keep non-combat specialists around she'd either not need to be a colossal bitch to a bunch of villages, or she'd be able to hold the territory and apply her system to the people she conquered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11837,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","user":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","date":". 11-15-2017, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T03:02:54-08:00","id":1157899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1157895#post1157895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A patronage system can be suggested all it wants. The simple fact is that her philosophy is incompatible with technological advance or more specifically the investments you need to make to make it happen. Nobody knows how to make a phone. There are people who can assemble the hardware, there are people who can write the software, there are people who can manage the networks, there are people who can build and maintain the infrastructure, and there are people who can do similar tasks for the infrastructure required for the phones to have infrastructure. No one can do every task needed to make phones work, much less keep a significant number of such operational. There are multiple full time jobs involved here. That's not even getting into making newer, better phones.<br /> <br /> The whole point of specialization is that it allows people to focus on specific tasks rather than trying to do everything. This allows people who are not particularly suited for some tasks to contribute by focusing on tasks they are suited for.<br /> <br /> This leads to some people being less powerful than others because the tasks they are suited for don't involve punching giant monsters to death or sticking sharp bits of metal into people who punch giant monsters to death. <br /> <br /> This is balanced by the fact that in specialization friendly societies the warriors can train more and more efficiently, as well as be supplied with superior tools, logistics, and support by the noncombat specialists. This father allows greater population concentrations so even as the percentage of fighters decreases their total number generally increases.<br /> <br /> However with a philosophy where the 'weak' are left to die alone there's only motivation to specialize as whatever the leader/tribe sees as a strong role. Which leads to the choice to become mercs, thieves, or dead. Raven does not have a patronage system, she has a lot of bullyboys who fit some minimum definition of strong in her mind, and then rapes and pillages other societies to get what her half-assed tribe can't make for themselves because they're too busy training to be better rapers and pillagers.If she was actually using some sort of patronage system to keep non-combat specialists around she'd either not need to be a colossal bitch to a bunch of villages, or she'd be able to hold the territory and apply her system to the people she conquered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you understand the difference between &quot;I am ideologically opposed to a thing&quot; and &quot;I will not provide the ideal environment for a thing to flourish&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T22:53:03-08:00","id":1158781,"title":"","content":"Another wasted episode. No fights, three separate settings. I'll save you some time, spoiler free. A) Ruby is special B) The Faunus are apathetic C) The White Fang is taking two scoops of Bad Guy Cereal. <br /> <br /> If you were in, say, film school and you wanted to give all of that information to the viewer in as efficiently as possible, you could do it in a single extended lateral camera move and make a nice three panel style vignette of Ruby sparring with a nervous Oscar telling him to focus and let go of his worries, cut to on of the &quot;Blake and Sun can't get signatures on their Help Not Fuck The World&quot; Campaign, and then cut to the Evil White Fang Priest Duo saying &quot;You know what is required of you. Capture X and kill Y&quot;. That could be done in a stylish, three beat single tracking shot lasting about 10-15 seconds. <br /> <br /> and then you wouldn't have wasted 15 minutes. I seriously learned nothing in this episode I didn't already know, and the plot <b>insists</b> on reminding me every chance it gets that Ruby is <i>just super special, guys</i>. 2/10 please resubmit for grading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T23:41:49-08:00","id":1158787,"title":"","content":"Okay I'm not gonna pretend that this was the best episode of the volume, let alone series, but c'mon, there were good parts.<br /> <br /> Spoilered just in case.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">While the petition montage went on far too long, IMO, Blake's talk with Sun was nice. And it was nice to see more of Menagerie. Even if we didn't learn anything we didn't already about Adam (he's a spiteful pissbaby), it was nice to see Blake's outlook.<br /> <br /> Ruby and Oscar's scene, IMO, was less about Ruby being special and more, to me, seeing Ruby actually show some semblances of her personality beyond &quot;Peppy Protagonist&quot;. Seriously, as likeable as she is, she was kind of lacking in depth through the first three volumes. Also, it was <i>really </i>nice for her to acknowledge being torn up about Penny's death, after going a volume without mentioning the poor robot.<br /> <br /> And with Those Two Fang Cultists, the real meat there is their working even behind Adam, and seem to be using HIM for their purposes. Were they behind Sienna rising, too? Are they trying to manipulate the Fang as a whole? Were <i>they</i> the real problem?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I mean, not the best episode and it feels like a bit of a stall after the previous one, but 2/10 is just being <i>unfair.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T00:28:46-08:00","id":1158794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1157899#post1157899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you understand the difference between &quot;I am ideologically opposed to a thing&quot; and &quot;I will not provide the ideal environment for a thing to flourish&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Do you understand that it doesn't matter if Raven is intentionally anti-tech, or if it's just a result, it still ends with the extinction of all non-Salem sapient life on Remnant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T03:43:03-08:00","id":1158852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1158794#post1158794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. Do you understand that it doesn't matter if Raven is intentionally anti-tech, or if it's just a result, it still ends with the extinction of all non-Salem sapient life on Remnant?</div> </div> </div> </div>One regionally-powerful bandit queen is enough to damn Remnant? Wow, Remnant is screwed.<br /> <br /> Again, you might have a point, <i>if Raven was High Queen of Remnant.</i> And got there without shifting priorities or methodology at all, continuing to rule as someone who wasn't in power, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T03:52:44-08:00","id":1158859,"title":"","content":"First, Blake really looks much better without the ribbon. I keep noticing that.<br /> <br /> Second <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">the Line Rose was strong with this one<br /> <br /> I hope they hurry up and gst the Menagsrie stuff done soon, or Blake wont be part of the RWBY reunion till next volume. Though, I can see two avenues to her going to Haven now. First, the Fang succeed and shes taken there (then escaping or helped to escape by Ilya). Or, she goes after the Fang after the assassination attempt, whether it suceeds or fails.<br /> <br /> I think Ilya is being set up for a heel-face turn. Just wondering if she'll join the protagonists or if she's a sacrificial lion type character </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T04:41:23-08:00","id":1158876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1158787#post1158787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay I'm not gonna pretend that this was the best episode of the volume, let alone series, but c'mon, there were good parts.<br /> <br /> Spoilered just in case.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">While the petition montage went on far too long, IMO, Blake's talk with Sun was nice. And it was nice to see more of Menagerie. Even if we didn't learn anything we didn't already about Adam (he's a spiteful pissbaby), it was nice to see Blake's outlook.<br /> <br /> Ruby and Oscar's scene, IMO, was less about Ruby being special and more, to me, seeing Ruby actually show some semblances of her personality beyond &amp;quot;Peppy Protagonist&amp;quot;. Seriously, as likeable as she is, she was kind of lacking in depth through the first three volumes. Also, it was <i>really </i>nice for her to acknowledge being torn up about Penny's death, after going a volume without mentioning the poor robot.<br /> <br /> And with Those Two Fang Cultists, the real meat there is their working even behind Adam, and seem to be using HIM for their purposes. Were they behind Sienna rising, too? Are they trying to manipulate the Fang as a whole? Were <i>they</i> the real problem?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I mean, not the best episode and it feels like a bit of a stall after the previous one, but 2/10 is just being <i>unfair.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>To quote a great movie, It's incredibly unfair. I don't grade on a curve and this isnt a macaroni-glued-to-plate project. RWBY is a show backed by an online indie powerhouse wih its own tie in Steam game, it has to play with the Big Boys. The stuff you mentioned should have all lasted maybe 3 minutes out of 15 and the remaining time should have been used for a Big Action Or Plot Setpiece. Preferably both. <br /> <br /> This is shit writing and it hurts me to say that. I'd expect this from a Digital Animation 102 final project. People pay to watch RWBY. Seriously, this episode was storyboarded and nobody cared that it was 15 minutes of shilling, Tell Dont Show, and oooh so mysterious plotting. What did the show have to even say about that bit? Maybe Team Terrorist isnt 100% loyal? No shit, they just <b>killed their leader last week</b>. <br /> <br /> 2/10. For Oscar adding a bit if character and maybe the &quot;Spite&quot; dialogue, which should have been overlayed over said character actually doing something. Instead of fleshing out a major, mysterious Antagonist we watched 2 characters sit and talk about someone. JFC, thats literally in Bad Film-making 101","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T05:33:22-08:00","id":1158897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1158876#post1158876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RWBY is a show backed by an online indie powerhouse wih its own tie in Steam game, it has to play with the Big Boys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Rooster Teeth is allowed to get indie cred anymore. They're not like ten people in a little office these days. They're a subsidiary of a subsidiary of a subsidiary of a subsidiary (Rooster Teeth to Fullscreen to Otter to AT&amp;T/Chernin) and they own their own bigass studio and have tons of employees and enormous cash flow and hold conventions with tens of thousands of people who show up just for their properties. They employ industry professionals from top to bottom.<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with that, of course. They make good shit and they've all worked hard for their success. But they aren't four guys cobbling together machinima together with mics they bought at Best Buy and some extremely basic screen-capture software and calling their buddies to do voice-acting anymore, and haven't been for a long time. They're a regular media company now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T09:14:24-08:00","id":1158978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1158897#post1158897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think Rooster Teeth is allowed to get indie cred anymore. They're not like ten people in a little office these days. They're a subsidiary of a subsidiary of a subsidiary of a subsidiary (Rooster Teeth to Fullscreen to Otter to AT&amp;T/Chernin) and they own their own bigass studio and have tons of employees and enormous cash flow and hold conventions with tens of thousands of people who show up just for their properties. They employ industry professionals from top to bottom.<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with that, of course. They make good shit and they've all worked hard for their success. But they aren't four guys cobbling together machinima together with mics they bought at Best Buy and some extremely basic screen-capture software and calling their buddies to do voice-acting anymore, and haven't been for a long time. They're a regular media company now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their work model still isn't quite triple a either. In this sense they are comparable to Ninja Theory.<br /> They're big. But they're far closer to Extra Credits than to Universal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T13:11:54-08:00","id":1159142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1158852#post1158852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One regionally-powerful bandit queen is enough to damn Remnant? Wow, Remnant is screwed.<br /> <br /> Again, you might have a point, <i>if Raven was High Queen of Remnant.</i> And got there without shifting priorities or methodology at all, continuing to rule as someone who wasn't in power, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>What even is your point? That raven isn't anti-tech because she's not actually in charge? That make no sense. My point, and complaint, has always been that her brain-dead philosophy is anti-civilization, thus inherently anti-progress and anti-tech.<br /> <br /> She's never going to be anything but a force of entropy as long as she tries to cleave to that nonsense, and thus the only sane methods of dealing with her are to deliver as swift a death as possible, or avoidance/evasion if you can't fight her, or you know dying bravely hen she attacks and you can't get away, but that one is less a sane choice and more a lack of better options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11837,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","user":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","date":". 11-15-2017, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T13:37:39-08:00","id":1159155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1159142#post1159142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What even is your point? That raven isn't anti-tech because she's not actually in charge? That make no sense. My point, and complaint, has always been that her brain-dead philosophy is anti-civilization, thus inherently anti-progress and anti-tech.<br /> <br /> She's never going to be anything but a force of entropy as long as she tries to cleave to that nonsense, and thus the only sane methods of dealing with her are to deliver as swift a death as possible, or avoidance/evasion if you can't fight her, or you know dying bravely hen she attacks and you can't get away, but that one is less a sane choice and more a lack of better options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Raven isn't anti-tech because she is not ideologically opposed to technology. That is what the words mean. Remember how words have definitions? Her ideology might logically have detrimental effects on civilization if applied universally in a large area, but 1) that is a consequence of her ideology, which is a DIFFERENT THING than a feature of an ideology, and 2) she's not in charge and she won't be.<br /> <br /> And yeah, bandits suck and should generally be wiped out ASAP, ideologically driven or not. But this character has an interesting past and possibly hidden motives and agendas, and I want to know what those are. As such, I am uninterested in seeing her killed off at this point. It's not like these are REAL PEOPLE dying, and having interesting characters who are, to some degree, monstrous, tends to be beneficial to many stories. Particularly ones like <i>Exalted.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T12:45:55-08:00","id":1159521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1159155#post1159155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Raven isn't anti-tech because she is not ideologically opposed to technology. That is what the words mean. Remember how words have definitions? Her ideology might logically have detrimental effects on civilization if applied universally in a large area, but 1) that is a consequence of her ideology, which is a DIFFERENT THING than a feature of an ideology, and 2) she's not in charge and she won't be.<br /> <br /> And yeah, bandits suck and should generally be wiped out ASAP, ideologically driven or not. But this character has an interesting past and possibly hidden motives and agendas, and I want to know what those are. As such, I am uninterested in seeing her killed off at this point. It's not like these are REAL PEOPLE dying, and having interesting characters who are, to some degree, monstrous, tends to be beneficial to many stories. Particularly ones like <i>Exalted.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>She is anti-technology because anti-technology is a subset of being anti-social. She opposes the societal foundations that would make technology possible. Worse even, she makes it harder for societies around hers to maintain those societal foundations by conducting banditry against them. Her philosophy is having a very real negative immediate effect on the well being of many towns, even at this scale. She is running a parasite-society, with an ideology that will make it difficult to impossible to perform the bandit equivalent of sustainable farming.<br /> <br /> Might makes right does not encourage long term thinking as it tends to put one into &quot;fight to live now, or die&quot; situations. One leader restrains themselves in their raidings to not wipe out all worthwhile targets within range, another contender will rise and promise more loot on their next raid. And we've seen that Raven's band will destroy villages.<br /> <br /> (She can't actually become in charge of Remnant, as her philosophy requires outside targets. Her philosophy will destroy her own people long before she'd get there.)<br /> <br /> But no one is talking about her being killed off in the show right now. The point is merely that she is clearly and utterly a force for evil, whatever her motivations, and that if she's going to become a force for good, she'll need to change dramatically (as often happens in stories, so I'm not ruling it out, just noting that dramatically both means 'in the story' and 'by a major amount' here). She's not THE big bad, but she is A big bad. like Torchwick was.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T12:49:24-08:00","id":1159522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1159521#post1159521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But no one is talking about her being killed off in the show right now. The point is merely that she is clearly and utterly a force for evil, whatever her motivations, and that if she's going to become a force for good, she'll need to change dramatically (as often happens in stories, so I'm not ruling it out, just noting that dramatically both means 'in the story' and 'by a major amount' here). She's not THE big bad, but she is A big bad. like Torchwick was.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>At the MOST charitable... She Ain't Helping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T19:05:50-08:00","id":1160086,"title":"","content":"NO she's actively part of the problem, she's basically Cinder with less ambition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T19:29:36-08:00","id":1160088,"title":"","content":"Anyone want to hear my speculation about the Kingdom of Atlas?<br /> <br /> I think they have Icewalkers and Dean Shomshack's Inglehamish. Frontiersfolk who reject the conformity of Atlas (and Mantle before it), but who still play important roles in the kingdom.<br /> <br /> The Icewalkers herd unpennable beasts southward for the winter, bringing food to the cities and reducing the amount of fertile land that would otherwise need to be devoted to livestock.<br /> <br /> The Inglehamish are basically Solitas' answer to the &quot;normal&quot; villages found elsewhere in the world. Without Fair Folk to make them suspicious, and with Grimm presenting a common foe, the Inglehamish would be more accepting of travelers, making their homes important waystations between cities.<br /> <br /> I've also written some speculation articles about their history, technology, and culture.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://sunder-the-gold.tumblr.com/post/159924972304/mantle-and-deep-sea-sailing\" target=\"_blank\">Mantle and deep-sea sailing</a></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://sunder-the-gold.tumblr.com/post/159939255448/speculation-regarding-ancient-mantle\" target=\"_blank\">Speculation about Ancient Mantle</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://sunder-the-gold.tumblr.com/post/166553428964/atlesian-patriotism-runs-deep\" target=\"_blank\">Atlesian Patriotism Runs Deep</a></span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-17-2017, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T17:43:23-08:00","id":1161351,"title":"","content":"Since the show made a point of separating them: How do I tell the difference between someone's semblence and magic, other than waiting for a character to tell me? Semblences seem to range from multiplication to illusions to lightning powers to super speed and magnetism, even including a fairy godmother with a 'magic' wand. What are the signs of semblences vs magic that will leave characters accept what they see vs denying as impossible?<br /> <br /> The only thing I could figure out is that everyone gets one superpower, and if they display a second, one of them has to be magic. But given the broad definition of some semblences and the so-advanced-it-looks-like-magic-at-times dust technology, I'm still caught off guard by not figuring out what's meant to be surprising and what's not at times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T19:35:15-08:00","id":1161391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1161351#post1161351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the show made a point of separating them: How do I tell the difference between someone's semblence and magic, other than waiting for a character to tell me? Semblences seem to range from multiplication to illusions to lightning powers to super speed and magnetism, even including a fairy godmother with a 'magic' wand. What are the signs of semblences vs magic that will leave characters accept what they see vs denying as impossible?</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually seems like it would almost have to be a point of contention within the setting itself. Like, you literally have Weiss going &quot;we have Dust, Semblances, but there's no such thing as magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, I know she wasn't actually talking to Yang; she was talking to us, the viewers, in the same way that when Pyrrha explained Aura to Jaune she wasn't actually talking to him either. But in the context of the actual world itself Weiss doesn't know a bunch of weird creeps are watching her most of the time. Which means that &quot;magic&quot; being something that can be confused with the effects generated by Dust and Semblances has to be something that's confusing enough within the World of Remnant that Weiss feels the need to point it out to Yang.<br /> <br /> The only explanation I can come up with that makes sense is that in the context of the World of Remnant, &quot;magic&quot; would encompass two things:<br /> <br /> The first would be someone who displays the ability to actually work their will upon the world in massively flexible and powerful ways that clearly violate natural law and aren't a part of any plausible Semblance. A classic wizard in the tower, who can call down lightning and fire and raise demons from the vasty deeps and foretell the future and fly through the air and craft items of wondrous power might qualify, as would the classic witch archetype who can brew potions and curse her enemies and blight crops and suchly. Doing all of those things all at once would shatter what people know of Semblances are capable of, I think, and be regarded as a form of magic.<br /> <br /> The second would be a singular power so out of bounds of what Semblances are known to be able to provide it acquires unearthly, ethereal connotations and significance.<br /> <br /> The problem here is that people inhabiting the World of Remnant marinate in this stuff as part of their life; it's exceptional to them, like when Nora specifically describes Semblances as superpowers, but something they've internalized. We, the viewers, don't have that. Which, as you say, Bjorn, makes it really friggin' hard to know if what we're seeing is something that should be shocking or not.<br /> <br /> Like when Qrow turned into a bird for the first time. That got a pretty huge reaction... but like 90% of people seeing it were like &quot;Qrow's Semblance is fuckin' awesome/deeply lame.&quot; (Pick one.) Not &quot;Qrow was gifted with magical powers by Ozpin.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T23:53:37-08:00","id":1161438,"title":"","content":"I really appreciate that the RWBY team is trying to do more with cinematography and plotting, I think it's great and they are making big strides in moving from &quot;Fight show with dialogue&quot; to &quot;Story with Fights&quot;. They keep stumbling over their feet, but they are trying and I respect that.<br /> <br /> For the love of god, though, <b>hire a $%&amp;#ing script writer</b>. They bloat and cruft on the &quot;Let me tell you some Secrets&quot; scene was insane. The actual pay off was one single line of &quot;X did Y and there's a Z; and also, W ain't what you think&quot;, which was built upon another 90% of a scene where characters sat around and said &quot;I sure am angry at you for reasons extensively covered in almost every episode&quot; &quot;She sure is angry at you&quot; &quot;What if the Good Guys........... <i>weren't Good? </i>Hm? What if I were to <i>imply that about people you like</i>? &quot;<br /> <br /> JFC Raven you don't have to stall for the commercial break- just tell everyone upfront what you want to tell them. You didn't even monologue, you implied you might have a monologue for like 5 minutes. Her last minute sales pitch is &quot;Leave now in my magic portal that I can make literally whenever I want at no cost&quot; or &quot;Give up on your sister and I'll tell you the other 5 minutes of info I have&quot;. What kind of shit plan is this? It's not even &quot;Oh that's what her Character would do&quot;. No, it's what a goddamn moron would do. Raven should have explained all or most of what she knew and how it happened, give Yang a valid chance to express her feelings, and then dropped the &quot;we can be a family again&quot; ploy. She runs a bandit gang and she can't even handle Manipulation Level 1.<br /> <br /> But hey, at least we get to keep up the <i>mysterious villains</i> shtick. That was a productive use of 10 minutes.<br /> <br /> Ok, to balance out that salt, I will say that the big final moment was really touching, and Qrow's last bit was a nice addition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T06:12:49-08:00","id":1161488,"title":"","content":"Raven\u2019s speech was mostly about Yang learning that Raven is a piece of shit who never had a wholesome reason for any of the shit she has done.<br /> <br /> It was about Raven burning any connection Yang might have had left to her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T13:12:02-08:00","id":1161596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1161488#post1161488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raven\u2019s speech was mostly about Yang learning that Raven is a piece of shit who never had a wholesome reason for any of the shit she has done.<br /> <br /> It was about Raven burning any connection Yang might have had left to her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, it made Raven come across as clueless in the process.<br /> <br /> Yang: I need you to take me to Qrow so I can save my sister.<br /> Raven: Qrow is bad, you should stay here.<br /> Yang: If Qrow is bad, that's all the more reason to go save my sister, surely?<br /> Raven: ...yeah, I guess. But! You can either go now, and never learn what I know, or you can learn and stay here for good!<br /> Yang: If it's the only way to save my sister, you leave me no choice but to go now.<br /> Raven: ...dammit.<br /> <br /> Yang made clear why she wanted to go, and Raven failed to address that motivation in her argument. She is clearly too callous to get Yang's love for Ruby, but she is also seemingly just crap at talking to people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T13:50:28-08:00","id":1161605,"title":"","content":"I dont know if it's that she's callous. She seemed to care enough to try and stop Yang from getting involved. She just seems to not be able to show it right. And from the quiet way she responded to Yang pointing out she wssnt nice, She does realize and regrets it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T13:55:23-08:00","id":1161606,"title":"","content":"Raven is supposed to come off as pathetic. She\u2019s a coward, thief, murderer, willfully absent wife and mother, and a liar who lies to herself.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s Cinder without ambition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T17:23:37-08:00","id":1161664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1161606#post1161606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raven is supposed to come off as pathetic. She\u2019s a coward, thief, murderer, willfully absent wife and mother, and a liar who lies to herself.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s Cinder without ambition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Citation Needed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T18:26:32-08:00","id":1161679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1161664#post1161664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Citation Needed</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we can definitively prove she's a thief and a murderer, and that she abandoned her family. That's three of five. There's not a lot of evidence she's a liar in the strict &quot;knowingly voicing an untruth&quot; sense, cowardice is up in the air (Raven appears physically brave, but she's also scared enough of Salem to abandon what may well be an existential struggle), and &quot;Cinder without ambition&quot; is an entirely subjective judgement.<br /> <br /> So Sunder is three of five, with decent odds on the other two. That ain't bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T18:39:21-08:00","id":1161683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1161679#post1161679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">cowardice is up in the air (Raven appears physically brave, but she's also scared enough of Salem to abandon what may well be an existential struggle)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also how she has watched her daughter as a bird without ever meeting her face-to-face. The one time she was standing right next to Yang, it was only when Yang was unconscious, and she made sure to escape before Yang woke up and starting asking questions.<br /> <br /> Seems mighty cowardly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T21:04:03-08:00","id":1161746,"title":"","content":"To play devil's advocate:<br /> <br /> To view it from Raven's point of view, she views/viewed the whole shapeshifting thing as something &quot;inflicted&quot; on her, by Ozpin. Generally, if someone views something as an &quot;affliction&quot;, it wasn't welcomed, and therefore was something forced on them.<br /> <br /> If Ozpin was both willing and capable of forcing something on two powerful huntsmen..... What would he be willing to do to keep the Huntsmen under his control? Blackmail them? Threaten something they care about?<br /> <br /> Insert &quot;cant use your newborn daughter to manipulate you if you dont care about her&quot; meme here. <br /> <br /> Therefore, she couldnt appear to care for Yang at all. If she did, ozpin could con her into basically committing suicide by salem. <br /> <br /> She also thinks of taiyang and qrow as fools, specifically because they continue to slurp down ozpins kool-aid. She is angry because ozpin directly caused her team to collapse, and it appears he is doing the same with her daughter and.... Whatever ruby is, relation-wise. She views the fight against salem as one already lost, and sees no reason to fight a worthless fight. Ozpin has already failed, MULTIPLE TIMES, and he is willing to sacrifice multiple people regardless of that fact. <br /> <br /> Finally, she was how old when yang was born? What, early 20s? Knowing what she knows about the world, her panicking and running away is.... Understandable. Not acceptable, but understandable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T03:42:12-08:00","id":1161813,"title":"","content":"It's very common to see something as an unwelcome curse because of regret. It's more plausible than the alternative knowing that his sins on volition are of ignorance rather of domination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T08:45:34-08:00","id":1161881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1161746#post1161746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To view it from Raven's point of view, she views/viewed the whole shapeshifting thing as something &quot;inflicted&quot; on her, by Ozpin. Generally, if someone views something as an &quot;affliction&quot;, it wasn't welcomed, and therefore was something forced on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Name the last time Ozpin forced anything on anyone.<br /> <br /> He didn't demand that Blake out herself as a faunus; he let her keep wearing the ribbon even though he thought she shouldn't. He all but told her that he knew she was part of the White Fang, but didn't actually come out and say it or force her to admit it, or to reveal everything she knew.<br /> <br /> He didn't demand that Team RWBY explain what had really happened at the docks, or with the stolen Paladin that was found wrecked in the city after causing several traffic accidents and destroying high-rise support pillars.<br /> <br /> He didn't ask Team RWBY to go scouting in Mountain Glenn; they were going to do that on their own. Instead, he let them know they weren't actually getting anything past him, and stuck them with a babysitter and bodyguard who would send them all home to safety if he thought they couldn't handle the danger. (It's not Oobleck's fault that Ruby went sneaking out and had an entire street randomly collapse under her little girl weight and send her plummeting a hundred feet.)<br /> <br /> He didn't force Pyrrha to become the Fall Maiden. Even when she said yes the first time, he refused to accept her answer until she'd heard about the possible side-effects, and then he gave her time to think about. Even when Beacon was under attack and he needed to do the procedure NOW, he stopped long enough for her to give clear, spoken consent.<br /> <br /> He never told Ruby about the Silver Eyes because he didn't want to put that responsibility on her just yet. He wanted her to enjoy being a kid, like he told Glynda after the food fight.<br /> <br /> Ozpin has at least some influence in who gets appointed as a headmaster of a hunting academy, and he leaves instructions for them to follow, but he has never demanded obedience. Each headmaster runs their academy in their own way according to their own choices. Leonardo Lionheart could go for months of radio silence without Ozpin going over or sending someone to demand an explanation. Ozpin wants cooperation between equals, even when that means he doesn't get the cooperation that he wants.<br /> <br /> Ozpin also doesn't have a choice about his soul attaching itself to Oscar; that's the curse of the gods.<br /> <br /> So, when was the last time Ozpin struck you as someone who forced things on anyone?<br /> <br /> (This isn't even counting the Last King of Vale, who &quot;forced&quot; an end to war, and a new culture of freedom and democratic republic upon the world, while stepping down from his position of power over the whole word and even his own kingdom in order to give the new system of government proper legitimacy. He gave up his power to force anything else on anyone, ever again.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She is angry because ozpin directly caused her team to collapse </div> </div> </div>Her team collapsed because SHE left, and she left because she abandoned them to fight Salem on their own.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just because Ozpin is a secretive authority figure doesn't make him evil. Just because he doesn't tell everyone absolutely everything, give away everything he owns, and agree to help them do whatever they want, doesn't make him evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-23-2017, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T15:44:17-08:00","id":1161984,"title":"","content":"Sunder, just gotta give you some applause. I brought up similar sentiments on the RWBY reddit and learned that while some people have legit reasons to not trust Ozpin, by far most people who have problems with Ozpin outright make shit up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T15:59:59-08:00","id":1161988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1161984#post1161984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sunder, just gotta give you some applause. I brought up similar sentiments on the RWBY reddit and learned that while some people have legit reasons to not trust Ozpin, by far most people who have problems with Ozpin outright make shit up.</div> </div> </div> </div>So many fans seem to have some kind of trauma regarding authority figures, and so ignore most of Ozpin's actions and instead accuse him of things he never did.<br /> <br /> Other fans have just been trained by all previous media to expect authority figures to be proven evil. Remember how refreshing it was to have a military general like Ironwood who is unambiguously a good guy who cares about the lives of his soldiers and civilians, and finds Hard Decisions actually morally difficult to make?<br /> <br /> So they jump all over themselves to take murderers like Cinder, Salem, and Raven at their word when they paint the villain of their personal stories -- Ozpin -- as a villain, even though he's the guy who spends each new life-time working as hard as he can to save as many lives from Salem as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T16:25:24-08:00","id":1162001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1161988#post1161988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So many fans seem to have some kind of trauma regarding authority figures, and so ignore most of Ozpin's actions and instead accuse him of things he never did.<br /> <br /> Other fans have just been trained by all previous media to expect authority figures to be proven evil. Remember how refreshing it was to have a military general like Ironwood who is unambiguously a good guy who cares about the lives of his soldiers and civilians, and finds Hard Decisions actually morally difficult to make?<br /> <br /> So they jump all over themselves to take murderers like Cinder, Salem, and Raven at their word when they paint the villain of their personal stories -- Ozpin -- as a villain, even though he's the guy who spends each new life-time working as hard as he can to save as many lives from Salem as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Harry Potter all over again.<br /> <br /> Though Ozpin is arguably even more moral than Dumbledore. Sure, he keeps things on Need To Know, but if you become Need To Know then he will make sure you know.<br /> <br /> Like you mentioned, with Pyrrha as the Maiden, when she says yes, Ozpin says &quot;Okay here is a list of possible effects. Take some time, think on it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T16:42:38-08:00","id":1162007,"title":"","content":"It could just be my fading memory, but I don't remember &quot;Dumbledore Is Evil&quot; being true outside of juvenile fanfiction.<br /> <br /> I don't remember Dumbledore forcing or even tricking Harry into doing anything. I remember Harry getting into all sorts of trouble on his own... or someone putting Harry into trouble despite the two of them trying to avoid it, like the Goblet of Fire business.<br /> <br /> I do remember Dumbledore keeping a lot of secrets from Harry, but mostly because he wanted Harry to stay out of trouble and enjoy his childhood a little longer.<br /> <br /> I remember at least one time where Dumbledore admitted that he probably fucked up by keeping a particular secret, and apologized to Harry about it. He let Harry break a bunch of priceless artifacts in his office without a word to stop him.<br /> <br /> I remember Dumbledore making a huge mistake by putting on that ring, but he was overcome by the desire to speak to his dead sister again. That makes him human, not evil.<br /> <br /> He put a bit more faith into Snape and Harry trying to work out (or at least <i>past</i>) their differences with the Occulemins lessons than perhaps he should have, but is that really a slight against him, or against Snape and Harry?<br /> <br /> He didn't tell Harry that Harry was likely one of Voldemort's soul-jars, because he didn't want to put that responsibility on Harry until absolutely necessary. What, was he supposed to tell an eleven year old kid that Voldemort -- the man trying to kill him and everyone he loves -- won't stop trying to kill him until he (Harry) dies anyway?<br /> <br /> If Dumbledore were really evil, he would have killed Harry as a baby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-23-2017, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T17:04:20-08:00","id":1162014,"title":"","content":"Times Ozpin forced something on someone? I'll try:<br /> <br /> - He catapulted Jaune off to his doom despite the fool clearly showing a lack of sufficient preparation. If you say 'prepare your parachute' and they ask 'what's a parachute', you don't kick them out of the plane. That said, we don't know that Ozpin didn't know something about Jaune that we don't know yet and that he thus wasn't in danger. Besides, he did sign up for a possibly lethal test to begin with.<br /> - Oskar sure didn't volunteer for what happened to him. But we don't know that Ozpin did, either.<br /> - He decided the team leaders, forcing responsibility on various students (which Jaune in particular seemed not keen on). But that's his job as a teacher.<br /> ...<br /> That's it. There is enough room for him to have dark motives and schemes that we don't know yet, but he doesn't seem to require any to explain his actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T18:18:52-08:00","id":1162025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1162014#post1162014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oskar sure didn't volunteer for what happened to him. But we don't know that Ozpin did, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming Oz is telling the truth, that one act is actually pretty solid evidence that the gods of Remnant, such as they are, are evil sons of bitches, because it meant they were okay with grotesque violations of the bodily autonomy of hundreds of people yet unborn for no better reason than to punish a dude they'd considered done fucked up.<br /> <br /> The way the Maiden powers don't care about who they latch onto is also slightly sketchy, but the person receiving them can decide not to use them if they want. They don't have a whole other person crammed into their heads against their will, who has at least some ability to grab the car keys, and who they'll eventually merge with whether they want to or not.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T18:34:30-08:00","id":1162029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1162025#post1162025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Assuming Oz is telling the truth, that one act is actually pretty solid evidence that the gods of Remnant, such as they are, are evil sons of bitches, because it meant they were okay with grotesque violations of the bodily autonomy of hundreds of people yet unborn for no better reason than to punish a dude they'd considered done fucked up.<br /> <br /> The way the Maiden powers don't care about who they latch onto is also slightly sketchy, but the person receiving them can decide not to use them if they want. They don't have a whole other person crammed into their heads against their will, who has at least some ability to grab the car keys, and who they'll eventually merge with whether they want to or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>This just in: Gods are jackasses. Putting this shocking reveal alongside literally all mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T18:56:49-08:00","id":1162042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1162014#post1162014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Times Ozpin forced something on someone? I'll try:<br /> <br /> - He catapulted Jaune off to his doom despite the fool clearly showing a lack of sufficient preparation. If you say 'prepare your parachute' and they ask 'what's a parachute', you don't kick them out of the plane. That said, we don't know that Ozpin didn't know something about Jaune that we don't know yet and that he thus wasn't in danger. Besides, he did sign up for a possibly lethal test to begin with.<br /> - Oskar sure didn't volunteer for what happened to him. But we don't know that Ozpin did, either.<br /> - He decided the team leaders, forcing responsibility on various students (which Jaune in particular seemed not keen on). But that's his job as a teacher.<br /> ...<br /> That's it. There is enough room for him to have dark motives and schemes that we don't know yet, but he doesn't seem to require any to explain his actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>So. One act done wholly for comic value, one thing he's wholly not responsible for until we actually get evidence that he's lieing and can pick who to possess, and he did his job as a teacher.<br /> <br /> He's an immortal enemy of salem, one that keeps his cards too close. This is enough to give him room for dark motives, sure.<br /> But beyond that? Grasping at straws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T22:32:51-08:00","id":1162098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1161679#post1161679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, we can definitively prove she's a thief and a murderer, and that she abandoned her family. That's three of five. There's not a lot of evidence she's a liar in the strict &quot;knowingly voicing an untruth&quot; sense, cowardice is up in the air (Raven appears physically brave, but she's also scared enough of Salem to abandon what may well be an existential struggle), and &quot;Cinder without ambition&quot; is an entirely subjective judgement.<br /> <br /> So Sunder is three of five, with decent odds on the other two. That ain't bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>the post I quoted started with this line: <b>&quot;Raven is supposed to come off as pathetic.&quot;</b> Raven is the leader of a bandit gang, she scares off Neo, and one of the most powerful characters in the show (Qrow) is wary of her. She is in no way &quot;supposed to come off as pathetic&quot;. Jaune is supposed to come off as pathetic. Raven could easily be the strongest fighter in the series for what we know about her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 11-24-2017, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T03:33:46-08:00","id":1162132,"title":"","content":"Would &quot;scared&quot; be a better adjective?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T07:33:05-08:00","id":1162171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1162098#post1162098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the post I quoted started with this line: <b>&quot;Raven is supposed to come off as pathetic.&quot;</b> Raven is the leader of a bandit gang, she scares off Neo, and one of the most powerful characters in the show (Qrow) is wary of her. She is in no way &quot;supposed to come off as pathetic&quot;. Jaune is supposed to come off as pathetic. Raven could easily be the strongest fighter in the series for what we know about her.</div> </div> </div> </div>You speak as though fighting ability is the only thing that makes a person admirable or pathetic.<br /> <br /> There's no question that Raven is dangerous in battle, but what else does she have going for her? Her bandits are no real physical threat to the kingdoms even with a Seasonal Maiden, and she and her Maiden use their unmatched powers to prey upon the weakest targets possible in order to steal the food they need to eat, day-to-day.<br /> <br /> They rely on the very people they deride as weaker than them just to eat. They rely on the very people that Raven derides as &quot;blind&quot; to protect them from Salem.<br /> <br /> Raven and her bandits are self-serving parasites, but she dresses it up in language.<br /> <br /> She tries to tell Yang that she was kind to her this time, and after Yang denounces that lie, Raven even admits it quietly to herself, hanging her head in shame.<br /> <br /> Raven ran away from a war that is soon going to be marching right up to her front door and demanding that she pick a side. And something tells me that she's going to regret the side she forsook and the side she's going to be forced to take.<br /> <br /> <br /> Jaune was supposed to appear pathetic, at first. But he improves all of the time, striving to become a better person as well as a better fighter. Someone who stands by his friends, and fights to make the world a better place.<br /> <br /> Even at his most pathetic, he took the time to offer Ruby Rose a hand of friendship to help her stand back up on her feet. After her sister abandoned her, Weiss yelled at her, and Blake ignored her, JAUNE was the first person to make Ruby feel welcome at Beacon Academy despite her two-year age handicap.<br /> <br /> Was that anywhere near as pathetic of him as Raven abandoning her team, her lover, and her newborn daughter because she would rather steal from vulnerable targets every day to survive rather than fight a strong opponent every day to survive?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T08:50:52-08:00","id":1162192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1162171#post1162171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was that anywhere near as pathetic of him as Raven abandoning her team, her lover, and her newborn daughter because she would rather steal from vulnerable targets every day to survive rather than fight a strong opponent every day to survive?</div> </div> </div> </div>One can reasonably argue that the only somewhat noble thing Raven did was let Yang be raised by Taiyang and Summer, sparing Yang the problem of being raised by such a horrible person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T08:56:57-08:00","id":1162194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1162192#post1162192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One can reasonably argue that the only somewhat noble thing Raven did was let Yang be raised by Taiyang and Summer, sparing Yang the problem of being raised by such a horrible person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Originally (in Volume 4), I though even Raven believed that, which is why she did it.<br /> <br /> After seeing that her &quot;tribe&quot; appears to be nothing but a random collection of bandits rather than an extended, multi-generational familial unit... I think it's more plausible Raven simply didn't want to raise a child on her own, seeing as she wouldn't have anyone else in the camp capable of handling it for her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T09:03:59-08:00","id":1162475,"title":"","content":"Edit: removed spoiler tags now that it is out.<br /> <br /> <br /> Qrow confirms that he and Raven voluntarily accepted the power to transform into birds, and Ozpin didn't force anything on them.<br /> <br /> I guess it goes to show that you can't trust a murderer who is deliberately trying to create suspicion towards a man that she needs to make seem like a bigger villain than herself.<br /> <br /> <br /> It does, however, also suggest that Raven continued to work for Ozpin a little while longer after learning about Salem. Given that Raven explained her own reasons for working for Ozpin to be gathering information about the truth of the world so that she could protect her tribe from it, that doesn't contradict anything we've heard or that I've extrapolated so far.<br /> <br /> I do think Raven might have wavered about staying with STRQ and abandoning the bandit life, given that she had Taiyang's child, but whatever inciting incident led her to return to her old life probably wasn't Ozpin's fault. Definitely wasn't because he did anything evil, or else she would have gleefully shared that secret.<br /> <br /> And it certainly wasn't because of Summer Rose's death, because Summer died YEARS AFTER Raven abandoned them. Summer's death is likely more Raven's fault than Ozpin\u2019s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-04-2017, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T10:05:42-08:00","id":1162499,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar636_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"636\" data-vbnamecard=\"636\">Sunder the Gold</a> - Spoiler tag that, the episode JUST dropped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T11:41:45-08:00","id":1162515,"title":"","content":"Fine, but it wasn\u2019t even a spoiler for people who were paying attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T14:32:22-08:00","id":1162554,"title":"","content":"It's the principle of the thing. Don't be a butt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T18:07:46-08:00","id":1162846,"title":"","content":"So Raven had made it sound as though being given the ability to turn into a bird was a betrayal or some kind of abuse of trust, that Ozpin did wrong by her. How? From all I can tell, she and Qrow can turn into birds at will, so what about this rubbed Raven so wrong that she left (if that is indeed why she left)? Are there side effects?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T18:17:03-08:00","id":1162849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1162846#post1162846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Raven had made it sound as though being given the ability to turn into a bird was a betrayal or some kind of abuse of trust, that Ozpin did wrong by her. How? From all I can tell, she and Qrow can turn into birds at will, so what about this rubbed Raven so wrong that she left (if that is indeed why she left)? Are there side effects?</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">My figure on this is that she was using it to sling shit at Ozpin, given that Qrow mentions that they fucking signed up for it.<br /> <br /> My assumption is that Raven agreed to this because hey, more power, she LIKES more power!<br /> <br /> And she left because she realized that Salem was NOT going to be as easy a foe as she assumed. There was actual like, RISK and stuff! Ozpin didn't say she was that strong except when he did! Fuck this, she's gonna go guard her shitty bandit camp rather than risk her life against a goddess</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T19:06:16-08:00","id":1162855,"title":"","content":"Okay I'm an episode or two behind, but a point that occurred to me during some of the earlier posts. Have they said what Salem is? Cause if I recall Ozpin explained his body jumping thing as divine punishment for failing to stop Salem. Now I know we don't know how many times Ozpin has ended up in his current state, but I think more than 3 times is a safe bet, wouldn't that mean that Salem is at least as old as Ozpin? <br /> <br /> Which would lead me to question whether or not the they're dealing with a potentially millenia old entity of -not insignificant power- or if Salem is like Ozpin and killing her just leads to some poor sod getting her in their head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T19:20:40-08:00","id":1162864,"title":"","content":"Wild tangent: had anyone else noticed that RWBY matches one-to-one to the four alchemical operations (Reddening, Whitening, Blackening, Yellowing)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T20:44:47-08:00","id":1162889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1162864#post1162864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wild tangent: had anyone else noticed that RWBY matches one-to-one to the four alchemical operations (Reddening, Whitening, Blackening, Yellowing)?</div> </div> </div> </div>They also match the color scheme of the Grimm.<br /> <br /> So far, it seems merely coincidental, rather than meaningful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T20:54:04-08:00","id":1162891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1162855#post1162855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which would lead me to question whether or not the they're dealing with a potentially millenia old entity of -not insignificant power- or if Salem is like Ozpin and killing her just leads to some poor sod getting her in their head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless Salem gets cursed by the Gods for failing to fuck up humanity, I doubt that's a problem.<br /> <br /> Edit: That is, my best guess is that Salem was a pupil of Ozpin Prime's before she ate a power field bigger than her head and gained control of all Grimm. Ozpin Prime was killed against her, and the Gods reacted by going &quot;Dude you failed to stop her. Go try again&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 11-26-2017, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T21:03:49-08:00","id":1162895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1162889#post1162889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They also match the color scheme of the Grimm.<br /> <br /> So far, it seems merely coincidental, rather than meaningful.</div> </div> </div> </div>To add to this, the procedure of alchemy isnt followed in order(B-&gt;W-&gt;Y-&gt;R as opposed to R-W-B-Y in both intros and team name), and they don't have a common material their interacting with or shaping at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T21:33:07-08:00","id":1162898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1162891#post1162891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless Salem gets cursed by the Gods for failing to fuck up humanity, I doubt that's a problem.<br /> <br /> Edit: That is, my best guess is that Salem was a pupil of Ozpin Prime's before she ate a power field bigger than her head and gained control of all Grimm. Ozpin Prime was killed against her, and the Gods reacted by going &quot;Dude you failed to stop her. Go try again&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well according to the story Qrow told last season there was a malevolent god too. But yeah we don't really know anything about Salem aside from her and Ozpin being old enemies, she's presumably really powerful, can command Grimm, and safe bet does not have the best intentions of the other races of the world at heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T21:41:43-08:00","id":1162899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1162898#post1162898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well according to the story Qrow told last season there was a malevolent god too. But yeah we don't really know anything about Salem aside from her and Ozpin being old enemies, she's presumably really powerful, can command Grimm, and safe bet does not have the best intentions of the other races of the world at heart.</div> </div> </div> </div>But both of the Brothers made humanity, supposedly. So who knows where the God of Destruction is going.<br /> <br /> (And I personally refer to them as the Gods of Creation and Destruction, rather than Light and Dark, because those actually <i>make sense</i> given the story. The older brother <i>makes things</i> and the little brother makes things to <i>destroy them</i>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T21:53:08-08:00","id":1162903,"title":"","content":"Not only does the God of Destruction cooperate in making humanity, the illustrations used for Qrow\u2019s story very deliberately portray the brothers as Yin and Yang to each other. One is bright with a dark core and one is dark with a bright core.<br /> <br /> Allegedly, the Grimm weren\u2019t originally meant to kill humans, but anything with form. The fact that they now only attack humans (a creation of the their creator) and nothing else suggests the possibility that they have been corrupted and repurposed.<br /> <br /> Dr. Merlot\u2019s theme song, written by a man contracted to Rooster Teeth, likewise suggests that the Grimm have somehow been perverted from some original state. This song\u2019s melody has reappeared outside of Merlot\u2019s story as background music for scenes of the Grimm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T22:50:12-08:00","id":1162910,"title":"","content":"So what we're saying here is that Grimm are a surprisingly effective Horror for the Beast the Primordial game. :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T13:14:11-08:00","id":1163319,"title":"","content":"Good god, Emerald and Mercury showed up. Doing things! Mercury had a <i>line.</i><br /> <br /> These are crazy times we lived in.<br /> <br /> (Team ACME? Team CAME? Not sure what's happening there.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T02:00:06-08:00","id":1163849,"title":"","content":"Sorcerous Overlord's weekly bitch about RWBY post, feel free to ignore. <br /> <br /> The dinner scene was great! Great payoff, great characterization. The Oz/Qrow little league stern talking too was passable as well. Most of us totally called the minor reveal as well. I'm happy for the creators of Rwby. <br /> <br /> Now where the hell was any action? This episode was three minutes shorter than the next shortest, and it cuts off right as a combat scene is about to start. Season 5 had the Hornet fight, which wasn't my cup of tea but I'll acknowledge, and the Bandit Brawl. Seriously, that's been it so far. Are the choreographers on strike? Season 1 had the Dust shop, and the entire Forest Arc by now. Getting pretty worn out waiting for shit to pay off. This is RWBY, from the guy who did DEAD FANTASY. The <i>entire point</i> of this show is fight choreography, and we're just... skipping it? I used to hungrily await new episodes, and now i just remember that i can kill 15 minutes while doing laundry. <br /> <br /> The whole Raven thing is stupid, and the bird thing is stupid. We as an audience have no idea what the mechanics behind semblances are, how that differs from &quot;real magic&quot;, and what Aura does in relation to those 2 things. Nora's Semblance is that she gets super strong from lightning, Pyrrha is Magneto, Qrow manipulates luck, and Raven can make portals. Hell, Sun can make Aura clones, Glynda is Telekinesis, and Blake has straight up videogame magic as well as summoning. Oh, and Emerald has Mass Illusions. What is and is not a Semblance ability? Why should anyone be surprised that Qrow can turn into a bird if they give summoning and telekinesis a free pass? I would have said &quot;body manipulation&quot;, but Quint (The Trumpet player) makes physical clones of himself, while Nora and Yang both enhance their bodies. If you're going to play up &quot;True Magic&quot; as being a Really Big Deal then we viewers need to know WHY it's a Really Big Deal. Besides, all I've seen so far is a couple of energy blasts and some hovering. Hardly outside of the scope of what Semblances already do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T11:07:27-08:00","id":1163987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1163849#post1163849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and Emerald has Mass Illusions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slight point of order. Emerald's illusions are entirely mental, and she can't work them on many people. She mentioned in V3 that she can basically control the sensory input of one person with no trouble, but two is pushing it.<br /> <br /> This is a nitpick that doesn't really address the main push of your argument, because honestly the best distinction I can think of for Semblance vs Magic is &quot;Semblances do generally one thing, Magic does <b>All The Things</b> at once&quot; but by that logic the Schnee Glyphs basically <i>are</i> magic.<br /> <br /> ... Y'know if it's revealed that the Schnee Glyphs are a form of magic that became a Hereditary Semblance, that might be some interesting payoff. I mean, let's be fair, the Glyphs are an exception to pretty much all the Semblance rules.<br /> <br /> Every person's Semblance is unique... Except for the Schnee Glyphs.<br /> <br /> Every person's Semblance does one thing... Except for the Schnee Glyphs, which can explicitly do multiple things.<br /> <br /> Granted back in the days of V3 I had a theory that the Mantle of the Winter Maiden got damaged somehow, and it glommed onto one of the Schnees and has been passing down through the line. To restore the full power of the Winter Maiden, you'd need to kill every Schnee and collect their escaping Aura.<br /> <br /> This was written <i>before</i> it was revealed that the &quot;Entire Schnee Family&quot; consists of five people, one of whom is only in by marriage.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, also, something that might help make them more distinct - If Magic is something you could have <i>without</i> an Awakened Aura, because those two power sources are different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T13:10:23-08:00","id":1164033,"title":"","content":"The thing that makes Weiss's glyphs differ from magic is that glyphs use Dust in order to do their thing. That's why Myrtenaster has a revolver hilt. They are likely limited to a small list, based entirely on what types of Dust they have on hand. Also, other people probably have glyphs as Semblances. It's probably a common one and the Schnee family is just a bit weird in that the Semblance has been hereditary.<br /> <br /> \u200bMagic doesn't need Dust.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1163849#post1163849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quint</div> </div> </div> </div>Flynt Coal","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":74,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","user":"Kyeudo","date":". 11-30-2017, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T18:14:56-08:00","id":1164122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164033#post1164033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing that makes Weiss's glyphs differ from magic is that glyphs use Dust in order to do their thing. That's why Myrtenaster has a revolver hilt. They are likely limited to a small list, based entirely on what types of Dust they have on hand. Also, other people probably have glyphs as Semblances. It's probably a common one and the Schnee family is just a bit weird in that the Semblance has been hereditary.<br /> <br /> \u200bMagic doesn't need Dust.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Flynt Coal</div> </div> </div> </div>If the biggest, world shakiest thing about Magic is &quot;its like a semblance, but without dust&quot; than why is it so important? <br /> <br /> My point (which honestly i didnt express well) was that we dont know any of how this works and the show wants it to be an important plot point. <br /> <br /> Also, my bad on Flynt. I looked it up on a wiki and must have copied it wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T18:26:15-08:00","id":1164127,"title":"","content":"Judging by people's reactions to Qrow and Raven's secret, apparently Semblances don't ever involve shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> So, magic seems capable of doing things which are impossible with Semblances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T19:37:39-08:00","id":1164154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164127#post1164127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Judging by people's reactions to Qrow and Raven's secret, apparently Semblances don't ever involve shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> So, magic seems capable of doing things which are impossible with Semblances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is great if you're Yang and Weiss and are legitimately freaked out about people turning into birds.<br /> <br /> <i>We</i> are not <i>they</i>. It's hard to know what we're supposed to regard as weird and freaky in a universe where the monkey-man hybrid can create glowing golden clones of himself to go along with the weird shadow copies of his not-girlfriend, who is on a team with someone whose family made their fortune selling rocks with crazy elemental powers, and all of this is perfectly normal. We need more context than that.<br /> <br /> Like... Ruby's weird silver eye thing caught everyone off-guard as something obviously weird and special because we really weren't prepared for Ruby to start vomiting streams of silver death light out of all her head orifices that froze a Grimm the size of a small town into place and super fucked up the lady who'd just murdered Pyrrha Nikos. That was, clearly, something exceptional not only to everyone in Vale, but also to us, the viewers. Similarly, the Four Maidens were presented in a way that obviously made us instantly recognize these were special, unique beings, touched by power and destiny in a way that a regular person with a Semblance is not. Ozpin possessing a fourteen year old was also something clearly not, you know... regular. The show presented all that well.<br /> <br /> Qrow and Raven... were sort of a conceptual failure in this regard, because literally for like a year people just thought turning into a birb was Qrow's Semblance, and it was like &quot;okay, he's a bird. Cool Semblance bro.&quot; (In some cases, &quot;ha ha, lame Semblance, bro.&quot;)<br /> <br /> They need to present this stuff a little better. Volume 5 has been a very, very talky volume with a lot of exposition dumps that aren't really doing it for me. It isn't like they haven't done that in the past, but... I dunno. Remember when Yang and Blake became Level 5 friends and that unlocked Yang's tragic backstory vis-a-vis the wagon trip with Ruby that went sideways? That was accompanied by cool-ass visual storytelling in kind of a uniquely animated style that was rad as hell.<br /> <br /> It wasn't just Yang talking her exposition into Blake's face for five minutes, which is what we're getting a lot of this year. These exposition dumps are very rarely even conversations, which are at least interesting; Qrow and Raven at the Higanbana bar was an exposition dump, but it was also verbal fencing between two siblings with a messed up relationship with different conflicts and give-and-take happening on, and under, the surface.<br /> <br /> That's way more interesting than Ozpin revealing what he's capable of in dribs and drabs.<br /> <br /> I also feel like the show is either making the kids stupid, or hiding things that they know and are conversant with from us, the viewers, which is also annoying. Like... NONE of the kids have asked &quot;So wait, the Grimm have a Queen? How does that fucking work? Is she a Grimm herself or something different? Why the hell aren't we all just dead if the Grimm have actual purpose and direction behind them? What's her specific agenda? Why would regular humans work for the things that want to kill all humans? DO they want to kill humans?&quot; to Qrow or Oz? At all?<br /> <br /> Because that seems like something someone with half a brain would ask!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T20:15:43-08:00","id":1164163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164154#post1164154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>We</i> are not <i>they</i>. It's hard to know what we're supposed to regard as weird and freaky in a universe where the monkey-man hybrid can create glowing golden clones of himself to go along with the weird shadow copies of his not-girlfriend, who is on a team with someone whose family made their fortune selling rocks with crazy elemental powers, and all of this is perfectly normal. We need more context than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point. Like, we had that World of Remnant where Aura was mentioned... But all it said about Semblances was that it was an Outwards Expression of one's Aura.<br /> <br /> We see that Flynt can literally make four different colored versions of himself. Qrow can create bad luck. Raven can violate the laws of space.<br /> <br /> Like, I'm enjoying the interactions of this volume, but I'd appreciate if there were like, I don't know, a World of Remnant or something that sat down and said &quot;What can a Semblance <i>do</i>?&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: Granted I'd also unironically enjoy a WoR where Qrow explained Basic Huntsmen and Huntress courtesy. Like &quot;What do you do if you and someone else are chasing the same bounty&quot; or &quot;So here's what you don't do to someone else on the field or else you got blacklisted&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T23:39:47-08:00","id":1164187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164122#post1164122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the biggest, world shakiest thing about Magic is &amp;quot;its like a semblance, but without dust&amp;quot; than why is it so important? </div> </div> </div> </div>You apparently missed the &quot;short list&quot; part, but then I didn't exactly emphasize that. From context, it looks like Dust can't just do whatever you want it to. Weiss does flame blasts, but nothing like what Cinder can do with the Fall Maiden's power.<br /> <br /> It looks like magic could quite possibly do everything that any Semblance can do, plus things beyond what a Semblance can do. I would not be surprised to see Ozpin giving a lesson on Semblances to Juan in an upcoming episode, both to help us understand what they can do and to set magic apart now that the specifics are starting to matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, my bad on Flynt. I looked it up on a wiki and must have copied it wrong. </div> </div> </div>It's a running joke for the Achievement Hunters when playing Minecraft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T04:35:31-08:00","id":1164222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164163#post1164163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, I'm enjoying the interactions of this volume, but I'd appreciate if there were like, I don't know, a World of Remnant or something that sat down and said &quot;What can a Semblance <i>do</i>?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the writers are waiting until they actually know that themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T05:36:26-08:00","id":1164234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164222#post1164222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe the writers are waiting until they actually know that themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because they\u2019re not revealing things as fast as you please doesn\u2019t mean they\u2019re making it all up as they go along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T08:06:26-08:00","id":1164276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164234#post1164234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just because they\u2019re not revealing things as fast as you please doesn\u2019t mean they\u2019re making it all up as they go along.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, they have a history of doing just that, so it isn't like it would be unprecedented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T09:14:39-08:00","id":1164296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164276#post1164276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, they have a history of doing just that, so it isn't like it would be unprecedented.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Whatever Cinder was supposed to be originally, Monty expanded it into three other ladies. But that was an improvisation within the framework they already had, since Pyrrha and Cinder both had the autumn leaf symbolism in Season 2 before he made the expansion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T09:40:38-08:00","id":1164303,"title":"","content":"I'm actually talking about Miles Luna just in general. He's worked on more than just RWBY, and his Red vs. Blue track record includes a fair amount of just making things up as he goes along as opposed to having a detailed road map.<br /> <br /> (I'm looking in your direction, Chorus Trilogy.)<br /> <br /> I can't speak to Shawcross and Haddock.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T11:09:50-08:00","id":1164328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164303#post1164303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually talking about Miles Luna just in general. He's worked on more than just RWBY, and his Red vs. Blue track record includes a fair amount of just making things up as he goes along as opposed to having a detailed road map.<br /> <br /> (I'm looking in your direction, Chorus Trilogy.)<br /> <br /> I can't speak to Shawcross and Haddock.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>From what I've heard, volumes 1 and 2 were the RWBY volumes that had the most 'Let's write by the seat of your pants'. IIRC, V3 was the first one to use an actual storyboard","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T11:50:11-08:00","id":1164348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164328#post1164328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I've heard, volumes 1 and 2 were the RWBY volumes that had the most 'Let's write by the seat of your pants'. IIRC, V3 was the first one to use an actual storyboard</div> </div> </div> </div>Right; the most infamous example of this is the genesis of Neo, who was reportedly designed and implemented as a character by Monty mid-season over the course of about two weeks after seeing a cosplay picture while ruminating over whether and what sort of henchman to give Roman. But Volume 2 is infamous for its production problems and delays and patchwork.<br /> <br /> Monty isn't on the show anymore, tho, god rest his soul. Miles and Kerry are, and Miles specifically has a history even outside of RWBY of writing by the seat of his pants.<br /> <br /> Now, there's nothing wrong with this, per se, but man, you had better keep your stuff STRAIGHT if you want it to all hang together.<br /> <br /> Watching RWBY slowly turn from Monty Oum's weird side project that was approved by Burnie Burns contingent on him getting all his RvB work done in a timely manner and whose cast was basically &quot;people we found around the office&quot; into a real show has been interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T21:52:50-08:00","id":1164468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164348#post1164348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Watching RWBY slowly turn from Monty Oum's weird side project that was approved by Burnie Burns contingent on him getting all his RvB work done in a timely manner and whose cast was basically &quot;people we found around the office&quot; into a real show has been interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn straight it has. It's almost surreal, considering I remember when the Red trailer hit.<br /> <br /> I'm amused by people who expected Ruby to be a kind of quiet serious girl from the trailer... And then later Monty said &quot;Eeeeeh looking back that's more a trailer for her scythegun than for RUBY-&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T04:32:41-08:00","id":1164502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164234#post1164234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just because they\u2019re not revealing things as fast as you please doesn\u2019t mean they\u2019re making it all up as they go along.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're five seasons into this show, and people are still confused about the function of basic building blocks of the setting, ones that we see routinely used in fight scenes. As well as about how and if they differ from powers we're meant to believe are amazing and legendary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T06:47:00-08:00","id":1164516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164502#post1164502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're five seasons into this show, and people are still confused about the function of basic building blocks of the setting, ones that we see routinely used in fight scenes. As well as about how and if they differ from powers we're meant to believe are amazing and legendary.</div> </div> </div> </div>And no one knows how badass you have to be to kill just one Beowolf on your own, let alone only half of the horde that Ruby slaughtered in the Red Trailer.<br /> <br /> Well, we can make guesses compared to our own abilities on Earth, but that doesn't tell us much about the common level of superhuman ability on Remnant, where anyone can become a demigod if they train.<br /> <br /> I put that one at Monty's feet. He was so obsessed with rule of cool that he neglected to establish a baseline which would help give us perspective on HOW awesome Team RWBY is, and therefore how much of a threat the Grimm are to anyone else.<br /> <br /> Volume 1 focused more on the characters than their world, and didn't get to show us as much of either as Rooster Teeth originally intended.<br /> <br /> Basically, Rooster Teeth fumbled their starting jump and landing, and they've been struggling to make up for ever since.<br /> <br /> Someone once remarked that every Volume, Rooster Teeth has reached beyond their capabilities, and therefore made mistakes... but in making those mistakes, they learned from them, and applied those lessons to the next Volume.<br /> <br /> This has always been a project where Rooster Teeth is straining to keep up with their own ambition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T12:12:02-08:00","id":1164590,"title":"","content":"what the hell is this trend I see lately. it seems the bigger a fan you are the more you hate on the thing you're a fan of. it's all over the internet and it's weird. no one talks about what they like about thier interests anymore. nothing but complaints and hate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T13:51:34-08:00","id":1164625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164516#post1164516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I put that one at Monty's feet. He was so obsessed with rule of cool that he neglected to establish a baseline which would help give us perspective on HOW awesome Team RWBY is, and therefore how much of a threat the Grimm are to anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think that they did a decent job doing some retrenchment work on this with a fair bit of subtlety in Volumes 2 and 3.<br /> <br /> Pyrrha, for example, beats up literally all of Team CRDL. That's a great scene not just because it's an excellent fight scene. It's a great scene because it also does some character work with Pyrrha using only body language, because it allows the villains to do something with themselves at the same time... AND because it lets them demonstrate, without smashing us in the face with it, that Pyrrha Nikos is an exceptional fighter and exceptional Hunter, clearly something out of the common way when it comes to her skill and dedication.<br /> <br /> Excellent scene. Great narrative economy.<br /> <br /> The other example, and I'm out on a bit of a limb here but I think I'm right, is Qrow vs. Winter.<br /> <br /> Team RWBY had always seemed fairly badass, and they ARE fairly badass. They fight high-end military equipment and a large terror cell by themselves. But I think the Qrow and Winter fight had a secondary purpose, which was to show the audience &quot;Team RWBY are still just students; this is what truly elite Hunters look like when they throw down.&quot; Qrow and Winter moved, and fought, differently than Team RWBY did, with significantly more power, impact, and control. That whole thing conveyed the impression that if either Ruby or Weiss had actually decided to get involved, they'd have been stomped flat, because they simply don't play at that level yet.<br /> <br /> Volume 3 was far and away the best volume in so many ways. They did a lot of showing and not a lot of telling, and many of the scenes work on multiple levels.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T16:23:26-08:00","id":1164684,"title":"","content":"Okay.<br /> <br /> One thing I gotta say about Vol. 5's technical side.<br /> Too much dead animation. They spend too damn much time on shots that could have been cut and sharpened up with a few quick cuts and faster movements. For a series about martial artists, they seems sluggish as all hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T18:56:22-08:00","id":1164720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164590#post1164590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what the hell is this trend I see lately. it seems the bigger a fan you are the more you hate on the thing you're a fan of. it's all over the internet and it's weird. no one talks about what they like about thier interests anymore. nothing but complaints and hate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because only controversy sparks debate. Just look at this thread. The places where we all agree, there's maybe one or two posts on the subject. Where we disagree, we find variety in our disagreement. Even where we think something could have been done better, what that better would look like varies from person to person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T19:52:27-08:00","id":1164724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164590#post1164590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what the hell is this trend I see lately. it seems the bigger a fan you are the more you hate on the thing you're a fan of. it's all over the internet and it's weird. no one talks about what they like about thier interests anymore. nothing but complaints and hate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't look at me, I'm still enjoying the hell about this show. I have nitpicks, sure, but I still tune in every week with excitement rather than pained resignation that comes from being too entrenched in something that you feel committed to seeing it through.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">SO HOW 'BOUT THIS WEEK, HUH?! 8D<br /> <br /> Jeeze, okay, I'm sure that NEITHER of Blake's parents are coming out of this unscarred. Alive? Potentially. But they're not getting out if this unhurt</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T05:54:00-08:00","id":1164765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164724#post1164724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't look at me, I'm still enjoying the hell about this show. I have nitpicks, sure, but I still tune in every week with excitement rather than pained resignation that comes from being too entrenched in something that you feel committed to seeing it through.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hear hear!<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164724#post1164724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">SO HOW 'BOUT THIS WEEK, HUH?! 8D<br /> <br /> Jeeze, okay, I'm sure that NEITHER of Blake's parents are coming out of this unscarred. Alive? Potentially. But they're not getting out if this unhurt</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Next chapter will be bloody no matter where it chooses to go...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T13:35:16-08:00","id":1164876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164590#post1164590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what the hell is this trend I see lately. it seems the bigger a fan you are the more you hate on the thing you're a fan of. it's all over the internet and it's weird. no one talks about what they like about thier interests anymore. nothing but complaints and hate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lately? Welcome to the internet. <br /> <br /> I want to like RWBY. I love the fights, I wanna see the Grimm go down, and I love the unrepentant kung fu movie cum gunfight via video game set pieces. This is a thing made for people like me. <br /> <br /> And I'm watching this thing I love stumble around blind while trying to put away its swords and awkwardly read out passages from <i>Drama and Pathos, A Beginner's Guide</i>. <br /> <br /> Its stopped being what we love it for and got caught up trying to be a Serious World For Serious People.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T14:16:26-08:00","id":1164891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164876#post1164876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its stopped being what we love it for and got caught up trying to be a Serious World For Serious People.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it's still what I loved it for.<br /> <br /> Everything after Volume 4 is actually more like what the four Color Trailers promised than the first three Volumes. Team RWBY's time at Beacon was meant to be our introduction to Remnant, though Rooster Teeth didn't manage that as well as they wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T14:22:21-08:00","id":1164895,"title":"","content":"Thoughts on chapters 6, 7 and 8 of volume 5.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yeah, we sure lost a good bit of tempo here, didn't we? I'll agree with much of the criticism levied previously in the thread: there's a lot of wasted time. The thing I said about Blake being the low-energy front has gotten turned around, but not due to an increase in the pacing of Blake's story. This whole Ozpin training camp had some great potential, but it's essentially amounted to Ruby half-heartedly beating up a farmer boy. I'm not even sure Jaune, who was specifically called out by Ozpin, has done any onscreen training.<br /> <br /> RWBY is decidedly mediocre show when it comes to writing. Not only lines and dialogue, but in terms of event density. I'm currently reading <i>Oathbringer</i> by Brandon Sanderson, and I was recently struck by the vast difference in scene composition. Sanderson almost never lets a scene be just one thing; if he sets up a scene, it will serve the purposes of several different characters almost unfailingly. In RWBY, there are such scenes, but they are exceptions, as the show often favours dialogues between two sides about one thing.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, though; some things have happened that are cool. Raven's and Yang's meeting and subsequent acquisition of Weiss was a good example of a multipurpose scene, and also a kind of hype moment that was cool to see. But it was also a very long scene, drawn out over two episodes (or, I guess, two separate scenes of which only the former was really multipurpose), and it's kind of emblematic of how RWBY goes. Hopefully we're getting out of the mid-season slump now when Cinder and team has shown up.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Despite the criticism above, I will say that RWBY is still a pretty cool show. I do like watching it, even if it's decidedly been a &quot;sure, why not&quot; kind of deal for a long time (in fact, the short episodes and slow plot progression makes it very easy to follow with very low investment; not sure that's a compliment?). As such a &quot;fan&quot;, I kind of feel I want to speak on some of the current topics in this thread.<br /> <br /> RWBY has changed. It's definitely become something quite different from what it started out as. I've heard there were plans laid for a large amount of seasons already before the premiere, but then we've also heard that Monty tended to come up with new shit he thought was cool now and then and just kind of put it in there. Therefore, it's impossible to say if the show had been more consistent throughout if he had gotten to remain with us, but I'm thinking odds are, it would have changed a fair bit none the less. We don't know how, exactly; perhaps more of the initial comedy and combat style had remained despite the shift in setting and plot lines.<br /> <br /> But how it might have been doesn't really matter now. Monty is gone, and I'm not sure if anyone thought that <i>wouldn't</i> impact the show? Monty was the primary combat choreographer and animator on the team, and when he was gone, there's really no way it wouldn't change. It'd have to, really. Now, it's fine to dislike that change; I certainly miss the tight combat animation, and the combat solutions they use now do have a decidedly different feel even if they're getting better by the volume. But I'm not sure I see the point of complaining about how things aren't the same. Yes, we know. Literally everyone wishes they were. There's a very tragic reason they aren't, and it's kind of impossible to do anything about.<br /> <br /> On another but related note, regarding fans criticising what they're fans of. Hopefully, unless it's your job to review stuff, people who don't like a show probably just won't watch it. Also, I think raising criticism about a show is a healthy sign of the ability to take a complex position on an issue, a quality direly lacking in certain aspects of society today. It might sometimes tip over on the negative, because it's easier to talk about on the internet, but I still think there's value in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T21:09:06-08:00","id":1164963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164876#post1164876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lately? Welcome to the internet. <br /> <br /> I want to like RWBY. I love the fights, I wanna see the Grimm go down, and I love the unrepentant kung fu movie cum gunfight via video game set pieces. This is a thing made for people like me. <br /> <br /> And I'm watching this thing I love stumble around blind while trying to put away its swords and awkwardly read out passages from <i>Drama and Pathos, A Beginner's Guide</i>. <br /> <br /> Its stopped being what we love it for and got caught up trying to be a Serious World For Serious People.</div> </div> </div> </div>And just what we are you refering to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T22:22:25-08:00","id":1164968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1164963#post1164963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And just what we are you refering to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Im honestly not sure what you meant to say. <br /> <br /> I quoted you because you said LATELY people have been complaing about stuff they supposedly like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T14:57:17-08:00","id":1165151,"title":"","content":"Firzt, it was aquote from the show. Which you might know if you watched it instead of bitching about it<br /> <br /> Second, you presume to speak for the entirety of the fandom. You dont. I for one like storytelling.<br /> <br /> And lastly, if you want the show to be nothing but action sequences, like the preview trailers were, you're alrwady too late. That ship sailed SIX years ago. Monty said this wssnt non-stop action. It's a story. The action was only part of it.<br /> <br /> I like being told stories. I hate all-poitless-fight works. Just imagine what if George Lucas made Star Wars nothing but endless lightsaber battles and laser blaster fights....<br /> <br /> Oh wait, that was Attack of the Clones","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T20:10:25-08:00","id":1165218,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'm not sure I see what people mean by tempo. If you zoom out and look at the big picture, the series has never had particularly consistent pacing<br /> <br /> The first two seasons were mostly introducing the characters and setting. Yes, there were a lot of flashy fight scenes, but very few major plot developments outside of character introductions. (Remember when Roman Torchwick was the main onscreen villain? Man, all that time spent on him sure paid off, didn't it?)<br /> <br /> The third season was a giant tournament arc with one really important plot development at the end of it.<br /> <br /> The fourth season mostly introduced how the setting and characters had changed as a result of that.<br /> <br /> The fifth season is bringing everyone back together and seems to be building up for one big plot-heavy episode at the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 12-04-2017, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T20:17:46-08:00","id":1165219,"title":"","content":"That said, I almost forgot. The thing that amused me most about Episode 7 was the part of Raven's story that really made Yang flip out when it was confirmed:<br /> <br /> OZPIN: Yes, Salem is real. There's an evil mastermind behind the Grimm, who cannot be stopped or reasoned with and will never yield until all of humanity is dead. I have known this, forever, constantly reincarnating and controlling every government in the world from behind the scenes through my loyalists. However, I've never told any of you about any of that, even as I asked you to constantly and repeatedly risk your lives to fight our enemies while lacking vital information about them, because reasons.<br /> <br /> YANG: Ok, that makes sense.<br /> <br /> OZPIN: Also I gave Qrow and Raven the ability to turn into birds.<br /> <br /> YANG: WHAT? Why would you do something like that? What is <i>wrong</i> with you?<br /> <br /> <br /> ...although, in retrospect...<br /> <br /> YANG: Please tell me it wasn't solely because of their nam--<br /> <br /> OZPIN: Naturally, I chose them because of their names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 12-04-2017, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T20:53:12-08:00","id":1165227,"title":"","content":"Yeah I though Yang's attitude on the bit about Qrow and Raven having that ability was weird. Her tone came off more as the tone one would use if Ozpin had just turned them into birds flat out and it was a fluke and luck that they were able to ever return to being human, not can change between forms.<br /> <br /> Though I did like the group interaction at the beginning of the episode; that was amusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T21:18:41-08:00","id":1165231,"title":"","content":"It struck me as especially weird since logically the bit with Salem would be vastly more alarming. I can guess why he keeps it a secret, but still, if people had known they might be targeted by human-intelligence enemies who were siding with the Grimm, Cinder's plan in Part 4 might have failed - and assuming Ozpin's goal is to prevent mass panic, it seems completely backwards, since Salem's goal is to <i>cause</i> mass panic and she can release all the information she wants whenever it is most convenient for her and most damaging to Ozpin. Logically he should be revealing everyone to as many people as possible - possibly slowly and carefully, planning it out to limit the panic that results, but he's had thousands of years and his plan seems to be &quot;lie to everyone, hide everything, hide Salem's existence because it would help her if people knew about her, hope Salem cooperates with this plan.&quot;<br /> <br /> From a meta reason I assume it's because the viewers already knew about Salem but didn't know about the bird thing, so it was more shocking and the writers wanted to make it the focus. But logically I would expect Yang or Juane to put 2 + 2 together and realize that Pyrrha died, in part, because she didn't have enough information and that Ozpin is therefore directly to blame for what happened. (ie. if she'd known <i>exactly</i> what the Maidens were and were capable of, known who they worked for, etc, things might have gone differently, and Ozpin doesn't really have a justification for keeping all these vital things a secret for so long.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T22:15:01-08:00","id":1165234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1165151#post1165151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firzt, it was aquote from the show. Which you might know if you watched it instead of bitching about it<br /> <br /> Second, you presume to speak for the entirety of the fandom. You dont. I for one like storytelling.<br /> <br /> And lastly, if you want the show to be nothing but action sequences, like the preview trailers were, you're alrwady too late. That ship sailed SIX years ago. Monty said this wssnt non-stop action. It's a story. The action was only part of it.<br /> <br /> I like being told stories. I hate all-poitless-fight works. Just imagine what if George Lucas made Star Wars nothing but endless lightsaber battles and laser blaster fights....<br /> <br /> Oh wait, that was Attack of the Clones</div> </div> </div> </div>You gotta permit for that Strawman there?<br /> <br /> First, I don't remember every quote. But you're right, instead of taking 10 minutes to type out what bothers me about an episode on a forum i visit I should instead rewatch the show over and over. That's normal.<br /> <br /> Second, Where the hell are you getting this &quot;Whole fandom&quot; thing from? seems like you're just inventing a grievance here.<br /> <br /> Third, I also never said I wanted nothing but action sequences. I have complained about how few action sequences there are in a show literally designed around action sequences. Again, you are inventing a complaint to justify being mad at me. But I guess it's good that you Like Stories? It must be rare enough to point out that you like being told stories.<br /> <br /> Also, what kind of fumble is this Star Wars parallel you are trying to draw here? Attack of the Clones is bad, so I must have bad taste for wanting more action in RWBY; do I have that right? How about I make a comparison to &lt;Excellent Action Property&gt; that has that &lt;Great Action Setpiece&gt; and the &lt;Meaningful Characterization Scenes&gt;. Is that how this works?<br /> <br /> Oh, and stop making shit up. It seems like you want me to be this villain who doesn't appreciate your beloved show for not being pandering drivel, when all of my posts contain numerous examples of RWBY not being competent with story missteps and poor design. I literally can't be the strawman you want me to be when the lion's share of my bitching is about how to correct the story.<br /> <br /> It's ok if people don't like a thing you like. Really, me complaining about RWBY is not an attack on you for liking it. I'm going to continue to voice my opinions on how bad RWBY is in this thread though, because like it or not I am <i>also</i> a fan, albeit one who wishes the show was better. That's part of being in a fandom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T22:22:44-08:00","id":1165235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1165219#post1165219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I almost forgot. The thing that amused me most about Episode 7 was the part of Raven's story that really made Yang flip out when it was confirmed:<br /> <br /> OZPIN: Yes, Salem is real. There's an evil mastermind behind the Grimm, who cannot be stopped or reasoned with and will never yield until all of humanity is dead. I have known this, forever, constantly reincarnating and controlling every government in the world from behind the scenes through my loyalists. However, I've never told any of you about any of that, even as I asked you to constantly and repeatedly risk your lives to fight our enemies while lacking vital information about them, because reasons.<br /> <br /> YANG: Ok, that makes sense.<br /> <br /> OZPIN: Also I gave Qrow and Raven the ability to turn into birds.<br /> <br /> YANG: WHAT? Why would you do something like that? What is <i>wrong</i> with you?<br /> <br /> <br /> ...although, in retrospect...<br /> <br /> YANG: Please tell me it wasn't solely because of their nam--<br /> <br /> OZPIN: Naturally, I chose them because of their names.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's almost funny how on the nose this is. The Bird Thing is set up like they had to kill a child to get the power or something, when its basically just Oz dicking around.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the world ending forces of evil have a sentientmalevolentunstoppablequeenandimactuallypup peteeringthehumanrace, but let's not dwell on that for no reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T00:43:09-08:00","id":1165252,"title":"","content":"Also, Yang made Ozpin promise to stop lying to them, and then... immediately changed the subject to what she could do for him?<br /> <br /> I expected them to ask like a million questions, starting with &quot;tell us EVERYTHING about Salem, who she is, why she wants what she does, why and how you fought her, what her powers and abilities and weaknesses are, etc.&quot; And also &quot;who are you and where did your powers come from originally?&quot; (His reincarnation is his semblance, meaning his magic is something else.) And &quot;why did you <i>really</i> create the Maidens? Why do they reincarnate in such a bizarre and exploitable way?&quot;<br /> <br /> Seriously, what's the point of making him promise to tell the truth if you're not going to push him for information?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T01:01:17-08:00","id":1165254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1165252#post1165252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Yang made Ozpin promise to stop lying to them, and then... immediately changed the subject to what she could do for him?<br /> <br /> I expected them to ask like a million questions, starting with &quot;tell us EVERYTHING about Salem, who she is, why she wants what she does, why and how you fought her, what her powers and abilities and weaknesses are, etc.&quot; And also &quot;who are you and where did your powers come from originally?&quot; (His reincarnation is his semblance, meaning his magic is something else.) And &quot;why did you <i>really</i> create the Maidens? Why do they reincarnate in such a bizarre and exploitable way?&quot;<br /> <br /> Seriously, what's the point of making him promise to tell the truth if you're not going to push him for information?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same reason they left Raven before learning anything actually valuable- it preserves the &quot;spooky mystery&quot; of the villains.<br /> Edit: /Doyalist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T01:03:02-08:00","id":1165256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1165218#post1165218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'm not sure I see what people mean by tempo. If you zoom out and look at the big picture, the series has never had particularly consistent pacing</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough. I've tried to separate what I mean by tempo with the idea of pacing. I actually think there's some decent pacing work in RWBY, particular taken over several sessions; when Pyrrha died, it was impactuful because they managed to build up her relationship with Jaune and the others, and it was a properly targic moment to see her sacrifice that. That's a properly done slow pacing, <br /> <br /> What I mean by tempo is how much I feel is happening from episode to episode and how much it excites me. At the start of volume 5, there were a few chapters that really felt packed with significant events. Now, it takes much more time for something like that to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T01:03:02-08:00","id":1165257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1165218#post1165218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'm not sure I see what people mean by tempo. If you zoom out and look at the big picture, the series has never had particularly consistent pacing</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough. I've tried to separate what I mean by tempo with the idea of pacing. I actually think there's some decent pacing work in RWBY, particular taken over several sessions; when Pyrrha died, it was impactuful because they managed to build up her relationship with Jaune and the others, and it was a properly targic moment to see her sacrifice that. That's a properly done slow pacing, <br /> <br /> What I mean by tempo is how much I feel is happening from episode to episode and how much it excites me. At the start of volume 5, there were a few chapters that really felt packed with significant events. Now, it takes much more time for something like that to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T06:16:15-08:00","id":1165282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1165219#post1165219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OZPIN: Yes, Salem is real. There's an evil mastermind behind the Grimm, who cannot be stopped or reasoned with and will never yield until all of humanity is dead. I have known this, forever,</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201c...and never had the proof to convince people she was real, because she always works through agents who would rather die than betray her, and I have never managed to find where exactly she hides. Every time I tried, I was eaten by Grimm.<br /> <br /> \u201cI probably became desperate enough to try telling people about her, once or twice, but it obviously didn\u2019t work, which is probably around the time I quit and became a hermit in despair.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> controlling every government in the world from behind the scenes through my loyalists. </div> </div> </div>\u201cThough the <i>only</i> government in which a school headmaster has any legal voice is Atlas, which explicitly deviates from the model I set down at the Vytal Accords. Ironwood also continues to run his school like a military recruitment academy, which is markedly different from how I choose to run Beacon. <br /> <br /> \u201cIronwood also disobeys me enough to bring entire aerial fleets and robot armies to my kingdom without even warning me beforehand, let alone asking my permission.<br /> <br /> \u201cVacuo doesn\u2019t even <i>have</i> a federal government anymore, and if Shade Academy tried acting like one, it would likely get burned to the ground as well.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd Lionheart can go for months of radio silence during a major crisis without worrying me enough to send Glynda to see what is going on.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo yes, clearly I wanted to control the world and not just keep the Maidens safe from murderers and the Relics safe from thieves by keeping a secret in the best way possible: Limiting the number of people who know the secret.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf I ever intended to use the Relics for myself, I would have used Creation to build impenetrable cities, Knowledge to learn where Salem is, Choice to make people believe she existed, and Destruction to defeat the Grimm. Obviously it is not that simple.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, I've never told any of you about any of that </div> </div> </div>\u201cBecause it was the responsibility of adults and not children, but none of them would believe me.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> even as I asked you to constantly and repeatedly risk your lives to fight our enemies while lacking vital information about them, because reasons. </div> </div> </div>He didn\u2019t ask Ruby to foil Torchwick\u2019s Dust heist.<br /> <br /> He didn\u2019t ask Blake and crew to stop the White Fang at the docks.<br /> <br /> He didn\u2019t ask them to investigate the White Fang or fight Torchwick and his Paladin.<br /> <br /> He didn\u2019t ask Ruby to try to stop Cinder at the CCT Tower during the dance.<br /> <br /> He didn\u2019t ask them to go Mountain Glenn. He saw they were going with or without permission, so he made sure they had a professional hunter as a leader, for their protection. If Bart hadn\u2019t gone along, things would have turned out much worse for Team RWBY and Vale. <br /> <br /> Ozpin didn\u2019t ask Team RNJR to go to Mistral. It was <i>Qrow</i> who dropped the hint of where Cinder fled, but it was Ruby who decided to go, and it was Team JN_R that decided to follow her. <br /> <br /> So the only person we ever saw Ozpin asking to help him with shadow war stuff was Pyrrha, and he wasn\u2019t even asking her to fight anyone personally.<br /> <br /> In fact, Ozpin expressed a number of times that he just wanted his students to enjoy being carefree kids for as long as possible. He encouraged Ruby to dance and let RWBY and JNPR get away with destructive food fights. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> YANG: Please tell me it wasn't solely because of their nam--<br /> <br /> OZPIN: Naturally, I chose them because of their names. </div> </div> </div>That is funny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-05-2017, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T07:24:47-08:00","id":1165299,"title":"","content":"And another thing: the only Grimm we have ever seen Salem actually control are the Seers. The tentacled crystal ball things.<br /> <br /> She couldn\u2019t control the Grimm at Vale, or else Cinder\u2019s terrorism wouldn\u2019t have been necessary to provoke the attack.<br /> <br /> She can\u2019t control the Grimm on Anima well enough to send any along with Tyrian when he hunted Ruby, or with Cinder to meet Raven and Vernal. <br /> <br /> Cinder apparently had to try hypnotizing the Dragon herself, and didn\u2019t seem pleased with her results given that she looked ready to blast it before Pyrrha interrupted. <br /> <br /> Salem clearly has some form of influence over the Grimm, but it should be just as clear that this influence falls far short of total control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T07:56:22-08:00","id":1165305,"title":"","content":"Concerning the &quot;name&quot; issue - I wonder if that actually facilitated the process in a practical sense, rather than just being suggestive or funny to Oz. Magic is often depicted as working on odd rules, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T09:18:07-08:00","id":1165330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But logically I would expect Yang or Juane to put 2 + 2 together and realize that Pyrrha died, in part, because she didn't have enough information and that Ozpin is therefore directly to blame for what happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, but I don't think that Jaune specifically wants to start a conversation about precisely who is responsible for what in those catacombs underneath Beacon.<br /> <br /> Jaune wouldn't like how that conversation went.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1165282#post1165282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201c...and never had the proof to convince people she was real, because she always works through agents who would rather die than betray her, and I have never managed to find where exactly she hides. Every time I tried, I was eaten by Grimm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, of course, for the cabal of important teachers, headmasters, politicians, agents, and (most likely) literal kings who he totally managed to convince she was real.<br /> <br /> The idea that Salem has always worked through agents who would rather die than betray her is dubious at best. Based on what we know about them, it seems very likely that both Merc and Emmy would give up the location of the Legion of Doom if sufficient pressure were applied to them. CINDER is a true believer. Her goons are not.<br /> <br /> We also don't know that Ozpin doesn't know where Salem hides. Or that Salem only hides in one place. Or that she's &quot;hiding&quot; at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cI probably became desperate enough to try telling people about her, once or twice, but it obviously didn\u2019t work, </div> </div> </div>Except for all of the kids in that room. And Amber. And Vernal. And Qrow. And Raven. And Glynda. And Jimmy Jims. And possibly Winter, by proxy, as the odds seem good that Jimmy brought her inside. And Leo. And whoever is Shade's headmaster. (I'm assuming some variation on the name Dorothy Gale.)<br /> <br /> Man, it's super fortunate that through all the eons of Ozpin's existence, the only people who would be convinced as to the existence of Salem and her accomplices are all alive now, when it is convenient for the story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cThough the <i>only</i> government in which a school headmaster has any legal voice is Atlas, </div> </div> </div>We don't know this, unless by &quot;legal voice&quot; you mean &quot;formal vote on the formal council.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cVacuo doesn\u2019t even <i>have</i> a federal government anymore, </div> </div> </div>Or this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cAnd Lionheart can go for months of radio silence during a major crisis without worrying me enough to send Glynda to see what is going on. </div> </div> </div>Part of the problem would seem to be that Oz didn't see what was going on vis-a-vis the Vytal Festival AS a major crisis.<br /> <br /> I mean, he didn't even haul in Leo or Shade and keep them briefed, or ask them to send a representative. Like... who was in charge of the Haven and Vacuo kids during the festival? Did NO teachers come with them? Presumably if Leo had gone silent, Oz could have asked whatever teacher was riding herd on the Haven kids coming to rep their kingdom and gone &quot;Hey, Leo isn't taking my calls. He's your boss; is he taking yours?&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't usually like to defend Jimmy Ironwood, who seems like he loves him some fascism, but deciding that Ozpin wasn't taking security seriously enough and showing up in person and with his battle fleet was precisely the right thing to do given the information he had at the time. Not having better IT security is perhaps criminally incompetent (we don't know if the Black Queen program was magic or not) but that's a separate issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cBecause it was the responsibility of adults and not children, but none of them would believe me.\u201d </div> </div> </div>Except for the enormous cadre who did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the only person we ever saw Ozpin asking to help him with shadow war stuff was Pyrrha, and he wasn\u2019t even asking her to fight anyone personally. </div> </div> </div>No, he was just asking her to put a giant target on her back that would be there for her entire life, while withholding incredibly vital information about precisely what that entailed. Not telling Pyrrha about Salem before asking her to sign up for Maidenhood was pretty disgusting on his part.<br /> <br /> This isn't technically asking her to personally fight anyone, but that's a very fine distinction. If I ask someone to cross a road, I'm technically not asking them to dodge traffic, but that sort of comes implied.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T09:39:53-08:00","id":1165341,"title":"","content":"As far as Salem's ability to control Grimm goes we haven't seen much obvious use of it. Remember season 2 had mention that Grimm get smarter as they get older and more powerful, so unless Grimm are seen acting severely ooc it would be hard to prove Salem can command any of them. The most common ones we've seen her control are Seers and since their most common function seems to be as a phone I kind of feel like those are not a natural outgrowth of Grimm evolution. <br /> <br /> As far as the name thing goes I kind of imagine that Ozpin listed the reasons why he made them into birds, faster travel*, better vision, and harder to detect. So the bird thing was probably just the plan and the pun was either a happy coincidence or just something that informed the kind of bird he made them into.<br /> <br /> *Technically Raven can move way faster, but since she can only move to specific people the bird form would allow for a more versatile way of getting around quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T10:02:05-08:00","id":1165345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1165341#post1165341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Technically Raven can move way faster, but since she can only move to specific people the bird form would allow for a more versatile way of getting around quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>... oh dang, I just realized something.<br /> <br /> Raven almost certainly has a portal bond to Vernal.<br /> <br /> Unless when she bailed on Qrow at Higanbana she went to Taiyang or Yang, but that seems unlikely.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T11:03:43-08:00","id":1165366,"title":"","content":"Thought just struck me: do we know what happened to Goodwitch? We've not seen her since Beacon, and I don't know that we heard what she's doing now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T11:16:34-08:00","id":1165369,"title":"","content":"I don't think we have. My assumption is that she's managing things in Beacon - even with the academy lost, there's presumably a bunch of survivors in the surrounding area that need to be cared for, surviving hunters and students need to be gathered and managed, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T11:32:00-08:00","id":1165376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1165366#post1165366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thought just struck me: do we know what happened to Goodwitch? We've not seen her since Beacon, and I don't know that we heard what she's doing now?</div> </div> </div> </div>We have. According to Port and Oobleck, in V4C4, Glynda is busy at work restoring Beacon. Pull quote: &quot;Professor Goodwitch is working 'round the clock to restore Beacon to its former glory.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's some debate as to what this actually means, as it makes it sound like they've retaken the academy proper, but that seems unlikely to be the case. More likely, they're attempting to put a positive spin on things in front of Yang; Tai changes the subject super fast when Port starts to talking about this.<br /> <br /> It seems likely that Glynda is point woman on whatever the plan is to drive the Grimm out of the campus and deal with the Wyvern.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T17:48:16-08:00","id":1165472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1165330#post1165330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except, of course, for the cabal of important teachers, headmasters, politicians, agents, and (most likely) literal kings who he totally managed to convince she was real.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which he probably <i>only </i>managed by revealing the magical stuff that he needed to reveal <i>to as few people as possible</i>.<br /> <br /> Sure, he could prove the existence of magic to the whole world in order to try and convince them about Salem, but then he has to deal with the whole world knowing about the Maidens and the Relics, when the best protection those girls and objects have is that people don't know about them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea that Salem has always worked through agents who would rather die than betray her is dubious at best. </div> </div> </div>I direct your attention to Torchwick, who very much kept his mouth shut when arrested, and who didn't dare trying to run away from Vale and Cinder before he was arrested because he feared that &quot;the people behind him&quot; would FIND him.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Based on what we know about them, it seems very likely that both Merc and Emmy would give up the location of the Legion of Doom if sufficient pressure were applied to them. </div> </div> </div>Which seems dubious given the aforementioned example of Torchwick.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We also don't know that Ozpin doesn't know where Salem hides. Or that Salem only hides in one place. Or that she's &quot;hiding&quot; at all. </div> </div> </div>If Ozpin knew, why would he keep it secret from his allies?<br /> <br /> If Ironwood knew, why didn't he fly over with his fleet of airships and hammer the place?<br /> <br /> In a World of Remnant episode, Qrow talks about the places of Remnant where no one comes back alive from exploring, and says &quot;somewhere&quot; out there is where Salem is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We don't know this, unless by &quot;legal voice&quot; you mean &quot;formal vote on the formal council.&quot; </div> </div> </div>We do know this. Weiss mentions how different Vale is from Atlas in that &quot;the school, the military, and the government are completely separate&quot;.<br /> <br /> Lionheart speaks about the council of Mistral as though he's NOT a part of that governing body.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or this. </div> </div> </div>So I take you skipped World of Remnant: Vacuo, where Qrow shows the people burning their federal government office to the ground.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Part of the problem would seem to be that Oz didn't see what was going on vis-a-vis the Vytal Festival AS a major crisis. </div> </div> </div>Maybe it seems that way to you, but you appear to see a lot of things that I don't think exist.<br /> <br /> Ozpin felt pressured enough about what was going on to ask Pyrrha to become the new Fall Maiden, which would better protect that power and also allow her to open the vault to the Relic of Choice, in case he needed to relocate it.<br /> <br /> Ozpin surely expected an attack of some sort; but without the audience's benefit of knowing who the culprits were, where they were, and what they were doing, he had no way of knowing WHEN or HOW they would attack. So he had no better option than to wait and watch, and respond to whatever fire his enemies started.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> withholding incredibly vital information about precisely what that entailed </div> </div> </div>She was standing over the breathing corpse of Amber! I'm pretty sure that was ample evidence about the threat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not telling Pyrrha about Salem before asking her to sign up for Maidenhood was pretty disgusting on his part. </div> </div> </div>You might have a point if Salem could sicc Grimm after her, but Salem has never displayed such an ability, or Ruby would be dead now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T18:11:58-08:00","id":1165479,"title":"","content":"Re- Pyrrha not being told about Salem: I had assumed that had Cinder not attacked, then Oz would have dumped all the info on Pyrrha after the two days thinking on it. It fits Ozpin's MO of trying to balance keeping the information need to know while still telling people when he can.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Cinder attacked. Everything was on fire. There was no time. They had to try the procedure.<br /> <br /> Basically, for all the judging people have done of Ozpin, I'd lay money that he's done far better in his situation, and been more upfront where he could afford to be, than 90% of the people on this forum would have been in the same circumstances.<br /> <br /> Be honest: How many of you would have waited to HEAR Pyrrha give her consent before starting the soul transfer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 12-05-2017, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T22:41:13-08:00","id":1165522,"title":"","content":"Let's be fair I think most of us would have waited till we at least got some acceptance from Pyrrha if only because you'd want as little resentment as you can manage on the part of a person you're about to give immense power to.<br /> <br /> Though I think at the moment the big issue with Ozpin keeping Salem a secret is that we haven't received as solid a reason for it as keeping the existence of the maidens quiet. Though a point occurs to me, why hasn't Salem revealed her existence to the world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T23:28:46-08:00","id":1165523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1165472#post1165472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which he probably <i>only </i>managed by revealing the magical stuff that he needed to reveal <i>to as few people as possible</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I direct your attention to Torchwick, who very much kept his mouth shut when arrested, and who didn't dare trying to run away from Vale and Cinder before he was arrested because he feared that &quot;the people behind him&quot; would FIND him. </div> </div> </div>Torchwick keeping his mouth shut because he knows he's going to be sprung eventually as part of phase three's contingency plans is equally as likely. Roman Torchwick may, in fact, not even know about Salem.<br /> <br /> And Torchwick is just one guy. You trotted out &quot;always.&quot; Salem ALWAYS works through agents who would rather die than betray her. This is a bold claim to deploy as a statement of fact given the immense amount of time Salem has been operating and the vagaries of human nature. Torchwick, for example, has heavily implied that his primary goal is survival. If this is true, that likewise implies that given the choice between immediate survival and betraying Salem, he would one hundred percent betray Salem, because Salem only might succeed at killing him as opposed to imminent far-more-certain death.<br /> <br /> And that's before you even get into people further down the chain. I would submit it is HIGHLY likely that Emerald's loyalty is to Cinder, not Salem. We haven't gotten inside Merc's head that much, but Merc doesn't seem like the kind of guy who'd die to keep Salem's secrets, or even Cinder's, really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Ozpin knew, why would he keep it secret from his allies? </div> </div> </div>We don't know that he has, and we also don't know what reasoning he might have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Ironwood knew, why didn't he fly over with his fleet of airships and hammer the place? </div> </div> </div>The possibility exists that Salem commands sufficient might to stand off anything less than a full-scale military assault by an entire kingdom, or even something more, and that if such an assault were tried she'd simply scurry into a hole and emerge somewhere else, thus making such an assault useless.<br /> <br /> Or that Salem has multiple bases of operation she moves between, and that the Ozluminati have a pretty good idea where they are but not whether Salem is in residence at any given time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In a World of Remnant episode, Qrow talks about the places of Remnant where no one comes back alive from exploring, and says &quot;somewhere&quot; out there is where Salem is. </div> </div> </div>Which is in no way dispositive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We do know this. Weiss mentions how different Vale is from Atlas in that &quot;the school, the military, and the government are completely separate&quot;.<br /> <br /> Lionheart speaks about the council of Mistral as though he's NOT a part of that governing body. </div> </div> </div>There are many different ways to have a legal voice without being part of one specific governing body. If you mean <i>specifically</i> that the other three schools don't have a formal vote on the council in the person of their headmaster, yes, we do know that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I take you skipped World of Remnant: Vacuo, where Qrow shows the people burning their federal government office to the ground. </div> </div> </div>First of all, it shows no such thing. It does show the building cracking apart in a stylized explosion, but there are no people present.<br /> <br /> Second of all, the Worlds of Remnant often use stylized animation that is not actually meant to be taken literally. It is entirely possible that Vacuo is a lawless Somalia, with order maintained only by whatever the Hunters of Shade Academy can enforce and whatever local governments and warlords can enforce through strength of arms. Sure. This is possible.<br /> <br /> It's also possible that when Qrow says &quot;people didn't much care to uphold it's laws&quot; he didn't mean that Vacuo literally did not have a government, merely that it was weak and had a lot of trouble being the only legitimate source of violence in the Kingdom (the sine qua non of a government) and so Shade has to do a lot of that heavy lifting.<br /> <br /> This seems much more likely to me than Vacuo being a failed state.<br /> <br /> (Honestly, World of Remnant: Vacuo was just sort of baffling to me. &quot;If you can survive here, you're welcome here.&quot; Bull <i>shit</i>. &quot;Surviving&quot; someplace without order being provided in at least a semi-legitimate way means having to deal with people who want to knock you down and take your shit, which isn't what I'd call &quot;welcoming.&quot; It seems like they want to have Vacuo be this rough-and-tumble place, but not TOO rough-and-tumble, and they haven't thought through the tensions and unanswered questions in what they've represented.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe it seems that way to you, but you appear to see a lot of things that I don't think exist. </div> </div> </div>No, I express potentialities as <i>being</i> potentialities. You state as <i>facts</i> things that you have trouble backing up <i>as</i> facts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ozpin felt pressured enough about what was going on to ask Pyrrha to become the new Fall Maiden, which would better protect that power and also allow her to open the vault to the Relic of Choice, in case he needed to relocate it. </div> </div> </div>Which would have worked out <i>great</i> against the terrorist army and the super-Grimm that descended on his school, an eventuality that Ironwood seems to have prepared for by bringing a counterforce.<br /> <br /> (Although one wonders what the fuck Vale's <i>actual</i> army and fleet were up to. Remnant is a dangerous world, where survival depends on humanity having a firm base in their walled citadel kingdoms. You'd think Vale would have a significant military presence in, you know, their <i>capital</i> all the time. Maybe they rely too much on Hunters.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ozpin surely expected an attack of some sort; but without the audience's benefit of knowing who the culprits were, where they were, and what they were doing, he had no way of knowing WHEN or HOW they would attack. So he had no better option than to wait and watch, and respond to whatever fire his enemies started. </div> </div> </div>Ironwood knew just as much as Oz did, if not less, and he was smart enough to perceive that an army might be required and he exercised his option to produce that army.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She was standing over the breathing corpse of Amber! I'm pretty sure that was ample evidence about the threat. </div> </div> </div>Please to be explaining to me how Amber's presence is ample evidence as to the fact that the Grimm have an ancient god-queen who has some rather sinister desires vis-a-vis the Maidens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You might have a point if Salem could sicc Grimm after her, but Salem has never displayed such an ability, or Ruby would be dead now. </div> </div> </div>You. Don't. Know. This.<br /> <br /> You continually state as <i>facts</i> things that you cannot possibly <i>know. </i><br /> <br /> It is entirely <i>possible</i> that Salem can't just sic Grimm on people, although I would say it's clear she has some manner of command and control over them that can be meaningfully exercised even at a distance. (She refers to &quot;our forces&quot; with respect to the Grimm occupying Beacon, and wants those forces increased.)<br /> <br /> It's <i>also</i> possible she <i>absolutely</i> has the power to sic Grimm on people, but that this power comes with certain limitations that make deploying a hit squad of them problematic. It might be like deploying a bunch of Blood Apes as a hit squad; they'll do their best, but their nature limits them.<br /> <br /> That aside... Salem has resources that aren't Grimm. And even if she didn't, becoming a Maiden apparently puts an immense Salem-related target on your back. Not explaining, in as much detail as you are capable, the precise nature of the threat the person you are asking to take on that mantle on is facing is, in my opinion, not cool. It's rather monstrous, in fact. You're asking a young woman, a girl really, to shoulder an enormous burden she cannot put back down without dying. Basic ethics demand full, complete, and unvarnished disclosure on your part when you do that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T09:26:43-08:00","id":1165593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1165523#post1165523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That aside... Salem has resources that aren't Grimm. And even if she didn't, becoming a Maiden apparently puts an immense Salem-related target on your back. Not explaining, in as much detail as you are capable, the precise nature of the threat the person you are asking to take on that mantle on is facing is, in my opinion, not cool. It's rather monstrous, in fact. You're asking a young woman, a girl really, to shoulder an enormous burden she cannot put back down without dying. Basic ethics demand full, complete, and unvarnished disclosure on your part when you do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured that Ozpin didn't reveal Salem to Pyrrha right away because he believed dumping that magic is real and the story of the Maidens on her was shocking enough. Dumping the stuff about Salem and the Shadow War and that Ozpin was the Immortal on top of that could have been overwhelming. While he <i>suspected </i>that Salem was moving, he didn't know that Cinder was going to strike before the end of the tournament.<br /> <br /> That's why I'm so adamant that I believe it would have gone like this, had Cinder not attacked:<br /> <br /> Pyrrha: I've made my choice. I'll do it.<br /> <br /> Ozpin: I'm glad to hear it. Now, before you do it, I'll need to tell you whom you'll be fighting. You see-<br /> <br /> However, Ozpin didn't have a chance to do that. Because Cinder <i>did</i> attack before the end of the tournament. The Grimm were invading, the Atlas robots were attacking indiscriminately, the Fang were gunning people down... And Amber was going to be found. Soon.<br /> <br /> <i>There was no time</i> to sit Pyrrha down and explain everything about Salem. And to use a line I used on another forum... &quot;Sometimes you don't have the option of a <i>good</i> plan. Sometimes in a shitty situation, all you have is a desperate gamble&quot;.<br /> <br /> I've no doubt that Ozpin would have informed Pyrrha had things not gone to shit, BEFORE starting the transfer, and given her one last chance to walk away and live a normal life.<br /> <br /> Because you <i>are</i> right in that it's not something that Pyrrha should have had to bear. It's not something that they should have had to do. Pyrrha SHOULD have just been a student enjoying her time at school while training to become a warrior to protect people, without having to take on this greater responsibility. I'm sure if you asked, Ozpin would have said the same thing.<br /> <br /> It's just that Salem doesn't give a shit about how things <i>should</i> be.<br /> <br /> Edit: And another thing, to address the comment of &quot;Ozpin isn't telling the students-&quot;<br /> <br /> ... Do they NEED to know more about Grimm if they're not going to take direct action against Salem? Like... It's not like say, hiding that Grimm will just respawn later if you don't kill it with a silver weapon, and thus no actual progress is made unless you have a silver knife on you, and only Ozpin's favorite students are given silver knives. Like, Team CFVY still kill Grimm. By the bucketloads. And each Grimm dead is one Grimm fewer to eat people.<br /> <br /> They don't need to know about Salem to know &quot;Grimm Bad, kill them&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 12-06-2017, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T13:51:02-08:00","id":1165663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1165523#post1165523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which would have worked out <i>great</i> against the terrorist army and the super-Grimm that descended on his school, an eventuality that Ironwood seems to have prepared for by bringing a counterforce.<br /> <br /> (Although one wonders what the fuck Vale's <i>actual</i> army and fleet were up to. Remnant is a dangerous world, where survival depends on humanity having a firm base in their walled citadel kingdoms. You'd think Vale would have a significant military presence in, you know, their <i>capital</i> all the time. Maybe they rely too much on Hunters.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ironwood knew just as much as Oz did, if not less, and he was smart enough to perceive that an army might be required and he exercised his option to produce that army.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There has been more than a few indications (mainly that Vale defense forces are <u>never</u> mentioned, not even in passing) that Vale in all actuality doesn't have an army or navy. Seriously. Apparently, they depend on Hunters. Which is amusing, because the fall of Vale just proves that the Hunter system doesn't work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T15:44:04-08:00","id":1165688,"title":"","content":"Vale City most likely has a militia. Which was most likely stationed at the country borders, to keep the Grimm out.<br /> <br /> Problems inside the city would be civil matters for the police.<br /> <br /> The system worked. It took a major campaign of terror to cause trouble, and the White Fang airmailed Grimm inside the city, and the robots and air ships were turned against their masters.<br /> <br /> It was an amazing push against the city that failed to kill the city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T17:02:57-08:00","id":1165707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1165663#post1165663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There has been more than a few indications (mainly that Vale defense forces are <u>never</u> mentioned, not even in passing) that Vale in all actuality doesn't have an army or navy. Seriously. Apparently, they depend on Hunters. Which is amusing, because the fall of Vale just proves that the Hunter system doesn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The system that worked Damn well for like 80 years finally had a hiccup after an in-depth infiltration plot. Clearly we need to throw the whole system out rather than refine it to adjust for this newly-revealed shortcoming&quot;<br /> <br /> Though, exageration for the sake of humor aside, perhaps Vale could do more in the future to encourage kids to become cops, or militia, in addition to Huntsmen and Huntresses.<br /> <br /> Or at least open up Huntsmen and Huntresses that work long-term with the cops. Because it seemed until the Vytal Sabotage attracted approximately ALL OF THE GRIMM, Vale's geographic defenses and it's weaponry worked well until they got overwhelmed by sheer numbers.<br /> <br /> Remember, Sun was shocked that the Gryphon and the Nevermore made it past the defenses in V3. I figure that Vale's defenses normally work for what they have to face 99.99% of the time.<br /> <br /> It's easy to forget that just because we saw an instance where Salem's forces managed to win, that this was after 80 years of growth and prosperity after a debilitating war... And MUCH longer after the pushback started by the discovery of Dust. Remember the V1 intro monologue, where Salem was musing that humans were almost stomped out by the Grimm before Dust was utilized.<br /> <br /> So saying it doesn't work may be jumping the gun somewhat","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T17:27:49-08:00","id":1165708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1165688#post1165688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vale City most likely has a militia. Which was most likely stationed at the country borders, to keep the Grimm out.<br /> <br /> Problems inside the city would be civil matters for the police.<br /> <br /> The system worked. It took a major campaign of terror to cause trouble, and the White Fang airmailed Grimm inside the city, and the robots and air ships were turned against their masters.<br /> <br /> It was an amazing push against the city that failed to kill the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have any proof, or is this just conjecture?<br /> <br /> The system <u>didn't</u> work. It took three, <u>three</u> events to take out one of the bastions of humanity on Remnant, two of which would have been prevented entirely by some basic IT and operational security.<br /> <br /> 1) Why were the rail lines from Mountain Glenn not destroyed when the settlement was abandoned? There was at least one subterranean rail line, <u>open to the Grimm,</u> that ran entirely unimpeded under Vale City.<br /> <br /> 1a) There was no, absolutely none zip zilch nada mention of any sort of Vale Milita when the Breach occured. Not even a 'Gee, I wish the militia was here, not on the borders of the Kingdom!' Why is that? An <u>intelligently designed</u> force has a little something called a 'strategic reserve&quot;, aka forces held back to plug holes in the defensive line.<br /> <br /> 1b) Why was there no mention of Vale's sovereignty when Atlas effectively invaded it? You would think <u>somebody</u> would complain, considering how in the current cast's grandparents time, Atlas's parent-nation was almost literally the Third Reich. Now they are seemingly up to their old tricks.<br /> <br /> 1c) Why doesn't Atlas, the most advanced kingdom on Remnant, have mounted/motor infantry for patrolling? Why are their infantry so undisciplined as to be basically watching TV on patrol? Why doesn't their infantry have heavy support weapons? Why do none of their airships have point-defense systems? Why can a frigate be piloted by a single man? Why didn't Ironwood use Mountain Glenn as a base?<br /> <br /> 2) Why wasn't the CCT actually protected? Why weren't Hunters kept on contract to protect the single most vital piece of intercontinental communications in the world? Why do random-ass people have access to the building at night, much less the actual guts of the system? Why does a random-ass public-access computer in the public areas of the facility have access to the workings of the system? Why weren't there backups for the backups for the backups, just in case?<br /> <br /> The US and the UK have undersea telegraph cables, <u>specifically</u> in case something knocks out satellite communications and phone lines. The US and Canada have multiple redundant lines of communication, including literal couriers on bikes, in order to facilitate communications in case of emergency.<br /> <br /> 2a) After Ruby tells the leading people of the world that she saw someone messing with the Valen CCT facility, after said person killed the guards...... why didn't the CCT get taken down and gone through with the finest of fine-toothed combs?<br /> <br /> There are many, many other issues with RWBY, I am just too exhausted to debate them. Does this mean I don't like RWBY? Of course not, I just recognize its flaws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","user":"Boston123","date":". 12-06-2017, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T17:39:37-08:00","id":1165713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1165707#post1165707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, exageration for the sake of humor aside, perhaps Vale could do more in the future to encourage kids to become cops, or militia, in addition to Huntsmen and Huntresses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate to admit it, but I think the Atlesians have the right idea here.<br /> <br /> Atlas appears to have a special group of Hunters (the, er, specialists) who operate within their armed forces as a force multiplier. This strikes me as a highly sensible move rather than relying on, as an old webcomic once put it, the &quot;unique super-powered freak model of warfare.&quot;<br /> <br /> To put it another way; Winter Schnee is a colossal badass. But Winter Schnee trained to operate in concert with conventional military forces in a synergistic way probably is an even huger badass and both she and the conventional forces are likely many times more effective than either would be separately, or even trying to cooperate together in an ad-hoc, unprepared way.<br /> <br /> If it were up to me, I would adopt this model, but also keep the freelance Hunters around in order to allow an outlet for people who are skilled and dedicated Hunters, but do not fit will into a military hierarchy (Qrow, probably Yang) to still contribute.<br /> <br /> Really, Remnant is such a dangerous place to any concentration of humanity that the kingdoms really ought to be more militarized than they're shown to be, even given the recent trauma of the Great War. I'm not talking the full Cadia here, but these guys are really willing to tolerate a lot of vulnerability. Grimm can manifest inside even relatively tame safe zones, like Patch... and people let their kids go on walks in the woods unsupervised?<br /> <br /> (The Patch thing made me legitimately wonder if its possible for Grimm to manifest INSIDE cities. The cities clearly have areas of urban blight, or at least Mistral does; can Grimm manifest inside city walls? Do they require those spawning pools, or can they literally coalesce out of the air? How does a spawning pool form? Lots of unanswered questions.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T18:59:25-08:00","id":1165730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1165713#post1165713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hate to admit it, but I think the Atlesians have the right idea here.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why Ironwood's forces utterly repelled all the Grimm and saved Vale-<br /> <br /> wait.<br /> <br /> Though to be fair, that was more 'don't assign 80% of your troop power to robots that are one hijacked system away from being compromised'. Maybe taking some inspiration from one-another will work better.<br /> <br /> Edit: Semi-related. Either Atlas makes those Paladins really simple to operate, or Torchwick had Atlas military training and the Pales in controls are similar enough to other Atlas hardware that he could manage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 12-06-2017, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T00:06:20-08:00","id":1165787,"title":"","content":"I genuinely enjoyed the latest episode. It had meaningful conflict, and some action! Also, Papa Belladonna is basically a Strongman Power Wrestler. <i>Swoon</i>.<br /> <br /> Also, Ghira isn't a color. Blake and Kali are both colors, so theire kinda cheating with Belladonna being a plant. Unless Gman was born before the &quot;Color Naming Schema&quot; trend took off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 12-07-2017, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T05:40:00-08:00","id":1165838,"title":"","content":"The rule is that a name has to evoke a color. Arslan\u2019s name means \u201clion\u201d which evokes the tawny yellow hide and brown mane of lions.<br /> <br /> Ghira at the very least might evoke Bagheera, the black jaguar (panther) of the Jungle Book. And that\u2019s assuming his name doesn\u2019t mean something in a language I don\u2019t know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T10:42:30-08:00","id":1165896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1165838#post1165838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rule is that a name has to evoke a color. Arslan\u2019s name means \u201clion\u201d which evokes the tawny yellow hide and brown mane of lions.<br /> <br /> Ghira at the very least might evoke Bagheera, the black jaguar (panther) of the Jungle Book. And that\u2019s assuming his name doesn\u2019t mean something in a language I don\u2019t know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing the color thing is more of Arslan's last name apparently &quot;Atlan&quot; means &quot;golden&quot; in Mongolian and &quot;Red Dawn&quot; in Turkic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T08:20:39-08:00","id":1166284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1165838#post1165838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghira at the very least might evoke Bagheera, the black jaguar (panther) of the Jungle Book. And that\u2019s assuming his name doesn\u2019t mean something in a language I don\u2019t know.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Bagheera <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">is literally Hindi/Urdu for &quot;black panther&quot;, putting him in the same category as Arslan and the Branwen twins in that his association with a colour is through an animal's.<br /> <br /> Edit:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1165366#post1165366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thought just struck me: do we know what happened to Goodwitch? We've not seen her since Beacon, and I don't know that we heard what she's doing now?</div> </div> </div> </div>We probably won't be seeing her again, as her voice actress and Rooster Teeth has had a falling out recently. &quot;Busy fixing Beacon&quot; is likely all we'll hear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12013,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12013-artex","user":"artex","date":". 12-09-2017, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12013-artex","name":"artex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12013_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T11:04:54-08:00",