 is literally Hindi/Urdu for &quot;black panther&quot;, putting him in the same category as Arslan and the Branwen twins in that his association with a colour is through an animal's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bagh is Hindi for &quot;Tiger&quot;. Black Panther is &quot;Kaala Cheeta&quot;. As for Urdu, none of the words I could think of (Black, Panther, Leopard, Black Panther) come out anywhere <i>near</i> Bagheera. So no, it literally isn't.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1047_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1047\" data-vbnamecard=\"1047\">vampire hunter D</a> , this is what we're doing now? RWBY slashfic comics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T00:17:08-08:00","id":1166645,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's what happens when I browse image galleries while drunk","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T01:19:04-08:00","id":1166657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1166645#post1166645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's what happens when I browse image galleries while drunk</div> </div> </div> </div>We'e all been there bud. We've all been there. *bro hug*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T02:38:58-08:00","id":1167551,"title":"","content":"Solid mediocrity. There just isn't much worth diving into in this episode.<br /> <br /> Raven's line's are written by a 15 year old trying to make Intimidate checks with his DnD character.<br /> Mustache McMenace has the character trait of... i guess being a person. He has a stock line about motives that is read flat and without <i>any</i> nuance or personality, devoid even of stoicism (which is almost impressive). Is his VA somebody's boyfriend or the cleaning guy?<br /> Mercury and Emerald exist.<br /> Vehr-nahl has a kind of punk aesthetic but she talks to people like they're her new step-dad. Seriously what even is her character other than &quot;a girl who has a power&quot;.<br /> Unnecessary cut to Qrow and Oscar to justify raven/crow bird scene transition. <br /> Arguably the worst choreography so far with Gheera. I was almost excited that he had a sense of &quot;weight&quot; to his movements which would have made him stand out from the rest of the cast but no dice.<br /> Sun reminded me of low production value cartoons from developing countries. what is that spin, and the way his head moves.<br /> Jackal Brothers just kind of sit around waiting to be not helpless and no one attacks them while they are defenseless.<br /> Blake didn't attack them from stealth for no reason, even though as a huntress she could probably have crippled one right off the bat.<br /> Gheera just kinda lets an obvious attack hit him without dodging for no reason<br /> <i>of course</i> the spear didn't hit, but did the &quot;cloak pin&quot; to the wall.<br /> Seriously that room is like 20 feet across how did you miss that bad.<br /> Fireball-Spear tracking shot was cool. That's was nice.<br /> Is Ilia just hanging around in her assassination mission hoping for this fight? I almost buy that, but it could have been communicated better.<br /> The Cinder and Raven meet was like a bad LARP session- everyone acts like they're the super special badass.<br /> It's funny that Team Evil still acts like Ruby is Ms Kryptonite. She pulled out a super move one time and barely survived an assassination attempt by Scorpion Dude because of Qrow.<br /> If it wasn't blisteringly obvious that Team Raven and Team Evil were going to have to betray each other, they had to include a message that they will Obviously Betray Each Other.<br /> That didn't even need clever writing. We all saw that coming.<br /> <br /> Ok, crazy idea here: we hire a screenwriter to eliminate the bloat and posturing, and we use the 5+ minutes saved there to show Emerald fighting some of Raven's goons. And then we spend a minute or two on an actual battle at House Belladonna.<br /> <br /> Alternate idea: RT gets an actual editor.<br /> <br /> Third idea: RT bribes a few film students and Lit. majors with swag and an NDA to look over the product at the story board/ script stage.<br /> <br /> Is the next episode the last? the pen-ultimate? What are we building up for here. White Fang attacks, people fight, gang is reunited. Plot thing happens to move season 6. Season 4 and 5 have been a serious drag. Even if the next 2 episodes are solid action it still wont make up for how bad the season has been until now.<br /> <br /> We know what has to happen now. Summer and Winter maiden revealed, Relics revealed. Relics go to Mt Doom and cause The End Of The World. Ruby activates Protagonist Plot Power. THe day is saved. Roll spinoff.<br /> <br /> The world building has been terrible this season, there's 2ish fights, the dialogue outside of RNJRWY is terrible. nothing has paid off and the stakes haven't been raised since the end of season 3. We still have no idea what magic is other than Fire Burns and Winds Blow and People Can Into Birds.<br /> <br /> 3/10 wait for a fan recut on youtube that cuts Season 4+5 into an hour long video.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T03:46:00-08:00","id":1167560,"title":"","content":"Ok, you hate the show and everything about it. We get that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T10:51:12-08:00","id":1167705,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m still having fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T13:03:35-08:00","id":1167755,"title":"","content":"You don't have to hate the show to see the problems. The show has never been amazing in meshing exposition, action and character building, but it's been passable with good and even great moments in each category. But season 4 and now 5 are seriously dragging their feet.<br /> <br /> And what's really weird is that I think the RWBY crew knows their short comings. They certainly use them for comedy fodder on RWBY Chibi a lot (eg Cinder was a lot more fun when she was W. E. Coyotying).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T00:13:15-08:00","id":1167845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1167551#post1167551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's funny that Team Evil still acts like Ruby is Ms Kryptonite. She pulled out a super move one time and barely survived an assassination attempt by Scorpion Dude because of Qrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>That wasn't really my reading of that scene. Doctor Watts doesn't see Ruby as important or particularly dangerous, he's just worried that Cinder is going to screw things up by focusing on Ruby to the exclusion of their mission - which is a serious danger when their mission depends on speed and stealth. Blowing their cover too early or wasting time fighting Ruby and co. could result in them having to fight literally an entire academy worth of hunters (or at least whatever part can rush back in time.)<br /> <br /> He doesn't even want to waste time fighting Qrow, who they legitimately need to get out of the picture and who is one of the main people running the opposition to them. Obviously he's going to be annoyed that Cinder is obsessed with wasting time and resources on an enemy who barely even pings his radar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 12-15-2017, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T00:19:18-08:00","id":1167846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1167560#post1167560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, you hate the show and everything about it. We get that.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet in each episode I find an entirely new way to hate it. There's a lot of media I just plain don't like, and so I don't care to watch and find faults with. RWBY is different- I was a HUGE fan of season's 1-3, and then RT has been changing RWBY into something it's not and they <i>absolutely suck at the transition</i>. RWBY wants to Be A Real Show and Eat Its Cake too- the episodes are blocked around dialogue and exposition heavy scenes that explain character motivation and world building, but the team just does not have the writing chops to pull that off, I'm sorry. I'm hella sorry, actually, <i><b>because I really want to really like RWBY</b></i>. I'm doing everything I can here to point out where the show can be fixed, even though there's next to no chance anyone at RT will see this. I want to foster discussion about the sticking points I have. I want things to be better.<br /> <br /> Tell me, D, with a straight face that you think the pacing and plot of Season 4 and 5 were as good as 1-3.<br /> <br /> Lemme throw some stuff at the wall- Season 1 had the intro fight, the beacon intro, the forest fights (action and character building together in one scene? using choreography to reveal inter-personal development? Sorcery!) Meaningful School Drama (Jaune!), The Reckoning of Cardin, and the Climatic Finisher. <b>9 &quot;Fights&quot;</b> if you count smaller setpieces as .5 of a fight.<br /> <br /> Season 5 has... Get to Haven (no city intro), Villain Filler, The Bee fight, Bandit Brawl, Raven Filler, The Reunion (Nice!), Raven AND Villain Filler. The seasons not done yet, but we have <b>2.5 fights</b> (i'm counting Bee as 1, Yang Brawl gets a .5, and the collective White Fang should be a .5 but I'll round up to 1).<br /> <br /> Can you see where I'm coming from? S1 RWBY used cool action set pieces to anchor the plot around. S5 RWBY has <i>no idea</i> how it wants to spend its time and the greater focus on world building is not met with a greater focus on good writing.<br /> <br /> You know, all said and done I <b>really</b> look forward to your replies <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1047_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1047\" data-vbnamecard=\"1047\">vampire hunter D</a> , because you're the only person here who doesn't just say &quot;yeah, basically&quot;. I like debating with you. I want a debate. What do you see in S5 that I don't? Let us continue to nerd battle in the spirit of Jolly Co-operation! (just no more slashfic stuff, ok?) ((unless like it's SUPER hot))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T00:22:34-08:00","id":1167847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1167845#post1167845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That wasn't really my reading of that scene. Doctor Watts doesn't see Ruby as important or particularly dangerous, he's just worried that Cinder is going to screw things up by focusing on Ruby to the exclusion of their mission - which is a serious danger when their mission depends on speed and stealth. Blowing their cover too early or wasting time fighting Ruby and co. could result in them having to fight literally an entire academy worth of hunters (or at least whatever part can rush back in time.)<br /> <br /> He doesn't even want to waste time fighting Qrow, who they legitimately need to get out of the picture and who is one of the main people running the opposition to them. Obviously he's going to be annoyed that Cinder is obsessed with wasting time and resources on an enemy who barely even pings his radar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ninja'd.<br /> <br /> That's fair, but i read the air in that scene as Mercury and Emerald suddenly worried about Cinder's reaction, and that Ruby was this dangerous topic on team evil. LIke plans must be built around the &quot;Ruby Factor&quot; while Qrow is brushed off despite being 10x the monkey wrench she is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T03:17:35-08:00","id":1167856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1167846#post1167846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, all said and done I <b>really</b> look forward to your replies <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1047_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1047\" data-vbnamecard=\"1047\">vampire hunter D</a> , because you're the only person here who doesn't just say &quot;yeah, basically&quot;. I like debating with you. I want a debate. What do you see in S5 that I don't? Let us continue to nerd battle in the spirit of Jolly Co-operation! (just no more slashfic stuff, ok?) ((unless like it's SUPER hot))</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't count the bubble for the whole. Complaining's a lot easier than complimenting. The thread's still getting a lot of reads, and you can't tell they're all agreeing with you, especially not on the scale you write.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T08:35:44-08:00","id":1167924,"title":"","content":"To be fair the silver eye thing seems to be something important and known to be a dangerous obstacle. (See Cinder apparently losing an eye and the dragon being taken out of play when Ruby lost it after Pyrrha died.) So it could also be a matter that Ruby is a problem based around Cinder's potential to tunnel vision and the silver eye thing making Ruby a larger potential threat with it being unknown precisely how dangerous she is at the moment. IE Qrow is the bigger threat, but he's also the threat that is most understood, whereas Ruby might represent too many unknown variables for the plan.<br /> <br /> You know kind of like if an unknown exalt type showed up fighting for the Bull of the North.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T12:05:32-08:00","id":1167986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1167551#post1167551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the next episode the last? the pen-ultimate? What are we building up for here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Five more.<br /> <br /> This season is 14, not 12. It's actually going to be their longest season.<br /> <br /> Shame so little has happened, although they've been moving at a brisker clip since Weiss and Yang made it to the others.<br /> <br /> The frustrating thing is that Miles Luna actually does know how to write and pace. Red vs. Blue is proof of that. But the last two season of RWBY have been... rough.<br /> <br /> It's not even that there aren't a lot of fights anymore, it's that they cut the fights and didn't replace them with much. And frankly the way the characters are moving doesn't make the action they do have look all that amazing.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna be super fuckin' blunt: whatever you think about the veracity of his open letter or not, firing Shane Newville and associated animation personnel was, I think, a HUGE mistake. And moving to Maya might have been a smart move in theory but might not have worked out in practice; they hired a lot of people who had experience with Maya, which is great, but those people apparently don't have experience rendering cool-ass action sequences in Maya with a heavy influence on mo-cap and a lot of high mobility character models. In which case, maybe you should have re-trained them on Poser.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T13:42:07-08:00","id":1168014,"title":"","content":"They may have a better overall animation team now, with the new tools and people, but I'm not sure the new staff were told what they're supposed to be doing well enough.<br /> <br /> Up to volume 3, the show was bursting with oddball characters, each with their own ridiculous weapon and fighting style (possibly even overstuffed with them). And the fights were immensely focused on impact and recoil. It got goofy at times (a trumpet guy who clones himself?) but it was always something different.<br /> <br /> That changed with volume 4. We've barely had new fighting characters introduced, and the fights we did have lost the impact and recoil focus that defined so many of the weapons and styles Oum created. Fighting moves became samey-er across characters and no fights make good use of the manifold distinct weapons anymore.<br /> Just take the latest example, the Jackal Brothers: They were (so far) as much of a snore fest in a fight as they were while spouting villain one-liners at each other. They barely moved during their brief action scene and their weapons were point and shoot 'wand-gun-things' that didn't require them to move. What exactly distinguishes them in a fight from their gun toting white fang goons?<br /> We may yet find out (unless next episode postpones that fight again), or we may not (if next episode starts having skipped over that fight, as with Emerald and the guards).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T18:22:21-08:00","id":1168285,"title":"","content":"So that new episode was good, I think. I liked it, at least the Menagerie part. The Jackal brothers showed some actual personality, the fights included attempts to merge them with character development, and a big helping of potential character drama is being prepared for the Yang-Blake reunion. I'm actually getting psyched for the rest of the season again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T06:00:04-08:00","id":1168510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1167986#post1167986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna be super fuckin' blunt: whatever you think about the veracity of his open letter or not, firing Shane Newville and associated animation personnel was, I think, a HUGE mistake. And moving to Maya might have been a smart move in theory but might not have worked out in practice; they hired a lot of people who had experience with Maya, which is great, but those people apparently don't have experience rendering cool-ass action sequences in Maya with a heavy influence on mo-cap and a lot of high mobility character models. In which case, maybe you should have re-trained them on Poser.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. From the letter it sounds like Shane was a nightmare to work with, and was deliberately not trying to play nice with the others.<br /> <br /> At some point skill and talent can't make up for being impossible to work with. Also, I wholeheartedly disagree with the 'train the new guys with Poser'. Poser is not meant to do what RT made it do. It would have been better to take choreographers and get them up to date on Maya, which IS better for animation.<br /> <br /> Have you looked at the non-fight animation in V1-3? It's really kind of awkward. Like &quot;only a few steps above Food Fight&quot; awkward. I saw someone on another forum note that it's not an animation skill problem. The new animation team is fine. What's more of a loss with Monty passing is choreography.<br /> <br /> Edit: I should probably say that it would have been <b>ideal</b> if Shane, Miles, and Kerry could have patched things up, Shane learned how to use Maya, and started teaching and working with the other new animators, but from what I gleamed of the letter, Shane seemed to view switching from Monty's methods (working 60 hour shifts, passing out under his desk, and waking up 12 hours before the premier and slapping together last-minute changes, also using a program in a way it was never intended to) as being disloyal to him, and honestly if it came down to <i>one</i> talented animator versus an entire team able to actually work together in a program they're familiar with... Yeah, I'd go so far as to say that letting Shane go was the better choice in that circumstance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 12-18-2017, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T12:59:41-08:00","id":1168612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1168510#post1168510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. From the letter it sounds like Shane was a nightmare to work with, and was deliberately not trying to play nice with the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming you take the letter as being accurate, it actually sounds like the exact opposite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have you looked at the non-fight animation in V1-3? It's really kind of awkward. Like &quot;only a few steps above Food Fight&quot; awkward. I saw someone on another forum note that it's not an animation skill problem. The new animation team is fine. What's more of a loss with Monty passing is choreography. </div> </div> </div>Except that Volume 3 was a 100% post-Monty Oum production, and the fights there look amazing, I'd say the best in the series. They were choreographed and animated just fine without him.<br /> <br /> This has... changed radically with volumes four and five, which have had LESS fights and they've also been somewhat less impressive. Bjorn is absolutely correct when he describes a lack of impact and recoil in them. And, again, you don't need Monty for that, because Volume 3 absolutely looks like a Monty Oum production despite Monty having not been involved in any way aside from them using a few of his assets.<br /> <br /> You are absolutely correct that the non-fight animation in Vols 1-3 looks really super awkward at times. You know what? I'll accept that in order for us to get the cool-ass fights. The new animation team is demonstrably NOT fine if they can't produce the number and quality of fights produced in Volume 3 with much, much more resources being thrown at them.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say that I just want pointless fighting all the time. I was actually very impressed when they decided that the Volume 5 premiere was strong enough to not require a huge, set-piece battle in it to justify itself, something that was absolutely the case with Volumes 1-4. You should be putting the fights where you need them... but when they're there, they should look good. This series was sold on the kind of high-impact, high-octane fights that characterized Oum's style. They sold a video game predicated on that style, and say what you will about Grimm Eclipse, you do FEEL like you're watching a RWBY fight when someone who knows how to handle the controls takes a run at it. Not being able or willing to reproduce that seems like a big, big problem.<br /> <br /> I mean... I don't think I'm being unreasonable here, but Sun's performance in Eps. 9 and 10 (spoilers I guess?) of V5 is actually very sad. This isn't the first time he and Blake have teamed up to fight the White Fang; that was all the way back in Volume 1, and that fight looked better than this one has. There was maybe a single five-second exchange with Ilia that came anywhere near the level of Sun's exchange with Roman back on that ship, and that one is still better. The rest of the time he and Ghira are just sort of... awkward, and slow. EVERYONE is sort of awkward and slow. (And have apparently gotten a lot weaker than they used to be; the amount of punishment these people can take is SUPER inconsistent.)<br /> <br /> I would honestly be satisfied with stuff that's at the level of, say, Weiss' character short this season. But they for some reason haven't gotten there? Are they saving the whole budget for the battle of haven?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":4742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","user":"Murcushio","date":". 12-18-2017, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T14:20:20-08:00","id":1168637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1168612#post1168612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Assuming you take the letter as being accurate, it actually sounds like the exact opposite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lemmie just say here (because I'm not nuanced enough to address the other points beyond saying non-committal fluff like &quot;Well I'm enjoying it so difference of taste, I'm sorry you're not enjoying it as much&quot; though I will admit that they could REALLY use a new choreographer), but my read on the Letter?<br /> <br /> The Shane Letter is an example of how you can say things that are true while still being utterly full of shit.<br /> <br /> I admit I don't have the letter in front of me, nor do I greatly desire to look it up, but from what I remember... Well, I don't doubt some of the things Shane mentioned as happening actually happened.<br /> <br /> It's just that the letter was written by someone mourning the loss of a friend, clearly dealing with it poorly, from other accounts his marriage was deteriorating at the same time, and IIRC Shane was dealing with a bad case of depression... So, for example...<br /> <br /> Shane insinuated that Miles and Kerry had worked extensively to change Monty's original vision of the series. There were ideas that were adjusted and changed at their insistence. Examples: There was supposed to be a fight between JNPR and Raven in Volume 3, and Pyrrha's death was totally reworked from what Monty originally planned.<br /> <br /> The thing is, while I don't doubt that these changes were made, <i>I doubt they were done in the context that Shane implied</i>. See, writers do something called <i>edit</i>, where they take their initial idea and prune it, adjust it, change it for better flow.<br /> <br /> JNPR vs Raven - It might have been cool, but would it have served a purpose? Volume 3 was already kind of bloated with <i>pointless</i> fights (As neat as JNPR vs BRNZ was, you could have cut it, and cut NDGO vs SSSN), so they probably didn't need it.<br /> <br /> Pyrrha's death - Shane mentioned that in the original draft, the Maidens weren't a thing (because Monty thought up the Maidens between Volumes 2 and 3), Pyrrha was originally going to be <i>winning</i> against Cinder... But Jaune would show up, distract Pyrrha, and Cinder would turn the tide against her as a result. I don't <i>think</i> I need to spell out why this idea was in fact a <b>horrible</b> one that deserved to be rewritten.<br /> <br /> The thing that stuck with me with the letter is that Shane clearly wrote it while in a <i>very</i> emotional place. A profoundly <i>negative</i> one. He was in pain, he'd just lost a friend, and he seemed to be implying in the letter, between the lines, that Miles and Kerry were trying to use Monty's death as an excuse to ruin Monty's vision.<br /> <br /> I also recall Shane seeming to take exception to them changing the workflow and changing the animation method and the departments, which he took exception to MOSTLY because that wasn't how Monty did it.<br /> <br /> And to wrap it up... I'm not saying that Shane was INTENTIONALLY trying to metaphorically burn RT down after leaving, but again: Written by a dude with acute depression while his life was crumbling and his friend died. Guy was hurting, and probably felt like he was doing the right thing. Just, well... Probably not in the right frame of mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T14:46:41-08:00","id":1168645,"title":"","content":"To talk about the episode itself rather than the production for a moment...<br /> <br /> Am I the only one mildly annoyed with the overall tone and moralizing in the whole White Fang arc? It feels like yet another extremely shallow &quot;caricatured Malcolm X as the villain&quot;, which <i>waaaay</i> too many shows rely on to address issues of racism and prejudice. Like, ok, yes, violent extremism bad, but it's noticeable that the show has devoted almost <i>no</i> time to legitimate Faunus complaints (beyond one brief bullying scene in chapter one, plus vague handwaving indicating that worse stuff is going on), whereas it's devoted an entire massive plot arc with intensive focus to the flatly Dangerous Radical Chaotic Evil villain who goes Too Far. It doesn't even make it into a fair argument about methods - it explicitly states early on that Adam isn't actually interested in helping his people anymore. And while it talks in <i>extremely vague terms</i> about doing things another way, it never actually shows it (beyond the obligatory &quot;fight on the side of the heroes in the big climactic confrontation&quot;, which does nothing to address the underlying structural issues.)<br /> <br /> It's just so... shallow. The breaking point for me was Blake's tearful &quot;stop looking for simple solutions&quot; speech. <i>Motherfuckers.</i> They literally made the decision about what direction the Faunus should go in into a choice between the heroes who want to save the world, and a raving &quot;dangerous radical&quot; mass-murderer stalker who wants to hurt people for the sake of hurting them. Then they have the gall to lecture the viewers about seeing things too simply? Literally everyone in the White Fang (aside from the leader-lady who existed solely for Adam to stab to show how evil he is) is either a smirking, cynical manipulator with no actual convictions, or a naif who keeps making wrong choices and is just one friendship speech away from dropping everything they ever believed in and switching sides.<br /> <br /> I am pissed. Like, yes, of course the White Fang and Adam as portrayed are scenery-chewing comic-opera villains with no depth, but it's annoying to have the show constantly present them as a parable for real-world issues of racism and prejudice and then lecture us about how we shouldn't go for simple solutions. How about we talk about those dust mines where the Faunus are being used as slaves? How about Ilia suggest that, you know, after we save Beacon academy, we march this army over to liberate some of the people there? Maybe, just maybe, in a world where Faunus are getting forcibly abducted and used as slave labor, there's an excluded middle ground between &quot;use violence indiscriminately against everyone for sexual gratification&quot; and &quot;never use violence at all, just nicely ask Schnee Dust Company to stop enslaving us.&quot;<br /> <br /> Like, I'm down for condemning Adam's violence, sure, but the show devotes huge amounts of time and focus to how horrible he is, and nothing beyond one or two bare mentions to the actual atrocities that have driven him to this point (in fact, it actually goes out of its way to say that he no longer cares about them, wtf.) Because, you know, if the Faunus bear collective guilt for Adam's actions unless they move to stop him, I am <i>pretty sure</i> you have to turn it around and ask what responsibility humanity has to address the stuff they did to the Faunus. And so far, the Faunus arc has been awfully light on that. Like... we're told Blake's father represents another path, but what, concretely, is he demanding?<br /> <br /> (I am hoping we eventually get a more concrete scene where Weiss has to grapple with the crimes committed by the Schnee Dust Company and her own responsibility to do something about it in the same way - there have been some hints of that, at least. But right now I'm not terribly hopeful.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, the &quot;Faunus are just as capable of hate as humans&quot; bit was eye-rolling. Like... I'm pretty sure they know that, Blake? It's the specific things that humans are <i>doing</i> that have them pissed, not some abstract Faunus Supremacy. Even the White Fang in its full-on scenery-chewing villainy mode is still focused on that. So it feels like Blake (and the writers) are trying to make the situation simpler than it is by turning the White Fang's position (and, by extension, the real-world people it's trying to represent) into a caricature of itself and then make themselves look deep and wise by saying &quot;look, <i>everyone</i> can be prejudiced!&quot; Yes, sure, most people learned that when they were five, but I'm glad you've caught up, Blake. Now share your plans to close the literal slave-mines, which is the actual complicated part of this problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 12-18-2017, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T15:40:02-08:00","id":1168653,"title":"","content":"I admit, part of me wonders if RWBY's narrative had been better if they hadn't even bothered making Faunus an oppressed minority. Like, just, &quot;Some people have cat ears and people are okay with it&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T19:12:11-08:00","id":1168701,"title":"","content":"I didn't see it as all that shallow, no. Yes, the topic wasn't as deeply explored as it could have been (but the White Fang is hardly alone in that respect within the show), but to me, the basic gist of what it was trying to say is there: &quot;This is not an Us vs Them situation.&quot;<br /> <br /> Adam isn't just violent and hateful, he is also a hypocrite. He is trying to force an all out war of faunus against humans, but he himself is violating those proclaimed battle lines: He deals with humans to get what he wants, and he assassinates faunus to get what he wants.<br /> <br /> The mask that he is trying to present to humans as representing all faunus is a lie, and Blake is trying to tear it off and show the liar underneath. Her plan is both about saving humans (she's seen the carnage in Vale after all) and about destroying the illusion that Adam speaks for the faunus.<br /> <br /> Once the lies are out of the picture, freeing the slaves can be pursued far more productively. Maybe there'll still be a war, maybe it can be done peacefully. But it won't be a war based on lies and greed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T02:54:15-08:00","id":1168747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1168645#post1168645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about we talk about those dust mines where the Faunus are being used as slaves?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe, just maybe, in a world where Faunus are getting forcibly abducted and used as slave labor, </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, sure, most people learned that when they were five, but I'm glad you've caught up, Blake. Now share your plans to close the literal slave-mines, which is the actual complicated part of this problem. </div> </div> </div>Aquillion, this isn't the first time you've suggested that actual literal faunus slavery still exists in the World of Remnant even in the wake of the Great War and the Faunus Rights Revolution. In fact, not only are you saying it still exists, but that faunus are actually abducted and transported in order to meet the demand for said slave labor.<br /> <br /> Do you have an actual cite on that? I'm not saying you're wrong, but I'm familiar with damn near everything put out in the show and in the ancillary materiel and I can't recall anything of this nature at all. I am not, however, all-knowing. Can you point me in the direction of the materiel where it discusses this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T04:31:31-08:00","id":1168763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1168747#post1168747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Aquillion, this isn't the first time you've suggested that actual literal faunus slavery still exists in the World of Remnant even in the wake of the Great War and the Faunus Rights Revolution. In fact, not only are you saying it still exists, but that faunus are actually abducted and transported in order to meet the demand for said slave labor.<br /> <br /> Do you have an actual cite on that? I'm not saying you're wrong, but I'm familiar with damn near everything put out in the show and in the ancillary materiel and I can't recall anything of this nature at all. I am not, however, all-knowing. Can you point me in the direction of the materiel where it discusses this?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I can tell, it's just that the faunus are generally poor and have limited and often unsafe employment options. And people are socially nasty to them, also. For... reasons, I guess? Education options are therefore relatively limited, though not extremely so, as we're seeing. All signs point to a late-stage of underclass that will end with integration soon, in my opinion. As long as that isn't derailed by violent conflict, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T04:41:35-08:00","id":1168766,"title":"","content":"The faunus cause, as shown, has mostly boiled down to the very real, very ugly, and very <i>not anyone's responsibility</i> situation of impoverished or otherwise marginalized but not ostracized people: Everywhere depicted they can live their lives freely, most people not okay with it are down to petty or personal issues and most everyone else, as is normal over the world, is not okay with those fools but won't get in harm's way for a stranger.<br /> <br /> The white fang Pre-Khan is a righteous movement. The white fang Pre-Adam Post-Khan is already criminal, but at least on a frame we can empathize for even if it's still criminal.<br /> <br /> Just about all the shit being depicted right now is Post-Adam.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm far from a good writer, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar517_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"517\" data-vbnamecard=\"517\">Aquillion</a>, but tell me: How do you want to show that the white fang is not just that?<br /> <br /> Right now it's very much becoming that, and it's <b>obvious</b> once the show arrives in Menagerie, that the people associated with Pre-Khan Fang are mighty fine. From Season ONE we know that pre-adam Fang is righteous and just.<br /> I ask this especially because you have to remember that the show can't spend its time depicting everything, and spending entire scenes showing that the Pre-Khan Fang is cool is spending scenes on what's already left said.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Fang in the show, the Post-Adam Fang, is a degenerate violent supremacist movement, and the people used to Pre-Khan Fang, the people that are being shown <b>right now</b> in the series, are simply outside that. Inertia is a thing, you know?<br /> <br /> The Fang during the show is Post-Adam, and they're just as bad as the narrative is using them. You rage for the Pre-Khan Fang. That Fang is dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T18:19:29-08:00","id":1170055,"title":"","content":"I was busy, sorry to delay &quot;Sorcerous Overlord bitches about RWBY&quot;.<br /> <br /> Ok, we had a fight! Parts of it were really good too. the Sun v Ilia exchange was an animation bump, and the Blake v Ilia exchange was a nice animation bump too.<br /> <br /> Gheera is still kinda clunky.<br /> <br /> I have no idea what even was happening with Kali- she was just standing in the open trading shots with someone, and then a dinner tray was bulletproof? WHo was she even fighting? Why did that soldier just hide behind a pillar if his job was to protect her?<br /> <br /> If Bat Wings is supposed to be part of the cool kids ninja team strike force how did he get beat low key by a middle aged non-hunter 2handing a dinner tray? I can appreciate that we don't need to see every fight but she literally screamed and ran up to him, armed with an improvised bludgeon.<br /> <br /> Batwings is trying to stealth take down a guard, and it seems like he thinks that he's in a stealth game, except that he dropped into<i> an active firefight</i> <i><b>through a glass ceiling</b></i>. In the open, no less.<br /> <br /> I was kinda hoping Kali would bust out some Jun Kazama / Asuka Kazama Fancy Proper Japanese Lady Aikido. She has Hakama, a man can dream.<br /> <br /> Fennic and Jackalman are wildly inconsistent in power level. one of them can trade blow for blow with Gheera on an even level, but 2 on 1 they are outclassed. Sun is a major BA but they offscreen curbstomped him? Why was he like 2 minutes late to the battle?<br /> <br /> I really have no idea how strong I'm supposed to view the 2 brothers. Strong enough to tangle with Gheera, strong enough to knock Sun, weak enough to be easily dealt with by Gheera, weak enough to be taken out easily?<br /> <br /> Fennic, Jackalman, and Batwing are the new posterchildren for <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/StrongAsTheyNeedToBe\" target=\"_blank\">Strong As They Need To Be</a>.<br /> <br /> Ilia had some tricks but how was she capable of standing up to Blake, and why does Blake get a Sudden Dramatic Inconviently Timed Temporary-Down from hitting a chair? she took <i>one kick</i>.<br /> <br /> Sun's animation was flashy, but his fight against Torchwick was better animated.<br /> <br /> Blake has also had some better animation.<br /> <br /> Not sure I love the Camera Angle Rapid Pans. John Wick has kind of ruined me for that. Oh, and a little show called RWBY seasons 1-3 as well.<br /> <br /> Kinda Flash over Fight TBH.<br /> <br /> I don't want to be mister cynical pessimism over here, but I'm really getting out of RWBY. Plenty of shows get worse over time as the creators struggle to find ideas, but RWBY might be the only show I've ever seen where <i>the execution</i> is getting worse over time, not better. It's lost it's distinctive style of &quot;Videogame + Anime super choreography&quot; and has become kinda... brawlish. Yang v Mercury? some of the best fightwork I've ever seen. Yang v Henchmen? Punch up. Blake v Torchwick (s2 Train)? Awesome nonstop back and forth. Blake V Ilia? Swing, Swing, jump back and talk.<br /> <br /> I don't know. I'm out. The show went from Doublestuffed Oreos to just the biscuit parts.<br /> <br /> p.s. When is Chainsaw guy from Season 2 coming back? That guy was OG and he didn't even get a name!<br /> <br /> edit: Ok, you know what, I got more to say.<br /> <br /> S1: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=M2-aWwB3sCY\" target=\"_blank\">Sun vs White Fang and Torchwick</a> look <i>how good</i> that fight is. It feels like some grade at Tekken, Guilty Gear, Donnie Yen fusion. That's rad.<br /> S2: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HMfpCuSgmM4\" target=\"_blank\">Yang v Neo, Blake v Torchwick, OG Chainsaw v some rapier girl</a>. This fight is Legend. Neo is totally in control the whole fight and we can see how her misdirect style is just toying with Yang's Power Stance Brawler Shounen Style. Blake's constant back and forth, clone jutsu, and slice and dice vs Torchwhick's flare launcher Cane-based Wang Chung. Badass. OG Chain v Rapier girl- RG is dominating this fight with her precision attacks and her ballet defense being too dodge-heavy for OG Chain to use his straightforward power melee style, and the bad matchup is costing him big time. He eats a super attack from Rapier Girl (Magic OP pls Nerf) and then finally gets his chance to exploit his insane Defense + HP pool- he breaks stun and makes a counter grab when RG is midair, and his slam shows off how her min/max dodge build has made her <i>super glass cannon</i>.<br /> <br /> S5: Yang V Ilia, Sun V Ilia, Sun and Gheera V Fox and Jackal:<br /> <br /> Gheera opens his fight by throwing Jackal through a wall, fox backstabs him. How did he get stabbed if Aura protects him? Rapier GIrl took a Chainsaw and she's like 90 pounds.<br /> <br /> Blake get one shot by a kick tossing her into a <i>chair</i>. Jackal had just been thrown <i>through a hardwood wall</i>.<br /> <br /> Jackal and Gheera punch counter and are at parity. It might be that Fox is weak cuz he gets wrecked all the time, but seriously Ilia stands watching them for 5 IRL seconds, enough for Fox to get up, charge across the room, and then Gheera just shakes off the stand off.<br /> <br /> Whiskey Tango Actual Foxtrot. Where is the thematic style of each fighter? Where is their sense of weight and skill? <i>Why doesn't it look like a fighting game anymore?</i><br /> <br /> Sun V Ilia: it goes from 11:42 to 11:52. Exactly 10 seconds of choreographed fighting before Sun the &quot;push against each other bit&quot;. That's the <i>highlight</i>. Sun v Torchwick goes from 0:35 to 0:55, twice as long, and that's <i>just Sun's part of the fight</i>. Blake takes over for 20 more seconds and then Sun jumps back in for 10 seconds of pure, nonstop action. From 0:35 to 1:15 we have straight battle choreography. 40 seconds. Penny gets 30 seconds to herself as well. No filler, no bullshit jump back around and make meaningless, awkward swipes in the air. S1 is <i>full</i> of shit like that. it isn't even a special scene. This fight was the s5 payoff.<br /> <br /> <b>RWBY is literally an OBJECTIVELY worse show than it used to be. </b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 12-23-2017, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T18:49:07-08:00","id":1170064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1168612#post1168612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that Volume 3 was a 100% post-Monty Oum production</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it wasn't.<br /> <br /> He died before Volume 3 began airing, but he'd completed a number of Volume 3 things before he died. Such as expanding the concept of whatever Cinder was into &quot;there's four of them, one for each season&quot; and also parts of Penny's fight with Pyrrha, if not also parts of Yang's fight with Mercury.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would honestly be satisfied with stuff that's at the level of, say, Weiss' character short this season. But they for some reason haven't gotten there? Are they saving the whole budget for the battle of haven? </div> </div> </div>I believe so, since I can't imagine that Rooster Teeth wants to make fight scenes LESS awesome than Weiss' character short, <i>or </i>that they're not aware of how most of the action in this Volume still isn't on Monty's level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T17:59:36-08:00","id":1172122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1170064#post1170064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it wasn't.<br /> <br /> He died before Volume 3 began airing, but he'd completed a number of Volume 3 things before he died. Such as expanding the concept of whatever Cinder was into &quot;there's four of them, one for each season&quot; and also parts of Penny's fight with Pyrrha, if not also parts of Yang's fight with Mercury.</div> </div> </div> </div>By &quot;production&quot; I meant &quot;animation production&quot; as opposed to &quot;writing and conceptual development.&quot; My understanding is that Monty died well before actual animation work on S3 began; they used a number of his assets (rigs, models, etc.) and concepts but that actual animation production did not begin in earnest until after his death.<br /> <br /> But even if I'm technically wrong on 100%, Monty wasn't involved in the vast, VAST majority of Season 3 animation... and the fights still look amazing! They've got some of the best goddamn fights in the series in there, and they look and feel like a Monty Oum production. They actually to an extent feel BETTER than a Monty Oum production, because they have better assets and production quality backing them up than they'd ever had before. Actual backgrounds! Vivid colors! They managed to do that <i>without</i> Monty's presence.<br /> <br /> And then they fell off a cliff on Season 4 and 5. The main change between seasons was they changed how they animate, moving to a completely different set of tools. Now, I've defended that move in the past; Monty was kind of an insane genius who got a lot out of Poser, but Poser isn't fit-for-purpose when it comes to &quot;we're making a real show with a real production staff here.&quot;<br /> <br /> But those defenses were predicated on them being able to get equivalent results out of Maya when it came to the giant, set-piece battles. And if they straight-up can't do that, even while throwing vastly more resources than Monty Oum ever had in his possession at the series, when they <i>could</i> do it with their previous tools... then that's a big problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I believe so, since I can't imagine that Rooster Teeth wants to make fight scenes LESS awesome than Weiss' character short, <i>or </i>that they're not aware of how most of the action in this Volume still isn't on Monty's level. </div> </div> </div>Rooster Teeth has marked tendency to sometimes not realize they aren't firing on all cylinders until it's way, way too late. That happened with more than one season of Red vs. Blue.<br /> <br /> With RWBY, it's like... you can see what they WANT to do. When I take a look at the fights that have gone down this season, I can tell what they want the characters to be doing, but it's like they can't get there, like they threw up their hands at some point and went &quot;fuck this shit, we're out.&quot; There's an almost palpable sense of frustration.<br /> <br /> We know they <i>can</i> get there. The Ruby Volume 4 character short. The Weiss and Yang Volume 5 character shorts. To a certain extent the Geist fight way back when Volume 4 premiered. Those were all <i>quality</i> fights. They got REALLY close to being a Monty Oum Joint; close enough, I'd say. If everything were on that level, and it were occurring regularly, I'd have no complaints.<br /> <br /> But then you get stuff like the Blake Volume 5 character short. Hell, just about everything Sun has been involved in; I don't know who this guy is, but outside of a very brief ten-second window he sure as hell ain't the Monkey King from the first three volumes, that's for sure.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit baffled. Is it, like, a money thing? A time thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T19:52:27-08:00","id":1172138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1172122#post1172122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> snip</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be noted they didn't just lose Monty, after volume 3 both Shane newille(?) and Dillion goo were fired/quit. They where together responsible for every single high quality fight in V3 that was not based directly off Montys work.<br /> <br /> As for current volumes the issue seems to be money. Roosterteeth is rated poorly as a job for animators with a expected salary less than the average in other studios. It seems likely they have not been able to keep and maintain the same talent they had in V1-3.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T22:05:08-08:00","id":1172175,"title":"","content":"Oh dear. So I just saw episode 11. It was almost all fight scene...with 90% happening just off screen. This scene they rush through, after this slow a season? This should have been an epic 2+ parter, instead it feels like puppets being briefly knocked together in between dramatic close ups.<br /> <br /> This is a fight show. Why avoid showing the fights?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T23:03:50-08:00","id":1172196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1172175#post1172175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a fight show. Why avoid showing the fights?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly my multipage complaint essay distilled down into a single line.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T07:13:44-08:00","id":1172249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1172175#post1172175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh dear. So I just saw episode 11. It was almost all fight scene...with 90% happening just off screen. This scene they rush through, after this slow a season? This should have been an epic 2+ parter, instead it feels like puppets being briefly knocked together in between dramatic close ups.<br /> <br /> This is a fight show. Why avoid showing the fights?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they don\u2019t have the resources? Because there is so much essential plot to cover that they already had to extend the volume by two episodes to cover it all?<br /> <br /> Because eight different fights would require something like a tournament arc in length? Which isn\u2019t a good use of time when all of the fights are going to be interrupted when one of the fights comes to a frightening end, or when the chekov\u2019s gun goes off?<br /> <br /> Most of these duels aren\u2019t actually consequential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-01-2018, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T07:21:07-08:00","id":1172250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1172138#post1172138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for current volumes the issue seems to be money. Roosterteeth is rated poorly as a job for animators with a expected salary less than the average in other studios. It seems likely they have not been able to keep and maintain the same talent they had in V1-3.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, rated where?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T07:37:10-08:00","id":1172252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1172250#post1172250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, rated where?</div> </div> </div> </div>Glassdoor and payscale reports.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T09:38:00-08:00","id":1172285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1172249#post1172249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because they don\u2019t have the resources?</div> </div> </div> </div>They used to. What changed?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because there is so much essential plot to cover that they already had to extend the volume by two episodes to cover it all? </div> </div> </div>They're not doing so hot a job of that, either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because eight different fights would require something like a tournament arc in length? </div> </div> </div>This isn't &quot;eight different fights.&quot; Part of the problem is that they are treating it like eight different fights.<br /> <br /> This is a <i>group fight.</i> Remember those? The show used to have them and they used to be great.<br /> <br /> The Volume 3 group fights managed to involve everyone in the group in dynamic, interesting fashion and none of those required the entire length of the volume to resolve. People didn't just pair off and get slammed against each other in an awkward way, shuffled offscreen as soon as they had to be; they swapped foes, they bounced around, slammed into each other, used the entire environment, cooperated with their teammates. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which isn\u2019t a good use of time when all of the fights are going to be interrupted when one of the fights comes to a frightening end, or when the chekov\u2019s gun goes off? </div> </div> </div>It's... not a good use of the time for the fights to be awesome and cool? The heck?<br /> <br /> I mean. They're slamming the remains of Team CRME, Team RWBY, Team JNPR, the Branwen twins, one of Salem's top lieutenants who even Ozpin is terrified of, and TWO headmasters against each other. This should be an epic battle royale in which they're making full use of the space provided and using all of their talents and abilities to the maximum. And if they can't deliver that, they should not have written the confrontation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most of these duels aren\u2019t actually consequential. </div> </div> </div>Neither was the food fight! Or Weiss' and Yang's V5 character short! Or Team SSSN vs. Team NDGO, which was literally just there to have a cool fight.<br /> <br /> They still managed to park those pretty deep, tho. And this is the opening round of the Battle of Haven. It should be, you know, up there with the opening round of the Battle of Beacon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T09:49:23-08:00","id":1172289,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Nevermind. This isn't worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T10:40:12-08:00","id":1172305,"title":"","content":"What was so messy about this fight to me was that the heroes split up.<br /> <br /> Ren and Nora are the biggest offenders apparently saw Jaune fighting Cinder alone and apparently said to themselves &quot;He's clearly thinking straight, not out of his league battling a Maiden and has the situation <b>completely</b> under control... let\u2019s go fight the big guy he isn't doing anything!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T11:58:34-08:00","id":1172334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1172305#post1172305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was so messy about this fight to me was that the heroes split up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right? Like... this isn't like seven separate fights. This is ONE fight, just with a lot of people. Like the Vytal Festival fights or the Battle of Beason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ren and Nora are the biggest offenders apparently saw Jaune fighting Cinder alone and apparently said to themselves &quot;He's clearly thinking straight, not out of his league battling a Maiden and has the situation <b>completely</b> under control... let\u2019s go fight the big guy he isn't doing anything!&quot; </div> </div> </div>It's especially weird because... okay. Ren and Nora don't know what Hazel does or what he's capable of (which is another of Ozpin's failings) but Nora Valkyrie is a wrecking machine; she's got arms like cannons, legs like pistons, and hits, if you'll pardon the pun, like a hammer. She can both dish it out and take it.<br /> <br /> This doesn't make her invincible, but it does mean that you can probably detail her to fight the giant bear of a man by herself for at least a little while because she's unlikely to end up suddenly one-hit KO'd. You send the extra man to fight either Cinder, Raven, or Vernal.<br /> <br /> Actually, hmm. Thinking about it...<br /> <br /> You do want Qrow on Raven, because he knows her fighting style best and she's an experienced, hard-bitten warrior; she probably outclasses any of the kids by a wide margin. Qrow is the only &quot;elder&quot; fighter on Team Good Guys, and it makes sense to use him to lock down his sister.<br /> <br /> I'd put Nora on Vernal, because apparently a big part of Vernal's actual maiden powers involve lightning (we've seen her summon it out of a clear blue sky) and Nora's Semblance completely obviates that in a way Vernal likely isn't prepared for. Frankly, I'd be amazed if this doesn't come into play at some point anyway.<br /> <br /> You put Ruby on Cinder because Ruby has already proven that she has <i>some</i> capability of fucking Cinder right the fuck up, and because Ruby's high-mobility fighting style seems like it stands a good chance of keeping her out of reach of Cinder's big hits.<br /> <br /> I'd put Ren on Emerald because Ren is the most unflappable of all the fighters, which means he has the best chance of not being discombobulated by Em's illusions; he'll keep a level head and react calmly and logically to whatever mental fuckery she tosses at him.<br /> <br /> You want Jaune on Hazel; Jaune has a really, really strong aura and fights sword-and-board in a highly defensive style, and Hazel is one of the &quot;elder&quot; fighters here. Until you've taken his measure you need someone on him who can keep him occupied, away from the others, but also who can stand up to his strength.<br /> <br /> Yang on Merc is good; let the cyborgs battle it out. I think Yang is just straight up a better fighter than Merc is.<br /> <br /> Oscar on Leo also makes sense; Ozpin likely has a pretty good idea what Leo is capable of.<br /> <br /> That leaves Weiss as the extra man. I would detail her as a floater; she's the second most mobile of the fighters, right after Ruby. Detail her to go where she's needed. (This will probably involve Cinder or Hazel.) Plus, as the extra man that leaves her with possibly a chance to get her Semblance up and running, which takes some time and effort; Vernal kept getting interrupts off.<br /> <br /> You also want to use group moves and combo attacks whenever possible. Team Good Guy has one big advantage over most of Team Evil: they're composed (mostly) of two combat teams that trained and fought together as units instead of just an agglomeration of individuals. Ruby, Weiss, and Yang know how to fight as a unit; so do Ren, Nora, and Jaune. For that matter so do Ruby, Ren, Nora, and Jaune. On the other side, only Cinder, Mercury, and Emerald have that advantage; possibly also Raven and Vernal. But most of the component parts of Team Evil have not been practicing and training with each other for literally months on end like the component parts of Team Good Guy have.<br /> <br /> They should be leveraging the fuck out of that instead of pairing off and then kind of ignoring each other.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T14:52:58-08:00","id":1172390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1172249#post1172249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of these duels aren\u2019t actually consequential.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of, this is a fighting show (has been since it started with four fighting trailers), and this season has been lacking in fights so far. It needed these fights to be bigger.<br /> <br /> [Spoiler warning]<br /> But also, which of these fights aren't consequential? Brother and sister clashing in arms after a long time of mistrust? Yang getting revenge for having her name ruined? Jaune getting a chance to avenge his love? Ozpin discovering a traitor in his own inner circle? Rwby having to face the girl she once called a friend in deadly combat? The new guy Oz seems worried about who is an unknown and needs to be introduced as a threat? Weiss facing the girl who mocked her while she was a prisoner?<br /> And they are all fighting for their lives.<br /> None of this was inconsequential in my opinion.<br /> [/End of spoilers]<br /> <br /> Do RT not have any fight choreographers on their team at the moment? I'm not talking about proficient animators, I mean someone who actually knows enough about martial arts to come up with cool fights.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T17:28:21-08:00","id":1172453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1172334#post1172334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right? Like... this isn't like seven separate fights. This is ONE fight, just with a lot of people. Like the Vytal Festival fights or the Battle of Beason.</div> </div> </div> </div> I mean if this was Cinder employing divide and conquer tactics I'd have been okay with everyone being split up. It's not ideal but it saves effort with fight choreography that can be employed elsewhere down the line while fulfilling rule #1 of a good fight scene, telling you about the characters through their actions.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T22:01:42-08:00","id":1172537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1172252#post1172252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Glassdoor and payscale reports.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's depressing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T23:10:22-08:00","id":1172556,"title":"","content":"Ahahahahahaha.<br /> <br /> (Spoilers I guess?)<br /> <br /> So I just watched the fight again... and at one point, Weiss actually, with no prompting from anyone, propels herself backwards into a column at full speed. Just... hops right off a glyph and slams herself into it.<br /> <br /> You got RUSTY in the six to eight months you were up north, Weiss.<br /> <br /> Other random tidbits: Ozpin never actually asks Leo what happened to him. At first I thought Leo was just shrugging off the inquiry but Ozpin doesn't vocalize it; Oscar's mouth never opens. It's purely internal monologue.<br /> <br /> The Branwen twins appear a grand total of two seconds after Raven kicks Qrow offscreen; somehow the camera never manages to be on them ever again except when Ruby uses her flash-bang. They are ELUSIVE motherfuckers.<br /> <br /> We crucially do not see what Ruby's flashbang does to Vernal; there is NO footage of Vernal after it goes off. We don't know if it actually knocked her down and out for a bit like it did to Cinder or not. SOMEONE kicked Weiss across the room, presumably Vernal, but we don't know if Vernal avoided damage because she didn't have her maiden powers &quot;up&quot; at the time.<br /> <br /> Jaune could probably have cut Cinder clean in two if he'd had the presence of mind to slash instead of stab.<br /> <br /> Adam Taurus is a ridiculous man who says ridiculous things. His constant mugging for the camera is only excusable because a camera is actually on him... only he doesn't <i>know</i> that.<br /> <br /> I had forgotten how much I missed Cinder talking for extended periods of time. Her villain monologuing is A++; Jessica Nigri's voice fits the character extremely well. It's a little telling that she loses her temper somewhat more easily these days; she went three seasons without raising her voice, always the cool, controlled femme fatale, but now she can be tossed off-balance and fly into a range.<br /> <br /> Mercury thinks he is good at one liners but is actually shit at them. &quot;I'm thinking you owe me an apology for my leg, don't you... uh... think?&quot; isn't exactly Shakespeare there, Merc.<br /> <br /> I don't think I've laughed harder this season, or in fact the last two seasons, than I did when Cinder cut Jaune to pieces with &quot;Who are you again?&quot; But I'm not sure I laughed for the reason they wanted me to laugh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T15:02:33-08:00","id":1172760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1172556#post1172556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We crucially do not see what Ruby's flashbang does to Vernal; there is NO footage of Vernal after it goes off. We don't know if it actually knocked her down and out for a bit like it did to Cinder or not. SOMEONE kicked Weiss across the room, presumably Vernal, but we don't know if Vernal avoided damage because she didn't have her maiden powers &quot;up&quot; at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Ruby was focused on Cinder at the time, rather than Vernal, and Emerald clonked her on the head mid-eye-deployment anyway, I'm not sure how much we could read out of the scene concerning the Silver Eyes' effectiveness against Vernal even if they had shown her reaction.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'm still not completely convinced the writers themselves have any idea what they're doing with the whole Silver Eyes thing to begin with. Vol. 5 has sold me a little better on the Maidens as a concept, but the Silver Eyes still don't seem to fit well into the setting or story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T15:41:23-08:00","id":1172776,"title":"","content":"Cinder also grabbed the stump of her missing arm, where I suspect a Grimm-thing is growing as a replacement. That's the place that apparently hurt the most when Ruby blasted her.<br /> <br /> Silver Eyes might not affect Maidens; just people infected with Grimm-things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T16:06:44-08:00","id":1172783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1172776#post1172776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver Eyes might not affect Maidens; just people infected with Grimm-things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since it most powerfully affected a grimm dragon, that's what I always assumed.<br /> <br /> But for all the info dumping of this season and the time Ruby supposedly spent training with Ozpin, the man who actually knows most of what's going on and is clearly aware of the significance of the silver eyes, we still haven't been told squat about this rather important plot element. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T18:35:03-08:00","id":1172817,"title":"","content":"Holy shit, what a goddamn letdown. This is Peak Bad Shit.<br /> <br /> <u>Random thoughts:</u><br /> Why is Leo such a bad fighter? I get that he's a coward, but he's still a <i>headmaster</i>. Oscar is still relatively weak.<br /> <br /> Why the split up? We had group fights in S1 S2 S3, they couldn't pull that off again? I know there's been some behind-the-scenes drama but why did this show get so goddamn bad?<br /> <br /> The only good animation bits were Weiss bullet whacking and Juane's Camera-Sword opener. Everyone else just does Swing-Swing-Jump back and talk about our feelings. This isn't RWBY, its a low budget Saturday morning cartoon from a developing country.<br /> <br /> Other than Weiss, can you show me one <i>distinct</i> fighting style from this fight? 'member when Yang fought Neo? 'member when we had the food fight? I 'member. Remember Team CFVY and how we learned about their personalities just from a little bit of watching their fighting styles and team interaction? Where the F did that level of character detail go?<br /> EDIT: Just started watching Season 3 tournament arc again, and it's INSANE how much better those fights are. For shame, RWBY devs.<br /> <br /> What is StrongMan McReluctance's deal? He doesn't have a weapon, but he can just... block hits real good? he can't put down Lie Ren and Nora? He's on the same Evil Pay Grade as Tyrion and (maybe) Cinder. Why couldn't he just roflstomp half the team? Even if he really just doesn't want to fight- why do show him effortlessly aikido'ing Lie Ren and Nora and imploring them to stay down? Literally nothing is conveyed about his character, personality, or abilities- and not in a mysterious way. For all I know he just has constipation.<br /> <br /> Ok, Jaune. Let's talk Jaune. When he gets righteously mad there's a little &quot;ching&quot; sound effect. Next episode is going to be his Semblance, which I've suspected for a long time is Paladin/Group Heal. So far, so good. I like that they worked his Pyrrha emotions into finally seeing Cinder again. But... why the hell does he just fall over in the fight with Cinder? She gets hit with Ruby's Silver Eye Hero Power, Jaune misses her with a stab, and then just... falls over. Cinder leisurely stands up and puts a foot on him, and then calmly walks away for the big finish attack. <i>Jaune hasn't even been hit yet! </i>Oh wait, I'm sorry, he get's knocked down once while Cinder is evil gloating, before he gets back up and keeps fighting. Did he push himself too hard? He fought harder <i>against Cardinal</i> and still was picking himself back up. Is that fall supposed to be him overbalancing? we've seen his footwork and basic swordsmanship skills rise throughout the series. He charged, stopped when Silver Eyes hit, and then attacked again immediately. So Whiskey Tango Foxtrot? It's 3 seconds before Cinder get's up, and then 3 more for her to walk over to him. He was literally just full-charging at her, was he supposed to be hanging on by a thread there? When she gets off of him, why doesn't he grab his sword and try to fight back- the sowrd he was trying to reach when she was on top of him? Jaune literally does not give up. That's his whole schtick. So why is he suddenly helpless and about to be ko'd? But we gotta get that final scene.<br /> <br /> Any special reason Cinder attacks Weiss?. If you stop the scene right at 13:34 you can see the layout of the room. Ruby is down, Cinder hates Ruby, and Ruby is right next to her. But she attacks someone <i>across the room, over Ruby's prone body</i>? Oh, and Yang, Qrow, Lie Ren, Nora, <i>and</i> Oscar don't have a chance to do something dramatic to save her? Also, this is super petty, but the spear toss animation looks kinda off. Weiss was across an entire ballroom.<br /> <br /> Hey, remember when a bunch of people fought another bunch of people and Jaune turned out to be really, really good at making Team Tactics? Or remember when Ruby, Weiss, and Yang showed off that they had combo attacks? No? That's ok, the Devs do not remember it either.<br /> <br /> Remember when a 4-on-4 fight was a 4-on-4 fight and not a bunch of nonsensical 1-on-1s? ya member?<br /> <br /> I am super not a fan of Ruby's Silver Eyed So Special Protagonist Power, by the way. I didn't like that get out of jail free shit back in S3 and I don't like it now. She has Anti-Villain Magic, and it's an unblockable wave. Kinda lame. It invalidates fights.<br /> <br /> No really, Oscar is just Whacking at Leo like an old lady with an umbrella. Professor Port and Oobleck would have handed that kid his shit, but <i>Headmaster Leo</i> can't? yeah yeah, psychology. Yeah yeah, headgame. Leo's opening move is to stand still, fire up his Duel Disk, Summon Exod- dial in fire, dial in rock, and then shoot it straight ahead at someone basically 3 meters away. A+ effort on that. Just Horseshit.<br /> <br /> No Qrow/Raven, ok. sure. Didn't hype that up or anything.<br /> <br /> Whiskey Tango Foxtrot is up with two people holding swords to each other and talking. It's super goddamn lazy. In Food Fight it lasted half a second between Pyrrha and Blake and then it fed into a fakeout/attack. This time two of the most dangerous characters in the series are just chatting while sword pressing each other.<br /> <br /> Lie Ren and Nora don't fight like a co-ordinated pair. They date now, c'mon guys. you built that up a whole lot. Pay it off. Even in the tournament arc they had some pairwork.<br /> <br /> Yang and Mercury don't fight. Big let down.<br /> <br /> Emerald has an amazingly useful semblance and doesn't use it enough. Legit she should have made Ruby swipe Jaune (disguising him as Cinder), that would have been good. She still does sue it, but c'mon. that's A game material right there.<br /> <br /> Not really a this episode thing, but why doesn't Nora ever lighting-dust herself for super strength? She has a massively useful semblance that is only ever used twice due to sheer chance. Lightning dust exists!<br /> <br /> Ruby and Emerald fight in a circle about 4, 5 meters wide. Ruby once speed-shot through a 100 meter cafeteria (<i>without her gun</i>) just to sweep up debris. She can't, i don't know, <i>retreat</i>? Jump back, and then make a couple of shots at Cinder with her <i>goddamn Sniper Rifle!?</i><br /> <br /> Why doesn't anyone, literally anyone, team up?<br /> <br /> Why break up into 1 on 1 fights if you aren't going to give us 1 on 1 fights? It's literally just Weiss and Vernal.<br /> <br /> Weiss makes an ice block about ten feet wide as a time buyer, but she's in a <i>giant open ballroom</i>, and Vernal cuts through it. Ok, I'll actually forgive this one as being an in-character mistake. You know what could have helped? Lie Ren, Nora, or goddamn anybody trying to buy her some time. She's getting her ass kicked!<br /> <br /> Can we also talk about who fights who? Yang+Mercury, Qrow+Raven, and Oscar+Leo make sense. Jaune <i>wanting</i> to fight Cinder makes sense, but why anyone lets him doesn't. Lie Ren and Nora are his nakama. they have insanely good group dynamics and a lot of trust. Why don't they help him <i>fight the woman who <b>killed Pyrrha?</b></i> Why is Ruby incapable of getting passed Emerald?<br /> <br /> whenever people are walking it still looks kinda janky.<br /> <br /> Ok, something Nice: Weiss doing the bullet-ballet was pretty rad. I like it. The quick shot in the background of Mercury and Yang darting around was pretty great as well, even though the exchange lasted about 1 second. The animation was ok, but the choreography felt a little more like s1. Still not at the level of s2 train, but not bad.<br /> <br /> Weiss reaction shot at the end was really well done. I like the futility of the hands- nice work team.<br /> <br /> annnnnd, yeah ok. those are my specific impression of this episode.<br /> <br /> This season is such a goddamn shitshow of a shit show. The fights are worse animated, worse directed, nonsensical, and less often. The plot has never been great but the show absolutely sucks at introducing things and the creators have no goddamn idea what they are doing. The pacing is bad, the dialogue is bad, the characterization is bad, and more important that <i>ANY</i> of that:<br /> <br /> <b>They joy has gone out of the show</b>. I don't feel the passion due to a Labor of Love. I feel a product designed to be cheaply produced and slotted into a lineup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 01-02-2018, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T19:07:55-08:00","id":1172819,"title":"","content":"Have you <u>fought</u> before, Sorcerous Overlord?<br /> <br /> If you miss a blow, it can be pretty easy to fall off-balance. Jaune put a hell of a lot of effort and force into that blow, and he ultimately missed. All the inertia and momentum that he was trying to put into Cinders face got directed into open air, and he wasn't able to redirect his own momentum.<br /> <br /> <u>It. Happens.</u> Hell, it has happened to me before, when I sparred with a spear. I made a mild thrust, the opponent slipped the blow, and I stumbled. Guess what? That fight was <u>over</u>, in the space of half a heartbeat. And I didn't even slam into the ground like he did, just a quick stumble of a half-step.<br /> <br /> To comment on him not moving after he falls: again, he was doing a balls-out charge before slamming into the ground. Have you ever got the wind knocked out of you? It can take a couple of seconds to recover from that.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is why in a 'real' fight you don't go overboard like that. You don't need all that much effort to make a lethal thrust..... but Jaune is a <u>little</u> emotionally charged here, and I give him a pass.<br /> <br /> Other than that, spot on. The combat in this episode was by-and-large nonsensical.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T20:09:05-08:00","id":1172845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1172819#post1172819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you <u>fought</u> before, Sorcerous Overlord?<br /> <br /> If you miss a blow, it can be pretty easy to fall off-balance. Jaune put a hell of a lot of effort and force into that blow, and he ultimately missed. All the inertia and momentum that he was trying to put into Cinders face got directed into open air, and he wasn't able to redirect his own momentum.<br /> <br /> <u>It. Happens.</u> Hell, it has happened to me before, when I sparred with a spear. I made a mild thrust, the opponent slipped the blow, and I stumbled. Guess what? That fight was <u>over</u>, in the space of half a heartbeat. And I didn't even slam into the ground like he did, just a quick stumble of a half-step.<br /> <br /> To comment on him not moving after he falls: again, he was doing a balls-out charge before slamming into the ground. Have you ever got the wind knocked out of you? It can take a couple of seconds to recover from that.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is why in a 'real' fight you don't go overboard like that. You don't need all that much effort to make a lethal thrust..... but Jaune is a <u>little</u> emotionally charged here, and I give him a pass.<br /> <br /> Other than that, spot on. The combat in this episode was by-and-large nonsensical.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have, actually. I'm an ranked amateur boxer, I have a blackbelt in karate, and I've done a year's worth of Kendo. (EDIT: I also just started Judo) He started an attack from about 5 feet away, and he just <b><i>collapses</i></b>. He didn't trip from the charge- because we see he came to a full stop. so he stabs, nicks cinder, and just... drops his controller? If he's supposed to be gassed or at 1hp, why is he able to charge? We are told, and shown, and shown, and shown some more that Jaune isn't the novice kid he was in S1. They literally comment in the S3 Tournament that he's way better than he used to be. He takes down an <b>Ursa Major</b> with a flurry of strikes in the S2 finale. He can't make a downward thrust?<br /> <br /> If they had a reason for him to fail like that, they should have communicated <i>why</i> he failed so hard. We're out here guessing if reasons because the show <i>failed at informing us</i> something it expects us to believe. Now, with our Doyalist Hats on, he falls because the plot needs him to fall, but seriosuly- they couldn't animate in a counter attack from Cinder?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T20:56:09-08:00","id":1172865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1172819#post1172819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To comment on him not moving after he falls: again, he was doing a balls-out charge before slamming into the ground. Have you ever got the wind knocked out of you? It can take a couple of seconds to recover from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jaune once took a rock the size of his head, traveling at very high speed, right to the face, toppling him over and slamming him very hard into a tree.<br /> <br /> He shrugged that off in less time than it took him to get back up after overbalancing. He's also been swatted by heavy objects or very strong things many, many times before and seemed to barely notice it.<br /> <br /> Aura is supposed to be a thing, and Jaune's aura is supposed to be super tough. It sure would be nice if they remembered that.<br /> <br /> And I say this as someone who would shed no tears if Jaune died.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:21:25-08:00","id":1172890,"title":"","content":"I'm wondeting what is Raven up to. Just two episodes ago she said Team Evil will turn on them once they get what they want, but then went and made all the arrangements for the ambush for them.<br /> <br /> I think she's up to something. Notice, shecand Qrow vanished after initial exchange. And Vernal seems to be holding back. Or maybe I'm over analyzing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T21:56:35-08:00","id":1172914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1172865#post1172865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I say this as someone who would shed no tears if Jaune died.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, what's it like to be a monster? jk but seriously I love Jaune.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1172890#post1172890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondeting what is Raven up to. Just two episodes ago she said Team Evil will turn on them once they get what they want, but then went and made all the arrangements for the ambush for them.<br /> <br /> I think she's up to something. Notice, shecand Qrow vanished after initial exchange. And Vernal seems to be holding back. Or maybe I'm over analyzing</div> </div> </div> </div>You can see her and Qrow at the pan out at 13:34. They are just darting around fighting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T22:20:46-08:00","id":1172924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1172817#post1172817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy shit, what a goddamn letdown. This is Peak Bad Shit.<br /> [...]<br /> <b>They joy has gone out of the show</b>. I don't feel the passion due to a Labor of Love. I feel a product designed to be cheaply produced and slotted into a lineup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fully agree.<br /> <br /> Also, to me it seemed like the episode (and fight) was structured like standard geering up to show off Jaune finally discovering his semblance - all the beats were there: heroes are brought low, Jaune the lowest, and discover something new about themselves / himself - even a <i>hack writer</i> can make this work. Except nope. Everything winds down and yet another character is threatened with death. The stakes are ~sooo hiiigh~ you guys.<br /> <br /> Killing off Weiss would be a pretty sloppy move (her name is in the title of the show -_-), so she'll most likely survive, possibly due to Jaune discovering his Semblance (or something else, like Oz-magick), which should have happenned in that fight scene because ending the episode on &quot;everybody fails... again.&quot; just feels as though the writers bear ill will towards the characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T23:25:55-08:00","id":1172936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1172924#post1172924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fully agree.<br /> <br /> Also, to me it seemed like the episode (and fight) was structured like standard geering up to show off Jaune finally discovering his semblance - all the beats were there: heroes are brought low, Jaune the lowest, and discover something new about themselves / himself - even a <i>hack writer</i> can make this work. Except nope. Everything winds down and yet another character is threatened with death. The stakes are ~sooo hiiigh~ you guys.<br /> <br /> Killing off Weiss would be a pretty sloppy move (her name is in the title of the show -_-), so she'll most likely survive, possibly due to Jaune discovering his Semblance (or something else, like Oz-magick), which should have happenned in that fight scene because ending the episode on &quot;everybody fails... again.&quot; just feels as though the writers bear ill will towards the characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked that Cinder reminded us that she's the only certified Hero-Killer in the franchise, and the shot of Weiss herself coming to grips with what happened to her were really cool. It was a good piece... but you're absolutely right. There's no way Weiss is going to die, and we know Jaune is going to heal her. I'm glad they are trying new stuff, but it just didn't land. The fight was sloppy and Cinder went from &quot;literal killer&quot; to &quot;Alpha-Bitch from High School movie&quot;<br /> <br /> Pyrrha, Penny, and the Fall Maiden all died in S3 and it was a real shake up. As much as appreciate what they <i>wanted </i>to do, it's pretty lame and predictable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T00:03:18-08:00","id":1172940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1172890#post1172890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondeting what is Raven up to. Just two episodes ago she said Team Evil will turn on them once they get what they want, but then went and made all the arrangements for the ambush for them.<br /> <br /> I think she's up to something. Notice, shecand Qrow vanished after initial exchange. And Vernal seems to be holding back. Or maybe I'm over analyzing</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... I mean, she's already told us what she's up to in that selfsame episode where she says Team Evil will turn on them once they get what they want?<br /> <br /> The plan is to have Vernal crack the vault, and then instead of handing off to Cinder they take the relic and vamoose, using the relic's power to keep Salem at arms length rather than relying on Salem's &quot;generosity&quot; for services rendered.<br /> <br /> But in order to get to the part where the vault gets cracked they have to actually go through the whole ambush thing.<br /> <br /> Vernal is certainly holding back; Raven specifically instructed Vernal not to use her Maiden powers.<br /> <br /> I think there's a tiny, outside chance that Raven tipped off Qrow and they've got some kind of plan in the works and all of this is play-acting... but I highly doubt it. She and Qrow vanish after the initial exchange because the fight is poorly choreographed; they show up again for two seconds when Ruby pops her flashbang.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T12:32:15-08:00","id":1174614,"title":"","content":"Just saw ep 12. I knew Raven had something up her sleeve.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T12:40:38-08:00","id":1174617,"title":"","content":"That changes so many things. Her entire bandit thing might be a facade.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T13:57:01-08:00","id":1174639,"title":"","content":"Does give another possible reason why she left Yang. And why she never visited","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T14:39:43-08:00","id":1174658,"title":"","content":"That reveal was interesting, yes. But where did the ice blast come from? Cinder's thing is definitively fire, not ice. If she can do the opposite of her apparent theme, that's a big deal that needs an explanation, I would think? Does she already have the winter maiden's powers?<br /> <br /> But Ruby...please don't stop people doing what they're doing only to yell at them to not stop doing what they're doing *facepalm*<br /> <br /> edit: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1174639#post1174639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does give another possible reason why she left Yang. And why she never visited</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought she did visit, but only in raven form (Yang actually recognises the bird, so she must have done so somewhat frequently). So coming to see Yang was never the issue, only actually speaking to her? I'm not sure where this reveal factors in to explain that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":12735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","user":"BjornTheFellhanded","date":". 01-09-2018, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T15:03:15-08:00","id":1174667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1174639#post1174639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does give another possible reason why she left Yang. And why she never visited</div> </div> </div> </div>The timelines don't match.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Raven ran off shortly after Yang was born. Let's say, 16-17 years ago.<br /> <br /> Leo and Qrow both noted that the Spring Maiden ran from Haven ten years prior.<br /> <br /> Also, Qrow never once said to anybody that Raven was the Maiden, when I'm pretty sure HE would even if Ozpin felt like keeping it a secret for reasons.<br /> <br /> Honestly, my read is that either Raven met the previous Spring Maiden and either killed her or was nearby when she died, so she got the power about a decade prior. Vernal was a red herring, in and out of universe.<br /> <br /> It is also possible that when the previous Maiden died, her last thought was of Leo or something,<br /> and the mantle of the Spring Maiden randomly found Raven </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 01-09-2018, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T15:39:59-08:00","id":1174678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1174658#post1174658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reveal was interesting, yes. But where did the ice blast come from? Cinder's thing is definitively fire, not ice. If she can do the opposite of her apparent theme, that's a big deal that needs an explanation, I would think? Does she already have the winter maiden's powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>*cough* <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> 'scuse me. Sorry for butting in but got a comment here. Or maybe more a question<br /> <br /> IDK if Cinder has the Winter powers: I don't think so (I'd put my money on a dust vial personally, and have my own theory about Winter) but there's another line Cinder had this episode that might tie to an explanation. And I can't work it out for love or money.<br /> <br /> When she's going to drain Vernal, Cinder says &quot;So I will take... <i>what was mine.</i>&quot; (Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> ... Not 'what I deserve', 'what I have earned'. What was mine. So.... ok, maybe it's just an odd line, but doesn't this imply Cinder had already <i>held </i>Spring's power at some point? She's now showing what might be Winter's too. I don't have a firm answer to this, but I'm wondering if anyone else has an interesting theory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T16:09:39-08:00","id":1174682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1174678#post1174678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *cough* <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> 'scuse me. Sorry for butting in but got a comment here. Or maybe more a question<br /> <br /> IDK if Cinder has the Winter powers: I don't think so (I'd put my money on a dust vial personally, and have my own theory about Winter) but there's another line Cinder had this episode that might tie to an explanation. And I can't work it out for love or money.<br /> <br /> When she's going to drain Vernal, Cinder says &quot;So I will take... <i>what was mine.</i>&quot; (Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> ... Not 'what I deserve', 'what I have earned'. What was mine. So.... ok, maybe it's just an odd line, but doesn't this imply Cinder had already <i>held </i>Spring's power at some point? She's now showing what might be Winter's too. I don't have a firm answer to this, but I'm wondering if anyone else has an interesting theory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting point. The first time I watched I misheard it as 'what is mine' and put it down to Cinder's usual villainous presumption, but it is 'what was mine', you're right.<br /> <br /> The other thing I noticed on this rewatch of the scene was that the ice blast definitely came from Cinder's seemingly empty hand.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T17:43:50-08:00","id":1174715,"title":"","content":"The Maidens have multiple elemental powers. Amber used fire, wind, and ice in her fight against Cinder and co","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T18:08:38-08:00","id":1174721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quo