erText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Again, Leo and Qrow knew the Maiden when she ran off. Neither said that the Maiden was Raven. As whipped as he is, Leo would have told Salem and Cinder that Raven was the Maiden.<br /> <br /> No, I'll put money on Raven becoming the Maiden after the old one ran.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 01-09-2018, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T19:34:46-08:00","id":1174737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1174715#post1174715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Maidens have multiple elemental powers. Amber used fire, wind, and ice in her fight against Cinder and co</div> </div> </div> </div>She did? Fair enough. I guess I forgot. It's been two seasons, to be fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T20:58:25-08:00","id":1174761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1174726#post1174726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Again, Leo and Qrow knew the Maiden when she ran off. Neither said that the Maiden was Raven. As whipped as he is, Leo would have told Salem and Cinder that Raven was the Maiden.<br /> <br /> No, I'll put money on Raven becoming the Maiden after the old one ran.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Did Qrow know who the Maiden was? I got the feeling he didnt know the girl who had it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T22:56:45-08:00","id":1174785,"title":"","content":"Okay, this was worked interestingly to make everything line up properly, and I don't know if I'm impressed or deeply annoyed, because in general I don't like information that has to be at least somewhat well-known amongst multiple onscreen characters to be withheld from the viewers for the sake of a shock or a reveal, but sometimes I like it a lot.<br /> <br /> So let's work this out.<br /> <br /> Qrow initially figures out that the Spring Maiden is with Raven and her tribe because of the destruction of Shion Village; he takes a look at that, deduces &quot;this damage is consistent with the application of the power of the Spring Maiden&quot; and then basically demands of Raven point-blank to come clean with him. In fact, in hindsight, Qrow might have played Raven a little bit. He may not have KNOWN that it was her tribe that was responsible for Shion, but when he dangles it in front of her as an accusation she responds defensively, one might even say guiltily. Qrow might, internally, have been thinking &quot;Bingo. I didn't <i>know</i> it was you, but now I do, which means I also know you've either got the Spring Maiden with you or know who she is.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Not saying this was the case, but it's a possibility. Qrow is, generally, smarter than he acts. He played Winter Schnee like a fiddle and Winter is no dummy herself.)<br /> <br /> Later on, Qrow reveals this information to Leo and Ozpin. There's something crucial to note about the scene with Leo; neither Qrow or Leo use a NAME. It's always &quot;she&quot; or &quot;the Spring Maiden.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, this is clever because the show has a long history of not using names when it really should use names. In Volume 3, when Qrow is berating the Ozluminati, he doesn't say &quot;the people in this room, Leo, &lt;name of Shade's headmaster&gt;, we're the ones that keep the world safe.&quot; He uses the more awkward construction of &quot;the people in this room, the leaders of the other two academies,&quot; speaking very distantly, very abstractly of people who he knows personally well and is engaged in a conspiracy with. And the reason for that, of course, is that the writers weren't ready to introduce us to Leo yet and they're still not ready to introduce us to whoever is in charge over in Shade.<br /> <br /> Same deal in Volume 4. Qrow never refers to Leo by name even when it would make sense to do so. When he's telling Team RNJR about the Triforce Relics, he only refers to Leo as &quot;the Headmaster.&quot; Again, because the writers aren't ready to reveal Leo to us. Once they do, Qrow stops referring to Leo in the abstract, by his title; throughout Volume 5 he refers to him in a much more natural way for someone we've seen Qrow interact with and have a clear history with. He uses Leo's, y'know, name.<br /> <br /> So we're prepared for cast members to obliquely step around identifying people and not use proper names until the show is ready. And the writers use that to sort of trick us and make this work.<br /> <br /> If, during V5C1, when Leo is talking about the Spring Maiden running off, suppose he doesn't use &quot;she.&quot; Suppose he identifies her by name.<br /> <br /> If that were the case, the second Vernal shows up onscreen and with THAT name, presumably different from that of the previous maiden, and throwing lightning around, and with Raven presenting her as the Spring Maiden, there would have been immediate and rampant fan speculation as to if she was or wasn't the Spring Maiden. People would be all &quot;is she a fakeout? Does Raven not have the Spring Maiden as a friend and ally but just wants people to think she does? Or did Vernal kill the previous Spring Maiden, or is she related to her in some way that would make sense for the power to come to her?&quot; People would be doing things like going &quot;oh yeah, it's totally Vernal, look at her throw that lightning around&quot; or going &quot;when Vernal supposedly 'demonstrated her powers' her eyes didn't flare up like Amber and Cinders do. Maybe that's unique to the Fall Maiden, or maybe Raven and Vernal are big lying liars.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Sidebar: Raven's eyes didn't do the Maiden Glow when lightning comes out of a clear blue sky to interrupt Weiss and Yang's escape. Either that wasn't her, she can engage her powers without the glow to an extent, or Vernal's semblance is such that she can generate lightning strikes on her own.)<br /> <br /> Anyway. It's clear the writers didn't want any of that speculation and sleuthing going on... so they thread a very, very careful needle.<br /> <br /> How careful? Glad you asked!<br /> <br /> There's no fucking way that Leo didn't convey all of the Spring Maiden's particulars to Salem, who conveyed them to Cinder and Watts. (Or, if either Leo didn't or Salem didn't, then one or both of them are giant fuckin' dolts.) So when Cinder and Co. show up, and Vernal is presented to them, they have to be thinking &quot;wait, what? Who is this? This isn't who we were told to expect.&quot;<br /> <br /> In fact, in this context, Cinder demanding Vernal &quot;prove it&quot; makes a lot more sense; she wasn't expecting Vernal. She was expecting a different girl. But Cinder knows from experience you can murder your way into Maidenhood. So hey, maybe Raven's butch little lackey did the same thing... but Cinder is gonna demand she prove that before she accepts it on faith.<br /> <br /> None of this happens onscreen, tho. There's no whispered conversation between Watts and Cinder or anything like that. It might have happened offscreen; I can't imagine Cinder NOT needling Vernal with arrogant, bitchy, probing questions. &quot;So, how'd you get your powers? Did you kill the previous Spring Maiden? I got mine that way. Mmm, it's a real rush isn't it? The power surging into you. Were you prepared for it then? Are you even prepared now?&quot; That kind of thing. Probably called her &quot;sister&quot; once or twice, really rolling the word off her tongue in a way that I bet made Vernal want to punch out her other eye. But that's all offscreen.<br /> <br /> Then, again, when they all show up at Haven, you have to imagine there was an awkward meeting with Leo. &quot;Who's this?&quot; &quot;Vernal.&quot; &quot;... yes? Go on?&quot; &quot;The Spring Maiden.&quot; &quot;... what happened to the last one?&quot; &quot;Don't worry about it, Leo.&quot; &quot;... yes ma'am.&quot; But not onscreen, so the viewers don't know.<br /> <br /> And of course when the fight in V5C11 is going down, it all happens fast enough that Qrow and Ozpin (and maybe the others? Did the kids EVER get the full briefing? The kids are real fuckin' bad at asking for information and Oz and Qrow are real fuckin' bad at providing it) don't have time to ask for introductions vis-a-vis the girl with Raven who for all they know is just more muscle.<br /> <br /> They thread that needle all the way to their big reveal scene. And again, I'm not sure how I feel about it.<br /> <br /> I know a LOT of fanfiction writers are going to be super goddamn happy about this; &quot;Raven is the Spring Maiden&quot; has been a lot of peoples fanon for a very long time and now it is canon. So has &quot;you can be more than one Maiden at a time,&quot; which might not be possible naturally but Cinder, at least, believes it is possible through Grimm-based soul-sucking.<br /> <br /> I wonder what the cutoff age is on inheriting powers? Raven had to have been thirtyish and, you know, a MOTHER before she became the Spring &quot;Maiden.&quot; When do the powers decide &quot;nope, too old, won't bond to you, next candidate please!&quot;<br /> <br /> Closing random thought: Hazel is gonna regret shoving lightning dust into himself in a context in which Nora Valkyrie is in the room. He's gonna regret that at least once.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T23:08:57-08:00","id":1174789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1174785#post1174785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Sidebar: Raven's eyes didn't do the Maiden Glow when lightning comes out of a clear blue sky to interrupt Weiss and Yang's escape. Either that wasn't her, she can engage her powers without the glow to an extent, or Vernal's semblance is such that she can generate lightning strikes on her own.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Cinder's eyes haven't been flashing every time she flings fire, and that was something she only started doing after she got half of Amber's powers. Hell, even in the Amber, Mercury, Emerald, and Cinder throwdown, Amber's eyes didn't start glowing until she called down the storm.<br /> <br /> If I had to guess, my assumption was that the Glowy Eyes are like a Caste Mark. You tap into a little here and there, and there won't be much difference aside from the magic flying everywhere.<br /> <br /> But if you REALLY reach in and start calling down the Wrath of the Divine, your eyes are going to start burning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Closing random thought: Hazel is gonna regret shoving lightning dust into himself in a context in which Nora Valkyrie is in the room. He's gonna regret that at least once. </div> </div> </div>It'll probably come down to the first blow. Nora can absorb electricity to increase her strength and speed (as sayeth Port back in V3 during the Tournament). But that doesn't increase her Durability... And in the V3 finale, she got socked out by a Paladin, so she's probably not the hardiest fighter.<br /> <br /> And while Hazel is augmenting his fighting style with Lightning Dust (Aside: YEESH. And remember you have to willingly deactivate your Aura to leave your skin open to implantation) he's also fucking huge, and beefy enough that half the nicknames for Dave Ryder from the MST3K Space Mutiny riff could apply to him.<br /> <br /> ... Actually, he'll probably punch her, send her flying, she'll smash through a wall... And Ren will wryly comment &quot;Ooooooh <i>shouldn't have done that</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> And Nora's sparking arm will grab Magnhild, and she'll start laughing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T00:08:26-08:00","id":1174798,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how much point there is to speculate as to who has the power to hurt someone how bad and all that. The show has always played very fast and lose with what is and isn't a dangerous blow. Especially in the last few episodes where characters haven't so much fought as simply existed in proximity to each other until one or both fell over on cue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T02:16:00-08:00","id":1174806,"title":"","content":"Ok, let me settle into my rant pajamas so i can rant in comfort.<br /> <br /> I didn't think you could do fuck up more than last episode- and I was right. Ep 12 wasn't a fuck up or a train wreck, because trains have to be chugging along to wreck. This episode inherited a broken mess and then put the toys down on the floor and just stood around them for a few minutes. In rough chronological order:<br /> <br /> How do you fuck up Jaune's Big No moment? He just jogs over and slides next to her- no rage, no disbelief, no emotion other than a meager &quot;Weiss!&quot;.<br /> Everyone literally stops fighting so that the Hero Kids League can gather around their little dead friend. Team Evil just watches that happen and doesn't give a fuck.<br /> Hazel chastises Leo about sucking. I dont have more to say after last week's rant but Oscar is still just baseball whacking at Leo and it's embarrassing to watch.<br /> FrankenHazel, that's a neat one.<br /> Why didn't Oz recognize him that other time they met? They did meet, right? like at a crossroads.<b>EDIT: they totally did meet and I just completely forgot about it. I'll leave my shame here out in the open. </b><br /> <br /> Let's talk Cinder's Plan- She killed Ozpin in solo battle fairly quickly in S3, only moments after unlocking her full power upgrade. So now Ruby is down, Weiss is down, she's got the FrankenHazelNaut charged up, and Jaune is busy in triage. She's left with Cinder, FnHazel, Raven, Vernal, Emerald and Mercury and she's facing Qrow, Oscapin, Nora, Lie Ren, and Yang. Leo and Jaune effectively don't matter at this stage. Emerald and Mercury can dominate any two of the Kid Hero League (or tie up 3 of them, maybe), Qrow and Raven tie, FNHazel can crush Qrow if it matters but will easily stomp Oscapin. That means that Cinder, Vernal, and maybe Raven have a 3 person super weight Power Play advantage. Maybe just Cinder and Vernal if it matters. So what's her genius plan to stop <i>literally the only people in Remnant who can oppose her?</i> Better Split Up, Gang! Jesus goddam Christ, there's bad and there's just bullshit drama mechanics. This is &quot;slap the audience in the face&quot; level stupid, the part where you throw the book across the room in frustration. You massacred and entire fucking city! you can't take 20 seconds to kill the only people able to trouble you? Bullshit. Pure Bullshit.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ozpin is <b><i>here!?</i></b>&quot; &quot;Is that a problem?&quot; &quot;I'm not sure, but right now we've got the upper hand&quot;. No, no no no no no. You <i>KILLED</i> him when he was at full power, <i>by yourself.</i> He's weaker, and you have an advantage! There is literally no way he is a greater threat to you at this moment then he was in S3.<br /> <br /> Oz wants Oscar to run, but to where? FrankenHazel will definitely catch a scrawny fourteen year old farm kid.<br /> <br /> The number of people casually walking around in this life and death battle is too goddamn high.<br /> <br /> Does Frankenhazel only has the twofisted axehandle attack? C'mon man, you are holding back <b>QROW</b> with only one hand, just shook out a left hook and wrap this shit up.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Let's Talk Hazel's motivation. &quot;Hey Oz! my sister went to be a Grimm hunter at your school and she died. Now I have teamed up with the Head of the Grimm, the beings which killed my sister, for revenge on you for training her to fight Grimm which kill people.&quot; Oscar &quot;Hey, wouldn't your sister be upset about this turn of events&quot;, Hazel: &quot;Smash&quot;. In under a minute, i thought of this- what if Oz actually did get her killed during his politicking spy mission bullshit? Like, what if he had to actually own that death? Nah. Let's just stick to Dead Little Sister and call it a day. we need the writing time to set up Jaune's dramatic &quot;Make no reactions or have any emotions to saving your friend's life&quot; scenes.<br /> <br /> For Jaune's big, 5 season long Semblance reveal that ended on a <i>Weiss dying cliffhanger</i> we don't get a Righteous Fury, a Rage Filled No, a Manly Tears, or even a I'm Not Equipped To Handle This moment. We get <i>a close up shot of his face, eyes closed</i>. There's a Tinkerbell sound effect.<br /> <br /> I'm going to give that one another line because Wow, how did you fuck that up. You didn't have that on a sliver platter, you had that on a Platinum Iridium Platter held by a nubile maiden riding a White Elephant. The cliffhanger even did the work for you, all you had to do was Shout, Let It All Out.<br /> <br /> JFC we're only half done.<br /> <br /> Cutting to the elevator and back to Ballroom is shit. The creators do not have the narrative skill to pull that kind of <i>basic filmmaking</i> off. It's a moment killer and a mood whiplash.<br /> <br /> I used to like Jessica Nigri as Cinder, but her delivery here is terrible. &quot;Are you nervous, girl?&quot; &quot;Its a once in a lifetime honor&quot;, its too obviously an amateur giving a flat take on &quot;Evil Seductress- use husky voice and like you have 110% self confidence&quot;.<br /> <br /> FrankenHazel uses Massive Telegraphed Blows! He misses! He just stands there while Ozcapin jumps around him! This is the kinda shit I mean when I say the series fights have irrevocably gone downhill. Hazel punched Oscar across the room and Oscar picked himself up, but when Oz starts rapid machinegun stabbing him from <i>arms reach away</i> he just stands there and apparently is too beat to take it. I didn't know stunlocks worked like that in RWBY. The Animation bump wasn't even that good, and it's incredibly jarring when we get into the one 10 second long money shot that we are supposed to be impressed by. You spent 10 minutes animating marionette puppets, i'm not gonna get whipped up for the 10 seconds on smoother frame models.<br /> <br /> Why is the default animation style for Big Guy &quot;lumbering idiot&quot;? Gheera and Hazel animate like they are only allowed one step at a time. I watched Nora grenade launch over a canyon, I can believe that someone who powerlifts is light on their feet.<br /> <br /> You know, I was totally going to just right off people dealing damage completely arbitrary to their size because that's an anime/game thing, but this is a freak example. So roided up Hazel is a juggernaut, but Oz in Oscar can still damage him? Is this Oz's power backing his hits? Is Oscar's body capable of dealing that much damage? How the hell does anything work in this show. They opened Pandora's box when Nora gets Lightning Muscles, and I was ok with Coco being a superweight fashonista, but we see how weak Oscar is in training, and Oz is almost in a panic earlier about Hazel- look, I wouldn't be so hard on it if the show was so inconsistent with Power Levels.<br /> <br /> Jaune continues to have no idea what the power he's channeling does, even though it's been at least one whole in universe minute at this point, and Lie Ren straight up is like &quot;Yeah, She's getting a lot less dead&quot;.<br /> <br /> Just a reminder that Nora was sitting over Ruby, Lie Ren was sitting over Jaune, and the whole time Hazel, Qrow, and Oscar had this battle <i>Mercury and Emerald were beating the shit out of Yang</i>. The Mercury/Yang fight didn't last as long as this, and you could make a strong case that Mercury was trying to throw that fight and is a lot more powerful than Yang is. Does Emerald even need to use Illusion here? She's crazy powerful too, we saw her in S2 and S3. Mercury solo could win, Mercury with illusions should have crushed this battle, and Emerald and Mercury should have tag teamed Yang into the cement in 30 seconds flat. Has Yang just been punching air while Mercury kicks her in the face over and over?<br /> <br /> Even if part of the Raven/Cinder deal is that Yang doesn't die, people black out when they lose aura. Why not just beat her up, use Illusion to negate her Rage Mode, and then wrap it up?<br /> <br /> Seriously, Mercury is going to town on Yang's face like she's the combo-doll in a fighting game practice mode. She's the wingchung of getting her teeth Bruce Lee'd out of her head.<br /> <br /> This is an actual error instead of a complaint- at 10:17 Hazel is coming with an overhead left across and down his body. when he hits Qrow, it's a rising left body-hook. Sloppy scenework.<br /> <br /> Ruby taking Jaune's hands off of Weiss many people have covered. I get how this could happen in a live action work by accident, but someone had to <i>deliberately animate this</i>. Hopefully it was an intern or someone who drinks on the job.<br /> <br /> Ok, was Nora just waiting for someone to tell her what to do while watching her friends get steamrolled into the ground? She didn't want to help Oscar, Qrow, or Yang?<br /> <br /> When we had the S3 tournament arc, it was easy to assume offscreen characters were still battling and the pace of the action was rapid- now people are just standing around, talking about their feelings, walking in the middle of battle, and waiting to be screen relevant again.<br /> <br /> &quot;No, I'm angry&quot;. +1 Sin Counter.<br /> <br /> Back in the Basement- some banter. I don't think the reveal here really does anything. Ok, the new girl isn't the Maiden, it was the other character. You sure got us, hooo boy. Didn't see that coming, round of high fives at the office. But what does that matter? what did it do? Vernal (nice name distraction, and nice OP distraction) amounted to nothing in this show except a four or 5 episode &quot;gotcha&quot;. Raven being the Maiden doesn't <b><i>change</i></b> anything. Frodo didn't have a fake copy of the One Ring, Arthur didn't get a fake Excalibur. It's literally just a bait and switch reveal.<br /> <br /> Why was Vernal about to touch the door? what was the plan here? She seems honestly surprised that Cinder attacked, but shouldn't she have expected this to be the exact moment when Raven should turn on Cinder? How are you blindsided by inevitable betrayal when that was the only card in the deck?<br /> <br /> Grim Arm is neat.<br /> <br /> Way to get punked by a rookie move, Raven.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/7uajA\" target=\"_blank\">Really poor facial animation</a> on Raven for the reveal.<br /> <br /> Mandatory cliffhanger ending.<br /> <br /> I can't believe I have to say this, but even I am getting tired of hate-watching RWBY. Ep 12 wasn't even bad, it didn't do enough to warrant the grade of &quot;Bad&quot;. Here's all of the things that happened in <b>12 minutes</b>: Hazel hulks out, Jaune Semblance, Cinder kills Vernal, Raven Reveal. There was a single awkward fight scene.<br /> <br /> I don't have anything witty or profound to say at this point. RWBY sucks, the plot sucks, the action sucks, the reveal sucks, the script sucks, the direction sucks, and the animation sucks. Bloat has set in and we are at &quot;14 year old's fanfic diary&quot; level of show writing quality.<br /> <br /> oh and Edit: Could we be more obvious with the Nora/Hazel thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 01-11-2018, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T03:41:54-08:00","id":1174823,"title":"","content":"Oz DID recognize him. You're obviously fishing for things to get angry at at this point, no matter how much of what you find is legitimate.<br /> <br /> Why don't you just stop watching? It's not making you any good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 01-10-2018, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T05:08:44-08:00","id":1174828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1174823#post1174823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oz DID recognize him. You're obviously fishing for things to get angry at at this point, no matter how much of what you find is legitimate.<br /> <br /> Why don't you just stop watching? It's not making you any good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fishing for things that are legitimate is an unusual sentence. Yeah, this is an angry critique. RWBY used to be an amazing show and I am personally invested in it, even though its bad. I want it to be good. I'll keep watching because I'm hoping I'll be wrong and I legitimately want to be wrong. <br /> <br /> Making long, specific point by point critiques of RWBY is a healthy way to channel my disappointment in something I used to love. Its very cathartic, I recommend it (if you are the kind of person into long form media criticism). <br /> <br /> Plus I put out a few snippets of stuff I like. Its just that the awful outweighs the good. And reddit downvotes you into oblivion if you have even a single criticism that isn't wrapped in 5 layers of praise.<br /> <br /> Edit: i forgot the previous meeting. They did meet, right? On the road? Did Oz mention anything about it then? I care enough to hunt that down","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 01-10-2018, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T05:12:49-08:00","id":1174829,"title":"","content":"Oz said hazel was a particularly nasty enemy of his, and for oscar to not linger nearby.<br /> <br /> And I'm serious with my suggestion. &quot;I'm doing this to not feel bad after all the hate&quot; is not a better solution than &quot;don't hate&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T05:54:18-08:00","id":1174838,"title":"","content":"Oz and Crow walked past each other at a train station mid season 4, and Ozpin did warn Ozcar to be careful, but nothing further was said or shown about that encounter.<br /> <br /> As for 'don't hate', that's not how some people work. There is a both very insightful and entertaining rant about the Mass Effect series, for example, that ended up being nominated for a Hugo award, just because someone felt the need to put the specifics of their disappointment into enough words to fill a short novel.<br /> <br /> And given the stated desire (for RWBY to become good again), how is not watching it going to help? That's either not going to do anything, or, if enough people do it, kill the show through lack of audience. Then no one benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T06:27:15-08:00","id":1174846,"title":"","content":"I'm not talking to a general audience. I'm specifically looking at mr overlord over there spending week after week rambling to the point he admits it's that or welling up frustration.<br /> At that point rwby to him is not entertaining. It's stress, it's that job you don't like but it's what you have and you need something else to cope. Except he doesn't need it. And if he does, that's only worse.<br /> <br /> So I suggested to him that he ought to simply stop watching the show. It's not doing him any good.<br /> I like the show. Still like it. I recognize these two seasons are a shadow of the first three (even if nowhere near as down as he depicts them), and still want it to grow and improve and finish in a grandiose manner. But I'm not telling people to not watch it. I'm telling Overlord that he might be better off without.<br /> <br /> No sense in continuing to argue this, by the way. It's his prerogative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 01-10-2018, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T10:18:46-08:00","id":1174908,"title":"","content":"Honestly I stopped taking Overlord seriously when he claimed that there was no more love in the show. He's entitled to his opinion and I mostly ignore the things I disagree with, but that is something I find to be <i>profoundly</i> incorrect.<br /> <br /> Looking at how the team acts at the panels, at the streams for the show, how the VAs and animators interact with the fans on Twitter and on the forums... No. RWBY is still very much a labor of love from the team. To say that it's no longer a project of love is to imply that it was only ever Monty's thing, and to belittle how much the rest of the crew always cared about the show.<br /> <br /> Is it perfect? No. Nothing really is.<br /> <br /> Has it fallen back from Volume 3? In some ways, yes. The switch to Maya required them to get their feet again.<br /> <br /> But if they didn't care, they wouldn't be <i>trying </i>to improve. And in my mind, they are trying to improve. They <i>want</i> to make this show better. And it's never reached a point where I thought &quot;RWBY is dead, and this is just a mockery left&quot;.<br /> <br /> If it's reached that point for you, if you seriously and honestly think that RWBY will never be enjoyable for you... Then you probably <i>should</i> cut it out of your schedule. Read some fanfics or something, look at engaging fanart.<br /> <br /> When Bleach hit the point when I wasn't enjoying it anymore and no longer felt invested, I just stopped reading it. I didn't keep reading it and going &quot;This is SUCH SHIT compared to the original arcs!&quot;<br /> <br /> If the show isn't fun for you anymore, and watching it doesn't bring you any joy... Then you should probably just stop watching. Not out of a sense of &quot;Don't harsh my buzz, man&quot;, but in a sense of &quot;Why do you keep doing this to yourself?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1174828#post1174828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And reddit downvotes you into oblivion if you have even a single criticism that isn't wrapped in 5 layers of praise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also you clearly aren't seeing the same Reddit I am. There's people complaining about everything and how it's all been downhill since V3 all over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 01-10-2018, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T14:40:22-08:00","id":1174989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1174682#post1174682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting point. The first time I watched I misheard it as 'what is mine' and put it down to Cinder's usual villainous presumption, but it is 'what was mine', you're right.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1174724#post1174724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a line back when we saw Cinder first attack the old fall maiden about &quot;claiming what is ours.&quot; I mean granted depending on the circumstances it could just as easily be a belief in entitlement as opposed to fact, but it has made me wonder if the Maidens aren't a case of Ozpin's first form dividing up his own abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm.... I don't have a knock out theory on this, but I'm seeing two primary possibilities<br /> <br /> One is the simple, more direct and more likely one. Cinder is a past Maiden. Her powers were stripped from her, probably via Oz directly, and she views that as unfair. This solves pretty much everything, I think, though it leaves a fair few unanswered questions and is yet another secret that turns out to not really be so bad.<br /> <br /> ... which is what makes me lean towards my second theory. At least as something worth considering. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> See, the Four Maidens legend assumes that the power that is granted to the girls was always that of the Wizard<br /> <br /> What if it wasn't? What if Oz took this power away from Cinder, or her family or ancestor or whoever, and gave it to the Maidens? Oz sets up the dynamic between him and Salem as equal opposites, but it doesn't seem likely the two are the world's only sources of magic. This might explain the heavy elemental focus on the Maidens' powers too: the themeing might be retroactive. A way Ozpin tried to hide what he did within the legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T00:54:15-08:00","id":1175122,"title":"","content":"Oh, to be talked about but not to...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1174908#post1174908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I stopped taking Overlord seriously when he claimed that there was no more love in the show. He's entitled to his opinion and I mostly ignore the things I disagree with, but that is something I find to be <i>profoundly</i> incorrect.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I find the whole heart of the show lost and view it more like a Rooster Teeth product than Mounty's Crazy Labor Of Love. I don't interact with the behind the scenes stuff, so maybe that's the source of our difference, but the feeling has changed a lot, for me. I have articulated why in the last several rants.<br /> <br /> Also, you are &quot;entitled to your opinion&quot; but you don't refute a single one of my points- you just &quot;don't take me seriously&quot;. Ok, which part of my page and a half critique do you have qualms with? I would love to engage in debate or discussion, but you are commenting on my character and not my criticisms.<br /> <br /> Also, I went to the ep 12 reddit thread and sorted by &quot;best&quot; and &quot;controversial&quot;. All the &quot;best&quot; posts were throwing out <i>honest to god 10/10s</i>. 10/10? Even by just RWBY internal standards I'm not seeing 10/10. I respect that people want to gush and that's how Reddit algorithms work, I'm not going to throw shade on people gushing. I gush, not about RWBY but I gush.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar32_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"32\" data-vbnamecard=\"32\">Synapse</a> I did forget that Hazel and Oscar met. That one is a legitimate mistake on my part. I made a similar mistake last week trying to recall something from S4 without looking it up. Mea culpa. I'll edit the original post.<br /> <br /> I don't have some wellspring of actual hate, rage, ire, or stress about watching RWBY. I actually, in a kinda of screwed up way, enjoy watching RWBY and comparing it to the golden standard of S1-3 (which wasn't perfect but was great!). Writing up a big point by point criticism takes me around an hour, as I rewatch it in chunks as I write. I really <i>look forward</i> to that. I enjoy long form pop culture critique such as made by, basically, <i>everyone on the internet these days</i>.<br /> <br /> Also, and this is just to the void as it were, does anyone who disagrees with me have any refutation beyond &quot;I just don't like/agree with what you said&quot;? Because this is a discussion and I want to discuss.<br /> <br /> good, now that we've wrapped that bit up...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One is the simple, more direct and more likely one. Cinder is a past Maiden. Her powers were stripped from her, probably via Oz directly, and she views that as unfair. This solves pretty much everything, I think, though it leaves a fair few unanswered questions and is yet another secret that turns out to not really be so bad</div> </div> </div> </div>The legend of the Maidens is a fairytale at this point in Remnant. Unless Cinder is Really 700 Years Old I doubt that she, personally, could be one considering<i> -as far as we know-</i> you need to <b>die</b> to transfer the power.<br /> <br /> I'm not one much for speculation, but I'd say the whole &quot;Two Brothers&quot; and &quot;Salem/Ozpin&quot; thing is basically the same story retold down the ages. If Salem was the host of the powers originally or their source before she became whatever she is than I could see Cinder's angle on the &quot;taking what is ours&quot; line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T01:47:00-08:00","id":1175125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1175122#post1175122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The legend of the Maidens is a fairytale at this point in Remnant. Unless Cinder is Really 700 Years Old I doubt that she, personally, could be one considering<i> -as far as we know-</i> you need to <b>die</b> to transfer the power.<br /> <br /> I'm not one much for speculation, but I'd say the whole &quot;Two Brothers&quot; and &quot;Salem/Ozpin&quot; thing is basically the same story retold down the ages. If Salem was the host of the powers originally or their source before she became whatever she is than I could see Cinder's angle on the &quot;taking what is ours&quot; line.</div> </div> </div> </div>She doesn't say ours though. She says what was <i>mine</i>. Running with the idea that it's not just an awkward line, at minimum that means Cinder is a past Spring Maiden. She did claim to come from Mistral back in volume three, right?<br /> <br /> As to legends and other possibilities... I'll admit, the fact that this would mean Cinder is hundreds of years old is a big reason I'm reluctant to push the 'she was the source of the Maiden Powers' theory. Nothing explicitly contradicts it but just in general presentation and action she doesn't come across as ageless like that. However, there are still ways that theory could work. The Maidens could've been created recently; we're told they're an old legend but Oz is in a powerful position and is an ace manipulator. They could've originated just a generation ago or something. The elemental powers could be a family thing as I said, with them being stolen before Cinder. It's not something I'm sure on but the possibility remains IMO.<br /> <br /> Also Oz and Salem being the Two Brothers I don't quite buy. Oz refers to higher beings as Gods and there's the whole reincarnation thing with him. IDK just what part he plays in what's going on but I bet there's some more up the show's sleeve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T01:59:09-08:00","id":1175126,"title":"","content":"I don't think they've lost their love for the project. But I do think they suffer from a bad case of &quot;love is blind&quot;.<br /> <br /> The script and story needed more editing. The visual editing needs to be more confident. The fight scenes need to get back on screen where they belong, for which they'll need better choreography. And they need to cut things that clutter up stuffed scenes or requires exposition time they don't have.<br /> <br /> It's strange that since the team moved from one crazy men sleeping at his desk to (I'm told) a full on production team, the end result appears more and more amateur level. I believe that the team is on a mission of passion, but while the technical quality and tool proficiency improved a lot, I don't get the feeling that the team knows what to do with what they have.<br /> <br /> For all the exposition dumping (from the Man himself), what have we actually learned about what's going on?<br /> For all the action, what did we actually see on the screen in the way of awesome fights?<br /> For all the drama, how many character arcs have actually meaningfully progressed?<br /> <br /> The answer isn't nothing, but it's far short of where the show could have gone. Season 1 did more on every count with less screen time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T04:34:41-08:00","id":1175421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1175126#post1175126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they've lost their love for the project. But I do think they suffer from a bad case of &quot;love is blind&quot;.<br /> <br /> The script and story needed more editing. The visual editing needs to be more confident. The fight scenes need to get back on screen where they belong, for which they'll need better choreography. And they need to cut things that clutter up stuffed scenes or requires exposition time they don't have.<br /> <br /> It's strange that since the team moved from one crazy men sleeping at his desk to (I'm told) a full on production team, the end result appears more and more amateur level. I believe that the team is on a mission of passion, but while the technical quality and tool proficiency improved a lot, I don't get the feeling that the team knows what to do with what they have.<br /> <br /> For all the exposition dumping (from the Man himself), what have we actually learned about what's going on?<br /> For all the action, what did we actually see on the screen in the way of awesome fights?<br /> For all the drama, how many character arcs have actually meaningfully progressed?<br /> <br /> The answer isn't nothing, but it's far short of where the show could have gone. Season 1 did more on every count with less screen time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wholeheartedly agree. It feels like, I don't know how to phrase this, employee bloat? There's a team working on something they inherited and they don't have the same singular vision, so even though they are trying to do more they just get less done with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T12:59:06-08:00","id":1175539,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I agree with that. Volume 5 has had a definite focus in terms of screen time, namely on advancing the maiden/relic story, as well as some of the characters' arcs, at the expense of world building and action on screen.<br /> <br /> They know what they want to focus on, but a) I think it's a mistake to cease focusing on the action to this degree (by this point they are clearly avoiding having to animate fight scenes on screen) and b) I don't think they are doing the plot stuff well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T09:28:46-08:00","id":1175778,"title":"","content":"Just saw the episode and I will weigh in on that whole &quot;take what is mine&quot; line. When Cinder first stole her portion of the fall maiden's powers Cinder tells someone ,presumably Salem, something to the effect of&quot;I feel hungry. but I like it.&quot; Now presumably this was a side effect of splitting the power, but she still had to deal with that for a while. Not to mention after within hours ,at best, of getting the full power of the Fall Maiden, Ruby ended up taking Cinder out. I honestly wouldn't be surprised if that left ended up creating a hunger for power, and one Salem ended up nurturing to make a more effective servant.<br /> <br /> That said the line doesn't really indicate that Cinder has a preexisting claim. More likely she believes the powers of the maidens are hers by a destiny thing, that she is worthy to possess them and no one else. Because Cinder's line to Vernal was saying that Vernal wasn't worthy of having the powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 01-13-2018, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T11:08:02-08:00","id":1175802,"title":"","content":"Cinder\u2019s hunger could have been a result of the Grimm bug glove that infused into her body with the Maiden powers. The one that formed her personal digit on her back as a tattoo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T11:28:46-08:00","id":1175808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1175778#post1175778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just saw the episode and I will weigh in on that whole &quot;take what is mine&quot; line. When Cinder first stole her portion of the fall maiden's powers Cinder tells someone ,presumably Salem, something to the effect of&quot;I feel hungry. but I like it.&quot; Now presumably this was a side effect of splitting the power, but she still had to deal with that for a while. Not to mention after within hours ,at best, of getting the full power of the Fall Maiden, Ruby ended up taking Cinder out. I honestly wouldn't be surprised if that left ended up creating a hunger for power, and one Salem ended up nurturing to make a more effective servant.<br /> <br /> That said the line doesn't really indicate that Cinder has a preexisting claim. More likely she believes the powers of the maidens are hers by a destiny thing, that she is worthy to possess them any no one else. Because Cinder's line to Vernal was saying that Vernal wasn't worthy of having the powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might explain her surprisingly somber reaction to Pyrrha's line of &quot;Do you believe in destiny?&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> As for today's episode...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Well, we know where the Fight Budget went.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 01-13-2018, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T13:38:26-08:00","id":1175834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1175778#post1175778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just saw the episode and I will weigh in on that whole &quot;take what is mine&quot; line. When Cinder first stole her portion of the fall maiden's powers Cinder tells someone ,presumably Salem, something to the effect of&quot;I feel hungry. but I like it.&quot; Now presumably this was a side effect of splitting the power, but she still had to deal with that for a while. Not to mention after within hours ,at best, of getting the full power of the Fall Maiden, Ruby ended up taking Cinder out. I honestly wouldn't be surprised if that left ended up creating a hunger for power, and one Salem ended up nurturing to make a more effective servant.<br /> <br /> That said the line doesn't really indicate that Cinder has a preexisting claim. More likely she believes the powers of the maidens are hers by a destiny thing, that she is worthy to possess them and no one else. Because Cinder's line to Vernal was saying that Vernal wasn't worthy of having the powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm... I don't really disagree with any of the points you raise bar the conclusion, but you misremembered the line IIRC. It's 'Take what was mine'. Emphasis on the was. Take what is mine could fit with what you're saying as a shortened form of 'take what is mine by right' or the like, but was mine doesn't fit with Cinder wanting Spring's power if she never had it before.<br /> <br /> Could just be a weird line, a misused bit of grammar, but it seems like a weird mistake to me.<br /> <br /> As to this week.... predictions for next week!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Jaune is dead.<br /> <br /> Raven is likely dead. She spent most of her power on that fight and Yang is seven kinds of pissed off. I'm wondering if Cinder's gonna pull a revival and offer Yang a spot on Team Salem. Stranger things have happened.<br /> <br /> Also, where's Watts gotten to?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> PS, holy Maidens, <i>that fight</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T14:04:29-08:00","id":1175840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1175834#post1175834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mmm... I don't really disagree with any of the points you raise bar the conclusion, but you misremembered the line IIRC. It's 'Take what was mine'. Emphasis on the was. Take what is mine could fit with what you're saying as a shortened form of 'take what is mine by right' or the like, but was mine doesn't fit with Cinder wanting Spring's power if she never had it before.<br /> <br /> Could just be a weird line, a misused bit of grammar, but it seems like a weird mistake to me.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not misremebering it, I checked again to be sure. Even turned on the subtitles, the line is &quot; I will take what is mine.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T14:40:15-08:00","id":1175845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1175840#post1175840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not misremebering it, I checked again to be sure. Even turned on the subtitles, the line is &quot; I will take what is mine.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Subtitles? On YouTube? Those things autogen.<br /> <br /> *shrug* You heard what you heard I guess. I still hear it as was. Just listened to it again: that's undoubtedly a W sound IMO. I... guess this is an impasse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T15:20:35-08:00","id":1175850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1175808#post1175808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Well, we know where the Fight Budget went.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Also the budget for drawing every character in the scene? Poor Mercury and Emerald flickered in and out of existence.<br /> <br /> And how long was Yang falling? Due to the upstairs reaction shot to the earthquake, we know she jumped down before the maiden-mash reached its climax. But she still conveniently arrives too late to see anything revealing Raven as a maiden. Nothing stopped the writers from simply having Yang jump later (more Yang vs Mercury! or rather, any!), so...why this way? Blake could have walked in later, too, if that was meant to the reason.<br /> I think the fight downstairs was meant to play first, followed by the upstairs scenes (the chronology works better that way), but they realised that the upstairs scenes would have been a letdown after that fight. (why does adam now go down to a single punch?) </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T08:47:23-08:00","id":1176293,"title":"","content":"Raven's katana is basically the ultimate artifact for Single Shining Point into the Void. Every time you draw from the hilt, you get to choose which type of <s>Dust</s> Jade it's made of, for all its versatile elemental implications.<br /> <br /> Also, this was, hands down, the most animesque fight in the entire series. Which I personally don't think of as a bad thing.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I loved how each had their own &quot;CONJURE GIANT SWORD&quot; animation. Cinder dived right into the Uncanny Valley, looking all <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/LimpAndLivid\" target=\"_blank\">limp and livid</a>, while Raven was almost meditative and self-reflective.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12013-artex","name":"artex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12013_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T11:13:55-08:00","id":1176326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1176293#post1176293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raven's katana is basically the ultimate artifact for Single Shining Point into the Void. Every time you draw from the hilt, you get to choose which type of <s>Dust</s> Jade it's made of, for all its versatile elemental implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve already started trying to convert it into an Artifact. Looking into how each form of jade can be used to enhance or supplement Single Point\u2019s tricks. <br /> <br /> However, Raven\u2019s weapon is so versatile in possible applications that I want to wait until the Dragon-Blooded drops.<br /> <br /> The way I see it working, each color of jade blade helps a Terrestrial enter the associated Aura State, and the blade can also be shattered in place of expending that Aura state.<br /> <br /> Blades could also be shattered for sorcererous motes, but only for elemental spells matching the color.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T11:19:42-08:00","id":1176330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1176293#post1176293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raven's katana is basically the ultimate artifact for Single Shining Point into the Void. Every time you draw from the hilt, you get to choose which type of <s>Dust</s> Jade it's made of, for all its versatile elemental implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>I loved the visuals they got out of both of them fighting with breakable swords. While Dust and glass are both presumably more frangible than steel, the shattering blades helped sell the strength of their blows and the overall power level of the fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T11:34:36-08:00","id":1176559,"title":"","content":"Well, finally after 3 seasons of waiting I got to see Raven go all out and was mot disappointed. Cant wait till Saturday to watch that again on my big screen (the RT site video player doesnt work on any device hooked up to my TV so I watched it on my tablet). I hope they're not setting up a Yang/Raven fight though. I'd prefer a reconciliation.<br /> <br /> Now what happens to Emerald?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T11:37:37-08:00","id":1176560,"title":"","content":"Got a chromecast? The chrome cast on chromecast works perfectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T13:58:48-08:00","id":1176594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1176559#post1176559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, finally after 3 seasons of waiting I got to see Raven go all out and was mot disappointed. Cant wait till Saturday to watch that again on my big screen (the RT site video player doesnt work on any device hooked up to my TV so I watched it on my tablet). I hope they're not setting up a Yang/Raven fight though. I'd prefer a reconciliation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yang's down an arm, I don't think she'd be looking for a fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T14:50:34-08:00","id":1176610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1176594#post1176594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yang's down an arm, I don't think she'd be looking for a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>She couldn't have gone down there expecting anything else, frankly.<br /> <br /> Plus, her Semblance should be plenty charged up by this point, and her Aura is unbroken.<br /> <br /> It might not be immediately obvious to Yang, but Raven's Aura is broken, along with a significant number of her blades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T19:20:49-08:00","id":1176666,"title":"","content":"It's fine, Cinder fell into a very deep pit that we can't see the bottom of, so she's very definitely dead forever and I guess the Fall Maiden power has been inherited by, uh, someone random or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T21:22:21-08:00","id":1176687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1176666#post1176666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's fine, Cinder fell into a very deep pit that we can't see the bottom of, so she's very definitely dead forever and I guess the Fall Maiden power has been inherited by, uh, someone random or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>If she HAD died, it probably WOULD have gone to someone random, since her last thoughts probably would have been about Raven, who is too old to receive the power and also already has one of Maiden mantles already.<br /> <br /> It's apparently impossible to become a Double Maiden normally, which is why Raven and Vernal didn't expect Cinder to attack Vernal before the door opened.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cinder doesn't seem to care enough about Emerald to make her the last in her thoughts, especially when Emerald isn't even present, and we really would have noticed Emerald gaining the powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T21:33:56-08:00","id":1176689,"title":"","content":"Cinder is still alive. No way her last though was not about how much she hates Ruby. So since she hadnt shown signs of getting it yet.....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Btw, on the subject of Ships, is there a name for Taiyang+Raven? As in them getting back together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T21:43:45-08:00","id":1176690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1176689#post1176689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw, on the subject of Ships, is there a name for Taiyang+Raven? As in them getting back together.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Never, never&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or &quot;Nevermore&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T23:31:27-08:00","id":1176704,"title":"","content":"Given how little we saw most of the players in the upstairs fight once the downstairs fight started, I'm not confident we can rule out that one of them did gain Cinder's power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T23:45:35-08:00","id":1176706,"title":"","content":"If every episode was held to this standard, I wouldn't ever bitch about anything. Probably. Spoilers ahead.<br /> <br /> That was great! This is what S4 and S5 <i>should </i>have been delivering throughout. Raven v Cinder was incredible- I like that it moved more into high power anime fight style than the grounded videogame style, usually that's a bad thing (Naruto, for example, and Dragon Ball into DBZ), but since these are the Maidens having MaidenBrawl I think its fitting.<br /> <br /> Lets get to brass tacks:<br /> -Emerald and Mercury pop in and out of frame.<br /> -Hazel's Semblance is he can <i>ignore pain</i>, and this let's him handle the strain of injecting Dust... so anyone can inject dust and go monster mode? Do I have that right?<br /> -For how badass and hyped he's been all series, Adam goes down like a chump. He falls for Blake's shadow clone even though he's her exlover/mentor and should have seen that coming, and her counterattack is <i>a punch to the head</i>. Weak shit Adam.<br /> -The White Fang Goonsquad get a big &quot;we civilians and loved ones will stand up to you&quot; moment, Blake is there, Gheera their former leader is there, hundreds of their friends and family are there, and the airship police are there. The bombs are disarmed and they are hopelessly surrounded. So, naturally, after they have a &quot;Is that you, brother?&quot; moment they decide, sure, lets attack because our boss is getting shouty.<br /> <br /> That's it really. No lengthy tirade. I can't stress how much of a relief the maiden fight was, and how glad I am that the Maiden Subplot looks like it's finally paying off enough to get out of the way. Some things were clunky- Yang running passed Emerald and Mercury could have been a better transition. People are still guilty of &quot;standing around idly while their hated enemies are talking&quot; (something the <i>show itself</i> ridiculed in S3 with the JNPR fight), and stuff.<br /> <br /> But the animation was better and the passion came back. The show got out of its own way and I feel excited rather than cynical.<br /> <br /> Like, take Hazel. He lightning hadoken's Ren which sets up that he can channel lightning into attacks (which he did to Qrow last episode, but this was much more overt and noticeable). He moved like a dangerous combatant and not a jumping frog made out of lead. He deals with Nora in a way that is justified in scene and <b>not</b> just a setup for &quot;Nora eats lightning&quot;.<br /> <br /> This episode was good. Next week will hopefully be good. If you can deliver stuff like this more often I will be very happy with you, RWBY.<br /> <br /> (post script- This episode, while freaking great, doesn't makeup for the lackluster S5. I'm not going to say that &quot;it's all been worth it&quot; or anything, just that this level is the level I want to see from the show)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T06:25:01-08:00","id":1176761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1176706#post1176706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-For how badass and hyped he's been all series, Adam goes down like a chump. He falls for Blake's shadow clone even though he's her exlover/mentor and should have seen that coming, and her counterattack is <i>a punch to the head</i>. Weak shit Adam.</div> </div> </div> </div>That whole exchange doesn't quite &quot;work&quot; I think.<br /> <br /> If you look at it closely? Either Blake has Gumby arms, or Adam should have sliced her in two. He cuts towards his right in a flat arc, and she drops a shadow clone while dodging to her left (his right,) in other words in the exact direction he's cutting... but she's still close enough to him to clock him with her arms, meaning she should still be close enough to him for his sword to have gone right through her. And she doesn't step back in, either. That could have easily been avoided by animating the cut differently or having her nail him with Gambol Shroud instead.<br /> <br /> ... I know it sounds like I'm nit-picking but that really bothered me! Seriously, watch the scene again, or better yet a gifset. It's REALLY OBVIOUS that Adam's sword phases right through Blake.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T01:27:26-08:00","id":1176910,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile, on the interwebs<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i0.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/original/001/332/412/a0e.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10