 even worse human being than we already thought she was. Good job, Raven. Way to raise that bar.<br /> <br /> Tai, do NOT fucking let her back in that house. <i>Do not.</i> I'm goddamn serious. She's gonna rock up there looking all miserable and alone and you're gonna look at that gap between the top of her boots and the bottom of her skirt and the part of you that's forever a seventeen year old with a crush on his goth teammate is going to try and make you make a bad decision. <i>Do not listen to it.</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T02:59:24-08:00","id":1178017,"title":"","content":"That bar was indeed risen. I hoped the maiden thing was a consequence of a completely different story. Oh well, she's only getting worse XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T04:40:19-08:00","id":1178723,"title":"","content":"So I guess that ship I mused about is under full sail?<br /> <br /> Stll needs a name?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T12:53:22-08:00","id":1178906,"title":"","content":"Question: Assuming there was only ever going to be one fully animated fight in this finale, which one did you want to see the most?<br /> <br /> I ask because while impressive, I don't think the maiden fight was it for me. Cinder was not a focus of this season (and what screen time she did get seems to have forgotten about her troubled mind from season 4), and Raven had no particular beef with her until Vernal died. They had no history, no buildup of tension.<br /> <br /> Raven vs Crow, Ruby vs Cinder, Jaune vs Cinder, Yang vs Raven, Blake vs Adam, Oz vs Leo...all of these had clear tension and some of them were clearly being built up this season, only to not really happen (at least on screen).<br /> <br /> I think Raven vs Crow should have been the big fight of the season.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T13:11:31-08:00","id":1178912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1177991#post1177991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spoils I guess.<br /> <br /> It's kind of impressive that Raven is an even worse human being than we already thought she was. Good job, Raven. Way to raise that bar.<br /> <br /> Tai, do NOT fucking let her back in that house. <i>Do not.</i> I'm goddamn serious. She's gonna rock up there looking all miserable and alone and you're gonna look at that gap between the top of her boots and the bottom of her skirt and the part of you that's forever a seventeen year old with a crush on his goth teammate is going to try and make you make a bad decision. <i>Do not listen to it.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Well Tai didn't look happy to see her.<br /> <br /> Granted, I'm pretty sure that if Tai helps her out it won't be because he loved her once as much as it'll be because she needs help and Taiyang is too good for this crazy death world.<br /> <br /> Seriously though, I wouldn't mind seeing her and Taiyang interact more. Mostly because I felt like Tai and Yang's parts in V4 were the highlights","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T18:52:42-08:00","id":1179045,"title":"","content":"so....who got the power of the Autumn Maiden? <br /> <br /> No sign Ruby got it (my guess, as Cinder seemed focused on how much she hated her). But Emerald didn't show any Anima flare when she fired off her MegaSalem illusion either (there are thos on some discussions who thought she would).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T18:53:38-08:00","id":1179046,"title":"","content":"and now, because this made me giggle:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i0.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/newsfeed/001/334/777/0da.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T19:47:38-08:00","id":1179063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1179045#post1179045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so....who got the power of the Autumn Maiden?<br /> <br /> No sign Ruby got it (my guess, as Cinder seemed focused on how much she hated her). But Emerald didn't show any Anima flare when she fired off her MegaSalem illusion either (there are thos on some discussions who thought she would).</div> </div> </div> </div>If anyone was in Cinder's last thoughts, it would be Raven, who couldn't receive the power. Cinder doesn't actually care about Emerald, and would sooner think of Salem.<br /> <br /> I doubt Cinder's actually dead, but if she is, the power likely went to someone at random, as it does when the last person thought of doesn't fit the criteria.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T19:58:28-08:00","id":1179067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1177991#post1177991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spoils I guess.<br /> <br /> It's kind of impressive that Raven is an even worse human being than we already thought she was. Good job, Raven. Way to raise that bar.<br /> <br /> Tai, do NOT fucking let her back in that house. <i>Do not.</i> I'm goddamn serious. She's gonna rock up there looking all miserable and alone and you're gonna look at that gap between the top of her boots and the bottom of her skirt and the part of you that's forever a seventeen year old with a crush on his goth teammate is going to try and make you make a bad decision. <i>Do not listen to it.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm willing to bet you a supplemental Exalted book that Yang and Ruby will have a baby sister before the series is over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T20:11:16-08:00","id":1179069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1179063#post1179063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt Cinder's actually dead, but if she is, the power likely went to someone at random, as it does when the last person thought of doesn't fit the criteria.</div> </div> </div> </div>Echoing this. Rules of realism would say that being frozen and falling down a chasm would kill someone.<br /> <br /> Rules of drama and recurring villains, however... I'll believe Cinder's dead when we either see the body, when we see a new Fall Maiden, or when Salem says &quot;Well shit, we need a replacement for Cinder, who is dead.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T20:51:37-08:00","id":1179083,"title":"","content":"Well from what we've Cinder seems to not be a full human anymore, you know if her attack on Vernal is an indicator. This could very much be of a modified entity that is barely human enough to qualify as a viable host for her powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T19:24:46-08:00","id":1180323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1178906#post1178906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Assuming there was only ever going to be one fully animated fight in this finale, which one did you want to see the most?</div> </div> </div> </div>The battle royale in Haven's foyer.<br /> <br /> YES, that's one fight. You put them all together in a single room! That's a single fight even though there's a ton of people there, like how the tournament fights had eight people in each one but were still singleton fights.<br /> <br /> More to the point, it was Teams RW_Y and RNJR encountering the authors of all their misfortune for the first time in two volumes. That's a big fucking deal, and it demands a big fucking fight. Cinder and Raven? That's a fight you slot in if you have the resources. That's your &quot;okay, we're gonna have some fun with this&quot; fight, like Qrow on Winter was. (Although Qrow on Winter did actual narrative work as well.) It's not your flagship.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anyone was in Cinder's last thoughts, it would be Raven, who couldn't receive the power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know this?<br /> <br /> Like, Cinder seemed pretty sure she could go all double maideny. Cinder explicitly has an arm that sucks out Maiden powers, so that might be an exception, but where has it been said one person can't bear the power of multiple Maidens through the natural line of succession? Legitimate question, no snark.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm willing to bet you a supplemental Exalted book that Yang and Ruby will have a baby sister before the series is over </div> </div> </div>Jesus god, that's skin-crawling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rules of drama and recurring villains, however...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just that, basic... narrative closure.<br /> <br /> Cinder, as I said above, is the author of everyones misfortune. Sure, Salem is the moving force behind her, but Cinder, you know, fucking murdered Pyrrha Nikos in front of the shows main character and then got herself literally maimed by said main characters weird special power that makes her special. She spent all of Volume 4 obsessed with revenge. Her boss felt like indulging her to the point of detailing one of her goons to retrieve Ruby, and Cinder's last scene in V4 is literally her making Emerald create hallucinatory Ruby's that she can throw fire at!<br /> <br /> Cinder's narrative arc flows through Ruby and probably (ugh) through Jaune. It probably also flows through Emerald. It doesn't terminate underneath Haven in a fight with Raven. Or, if it does, it means Miles and Kerry are fucking shitty writers.<br /> <br /> This volume was just... it wasn't that good. It may be the worst one, in fact. It's the longest volume by far, and very little happened, and the stuff that did happen was largely blah. It's like they've forgotten how to pace, and they've forgotten how to leverage their large and growing cast, and they've forgotten how to close out narrative arcs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T21:07:21-08:00","id":1180335,"title":"","content":"Man you guys are hard to please. Remind me not to try to ST an Exalted chronicle fir any of you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T23:48:36-08:00","id":1180356,"title":"","content":"An exalted chronicle has one major advantage over RWBY: No need for a special effects budget. If you end up with a confrontation that demands 2 hours of fighting to let every protagonist shine and find their closure, you do it. This show either didn't have the budget or...made a really bad call in skimping over most of the confrontation this way.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T03:51:01-08:00","id":1180376,"title":"","content":"So, something I was wondering now. What happens to Ilia? Will she be a peripheral hanger on, like Sun? Or will she be joining in more.<br /> <br /> While I was expecting Oscar to join the JNPR remnants (forming team ORNJ), Ilia could fit in too forming Team JRNI (journey).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T03:53:21-08:00","id":1180377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1180376#post1180376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, something I was wondering now. What happens to Ilia? Will she be a peripheral hanger on, like Sun? Or will she be joining in more.<br /> <br /> While I was expecting Oscar to join the JNPR remnants (forming team ORNJ), Ilia could fit in too forming Team JRNI (journey).</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would she join RNJ? She's about the white fang and blake. Those guys got nothing on her.<br /> And now blake's kind of the center of a harem...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T08:41:49-08:00","id":1180424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1180376#post1180376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, something I was wondering now. What happens to Ilia? Will she be a peripheral hanger on, like Sun? Or will she be joining in more.<br /> <br /> While I was expecting Oscar to join the JNPR remnants (forming team ORNJ), Ilia could fit in too forming Team JRNI (journey).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I'd describe Sun as a peripheral hanger on. He's been in all five seasons, and in at least two of them there's an argument for Sun as &quot;main cast&quot; rather than &quot;supporting character.&quot;<br /> <br /> The smart thing to do is to write Ilia out somehow. RWBY has the classic Miles Luna problem; the cast constantly balloons but it isn't actually all that great at using it effectively and sometimes flounders with what to with everyone.<br /> <br /> I can see a potential use for Ilia going forward; they're going to Atlas (maybe the city setting will actually get used, unlike in V4 and unlike Mistral!) and Ilia is Atlesian.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T10:58:35-08:00","id":1180454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1180323#post1180323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This volume was just... it wasn't that good. It may be the worst one, in fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, if I had to pick one for the worst one (though I'd call that relative because I like all of RWBY), I'd probably point at V2.<br /> <br /> I mean, V2 had a lot of technical problems (JANKY animation, in many ways worse than some of V1's jankiness. Remember Cinder's disappearing mask?) and a lot of pacing problems. V2 had that plot tumor of The Fucking Dance, had Jaune at his absolute worst and most &quot;Wait I thought the show was about Team RWBY?&quot;, in terms of wasted time it not only had a bunch of painful Jaune Flirting, it also had an awkward dance number (the choreography was alright, but the MoCap animation with Poser was NOT up to capturing it).<br /> <br /> Also, IMO, the Breach is probably the least satisfying climax. There's a LOT of narrative bullshit in it, that looking back on it makes me legitimately annoyed.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh no, the White Fang have burst through the wall! The Grimm are inside the city! This is like the catalyst for Attack on Titan, people are going to be dying, Huntsmen and Huntresses are going to be scrambling to try and control the damage. SURELY this will be something that has long-lasting and far-reaching impact and implications-<br /> <br /> &quot;Aaaaaaand the Grimm Swarm was handled with one team of Second Year Students, two teams of <b>FIRST</b>-year students, a teacher, a dog, and maybe Emerald and Mercury helping. And the breach was fixed in like twenty seconds, and ten of that was Glynda's Angry Walk. Well nice to see that these threats and dangers built up in living on Remnant are actually total pushovers. Why are Grimm a threat again?&quot;<br /> <br /> Volume two also introduced Neptune, and marked the precise LAST time he would contribute meaningfully to anything in getting a single hit on the Paladin.<br /> <br /> Like, the only things V2 had going for it were the fight scenes, which is what RWBY was riding on, and introducing the Painting The Town outfits which were <i>adorable</i> outfits. There were also some great character moments, mostly with Team RWBY during Blake and Yang's talk in the classroom, as well as their introspection in Mountain Glen as to why they wanted to be Huntresses. Between that, though? WHOOOOOOOLE lotta fluff.<br /> <br /> In hindsight it emphasizes the &quot;Style over Substance&quot; and how heavily Rule of Cool outweighed literally everything else in the show, often to its detriment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 01-29-2018, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T13:17:06-08:00","id":1180486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1180454#post1180454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, if I had to pick one for the worst one (though I'd call that relative because I like all of RWBY), I'd probably point at V2.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm unsure how to properly contextualize V2 in my own mind because I peaced out of RWBY during the back half of V1, when they were releasing five-minute episodes every other week (it was moving sooooooo sloooooooow) and didn't come back in until midway through V3. So while I've always found V2 decent, I can't help but wonder if I'd have found it AS decent if I couldn't just mainline it in one two-hour gulp and move on to V3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, V2 had a lot of technical problems (JANKY animation, in many ways worse than some of V1's jankiness. Remember Cinder's disappearing mask?) and a lot of pacing problems. </div> </div> </div>Pacing problems might as well be RWBY's House Words.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> V2 had that plot tumor of The Fucking Dance, </div> </div> </div>You know, I liked the dance. Kind of. I like the <i>idea</i> of the dance.<br /> <br /> That thing had a lot of buildup surrounding Team RWBY and then ended up being...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> had Jaune at his absolute worst and most &quot;Wait I thought the show was about Team RWBY?&quot;, </div> </div> </div>Yes, this. Jaune's only role in the runup to the dance was harassing Weiss. That's it.<br /> <br /> Like... Ruby didn't want to go to the dance, and then she went, and then her good friend Penny, who she just found out is a robot lady, is there! It sure would have been nice if they'd talked, if they'd maybe danced, if Ruby had gotten a thing where she found out dressing up and talking to friends at a dance was neat. Blake and Yang had a whole goddamn... THING leading up to the dance, and Yang is all &quot;save me a dance&quot; and we don't see them talk? Neptune and Weiss have a whole thing that's never really resolved either.<br /> <br /> Instead it's all Pyrrha and Jaune. Pyrrha's stuff was pretty good, but it felt... badly executed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, IMO, the Breach is probably the least satisfying climax. There's a LOT of narrative bullshit in it, that looking back on it makes me legitimately annoyed. </div> </div> </div>Right? Although to be fair, Breach isn't undercut until V3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Oh no, the White Fang have burst through the wall! The Grimm are inside the city! This is like the catalyst for Attack on Titan, people are going to be dying, Huntsmen and Huntresses are going to be scrambling to try and control the damage. SURELY this will be something that has long-lasting and far-reaching impact and implications-<br /> <br /> &quot;Aaaaaaand the Grimm Swarm was handled with one team of Second Year Students, two teams of <b>FIRST</b>-year students, a teacher, a dog, and maybe Emerald and Mercury helping. And the breach was fixed in like twenty seconds, and ten of that was Glynda's Angry Walk. Well nice to see that these threats and dangers built up in living on Remnant are actually total pushovers. Why are Grimm a threat again?&quot; </div> </div> </div>There's a YouTuber who goes by the name FMF who does a lot of discussion, analysis, and deconstruction of RWBY. Some of it is absolutely ridiculous; he always puts the worst possible spin on any information in order to declare a plot hole or retcon. He insisted for two straight years that Mistral must have a way to tame Grimm because of the Kingdoms of Remnant board game, for example, rather than accepting the much more likely scenario that in the context of the board game, players would have the option to play cards simulating Grimm being drawn into, and participating in, battles. Because, you know, it also has a Sandstorm card, and it seems unlikely Vacuo has weather control technology. He got really angry about Remnant having things called Kingdoms that are actually democracies. (I wanted to ask him if he gets really angry that the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland calls itself a kingdom.) Stuff like that.<br /> <br /> But a lot of his takedowns are super on-point and insightful, and one of them is how the Breach is constructed. He really catalyzed that for me and got a lot of things that were floating around in my head to come together. To wit:<br /> <br /> The Breach in Volume 2 is structured as a narrowly averted crisis; Grimm got into the city, and some people got hurt and there was some property damage, but it was swiftly contained with limited loss of life. Team RWBY is happy and celebratory afterwards! They don't act like people whose city has just gotten its asshole reamed with Grimm with immense loss of life and property, they act like conquering heroes who just got their first major win as budding Hunters. The narrative treats them like this.<br /> <br /> Then we get to V3... and suddenly it's like &quot;Whoops! We need the Breach to have been a huge tragedy. We need it to represent an enormous failure on the part of those responsible for keeping Vale safe, because Cinder's whole plan relies on that. What if we just... ACT like it was a huge tragedy? We'll just have everyone act like that and hope our audience doesn't notice!&quot;<br /> <br /> They almost, <i>almost</i> get away with it because we the audience were primed to want to believe that anyway, and only Team CFVY showing up and being absolute combat monsters that made it not so.<br /> <br /> (Cinder's entire plan holds up great if you don't look too closely at it, because in the broad strokes &quot;incite a riot, attack Beacon with a huge army of Grimm backed up by White Fang, use distraction to score Maiden powers and/or Relic&quot; is a great plan. But man, if you dive into the details your head starts to hurt.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Volume two also introduced Neptune, and marked the precise LAST time he would contribute meaningfully to anything in getting a single hit on the Paladin. </div> </div> </div>The irony is that Neptune has been damn useful and is filling a needed role in RWBY Chibi. But otherwise he hasn't done much other than being Neptune. He contributed meaningfully to the fight with Team INDG (although he'd have been the MVP of that fight if Sun were a better leader) but that was a filler fight. I mean, in V5, nobody on Team RWBY even cared enough about him to go &quot;we're super shorthanded, we should call up our old buddy Neptune and see if he can pitch in.&quot; Sun didn't even consider, apparently, re-assembling Team SSSN for the minor little matter of &quot;the White Fang are about to do to Haven what they did to Beacon&quot; which you'd think would be of some minor concern to Neptune, Scarlet, and Sage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like, the only things V2 had going for it were the fight scenes, which is what RWBY was riding on, and introducing the Painting The Town outfits which were <i>adorable</i> outfits. There were also some great character moments, mostly with Team RWBY during Blake and Yang's talk in the classroom, as well as their introspection in Mountain Glen as to why they wanted to be Huntresses. Between that, though? WHOOOOOOOLE lotta fluff. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I gotta agree here. And honestly the introspection on Mountain Glenn was kinda hamfisted.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T15:54:28-08:00","id":1180522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1180486#post1180486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm unsure how to properly contextualize V2 in my own mind because I peaced out of RWBY during the back half of V1, when they were releasing five-minute episodes every other week (it was moving sooooooo sloooooooow) and didn't come back in until midway through V3. So while I've always found V2 decent, I can't help but wonder if I'd have found it AS decent if I couldn't just mainline it in one two-hour gulp and move on to V3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, as I said, 'Worst season' isn't how I'd describe it. I still had fun with V2.<br /> <br /> But I would certainly put it as the <b>weakest</b> Volume overall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T19:28:23-08:00","id":1180577,"title":"","content":"I would like to say, as the season winds down... y'all have been fabulous. This has been some top-notch RWBY commentatin' and arguin' here in this thread. Big shouts out to Kyman, Sunder, Aquillion, Lioness, Bjorn, VHD, and yes, even Sorcerous Overlord. You all are great, and even if I don't have a season roundup post I will see you all for V6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T19:54:25-08:00","id":1180580,"title":"","content":"I rather liked the board game scene in V2. That was exposition the way it should be done. We see the world map in the show for the first time (I'm pretty sure), all the kingdoms are name dropped along with a few traits being hinted at, we learn that, though allies for now, they are rivals in the end (because the game pits the against each other) and even the use of grim as terror weapons is foreshadowed by having the kingdoms play them as trap cards against each other. And we get some nice fun character moments. I think that was one of the best non-fight scenes in all of the show so far.<br /> <br /> Compare that to V3 with Weiss and Winter's chat, explaining their family semblence to each other. That was exposition the way it should never be done (see &quot;as you know, bob...&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T21:09:28-08:00","id":1180598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1180580#post1180580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I rather liked the board game scene in V2. That was exposition the way it should be done. We see the world map in the show for the first time (I'm pretty sure), all the kingdoms are name dropped along with a few traits being hinted at, we learn that, though allies for now, they are rivals in the end (because the game pits the against each other) and even the use of grim as terror weapons is foreshadowed by having the kingdoms play them as trap cards against each other. And we get some nice fun character moments. I think that was one of the best non-fight scenes in all of the show so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>No joke, I'd pay for a real-life version of that boardgame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T21:23:57-08:00","id":1180599,"title":"","content":"So, how far into V6 do you think we'll see Penny 2.0?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T02:20:51-08:00","id":1180649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1180599#post1180599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how far into V6 do you think we'll see Penny 2.0?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would the penny comparison actually be called? Her maker is probably the only character that would think of that, and only if he's of that disposition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T03:30:25-08:00","id":1180656,"title":"","content":"I'm sure Ruby might make the link. Just fepends how similar or different the next one is","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T14:54:22-08:00","id":1180891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1180580#post1180580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I rather liked the board game scene in V2. That was exposition the way it should be done. We see the world map in the show for the first time (I'm pretty sure), all the kingdoms are name dropped along with a few traits being hinted at, we learn that, though allies for now, they are rivals in the end (because the game pits the against each other) and even the use of grim as terror weapons is foreshadowed by having the kingdoms play them as trap cards against each other. And we get some nice fun character moments. I think that was one of the best non-fight scenes in all of the show so far.<br /> <br /> Compare that to V3 with Weiss and Winter's chat, explaining their family semblence to each other. That was exposition the way it should never be done (see &amp;quot;as you know, bob...&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I saw a video on YouTube of that, showing how all the stuff they did as moves in the game forshadowed the events of the Battle of Beacon. Playing the dialog from the boardgame over clips from V3 everythinh they said happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T15:01:14-08:00","id":1180892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1180599#post1180599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how far into V6 do you think we'll see Penny 2.0?</div> </div> </div> </div>Penny nothing, I want some Winter action.<br /> <br /> When the camera was in Atlas, she was in Mistral. When the camera was in Mistral, she was in Atlas. If they get to Atlas and she's in Vacuo I'm going to be miffed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T21:06:35-08:00","id":1180999,"title":"","content":"Winter and the Winter Maiden<br /> <br /> I wonder if they'll introduce someone new? Or will it turn out to be Weiss' mom?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T02:31:30-08:00","id":1181053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1180999#post1180999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Winter and the Winter Maiden<br /> <br /> I wonder if they'll introduce someone new? Or will it turn out to be Weiss' mom?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Barring Salem, the Maidens seem to be the 4 single-most powerful individuals in the entire setting. So, much like Exalted, it makes sense that the writers give them a crippling weakness that has nothing to do with how strong they are.<br /> In Cinder's case, it's her greed and pettiness. In Raven's, it's her fear.<br /> <br /> The idea of Weiss's mom as the Winter Maiden rings to me personally a lot like (First Age) Lilith. All the strength in the world, and she's trapped in a sham marriage with a charming, abusive little shit who seems incapable of truly loving anyone but himself. And it's broken her in half.<br /> <br /> There's good writing potential there. A Maiden with room for character growth, whom we could actively root for, as she (hopefully, eventually) overcomes her abuser.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12013-artex","name":"artex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12013_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T02:33:04-08:00","id":1181054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1180999#post1180999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Winter and the Winter Maiden<br /> <br /> I wonder if they'll introduce someone new? Or will it turn out to be Weiss' mom?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given her implied tendencies to pass out drunk, I hope not.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I think this was spoken of before but I don't remember it anywhere: Why are the displayed elemental superpowers off the maidens mismatched with the 4 maidens tale?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T02:37:37-08:00","id":1181055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1181054#post1181054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, I think this was spoken of before but I don't remember it anywhere: Why are the displayed elemental superpowers off the maidens mismatched with the 4 maidens tale?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the writers (Miles, I think?) mentioned in RWBY Rewind that the Maiden &quot;powerset&quot; is identical. Although it's subject to personal preference, and may manifest differently between generations of the same season, all four control whichever elements they desire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12013-artex","name":"artex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12013_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T02:45:42-08:00","id":1181058,"title":"","content":"Gotcha, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T08:30:30-08:00","id":1181136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1181055#post1181055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the writers (Miles, I think?) mentioned in RWBY Rewind that the Maiden &quot;powerset&quot; is identical. Although it's subject to personal preference, and may manifest differently between generations of the same season, all four control whichever elements they desire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, that seems like a copout. Why on earth have seasonally themed Maidens who... are not seasonally themed?<br /> <br /> I mean, the inheritance can be controlled, so it isn't even a personality thing. You just have four people who are superpowered all in the same way, and you can only identify which one is spring/summer/fall/winter by the way they glow. Or at least, I hope the eye glow is dispositive, because otherwise there'd be literally no way of telling them apart.<br /> <br /> This seems very uninteresting to me. Give them seasonally themed powersets! That introduces tension, conflict, contrast.<br /> <br /> I hope they didn't make this decision solely because it makes animation easier.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T09:22:43-08:00","id":1181153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1180999#post1180999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Winter and the Winter Maiden<br /> <br /> I wonder if they'll introduce someone new? Or will it turn out to be Weiss' mom?</div> </div> </div> </div>Y'know I hope that Winter isn't in any way related to the Winter Maiden.<br /> <br /> Too on the nose. And Raven kinda took the piss out of the whole &quot;Names that match the season&quot; thing. Like she mocked Cinder's last name for being &quot;So on the nose she clearly chose it&quot;, and Vernal was a decoy.<br /> <br /> I saw people using that logic to try and say Summer was a Maiden, and my response was &quot;Nah, too easy&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T04:21:53-08:00","id":1181359,"title":"","content":"But we dont know Weiss's mom's name. So it probably wont be related if she is the Maiden<br /> <br /> and the Winter Maidennis Not Winter Schnee. She is shown to be not in on the secrets as part of the Oz-luminati, so cant have the powers they're trying to keep secret","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T10:16:54-08:00","id":1181432,"title":"","content":"Unless Winter was under their noses the whole time!<br /> <br /> But, I doubt it as Winter and Ironwood seem to have a very close communicative relationship, at least on mission-critical details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T10:50:12-08:00","id":1181439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1181359#post1181359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She is shown to be not in on the secrets as part of the Oz-luminati, so cant have the powers they're trying to keep secret</div> </div> </div> </div>Is she?<br /> <br /> Volume 3 can easily be interpreted as &quot;Jimmy Ironwood brought Winter inside. Qrow doesn't approve of this, and to keep the peace when Qrow demands Winter be exiled from the room Jimmy decides that the most junior member of the conspiracy, who just fucked up by launching a very public attack on a far more senior member, in public, can go cool her damn heels while the grownups talk.&quot;<br /> <br /> The key thing for me is that Winter tells Qrow (and nobody contradicts her) that the Ozluminati thought there was a chance Qrow had been compromised. Who told Winter that? And why did they tell her that? That scene only really makes sense in the context of &quot;Winter knows that Ironwood and Friends are part of a cabal fighting a secret shadow war against someone.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":4742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","user":"Murcushio","date":". 02-01-2018, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T11:11:36-08:00","id":1181444,"title":"","content":"It doesn't make much sense for Qrow to demand that she leaves the room if she's the Winter Maiden, though. Excluding a Maiden isn't really an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T17:24:09-08:00","id":1181529,"title":"","content":"More likely she just is in the know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T04:01:16-08:00","id":1181615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1180577#post1180577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to say, as the season winds down... y'all have been fabulous. This has been some top-notch RWBY commentatin' and arguin' here in this thread. Big shouts out to Kyman, Sunder, Aquillion, Lioness, Bjorn, VHD, and yes, even Sorcerous Overlord. You all are great, and even if I don't have a season roundup post I will see you all for V6.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well shit, somebody finally thinks I'm purdy, Ma! I've had a lot of &quot;getting my life together&quot; type shit for the last couple weeks. It was... rough. I wont post here that often anymore.<br /> Just as an aside, though, thank you. It honestly does mean a lot to me when people appreciate what I wrote even if it's just for rebuttal. It makes the effort feel worthwhile.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the last episode was good. The Raven/Yang talk was a lot better written then I thought it would be. The relic bit works as a mcguffin,<br /> <br /> Emerald showed some character for i think the, *counts fingers* 4th time so far.<br /> <br /> The show still couldn't decide what to do with Hazel, which is a shame. Virtually nothing happened to the lightning/Nora connection and it seems like he was a boss battle that was cut. Kind of a let down.<br /> <br /> The entire Adam subplot didn't build up to anything more than Blake getting over him, which makes him mad (nice characterization, guys! Actually good work there). For how hype he's been it feels like, i don't know, a DLC hook? I really question the storyboard on the whole Adam arc.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if the Salem vision was supposed to be 100% Emerald illusion or if Salem helped out a little, Ruby weakening seems like it fits the latter although the rage breaking point of Emerald coping with Cinder's death seems like it was probably the former. I won't speculate on how exactly the 3 villains made it out of the great hall and passed all the guards and faunus and sky ships. I'll hand wave Raven finding another way out of the maiden chamber too.<br /> <br /> Leo did nothing, and I know the show wanted to write him out but I'm surprised he didn't just book it out a window once he saw the demon jellyfish.<br /> <br /> Oscar doesn't seem like he's mad at ozpin for brain-jacking him but that could be addressed later.<br /> <br /> The team is back together and we have a direction for the next season.<br /> <br /> Overall Season Comments:<br /> Very Weak. The direction for this season wanted to do a lot and they didn't stick the landing. The maidens, the White Fang, getting RWBY back together, etc was a lot to get done and it clearly came at the expense of the action- I don't follow behind the scenes or interviews or side materials so I won't speculate on the dev side, but the action was extremely lackluster. Outside of the one main fight -Cinder/Raven-, there were clear moments when the animators switched into high gear for what anime fans might recognize as the &quot;Sakuga Money Shots&quot;. Cinder v Raven, as characters, didn't have any emotional build up and very little narrative build up. The clear intention was the &quot;surprise maiden reveal&quot; which, in my opinion, was little more than a bait and switch. S4 suffered from Splitting the Party and S5 had to put them back together. It had some payoff, I won't deny that, but it did not play to the shows strengths and everything was slowed down to try to keep the plates spinning.<br /> <br /> Pop the champaign, boys and girls. We did it.<br /> <br /> - - - -<br /> Oh, and<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1047_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1047\" data-vbnamecard=\"1047\">vampire hunter D</a> <br /> <br /> We're great players. We take everything into context and avoid <i>clearly bad decisions</i>. *wink*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T04:26:06-08:00","id":1181617,"title":"","content":"There was no handwave on Raven's departure. You can hear a portal opening off camera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T15:19:56-08:00","id":1181817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1181617#post1181617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was no handwave on Raven's departure. You can hear a portal opening off camera.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally missed that. I don't know why that didn't occur to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T16:37:01-08:00","id":1182425,"title":"","content":"That's probably also why she seems to have gone to Tai-yang in the after credits scene: He was the only one she had a portal connection to who wasn't right there at the place she as trying to leave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T07:55:28-08:00","id":1182925,"title":"","content":"I binged season 5 after waiting for every episode to come out. I pity everyone who didn't.<br /> <br /> I liked this season overall, but I get the impression that when they were writing out the script for it, they did it like a feature film. Specifically, they wrote one of those eastern action movies (like &quot;Bodyguards and Assassins&quot; or &quot;Curse of the Golden Flower&quot;) where you have hours of character development and maybe a short fight or two leading up to a climax of violence that lasts for most of the final act. And then they chopped up that film into 12-15 minute chunks to put on the internet. I felt like it all comes together pretty well <i>if you watch all of it at once, </i>but not so much if you're going by one episode per week. I thought this about Season 4 as well, but I don't recall 4 ending on cliffhangers quite as often.<br /> <br /> All the character development from season 4 has paid off. The girls have each shown in some way that they're growing as people - Ruby is a bit more confident and serious, Weiss a <i>lot</i> more connected to other people, Yang a bit less rash, and Blake has shed some of her baggage.<br /> <br /> The fight choreography was average-to-good. I wish there had been more prolonged fights, especially in the big melee at the end. I feel like that group battle was managed poorly, especially with how cuts between combatants were handled (How many times did a character stop what they were doing to watch another character's battle, only to get blindsided by an opponent they were ignoring?). OTOH, the fight between Raven and Cinder came out much better than I expected.<br /> <br /> There were a number of things I thought were strange that went unremarked on, though:<br /> * As previously noted - why does everyone get so offended that Ozpin turned Raven and Crow into birds? That's an oddly specific thing to be upset about, especially since neither of them seem to be bothered by it.<br /> * Blake killed Fennec. She threw him under a collapsing structure. That's the first time I'm sure any of the RWBY crew has outright murdered somebody, but nobody commented on it afterwards.<br /> * Qrow's semblance is that he's a jinx - he says that's why he fights alone, and that is presumably why people he fights against have oddly bad luck (e.g. Tyrian randomly falling through a roof during their fight in Season 4). That didn't come up all in this season though, or not in any way I'd recognize. And he's okay with fighting in a group again.<br /> * Watts didn't show up for the melee at the end. Where'd he go, then?<br /> <br /> ...And one thing I thought was just silly:<br /> * The White Fang apparently planted bombs all over Mystral academy, then stood around out in the open admiring their handiwork for hours while Adam's allies were fighting inside. Despite staring directly at the tower where the bombs were set, they didn't notice Ilia messing with them - well, okay, she's a chameleon. But then they were then blindsided by two enormous mobs of Faunus that they didn't notice... because their visors give them terrible peripheral vision, or something?<br /> <br /> There was a lot of good stuff this season, but also a fair bit of wasted potential. I'd say this season overall was stronger than 4 but weaker than 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 02-06-2018, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T06:48:38-08:00","id":1184368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1181136#post1181136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, that seems like a copout. Why on earth have seasonally themed Maidens who... are not seasonally themed?</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be Ozpin's way of honoring the original maidens, who might very well have been named after the four seasons.<br /> <br /> The Spring Maiden would thus be the inheritor of the powers given to the maiden who was named Spring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T23:08:05-08:00","id":1184641,"title":"","content":"I can't quote Semicasual for some reason, so:<br /> <br /> -I read Raven as implying that <i>she</i> was offended at having been turned into a bird. She didn't give a reason; I read it as part of her larger pattern of finding reasons that her decisions arise from being attacked and manipulated, rather than from fear and selfishness.<br /> <br /> -Fennec went to go take Ghira down and die in the process. Blake pulled Ghira away so he wouldn't die. Fennec's death was a result of his attempted murder, not a conscious decision on any other character's part, unless I missed something major. The wiki suggests I didn't, though.<br /> <br /> -I kind of thought that all of Qrow's old Huntsman/Huntress friends being dead was maybe a representation of his being a jinx? But yeah, it definitely didn't show up in any other fashion.<br /> <br /> I agree that Season 5 was stronger than 4, and not as strong as 3. I found Season 4 pretty frustrating, but 5 was mostly satisfying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T04:38:44-08:00","id":1185892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1184641#post1184641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-I kind of thought that all of Qrow's old Huntsman/Huntress friends being dead was maybe a representation of his being a jinx? But yeah, it definitely didn't show up in any other fashion</div> </div> </div> </div>Leonhart betrayed them to Salem. Qrow's Jynx only applies to people physically close to him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T22:43:27-08:00","id":1186183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1182925#post1182925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Blake killed Fennec. She threw him under a collapsing structure. That's the first time I'm sure any of the RWBY crew has outright murdered somebody, but nobody commented on it afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Season 2, the train fight. They straight-up kill a bunch of White Fang goons; shotgunning people with un-awakened Aura right in the face, hurling them from a swiftly moving train, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be Ozpin's way of honoring the original maidens, who might very well have been named after the four seasons.<br /> <br /> The Spring Maiden would thus be the inheritor of the powers given to the maiden who was named Spring.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a potential in-universe explanation. Narratively, tho... why have four maidens, each named for one of the seasons, who... have completely identical powersets? What is gained by that as opposed to indivdualizing them based on their season, which lets you do all kinds of cool thematic shit and also have fights where they try and leverage their powersets against various situations and potentially each other?<br /> <br /> It doesn't seem like a good idea. It's like if the Exalted Maidens all had the same powers and portfolios. That would be a lot duller than what we have now, wouldn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T23:13:59-08:00","id":1186189,"title":"","content":"It could also be that there other abilities we don't know yet. I mean yes it is entirely possible that the distinction is only based on which of the doors they can open, but it could also be that neither Cinder nor Raven have really learned the full suite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T04:58:32-08:00","id":1186247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1186183#post1186183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Season 2, the train fight. They straight-up kill a bunch of White Fang goons; shotgunning people with un-awakened Aura right in the face, hurling them from a swiftly moving train, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but none of those people are <i>confirmed </i>to be dead. In seasons 1 and 2, plenty of humans and faunus get beaten up and thrown off-screen with the implication being that they're just KO'd. <br /> <br /> Starting in season 3, Rooster Teeth has gotten less cagey about showing actual injuries (e.g. impalement, mutilation) that indicate actual, permanent damage. In Season 5, people get thrown around like ragdolls all the time, but it seems like most attacks only do cosmetic damage until it becomes narratively important that they actually hurt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T05:43:00-08:00","id":1186259,"title":"","content":"Shotgunning un-Aura\u2019ed people in the face?<br /> <br /> What makes you say mooks on Remnant don\u2019t know how to use their Aura?<br /> <br /> Your average American citizen doesn\u2019t know the first thing about guns, but your average gangster almost certainly does. They learn real fast, because they want to LIVE.<br /> <br /> Plus, on Remnant, there are high-school equivalent \u201ccombat schools\u201d, of which the White Fang grunts might have been dropouts or even graduates. <br /> <br /> Also remember that their base was in the Grimm-infested wilderness and ruins of a slain city. Setting one foot outside for sunlight and fresh air would risk their lives.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s an enormous excluded middle of skill between your average citizen and Ruby Rose. In a small army of mooks, no single mook needs to be capable of personally destroying a small army of Beowolves.<br /> <br /> Kali Belladonna has virtually no skill at fighting yet could use Aura to knock a trained assassin out cold and carry him one-handed through her house with simple brute force. Menagerie probably has a lot of manual laborers who could do the same, because it helps them survive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-15-2018, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T08:46:50-08:00","id":1186321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1186259#post1186259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shotgunning un-Aura\u2019ed people in the face?<br /> <br /> What makes you say mooks on Remnant don\u2019t know how to use their Aura?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right that this is something that's very, very hard to tell, especially back before they started actually animating aura. I had been making a completely unwarranted assumption that the mooks were just mooks; an awakened aura always seemed like it would be something special to me, but maybe tons and tons of people have it.<br /> <br /> You're right to call me out on that.<br /> <br /> That said, it raises a bunch of questions, doesn't it? Can people with an awakened aura casually tell if someone else has one? Because if not, a lot of the actions undertaken during that fight and others have to be recast in the light of people being willing to kill, because they don't know that the person they're about to shoot in the face at point-blank range will just shrug off the shot as opposed to having their head reduced to a fine pink mist. That doesn't make them bad people, or taking incorrect actions, but it does mean the protagonists have a lot more grit than we've maybe previously assumed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kali Belladonna has virtually no skill at fighting yet could use Aura to knock a trained assassin out cold and carry him one-handed through her house with simple brute force. </div> </div> </div>Do we actually know this? I don't think we have confirmation either way that Kali has an awakened aura, although Ghira almost certainly does.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T10:26:20-08:00","id":1186349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1185892#post1185892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Leonhart betrayed them to Salem. Qrow's Jynx only applies to people physically close to him.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bI mean, yeah. I was reaching.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1186321#post1186321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That said, it raises a bunch of questions, doesn't it? Can people with an awakened aura casually tell if someone else has one? Because if not, a lot of the actions undertaken during that fight and others have to be recast in the light of people being willing to kill, because they don't know that the person they're about to shoot in the face at point-blank range will just shrug off the shot as opposed to having their head reduced to a fine pink mist. That doesn't make them bad people, or taking incorrect actions, but it does mean the protagonists have a lot more grit than we've maybe previously assumed.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Pretty sure Remnant works more or less on the Ex3 combat engine, with slightly less abstraction in order to accommodate a less gritty fight experience. In Ex3, a successful withering attack looks like gaining the advantage; in Remnant, it may look like taking a bullet (but not an </span></span></span><i>important </i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bbullet). </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Mooks get &quot;defeated&quot; by Withering attacks. The protagonists define &quot;defeat&quot; as nonlethal for people and lethal for Grimm, because Grimm can't be KO'd. Important characters can be injured when they still have available Aura, but they're fare more likely to be injured when they've been Crashed. When an attack is going to be Decisive, this is usually clearly communicated to the viewer through a) the attacker's intent, b) the defender's exhaustion, and/or c) the defender's distraction. It seems like the characters more or less understand what kind of situation they're in; if Yang makes a Withering attack that defeats an extra, she gets the cool outcome she wants, rather than accidental headsplosions.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 02-15-2018, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T10:56:05-08:00","id":1186357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1186321#post1186321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">an awakened aura always seemed like it would be something special to me, but maybe tons and tons of people have it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You think Jaune is normal for his world.<br /> <br /> \u201cNormal\u201d for Remnant is the Vytal Tournament. Where the commentators talk about Aura and the score boards visibly track the percentage of Aura each competitor has left.<br /> <br /> \u201cNormal\u201d for Remnant are combat schools that serve as high schools. <br /> <br /> Jaune didn\u2019t know what Aura was. He had never been to combat school despite a burning desire to go and the talent to succeed. He is not normal for Remnant<br /> <br /> Oscar is much more normal than Jaune, and no one talks about \u201cawakening\u201d his Aura in the way that Second Edition talker about \u201cenlightening\u201d a mortal\u2019s Essence. Remnant isn\u2019t Creation; it has different setting conceits.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re told again and again that Aura is something every living thing has. Salem says that what sets one apart as a warrior is the skill to use and amplify their Aura. <br /> <br /> When Ozpin and the others talk about what Oscar needs to do, they talk about learning how to use the Aura he has in ways that he hasn\u2019t yet learned to invoke unconsciously. <br /> <br /> Pyrrha\u2019s technique forced that skill upon Jaune, who would have died in that forest. It\u2019s not necessary for Oscar because he had two months of safety to learn and the benefit of absorbing Ozpin\u2019s procedural memories. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can people with an awakened aura casually tell if someone else has one? </div> </div> </div>Blake attempted to take Torchwick hostage with a surprise blade to his throat. His Aura protection was probably unprepared. He stalled for time until he was ready to fire an explosive round under Blake\u2019s feet, just as close to himself. Why not do that sooner? Perhaps he needed time to activate his protection subtly, so that she wouldn\u2019t notice and act?<br /> <br /> Why didn\u2019t Sienna Khan have her Aura ready? Adam made sure to make it look like he planned to capture and hold her, what with having so many men available to detain and watch her for escape. If they or at least Adam could sense her defense going active, that would have been like drawing a weapon, and Sienna didn\u2019t want to provoke a fight she couldn\u2019t win. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because if not, a lot of the actions undertaken during that fight and others have to be recast in the light of people being willing to kill </div> </div> </div>I am certain you would unconsciously assume that a criminal organization\u2019s enforcers are carrying loaded firearms. Why wouldn\u2019t a criminal organization arm their soldiers and make sure they have a basic understanding of firearms?<br /> <br /> Why would anyone assume that combatants on Remnant don\u2019t know how to use Aura?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do we actually know this? I don't think we have confirmation either way that Kali has an awakened aura, although Ghira almost certainly does. </div> </div> </div>I could believe that a man Ghira\u2019s size might be able to carry a man through his house one-handed like the morning newspaper without magic, but perhaps you have forgotten that Kali is a small woman and Yuma was bigger than her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T11:18:42-08:00","id":1186364,"title":"","content":"Oh, and Kali could also block gunshots with a wooden tea tray. So she seems to know enough about Aura to make her weapons unbreakable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T11:22:30-08:00","id":1186365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1186183#post1186183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't seem like a good idea. It's like if the Exalted Maidens all had the same powers and portfolios. That would be a lot duller than what we have now, wouldn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to be That Guy... But consider how literally every single Solar PC made in Exalted has the exact same powersuite in the form of Charm Selection, and it comes down to which powers you 'naturally' use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T12:00:46-08:00","id":1186371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1186357#post1186357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You think Jaune is normal for his world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, nobody acts like he isn't despite him displaying ignorance that should provoke a big reaction if it's out of the ordinary, which is a strong indicator.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't even try and work Jaune's ignorance of aura into the wider context of the world of Remnant. I chalk it up to bad writing and completely ignore it, because if you pay attention to it it comes disturbingly close to breaking the setting. It's like Torchwick's &quot;map&quot; of Vale; it's completely ridiculous and contradicts so much else shown onscreen that trying to reconcile it is a bit of a mug's game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cNormal\u201d for Remnant are combat schools that serve as high schools. </div> </div> </div>Normal isn't the same as common, tho. We don't how common combat schools are or how much of the populace attends them. Logically speaking, EVERY school should be a combat school, because literally everyone on Remnant ought to be trained at arms, capable of fighting to protect and defend themselves in a world where rage demons can literally congeal themselves out of nothing and can show up even in civilized, defended enclaves with no warning. But that doesn't seem to be the case, especially in the cities.<br /> <br /> I mean, hell. The students of top-tier combat schools panic and flee en masse in the face of Grimm attacks. Lots of people in Remnant, including those being trained at arms, just seem to be real shitty at fighting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oscar is much more normal than Jaune, and no one talks about \u201cawakening\u201d his Aura in the way that Second Edition talker about \u201cenlightening\u201d a mortal\u2019s Essence. </div> </div> </div>Presumably it was already unlocked (I fucked up the terminology; the show calls it &quot;unlocking&quot;) by the time that became relevant? Oz seems like he could have unlocked Oscar's for him.<br /> <br /> It does seem clear that it isn't just working all the time for everyone; you do need to have it unlocked. It's there, but can't be used, like most peoples Essence in Creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why didn\u2019t Sienna Khan have her Aura ready? Adam made sure to make it look like he planned to capture and hold her, what with having so many men available to detain and watch her for escape. If they or at least Adam could sense her defense going active, that would have been like drawing a weapon, and Sienna didn\u2019t want to provoke a fight she couldn\u2019t win. </div> </div> </div>Do we even know Sienna Khan is a warrior, a fighter, with an unlocked aura?<br /> <br /> She wasn't armed, after all. Perhaps she relied on her natural weapons, like Ghira does; Ghira didn't go around armed either despite <i>knowing</i> he was in personal danger. Perhaps she didn't see the need to be armed in her throne room. Or maybe she's an inspirational politician and leader of men because of her force of personality and skills at oratory and negotiation, rather than from her ability to beat the shit out of people. Perhaps she doesn't have an unlocked aura at all and Adam could simply gut her like a fish in the regular way.<br /> <br /> There's also the possibility that Adam's aura and/or semblance are useful for neutralizing those of others. Yang's aura was far from depleted and he cut right through her like she was literally nothing; her aura did jack and shit to protect her and she was out of that fight and in shock literally before she hit the ground; maybe his sword is special. I seem to recall that Adam's semblance has something to do with storing and releasing energy directed against him; if he can &quot;bank&quot; that for awhile, it might not have mattered if Sienna did have an unlocked aura that was at full strength; maybe he just cut straight through it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would anyone assume that combatants on Remnant don\u2019t know how to use Aura? </div> </div> </div>Having an unlocked aura seems enough out of the common way that I don't think I would assume that just because someone is wielding a weapon that they have it unlocked.<br /> <br /> But say I grant the point and most people would never, ever even pick up a weapon and try to fight without an unlocked aura unless there were literally no other option.<br /> <br /> That still raises questions. Can a fighter tell how much aura another fighter has? There are clearly ways of doing so, the Vytal Festival does it, but is that something that can be done regularly, so you can always tell how hard a hit a person can or cannot take without you punching through their aura and killing them? Aura doesn't seem to provide &quot;guaranteed last-hit protection as long as it's up, like Divine Shield in Hearthstone&quot; as some people once theorized; if it did Yang wouldn't be missing an arm. So if you don't KNOW how much aura someone has, when you hit them hard with a deadly weapon you ought to be acting with killing intent, because you don't know that you're not going to deplete their aura and just kill them outright.<br /> <br /> If fighters can sense each others auras, that makes things a lot easier, because you can always tell when to pull the blow if you aren't fighting to kill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I could believe that a man Ghira\u2019s size might be able to carry a man through his house one-handed like the morning newspaper without magic, but perhaps you have forgotten that Kali is a small woman and Yuma was bigger than her. </div> </div> </div>What's that got to do with the state of Kali's aura? Does aura make you super-strong?<br /> <br /> Also, Kali was not casually one-handing Yuma; she as dragging him along the ground, with the floor supporting his weight. If Kali is an athletic woman who keeps in shape, that ought to be entirely possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T12:27:44-08:00","id":1186378,"title":"","content":"Kali was holding Yuma\u2019s torso off the ground. His legs were dragging because he was limp. Most of his weight was carried by Kali.<br /> <br /> And why don\u2019t you think Aura is used for super-strength?<br /> <br /> Also, why are you talking about \u201canyone who picks up a weapon\u201d? I thought we were talking about Junior\u2019s goons and the White Fang grunts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T04:38:20-08:00","id":1186610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1186365#post1186365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to be That Guy... But consider how literally every single Solar PC made in Exalted has the exact same powersuite in the form of Charm Selection, and it comes down to which powers you 'naturally' use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dawn's can't Charmshare. Zenith can't mute their essence flare. Its not impossible that each maiden has a &quot;thing&quot;. Then again, it might just be that each one has a special locked door and thats what matters about their naming schema. <br /> <br /> Tbh, after i found out Mounty made them up on a whim between seasons i havent had any grand attachment to them. Whatever the series does with them will be a means to justify having them in the show, and not the other way around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T13:56:34-08:00","id":1186808,"title":"","content":"There is a difference between having access to the same charm selection and actually knowing and using the same charms. Because no character ever has enough XP to get all the charms they want, you still end up with parties where each character has a different charm set, prioritised according to their unique personal preferences. The difference stems from having to choose a subset of the total of available options.<br /> <br /> The Maidens, if they truly all have the complete set of seasonal powers, have no difference in that regard. They each got given the full set. That, and the fact that they are chosen rather than choosing to become maidens means that the maiden powers have pretty much zero character impact. Note that I'm not saying no maiden has character traits. I'm saying none of their traits will ever be reflected in their powers, and that is serious waste of storytelling potential in my opinion. Just like the silver eye thing, the maiden powers appear to simply be mcguffins so far.<br /> <br /> I mean, is there anything about Raven that suggests spring? Or is she just a scared madwoman who killed someone to gain some powers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T17:59:43-08:00","id":1186882,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://i0.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/newsfeed/001/342/503/1dc.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T11:35:34-08:00","id":1189436,"title":"","content":"Ok, this is the best Bumblebe image I've seen, and had to share:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://68.media.tumblr.com/e016c62639fc4590d7fc4009f1a06c15/tumblr_op1yf8l2Gu1r6qp7wo1_1280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> and an explanation of all the tatoos: <a href=\"https://y8ay8a.tumblr.com/post/160079863404/as-ive-had-several-people-asking-so-heres-the\" target=\"_blank\">https://y8ay8a.tumblr.com/post/16007...g-so-heres-the</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T22:08:25-07:00","id":1207887,"title":"","content":"*pokes head into thread*<br /> <br /> Huh. Weird place to put a RWBY thread, but alright.<br /> <br /> I finished Volume 5 and\u2026ugh.<br /> <br /> So\u2026here's the thing: much of Volume 5's issues are nothing new. That in my eyes, they're issues that have plagued the series from the beginning. The issue, of course, is that these problems reached their peak and just snowballed into this volume.<br /> <br /> -<b><i>Too much boring plot</i></b><br /> <br /> As well known by now, RWBY's major flaw since the beginning has been it's boring plot. That it's been weighed down with overly simplistic Light vs Darkness conflict played too straight, tropey McGuffin plots with the Maidens and the Relics, more &quot;it's your Destiny&quot; nonsense, and the politicking between factions and characters we don't really care about. While all of this is stuff that's nothing new\u2026the issue is that the show has quadrupled down on this aspect of the story.<br /> <br /> As has been noted by many others, Volume 3 was a shift in direction in that the series became much more story-driven then action-driven of Volumes 1-2. This shift has continued in Volume 4, and even more into Volume 5. But instead of really improving on and making the plot stronger and more interesting\u2026it just added more of what was already there. Suffocating the action pieces and characters that the show had previously known for.<br /> <br /> Which leads into\u2026<br /> <br /> -<b><i>A lot of exposition dumps (and talking)</i></b><br /> <br /> As discussed before\u2026yeah way too much talking and exposition.<br /> <br /> It's also kind of baffling that we have so much exposition dumps\u2026on top of the existing World of Remnant Lore series, we STILL have to stop everything to explain things. The aforementioned bit of Raven dropping Ozpin's &quot;secret&quot;, Ozpin explaining (partly) his true nature and relationship to Oscar, Ozpin having to stop to explain Hazel's backstory, it just keeps going. And that's on top of the constant Telling of the story instead of Showing: characters talking about their character and developing, progressing the plot by talking about it, instead of doing anything to show it.<br /> <br /> It even rears up during my favorite scene of the whole volume: Weiss and Yang reuniting with Team RNJR, them having dinner with each other, and everyone just bantering and interacting with each other, and was a microcosm of everything about Volumes 1-2\u2026but then it comes to a halt when the characters ACTUALLY STOP TO DECLARE WHAT THEIR CHARACTER DEVELOPMENT WAS LIKE.<br /> <br /> It leaves the impression that the setting, lore, and story have become way too big for the production team to reasonably matter and use.<br /> <br /> -<b><i>Too much set-up, unsatisfying payoff</i></b><br /> <br /> Although in Volume 5's case it's more about the unsatisfying payoff since the &quot;too much set-up&quot;.<br /> <br /> A historical problem with prior volumes stretching out setting up and foreshadowing plot points. Volume 5 payed off some of that set-up\u2026but badly. Where the degree of set-up in these developments doesn't really match the degree of pay-off given. A chief example was, as I mentioned before, Raven's &quot;reveal&quot; on Ozpin's dark secret\u2026and how said secret turned out to not be really special. Both on the new information given, but also how that information was presented being overall underwhelming. Other notes of underwhelming payoff include:<ul><li><b>Reveangence: Cinder vs Ruby</b>\u2026not actually being fulfilled. That she made it clear, multiple times throughout Volumes 4 and 5, that she would love nothing more to deliver payback on Ruby because of how she wounded her back in Volume 3, and likewise with Ruby on avenging Pyhrra. And yet when the two finally meet up again\u2026nothing. In fact, when Cinder does get killed, it's by Raven's hand and not Ruby's. And the context on why Raven fights her is completely separate and exclusive from Ruby's context. Which leaves that plot thread dangling and any potential development falling flat.</li> <li><b>Yang's pursuit for Raven</b> - one of the main character goals for Yang since the beginning is finding her mother Raven. For wanting to know why she abandoned her and what could possibly be more important than her own flesh-and-blood daughter. And yet when the two finally have their big meet-up\u2026Yang is just concerned on meeting back up with Ruby. Doesn't even bother questioning her mother the way she promised, all the way back in Volume 2. Oh but then they do get a proper verbal confrontation when they meet back up in the Spring Vault but it still felt\u2026off. It wasn't REALLY focused on why Raven wasn't there for Yang and her family\u2026or if it is it goes about it in such a roundabout way to not be obvious. And it ends unsatisfyingly as Raven kinda just\u2026fucks off and lets Yang grab the Relic of Knowledge.</li> <li><b>Blake and Adam</b> - The past few volumes Blake has had the most tangible character arc. Her fear of getting others hurt in her personal conflict came to a head with Yang in Volume 3, prompting her to run away, and Volume 4 lead with her dealing with her self-doubt and insecurities, with the rest of Volume 5 on her finally overcoming it and taking a stand against everything wrong with the White Fang. And it culminates in her confronting Adam, with Blake declaring that she won't stand for Adam and his hateful ways and won't be afraid of him anymore. On top of the militant arm of the White Fang being taken a huge blow when their fellow Faunus stand against them\u2026and then the wind gets taken out of it when Adam fucking runs off and evades capture! Even though now any conflict with Blake has been completely resolved, and his future appearances will be completely pointless. WHY. DRAG. IT. OUT. IT'S OVER. IT'S DONE. ROOSTERTEETH, STAHP PLEASE.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> I could go on: smaller stuff like the tease of Nora's backstory in Volume 4 isn't followed up on, Neo still remains mysteriously absent, Jaune's Semblance being unlocked through a death fakeout on Weiss, and once again YET ANOTHER VOLUME GOES BY WITHOUT EXPLAINING WHAT THE FUCK RUBY'S SILVER EYES ARE.<br /> <br /> -<b><i>Unmemorable fights</i></b><br /> <br /> So\u2026the main selling point of the whole show, the WHOLE REASON why a fanbase for Monty Oum even exists\u2026and are still underwhelming.<br /> <br /> Now granted, from my perspective the fight scenes within RWBY have been heavily flawed, even during the Volumes when Monty was still around.<br /> <br /> Previous volumes, while exciting, dynamic, and fun to watch they still felt kind of\u2026one note. That after a while all the fight scenes started to blend together and feel like the exact same fight, over and over again. The reason why fights like RWBY &amp; JNPR vs Death Stinger &amp; Nevermore from Volume 1 and the Food Fight at the beginning of the Volume 2 isn't JUST the fight choreography but everything else surrounding it. From the location of the fight, to the narrative context, or just set piece moments. Because outside of that? None of the fight scenes stood on their own. I could not tell you a think about the fight scenes at the end of Volume 1 and 2 without going back to rewatch the episodes. Because the context surrounding the fights are so one-note and forgettable, without big moments to set them apart.<br /> <br /> Within Volumes 4-5, it continued to carry those issues\u2026and more.<br /> <br /> As has been stated before, the fights in Volumes 3-4 have become more\u2026grounded. In the sense that fights become less dynamic, less air-time, and less visual flair. Compounding with the show's existing issues of lackluster narrative context, this makes the fights stand out even less. I can't tell you about any of the fights in Volume 3-4, much less 5. These issues still remain in Volume 5. That said, 5 has a much bigger issue with the fights (which I THINK also had roots in Volume 4, but I can't quite recall)\u2026and that's the ruined flow due to dialogue. Where characters stop to talk in during a fight, making the pacing of the fight grind to a halt, or the classic &quot;character standing on one side of the&quot; This is among the worst tropes associated with the Shonen action genre, and is regularly ridiculed whenever it crops up, and rightfully so. RWBY has always faced criticisms about using and relying on anime tropes unironically, with no self-awareness, and lazily enough to not do anything interesting with them. YMMV on how you feel about that (I personally was fine with it)\u2026but it becomes an even bigger issue if they start using the BAD tropes.<br /> <br /> Either that or the much more atrocious editing of fights, where a fight would start\u2026but then where we instead cut to different characters not engaged in any action, and once again back to the boring as hell dialogue scene. Breaking any pacing and flow in what are already mediocre fights.<br /> <br /> The ONE exception to this\u2026was the Raven vs Cinder fight. This was by far the most memorable fight in the whole volume. This whole scene really gave off the impression of two goddesses clashing. They were zipping around the (open air) space of the Spring Gate doing air juggles and combos. It's one Seasonal Maiden versus another. Cinder using the full amount of her summoned weapons, Raven keeping things simple with her sword. The (admittedly well-worn) fire vs ice aesthetics\u2026it all comes together so wonderfully!<br /> <br /> So yeah\u2026Volume 5 is currently RWBY at rock-bottom. While I feel it was never the animated classic that some people consider it, even with the association to Monty Oum, it still had a likeable charm to it. That charm is all but gone now. And the worst parts are getting magnified and deepened for everyone to see, with nothing really being done to address them. Aside from just adding more to it. And the series' future, if nothing is addressed, is dire.<br /> <br /> \u2026yeah, I think I'll do a thing reflecting on the series as a whole\u2026later.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T01:54:24-07:00","id":1207912,"title":"","content":"Yeah I thought Volume 4 was pretty turgid but it still managed to deliver better than Volume 5. Tyrian vs. team RNJR and Qrow was awesome with a fighting style every bit as manic as his posture and mannerisms suggested and the Nuckelavee was a terrifying enemy from the past for Ren and Nora.<br /> <br /> This time?<br /> Raven and the tribe were a massive disappointment. The set-up there was so intriguing, there was something kind of otherworldly about the meeting between the Branwen siblings and the reveal of Qrow's bad luck semblance made me wonder if they were taking different approaches to the same power. Nope! Semblances are just monkey shit random and non-magical unlike the ability to <b>turn into birds</b>. That's way more magical than teleportation via cutting holes in reality and passive bad luck that's left you a blight on your friends and loved ones.<br /> <br /> I'm curious what we'll learn about this in time because it reminds me of the Mass Effect series changing from the dark energy crisis to fears of the singularity in such an awkward way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-17-2018, 04:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T02:37:23-07:00","id":1207917,"title":"","content":"Oh, right, I should finish this one off. Literally forgot I was watching it at one point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T05:25:53-07:00","id":1207951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1207887#post1207887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026yeah, I think I'll do a thing reflecting on the series as a whole\u2026later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd start with a question - why watch the show at all? Maybe I'm missing something, but I don't see where you've described anything you unreservedly <i>enjoy</i> about the work, in season 5 or any previous season. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T11:58:24-07:00","id":1208094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1207951#post1207951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd start with a question - why watch the show at all? Maybe I'm missing something, but I don't see where you've described anything you unreservedly <i>enjoy</i> about the work, in season 5 or any previous season.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Because this is my first time posting in this sub-forum and even realizing that there IS a RWBY thread.<br /> <br /> 2. Yes, I have been with this show since the beginning. Without getting into too much detailed, my thoughts can be best summed up as &quot;entertaining but seriously flawed&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:39:38-07:00","id":1208150,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one that still likes this show at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:52:08-07:00","id":1208156,"title":"","content":"lol XD<br /> I like it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T14:34:07-07:00","id":1208182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1207912#post1207912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Nope! Semblances are just monkey shit random and non-magical unlike the ability to <b>turn into birds</b>. That's way more magical than teleportation via cutting holes in reality and passive bad luck that's left you a blight on your friends and loved ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget Flynt Cole, who can literally create multi-colored duplicates of himself. He <i>clones himself,</i> creating mass out of nothing.<br /> <br /> This is unremarkable, but apparently the bird thing is not.<br /> <br /> We have a discussion earlier in the thread about how... basically, the people in-universe can be expected to have some idea of &quot;this is within normal bounds of Semblances&quot; and &quot;whoa what the fuck is that, that's weird and scary, are you a witch?&quot;<br /> <br /> We don't! We don't live in Remnant! We don't have this frame of reference! The fandom almost universally assumed that Qrow's Semblance was his ability to turn into a birb, because this seems acceptable to us as something a Semblance lets you do. But I guess it isn't?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T16:30:46-07:00","id":1208232,"title":"","content":"That and everyone took the whole giving Qrow and Raven the ability to turn into birds like Oz had crossed some insane line or taboo. Which never made sense to me, I mean maybe if he'd canonically said he chose those birds because of their names then you could list it as a pun thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T18:07:04-07:00","id":1208265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208150#post1208150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one that still likes this show at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I unresevedly love this show, flaws and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T18:12:36-07:00","id":1208267,"title":"","content":"I also love this show.<br /> <br /> Aside from Jaune's character arc in Volume 1, the show has never disappointed me so much as to turn me against it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, now that we got Terrestrial Melee, I want to take another crack at statting up Raven's weapon.<br /> <br /> I'm undecided about whether the base weapon is black jade, moonsilver, or orichalcum, but all of the blades should be jade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T19:22:49-07:00","id":1208286,"title":"","content":"I enjoy the show, I still buy the soundtracks for each season cause I enjoy those. The last season just had some annoying problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T19:26:00-07:00","id":1208288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208182#post1208182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't forget Flynt Cole, who can literally create multi-colored duplicates of himself. He <i>clones himself,</i> creating mass out of nothing.<br /> <br /> This is unremarkable, but apparently the bird thing is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>The big deal about it, I felt, is not the transformation itself. It's the fact it's a bullshit power that is NOT a semblance. Everyone gets one bullshit power, and Qrow and Raven have TWO. It wouldn't make a lot of difference if the second power was weather control or the ability to read books <i>really</i> fast.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T19:26:48-07:00","id":1208289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208286#post1208286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I enjoy the show, I still buy the soundtracks for each season cause I enjoy those. The last season just had some annoying problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah! I love the show, but EVERY volume has some annoying problems.<br /> <br /> Hell, I don't know many wholly-professional productions that don't have some annoying problems.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208288#post1208288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big deal about it, I felt, is not the transformation itself. It's the fact it's a bullshit power that is NOT a semblance. Everyone gets one bullshit power, and Qrow and Raven have TWO. It wouldn't make a lot of difference if the second power was weather control or the ability to read books <i>really</i> fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the Schnee Semblance is at least three different bullshit powers in one.<br /> <br /> Rather, we haven't seen a single Semblance so far that physically CHANGES a person.<br /> <br /> Blake and Flynt are creating empty copies of themselves from Aura, but nothing of true flesh and bone, let alone doing anything to their own flesh and bone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-17-2018, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T20:16:37-07:00","id":1208299,"title":"","content":"The schnees are noted as an oddball, but it's more that their semblance is a very broad bullshit magic-thingie. &quot; a bunch of glyphs that do a bunch of elemental spacetime shenanigans &quot; is a far more unified concept than &quot;he's unlucky and turns into a bird&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 04-18-2018, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T21:34:12-07:00","id":1208316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208182#post1208182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't forget Flynt Cole, who can literally create multi-colored duplicates of himself. He <i>clones himself,</i> creating mass out of nothing.<br /> <br /> This is unremarkable, but apparently the bird thing is not.<br /> <br /> We have a discussion earlier in the thread about how... basically, the people in-universe can be expected to have some idea of &quot;this is within normal bounds of Semblances&quot; and &quot;whoa what the fuck is that, that's weird and scary, are you a witch?&quot;<br /> <br /> We don't! We don't live in Remnant! We don't have this frame of reference! The fandom almost universally assumed that Qrow's Semblance was his ability to turn into a birb, because this seems acceptable to us as something a Semblance lets you do. But I guess it isn't?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208232#post1208232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That and everyone took the whole giving Qrow and Raven the ability to turn into birds like Oz had crossed some insane line or taboo. Which never made sense to me, I mean maybe if he'd canonically said he chose those birds because of their names then you could list it as a pun thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously.<br /> <br /> It'd be one thing if...ooh, I dunno, if Raven and Qrow had no control over their transformations, or that they started to manifest since weird bird qualities that made them ostracized from human society...but nope! They can turn into birds and there doesn't seem to be any drawback at all!<br /> <br /> With the only revelation about Ozpin being the whole reincarnating thing...which doesn't seem like something inherently bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T23:26:59-07:00","id":1208339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208299#post1208299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The schnees are noted as an oddball, but it's more that their semblance is a very broad bullshit magic-thingie. &quot; a bunch of glyphs that do a bunch of elemental spacetime shenanigans &quot; is a far more unified concept than &quot;he's unlucky and turns into a bird&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Also I believe Winter said one of the anomolies with their family Semblance is that it is actually a thing that is inherited through the family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T00:19:57-07:00","id":1208352,"title":"","content":"I'm always careful to check if my feelings towards a show like RWBY are motivated by my love of Exalted.<br /> <br /> The reveal of Qrow's semblance last season made me go &quot;yes, this is what I want from Abyssals he's a cursed man with a sword/scythe who feels he needs to keep his distance from his loved ones&quot; and I know I was disappointed when Raven didn't have a similar deal because among other things that's cooler to me than a random superpower lottery.<br /> <br /> So I initially felt I was being unreasonable for feeling this way, I liked Qrow but I shouldn't just want Raven to be a female Qrow after being in the background for four seasons. Then we got to Downfall (more on that in a bit) and I still didn't understand her, initially it seemed like Adventure Time's decision to portray Finn's dad as a disappointing fuck-up of a human being rather than give us real answers about where he came from or even give us another big damn villain which I also didn't like but respected after reconnecting with my biological father much later in life. Except that's not who Raven is either, she's clearly been watching over Yang for years clearly checking in enough to sweep in for the rescue against Neo, maybe she took a break when Tai Yang (I love how his name is Big Yang, since learning this I've wanted to start calling someone in my life Big (Name of their Child), but it's not stuck yet) moved on with Summer Rose?<br /> <br /> I'm also not saying she can't be conflicted, but her goals? They're boring and it's arguably even worse once we learn she's the Spring Maiden. If she had someone extremely powerful but inexperienced at her side then that banditry could be training, gradually building up to something bigger. Instead she's one of the most powerful people in the entire series and isn't really doing anything with that.<br /> <br /> But yeah I dunno, it feels like we could've given them both the bad luck semblance possibly as something Ozpin gave them or enhanced and have it turn Raven into a bitter misanthrope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T01:24:45-07:00","id":1208355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208352#post1208352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm always careful to check if my feelings towards a show like RWBY are motivated by my love of Exalted.<br /> <br /> The reveal of Qrow's semblance last season made me go &quot;yes, this is what I want from Abyssals he's a cursed man with a sword/scythe who feels he needs to keep his distance from his loved ones&quot; and I know I was disappointed when Raven didn't have a similar deal because among other things that's cooler to me than a random superpower lottery.<br /> <br /> So I initially felt I was being unreasonable for feeling this way, I liked Qrow but I shouldn't just want Raven to be a female Qrow after being in the background for four seasons. Then we got to Downfall (more on that in a bit) and I still didn't understand her, initially it seemed like Adventure Time's decision to portray Finn's dad as a disappointing fuck-up of a human being rather than give us real answers about where he came from or even give us another big damn villain which I also didn't like but respected after reconnecting with my biological father much later in life. Except that's not who Raven is either, she's clearly been watching over Yang for years clearly checking in enough to sweep in for the rescue against Neo, maybe she took a break when Tai Yang (I love how his name is Big Yang, since learning this I've wanted to start calling someone in my life Big (Name of their Child), but it's not stuck yet) moved on with Summer Rose?<br /> <br /> I'm also not saying she can't be conflicted, but her goals? They're boring and it's arguably even worse once we learn she's the Spring Maiden. If she had someone extremely powerful but inexperienced at her side then that banditry could be training, gradually building up to something bigger. Instead she's one of the most powerful people in the entire series and isn't really doing anything with that.<br /> <br /> But yeah I dunno, it feels like we could've given them both the bad luck semblance possibly as something Ozpin gave them or enhanced and have it turn Raven into a bitter misanthrope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Raven bothers me more than anyone else in the show. The Maiden reveal was a bait-and-switch, and that aside, what is her motivation? <i>Don't die</i>? if she was a &quot;survive at any cost&quot; type she wouldn't have picked up a superpower that is primarily transferred <b><i>by murder</i></b>. If she was truly a Nietzschean power-seeker she wouldn't hide out in secret and let the world pass her by. She's been running a bandit camp for more than ten years, but she doesn't seem to have a clue how to manage or manipulate people. She knows that Yang is desperately searching for her and her plan for convincing her huntress-daughter to join up is &quot;how about stay with me forever and let your sister DIE&quot;, no deal, no plan, she doesn't even pull a &quot;I'll help you to prove how much better an option I am then they are&quot;. She fails at being an Opportunist (imo the only thing left to her after Survivor and Power Seeker).<br /> <br /> Her character seems to based solely on what will provoke drama and conflict, not on any agency she personally has.<br /> <br /> The &quot;what is Magic&quot; thing has been covered extensively in this thread already, and the fact that the <i>fandom majority</i> assumed that Qrow's semblance was shapeshifting shows how poorly the whole thing was handled. A single throw away line about semblances never changing the body would have helped. Everyone's reaction to the &quot;Magic&quot; was also nonsensical considering all the other stuff we've seen. The whole thing was poorly handled.<br /> <br /> Adam's S5 subplot didn't go anywhere and the payoff was thrown away instead of delayed. Hazel's Motivation is super contradictory which would have made for decent characterization except it doesn't get acknowledged at all. Cinder uses her hatred for Ruby as her motivation to get stronger and keep going, but when presented with a chance to kill her most hated foe and literal kryptonite she instead decides to kill someone else out of petty spite.<br /> <br /> And most of all, there weren't enough fights in a show designed around fights, and the fights we did get were mostly filler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T01:42:51-07:00","id":1208359,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think Raven being the way she is portrayed and still being the Spring Maiden would have felt a bit better if there was an indicator that she hadn't slaughtered its predecessor for it.* You know give some indicator that she has it against her will. <br /> <br /> *I admit I don't remember was her plan also to actually take the relic, or was it just kill Cinder when her back is turned and bail out not grabbing the relic because that's an even bigger target?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T01:49:43-07:00","id":1208362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208355#post1208355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cinder uses her hatred for Ruby as her motivation to get stronger and keep going, but when presented with a chance to kill her most hated foe and literal kryptonite she instead decides to kill someone else out of petty spite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh god, this.<br /> Putting aside my mixed feelings about the prominence of Jaune's role and the fact he's voiced by one of the head writers in a series that was sold to us as being about a team of four women inspired by fairytale heroines...<br /> <br /> What would have really changed if Cinder hadn't been contradictory and impaled Ruby instead of Weiss?<br /> You'd still have a fight that was going against Qrow and the Beacon students while Jaune did the healing only now the person coming off the bench (because nobody believed that character death fake-out) and turning the tide is the main character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T06:19:10-07:00","id":1208415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208362#post1208362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putting aside my mixed feelings about the prominence of Jaune's role and the fact he's voiced by one of the head writers </div> </div> </div> </div>Miles didn\u2019t create Jaune. Monty created Jaune.<br /> <br /> Miles didn\u2019t choose to voice Jaune. Monty chose him to voice Jaune. (Miles didn\u2019t even get to choose which kind of voice Jaune would have; that was Monty again.)<br /> <br /> Miles doesn\u2019t write for Jaune, and has grown extremely uncomfortable with any writing related to Jaune because of the backlash. Kerry is the one who writes for this character that Monty wanted in the show. Heck, Kerry is the reason Jaune\u2019s color is yellow instead of blue Jean. <br /> <br /> Please do not blame Miles for what you dislike about Jaune. Miles wanted to voice someone like Torchwick, as he does with Red Versus Blue\u2019s Felix. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> in a series that was sold to us as being about a team of four women inspired by fairytale heroines... </div> </div> </div>Please, the problem isn\u2019t strictly about Jaune. It\u2019s about Team JNPR as a whole. <br /> <br /> I think that Rooster Teeth made a huge mistake in trying to have eight main characters. I feel they should have focused on Team RWBY much more, especially in Volume 1, and introduced a second team of side characters in Volume 2.<br /> <br /> That side team would be either JNPR or CFVY, and would fill all roles thereof. They would be the ones to show up and help at the Breach, the ones to lose a team member like Pyrrha (probably Velvet, for CFVY), and the survivors would follow Ruby to Mistral. <br /> <br /> As it stands, Nora and Ren have not been handled like main characters. They have always been treated as secondary characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T06:30:25-07:00","id":1208418,"title":"","content":"As for Raven\u2019s character, she\u2019s a coward who runs away from her problems until she\u2019s backed into a corner, where she doubles down by making hasty decisions she knows are stupid.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s how she acted when found by Cinder. It\u2019s likely what happened when she failed to train the previous Spring Maiden.<br /> <br /> Raven is not the kind of woman who thinks bad decisions through. After all, she chose to return to the life of her childhood instead of using her amazing Semblance to comfortably earn lots of money funneling goods secretly and instantly between kingdoms.<br /> <br /> I think she killed the last Maiden in a fit of frustration. Maybe she didn\u2019t even mean to kill her, but instead endangered her life to force the Maiden to \u201ctoughen up\u201d.<br /> <br /> Raven can\u2019t bring herself to confess she killed Spring, and gets pissed off when Cinder implies Spring made a mistake in trusting her. Raven actually cries when she rants to Yang about the things she\u2019s \u201cbeen forced to do to survive\u201d. Raven is ashamed.<br /> <br /> But among the many things Raven fears, is appearing \u201cweak\u201d. So she puts up a front. She says bullshit she doesn\u2019t believe because it sounds dangerous and tough and like it might possibly justify the shit she does.<br /> <br /> Raven is biggest coward and liar in the show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T06:31:36-07:00","id":1208419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208415#post1208415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Miles didn\u2019t create Jaune. Monty created Jaune.<br /> <br /> Miles didn\u2019t choose to voice Jaune. Monty chose him to voice Jaune. (Miles didn\u2019t even get to choose which kind of voice Jaune would have; that was Monty again.)<br /> <br /> Miles doesn\u2019t write for Jaune, and has grown extremely uncomfortable with any writing related to Jaune because of the backlash. Kerry is the one who writes for this character that Monty wanted in the show. Heck, Kerry is the reason Jaune\u2019s color is yellow instead of blue Jean.<br /> <br /> Please do not blame Miles for what you dislike about Jaune. Miles wanted to voice someone like Torchwick, as he does with Red Versus Blue\u2019s Felix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you provide a link to the interview where Monty said he was forcing Miles to play Jaune<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T06:37:25-07:00","id":1208422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208419#post1208419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you provide a link to the interview where Monty said he was forcing Miles to play Jaune</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you provide a link to \u201cThe world in which Jaune being voiced by someone else would make a meaningful difference\u201d?<br /> <br /> Miles does an amazing job voicing Jaune, especially in scenes where Jaune is coming apart at the seams<br /> <br /> Also, Miles and Monty were friends. Miles is only on the probject because Monty wanted him there. Why wouldn\u2019t Miles do what Monty asked by voicing the character Monty knew Miles would do a great job at?<br /> <br /> Do your friends have to force you to do things for them? Did Monty strike you as coercive?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-18-2018, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T06:49:53-07:00","id":1208425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208422#post1208422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> snip</div> </div> </div> </div>So you do not have any proof that this was all montys fault then? Like I get its in vogue to throw montys corpse under the bus at the slightest whiff of criticism but this is pretty absurd. Miles loves voicing main characters or characters who soak up the spotlight like a sponge (Felix/David) So the idea that THIS TIME he was forced at figurative gunpoint to do it rings hollow.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T13:01:34-07:00","id":1208537,"title":"","content":"I just don't care that much. It wasn't even all that relevant to the point I was making just acknowledging that people view the character as a creator's pet and that the scene has problems that go beyond Jaune stealing the spotlight again.<br /> <br /> Also don't agree on team JNPR itself being a mistake because a lot of people predicted that Pyrrha would go the way of Achilles, the notion that they might all be similarly doomed by fate has good narrative potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T13:48:27-07:00","id":1208561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208537#post1208537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't care that much. It wasn't even all that relevant to the point I was making just acknowledging that people view the character as a creator's pet and that the scene has problems that go beyond Jaune stealing the spotlight again.<br /> <br /> Also don't agree on team JNPR itself being a mistake because a lot of people predicted that Pyrrha would go the way of Achilles, the notion that they might all be similarly doomed by fate has good narrative potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm personally not convinced by the &quot;JNPR is doooooooomed&quot; concept. When Pyrrha went the way of the dodo, she had regularly raised multiple red flags. When season 3 closed, she had to either die or it would be clear no main character would ever die in RWBY.<br /> A couple seasons later, Ren, Norra and to an extent, Qrow have raised SO MANY FLAGS. Further, Nora and Ren are pretty much spent story-wise, and neither bring much to the cast that another could not provide.<br /> <br /> The point I'm trying to make is, if they wanted JNPR dead, they'd have taken down someone either at the end of S4 or during S5. The alternatives is either to maintain the &quot;DOOOOOOM&quot; hanging above their head (which is pretty meh) or to have them attempt a suicide mission at the tail end of the story, affording team RWBY access to the story's end (but that only works when the character still have openstanding stories, which leaves us with Jaune)<br /> <br /> At this point, I'm expecting classic shonen invincibility for RWBY and JNR until the last 3 episodes of the series, barring voice contract shenanigans. They tried to keep us on our toes with Pyrrha, but they spent their &quot;expendable&quot; MCs and won't dare another kill unless viewership crashes. Then we *may* have a &quot;people die TONIGHT&quot; season end with Nora and Ren biting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T14:48:27-07:00","id":1208583,"title":"","content":"I'm not arguing how it's going to play out now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T15:00:28-07:00","id":1208590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sagara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208561#post1208561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm personally not convinced by the &quot;JNPR is doooooooomed&quot; concept...A couple seasons later, Ren, Norra and to an extent, Qrow have raised SO MANY FLAGS.</div> </div> </div> </div>...this is my first time hearing about this.<br /> <br /> Expound, please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T15:24:48-07:00","id":1208599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208590#post1208590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...this is my first time hearing about this.<br /> <br /> Expound, please?</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I've heard it is that since Nora and Ren haven't done a lot to elevate themselves beyond secondary characters, and Jean being based of Joan of Arc, they will invariably end up dying off every once in a while for dramatic purposes. Not a particularly good argument for my mind, but eh some people speculate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T15:39:46-07:00","id":1208604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208599#post1208599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I've heard it is that since Nora and Ren haven't done a lot to elevate themselves beyond secondary characters, and Jean being based of Joan of Arc, they will invariably end up dying off every once in a while for dramatic purposes. Not a particularly good argument for my mind, but eh some people speculate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having not heard of it, it dos make some sense. Joan of Arc met a tragic end (by fire, no less. Also, Cardin is named after the Cardinal that condemned her). Thor has a prophesized doom, Achilles has a really famous one. I'm not familiar with Mulan though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T15:50:52-07:00","id":1208611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208599#post1208599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I've heard it is that since Nora and Ren haven't done a lot to elevate themselves beyond secondary characters, and Jean being based of Joan of Arc, they will invariably end up dying off every once in a while for dramatic purposes. Not a particularly good argument for my mind, but eh some people speculate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got it.<br /> <br /> Which I mean...never say never, but eh. I agree with the notion that Ren and Nora being shoved in the background when it comes to characterization. Even with Ren's arc in Volume 4 (which in of itself isn't great because it's yet another &quot;You killed my father! Prepare to die!!!&quot; storyline), if you were to skip his arc and jump right into Volume 5...Ren and Nora don't really act differently enough from their base characters. It might as well have not happened. And if it's in the cards for them to die...feels less like a mercy killing and more like just a waste.<br /> <br /> Jaune I always found to be the secondary protagonist that wasn't on Team RWBY. Killing him off I feel would be unwise.<br /> <br /> As for Qrow...ok fair enough, what with the whole &quot;death of the mentor&quot; trope. Dude did almost die at the end of this Volume.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T15:58:59-07:00","id":1208615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208604#post1208604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not familiar with Mulan though.</div> </div> </div> </div>*checks wikipedia*<br /> <br /> Yup...Mulan dies too.<br /> <br /> To make a long story short, in the Sui Tang Romance novel, Mulan heads home to find her family long passed away, and because of some bullshit earlier in the story, she'd be recalled back to the Emperor to become his latest concubine. Instead of giving in to this fate Mulan instead chooses to commit suicide.<br /> <br /> ...granted I don't think Ren becoming a concubine is going to be a thing unless if RT wanted to turn RWBY into a very different kind of show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 04-18-2018, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T20:32:57-07:00","id":1208693,"title":"","content":"And now my thoughts on RWBY as we stand right now.<br /> <br /> So, just so I can clarify where I'm coming from: I only consider myself a casual Monty Oum fan.<br /> <br /> I enjoyed the hell out of Dead Fantasy and Haloid when I first stumbled upon them. The parts where he did the fight scenes in Red vs Blue was among the best moments yet. When it came to RWBY, I was right there with everyone on the hype train when the Red trailer first dropped. And (obviously) followed through on it until Volume 5. That said\u2026I'm not a hardcore fan of Monty. I didn't closely follow with the BTS docs for RWBY, I haven't seen most of the World of Remnant shorts, nor have I been hanging on every word the man has spoken in interviews, podcasts, panels, etc. My feelings on him as an artist or his work hasn't fundamentally changed since his passing.<br /> <br /> While he and his life story was many people's Spark of Inspiration\u2026he just wasn't for me. I understand why he was for others. Just not me.<br /> <br /> I say this because there is the sense online that those who are diehard fans have been\u2026defending RWBY more then they reasonably should. That because Monty is gone, that we have to do everything to keep his passion project alive, and support in unconditionally regardless of quality of the work. Sorry, but I disagree with this mentality. No artist's/creator's work is immune from criticism, no matter the circumstances. In fact, I'm of the belief that the hardcore fans SHOULD be the ones who are the most vocal critics. They're the ones who have invested into the work. They're the ones who know exactly how and why they enjoy the work to begin with. And not bending over backwards to make everything in series of works are the best thing ever.<br /> <br /> For instance, as much as I'm on the side of the fence that enjoys Final Fantasy XV, I completely understand why people feel that game just didn't live up to past games, 10 year development cycle or not.<br /> <br /> So when I say that RWBY has always been a flawed mess, please understand it's not out of malice for the show, or of being deliberately disrespectful to Monty's memory. This is just one guy's honest opinion and nothing more.<br /> <br /> But\u2026yeah, the show has always been flawed from the beginning. While entertaining, but still flawed.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Volumes 1-2</b></i><br /> <br /> +Energetic, fun fight scenes<br /> +Entertaining, likeable, and relatable characters<br /> +RoosterTeeth-style comedy<br /> <br /> -Unpolished presentation<br /> -Simplistic-to-boring plotline<br /> -Uneven pacing<br /> -Fight scenes happening with little-to-no proper narrative context<br /> -&quot;Rule of Cool&quot; creating diminished dramatic tension and stakes<br /> <br /> <b><i>Volume 3</i></b><br /> <br /> +Bold status quo change<br /> +Intersection of characterization and plot development<br /> +Steadily more polished presentation<br /> <br /> -Status quo changing too much, too fast<br /> -Too many character deaths at once<br /> -Beginning of more &quot;grounded&quot; and less dynamic fight scenes<br /> <br /> <b><i>Volume 4</i></b><br /> <br /> +Current peak of polished presentation<br /> +Expanding the world<br /> <br /> -Tropey as hell plot revelations<br /> -Insignificant-to-no plot progression<br /> -Rushed, half-baked character development<br /> -Continuing &quot;grounded&quot; fight scenes<br /> -Downplaying of RT-style comedy<br /> <br /> <b><i>Volume 5</i></b><br /> <br /> +Still current peak of polished presentation<br /> <br /> -Unsatisfying storyline payoffs<br /> -Questionable metaplot revelations<br /> -Characterization taking a back seat to plot<br /> -Doubling down on the bland and boring plot<br /> -&quot;Grounded&quot; fight scenes at their worse<br /> -Pacing-killing editing<br /> -Almost complete absence of RT-style comedy<br /> <br /> So in my opinion, the show has never reached its peak. There was always just too many issues getting in the way from ever being something great. More depressingly, the depiction of the show promised in the early Red, White, Black, and Yellow trailers? That vision of the show hasn't been achieved yet. I'm still waiting for the show to achieve that potential. Although with each passing Volume\u2026that confidence on that coming to past is getting less and less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T21:12:38-07:00","id":1208706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208615#post1208615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *checks wikipedia*<br /> <br /> Yup...Mulan dies too.<br /> <br /> To make a long story short, in the Sui Tang Romance novel, Mulan heads home to find her family long passed away, and because of some bullshit earlier in the story, she'd be recalled back to the Emperor to become his latest concubine. Instead of giving in to this fate Mulan instead chooses to commit suicide.<br /> <br /> ...granted I don't think Ren becoming a concubine is going to be a thing unless if RT wanted to turn RWBY into a very different kind of show.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the original version of the story, that I believe first appeared during the Han era, she did live.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T21:17:34-07:00","id":1208708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1148951-rwby-volume-5?p=1208415#post1208415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Please, the problem isn\u2019t strictly about Jaune. It\u2019s about Team JNPR as a whole. <br /> <br /> I think that Rooster Teeth made a huge mistake in trying to have eight main characters. I feel they should have focused on Team RWBY much more, especially in Volume 1, and introduced a second team of side characters in Volume 2.<br /> <br /> That side team would be either JNPR or CFVY, and would fill all roles thereof. They would be the ones to show up and help at the Breach, the ones to lose a team member like Pyrrha (probably Velvet, for CFVY), and the survivors would follow Ruby to Mistral. <br /> <br /> As it stands, Nora and Ren have not been handled like main characters. They have always been treated as secondary characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont see JNPR as main characters like RWBY are. They are very much the B team of the show. But I see your point about their story focusing mostly on Jaune and Pyrra. Pyrra obviously to set her up as the sacrificial lion. But now I'm thinking this means Jaune has an important role in the plot to play too.<br /> <br /> You dont suppose they've been planning on Lancaster from the beginning do you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T05:07:35-07:00","id":1208805,"title":"","content":"Thing is, if you base your characters off of real people, they all die in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T17:51:15-07:00","id":1209075,"title":"","content":"Even most fictional characters do, unless they're in a story environment that allows for apotheosis or immortality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}